\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5180\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"none\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5181\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"none\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5182\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"none\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5183\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"none\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5184\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"none\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5185\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5199\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5218\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5221\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5223\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5227\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5263\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5269\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5270\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5293\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5304\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5305\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5306\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5309\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5310\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"none\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5312\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5356\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5364\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5383\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5384\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"evidence_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"e5385\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}]', 'changed': 1, 'why_changed': 'The rung is unchanged, but the key supporting calculation is updated: the recently supplied first-half FY2027 figure of $164 billion and the Q3 revenue guide support an explicit estimate of about $390 billion, rather than the previous conclusion’s roughly $395 billion. New evidence also sharpens the balance between Rubin-driven reacceleration and ongoing supply constraints.', 'config_checksum': '4f2aad7d25dae54d', 'call_id': 9022, 'request_sha256': 'b78f2fd531a1ae985f2c807230080ca7b27475a78337bab494ce8cbae0ef9bda', 'publication_day': '2026-09-20', 'theme_pushes_json': '[{\\\\\\\"view_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"v16\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"view_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"v22\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"view_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"v26\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"view_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"v27\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"view_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"v6\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"view_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"v7\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}, {\\\\\\\"view_id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"v9\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"push\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"toward_first\\\\\\\"}]', 'reference': 'Morningstar estimates FY2027 NVIDIA Data Center revenue at $361 billion; that is rung 2 ($350 billion to less than $400 billion).', 'implied_outcome': 'About $390 billion: $164 billion reported in the first half, about $100 billion in Q3 using the $108 billion total-revenue guidance midpoint and 92.5% recent Data Center mix, plus an estimated $126 billion in Q4 as hyperscale growth reaccelerates and Vera Rubin supply builds, discounted for continuing constraints.'}\\\\nsamples [{'evidence_id': 'e109', 'quote': 'During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales.', 'one_line': 'NVIDIA’s Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenue in fiscal Q1 2027, equal to 92% of total sales.', 'speaker': 'tradingview.com', 'original_who': 'NVIDIA', 'original_day': '', 'tier': 'fact', 'event_time': 'Fiscal Q1 2027', 'created_seq': 62, 'created_from_input': 'gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a', 'id': 176, 'view_id': 'v8', 'seq': 62}, {'evidence_id': 'e110', 'quote': 'Revenues from the segment surged 92% year over year and grew 21% sequentially, driven by the rapid ramp-up of Blackwell 300 systems and robust networking demand.', 'one_line': 'NVIDIA Data Center revenue grew 92% year over year and 21% sequentially in fiscal Q1 2027.', 'speaker': 'tradingview.com', 'original_who': 'NVIDIA', 'original_day': '', 'tier': 'fact', 'event_time': 'Fiscal Q1 2027', 'created_seq': 62, 'created_from_input': 'gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a', 'id': 177, 'view_id': 'v8', 'seq': 62}, {'evidence_id': 'e173', 'quote': 'Perplexity is now looking to deploy Vera in its upcoming production system.', 'one_line': 'Perplexity is looking to deploy NVIDIA Vera in an upcoming production system; no amount or date was stated.', 'speaker': 'NVIDIA Corporation', 'original_who': 'Perplexity', 'original_day': '', 'tier': 'party_statement', 'event_time': 'upcoming production system', 'created_seq': 77, 'created_from_input': 'nvblog:nvidia-vera-max-single-threaded-cpu-at-scale', 'id': 260, 'view_id': 'v8', 'seq': 77}, {'evidence_id': 'e179', 'quote': 'Nvidia said that this plan highlights a transition in AI demand from model building towards production inference tasks, needing continuous running of infrastructure at scale.', 'one_line': 'NVIDIA said AI demand is shifting from model building toward production inference tasks that require infrastructure to run continuously at scale.', 'speaker': 'finance.yahoo.com', 'original_who': 'NVIDIA', 'original_day': '2026-07-01', 'tier': 'party_statement', 'event_time': '', 'created_seq': 81, 'created_from_input': 'gnews:ce5daf57bdca5da657e5f677', 'id': 268, 'view_id': 'v8', 'seq': 81}]\\\\nold-2 [('views', 43), ('evidence', 5102), ('evidence_sources', 5102), ('judgements', 1616), ('replacements', 0)]\\\\nlabels [('Yes', 26), ('No', 26), ('Strongly bullish', 15), ('Strongly bearish', 15), ('Neutral', 15), ('Bullish', 15), ('Bearish', 15), ('Below $800 billion', 1), ('Below $500 billion', 1), ('$900 billion to below $1.1 trillion', 1), ('$800 billion to below $900 billion', 1), ('$800 billion or more', 1), ('$700 billion to below $800 billion', 1), ('$600 billion to below $700 billion', 1), ('$500 billion to below $600 billion', 1), ('$1.2 trillion or more', 1), ('$1.1 trillion to below $1.2 trillion', 1)]\\\\nsource cats [('T1', 63), ('T2', 21), ('T3', 2), ('T4', 42), ('T6', 224), ('T7', 2740), ('T8', 2010)]\\\\nkinds [('NVDA', 'asset'), ('ai-capex', 'theme'), ('chip-export-controls', 'theme'), ('fed-policy-rate', 'theme')]\\\\nold-3 [('views', 49), ('evidence', 5447), ('evidence_sources', 5447), ('judgements', 1707), ('replacements', 0)]\\\\nlabels [('Yes', 31), ('No', 31), ('Neutral', 17), ('Strongly bullish', 15), ('Strongly bearish', 15), ('Bullish', 15), ('Bearish', 15), ('Upper-middle range', 2), ('Lowest range', 2), ('Lower-middle range', 2), ('Highest range', 2), ('Middle', 1), ('Lowest', 1), ('Low', 1), ('Highest', 1)