items where input_id=?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",(e['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''created_from_input'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],)).fetchone()))\\\\n'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"('truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-02-25', 'NVIDIA Corporation', 'NVDA Q4 FY2026 Earnings Call', \\\\\\\"# NVDA Q4 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\\\\\n**Operator:** Good afternoon. My name is Sarah, and I will be your conference operator today. At this time, I would like to welcome everyone to NVIDIA's Fourth Quarter Earnings Call. [Operator Instructions]. Toshiya Hari, you may begin your conference.\\\\\\\\n**Toshiya Hari:*\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-05-20', 'NVIDIA Corporation', 'NVDA Q1 FY2027 Earnings Call', \\\\\\\"# NVDA Q1 FY2027 Earnings Call\\\\\\\\n**Operator:** Good afternoon. My name is Sarah, and I will be your conference operator today. At this time, I would like to welcome everyone to NVIDIA's First Quarter Earnings Call. All lines have been placed on mute to prevent any background noise. After the speakers'\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26', 'NVIDIA Corporation', 'NVDA Q2 FY2027 Earnings Call', \\\\\\\"# NVDA Q2 FY2027 Earnings Call\\\\\\\\n**Operator:** Good afternoon. My name is Tiffany, and I will be your conference operator today. At this time, I would like to welcome everyone to NVIDIA's second quarter earnings call. [Operator Instructions]. Toshiya Hari, you may begin your conference.\\\\\\\\n**Toshiya Hari\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:transcript:AMD:2026-08-04', 'Advanced Micro Devices', 'AMD Q2 FY2026 Earnings Call', '# AMD Q2 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\\\\\n**Operator:** Greetings, and welcome to the AMD Second Quarter 2026 Conference Call. [Operator Instructions] And please note that this conference is being recorded. I will now turn the conference over to Matt Ramsey, VP, Financial Strategy and IR. Thank you, Matt. You m')\\\\n('truenorth:transcript:AMZN:2026-07-30', 'Amazon', 'AMZN Q2 FY2026 Earnings Call', '# AMZN Q2 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\\\\\n**Operator:** Thank you for standing by. Good day, everyone, and welcome to the Amazon.com Quarter Two 2026 financial results teleconference. At this time, all participants are in a listen-only mode. After the presentation, we will conduct a question-and-answer session')\\\\n('truenorth:transcript:ASML:2026-10-14', 'ASML Holding', 'ASML Q3 FY2026 Earnings Call', \\\\\\\"# ASML Q3 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\\\\\n**Operator:** Good day, and thank you for standing by. Welcome to the ASML 26 Third Quarter Financial Results Conference Call on 10/14/2026, After the speakers' introduction, there will be a question-and-answer session. To ask a question during the session, you will ne\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:transcript:AVGO:2026-09-02', 'Broadcom', 'AVGO Q3 FY2026 Earnings Call', \\\\\\\"# AVGO Q3 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\\\\\n**Operator:** Welcome to Broadcom Inc.'s Third Quarter Fiscal Year 2026 Financial Results Conference Call. At this time, for opening remarks and introductions, I would like to turn the call over to Ji Yoo, Head of Investor Relations of Broadcom Inc. Please go ahead.\\\\\\\\n**\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:transcript:CRWV:2026-08-11', 'CoreWeave', 'CRWV Q2 FY2026 Earnings Call', \\\\\\\"# CRWV Q2 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\\\\\n**Operator:** Hello, everyone. Thank you for joining us, and welcome to CoreWeave's Second Quarter 2026 Earnings Call. [Operator Instructions] I will now hand the conference over to CoreWeave. Please go ahead.\\\\\\\\n**Unknown Executive:** Thank you. Good afternoon, and welco\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:transcript:DELL:2026-09-01', 'Dell Technologies', 'DELL Q2 FY2027 Earnings Call', \\\\\\\"# DELL Q2 FY2027 Earnings Call\\\\\\\\n**Operator:** Good afternoon, and welcome to the Fiscal Year 2027 Second Quarter Financial Results Conference Call for Dell Technologies Inc. I'd like to inform all participants this call is being recorded at the request of Dell Technologies. This broadcast is the copy\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:transcript:META:2026-07-29', 'Meta Platforms', 'META Q2 FY2026 Earnings Call', \\\\\\\"# META Q2 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\\\\\n**Operator:** Hello, and welcome to Meta's Second Quarter 2026 Earnings Conference Call. At this time, I would like to welcome everyone to Meta's Second Quarter 2026 Earnings Conference Call. And this call will be recorded. Thank you very much. Chad Heaton, Meta's Vice\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:transcript:META:2026-10-21', 'Meta Platforms', 'META Q3 FY2026 Earnings Call', \\\\\\\"# META Q3 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\\\\\n**Operator:** Good afternoon. My name is Krista, and I will be your conference operator. Today. At this time, I would like to welcome everyone to Meta's Third Quarter 26 Earnings Conference Call. All lines have been placed on mute to prevent any background noise. After\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:transcript:MSFT:2026-07-29', 'Microsoft', 'MSFT Q4 FY2026 Earnings Call', '# MSFT Q4 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\\\\\n**Operator:** Greetings, and welcome to the Microsoft Fiscal Year 2026 Fourth Quarter Earnings Conference Call. As a reminder, this conference is being recorded. It is now my pleasure to introduce Jonathan Neilson, Vice President of Investor Relations. Please go ahead.')\\\\n('truenorth:transcript:MU:2026-09-30', 'Micron Technology', 'MU Q4 FY2026 Earnings Call', \\\\\\\"# MU Q4 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\\\\\n**Operator:** Hello, everyone. Thank you for joining us, and welcome to Micron's Fourth Quarter Post-Earnings Analyst Call. [Operator Instructions] I will now hand the conference over to Satya Kumar, Corporate Vice President, Investor Relations and Treasury. Satya, pleas\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:transcript:ORCL:2026-09-10', 'Oracle', 'ORCL Q1 FY2027 Earnings Call', '# ORCL Q1 FY2027 Earnings Call\\\\\\\\n**Operator:** Good day, everyone, and welcome to the Oracle Corporation First quarter fiscal year 27 earnings call. Just a reminder that this call is being recorded. If you have a question today, please press 1 on your telephone keypad. Please limit yourself to 1 quest')\\\\n('truenorth:transcript:SMCI:2026-08-11', 'Super Micro Computer', 'SMCI Q4 FY2026 Earnings Call', \\\\\\\"# SMCI Q4 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\\\\\n**Operator:** Thank you for standing by. My name is Jen, and I will be your conference operator today. At this time, I would like to welcome everyone to the Super Micro Computer, Inc. Q4 FY '26 Business Update Call. With us today are Charles Liang, Founder, President a\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:transcript:TSM:2026-10-15', 'Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing', 'TSM Q3 FY2026 Earnings Call', \\\\\\\"# TSM Q3 FY2026 Earnings Call\\\\\\\\n**Jeff Su:** Good afternoon, everyone, and welcome to TSMC's third quarter 2026 earnings conference call. This is Jeff Su, TSMC's Director of Investor Relations and your host for today. TSMC is hosting our earnings conference call via live audio webcast through the comp\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fa144-e165-7c82-9e62-eda545606513', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia Reportedly Moves to Backstop $250 Billion in OpenAI Data Center Financing, Michael Burry Says, 'Around and Around We Go'\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia Reportedly Moves to Backstop $250 Billion in OpenAI Data Center Financing, Michael Burry Says, 'Around and Around We Go'\\\\\\\\nNvidia is reportedly in talks to provide a $250 billion financing guarantee for OpenAI's data center project in Ohio, with Michael Burry and Ed Zitron raising concerns abou\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fa1ad-b65a-70f3-8475-22532b009667', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Deepens South Korea AI Push With $1 Billion NAVER Investment', 'Nvidia Deepens South Korea AI Push With $1 Billion NAVER Investment\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA plans to invest $1 billion in NAVER by purchasing newly issued shares, deepening its AI push in South Korea with a focus on expanding AI datacenter infrastructure using Vera Rubin and Blackwell systems.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fa5b7-4053-7212-a591-5ca748ead6bb', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Funds AI Frenzy: Timeline of its Circular Financing Deals ... So Far', 'Nvidia Funds AI Frenzy: Timeline of its Circular Financing Deals ... So Far\\\\\\\\nNvidia is in talks to finance a $250 billion data center for OpenAI, with potential total project costs exceeding $500 billion. This follows a pattern of Nvidia providing financing that recipients use to purchase Nvidia chip')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fa833-9f24-7c73-853c-6b0a122a3f9a', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Employee Detained in Taiwan as Prosecutors Allege AI Chip Smuggling to China: Report', 'Nvidia Employee Detained in Taiwan as Prosecutors Allege AI Chip Smuggling to China: Report\\\\\\\\nTaiwanese prosecutors detained an Nvidia employee for allegedly falsifying documents to smuggle advanced AI chips to China via Super Micro servers. The case is part of a broader global crackdown involving U.S')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fa914-c6dc-73a3-820a-7ad50cb9124f', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"NVDA Down 6% in Two Days: What's Happening to Nvidia's Default Insurance Costs?\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"NVDA Down 6% in Two Days: What's Happening to Nvidia's Default Insurance Costs?\\\\\\\\nNvidia's credit default swaps surged 14 basis points to a record high amid reports the company is in early talks to guarantee up to $250 billion in financing for OpenAI's data center project, raising concerns about balan\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fa924-cc13-75d2-b8ba-2f591f30d0b4', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Corning's AI-Fueled Expectations Crush the Stock\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Corning's AI-Fueled Expectations Crush the Stock\\\\\\\\nCorning (GLW) reported Q2 earnings that beat estimates (EPS $0.78 vs $0.76, revenue $4.74B vs $4.61B) with strong optical growth (+32%) and AI deals with NVDA and AMZN. However, Q3 guidance was in line with expectations, leading to a ~20% share price \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fa995-2c61-7c81-8d59-10fad4dba818', 'benzinga.com', 'Coherent, Lumentum, Ciena Stocks Fall After Corning Earnings Trigger Sector Selloff', 'Coherent, Lumentum, Ciena Stocks Fall After Corning Earnings Trigger Sector Selloff\\\\\\\\nCorning reported Q2 earnings beat (EPS $0.78 vs $0.76 est, revenue $4.74B vs $4.61B est) and in-line Q3 guidance, which triggered a sector selloff in optical/connectivity peers Coherent, Lumentum, and Ciena.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fcc91-2844-75f3-8908-cb6005710f67', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"'Nvidia, Dell Back AI Cloud Startup Volta at $2.4 Billion Value' - Bloomberg\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"'Nvidia, Dell Back AI Cloud Startup Volta at $2.4 Billion Value' - Bloomberg\\\\\\\\nNvidia and Dell have invested in AI cloud startup Volta at a $2.4 billion valuation, according to Bloomberg.\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fce63-1014-7d81-a427-f420fc66466c', 'benzinga.com', 'SpaceX Is Partnering With NVIDIA To Design The Starmind AI1 Satellite Compute Payload; Each Of The Starmind Satellites Will Include NVIDIA Rubin GPUs And Vera CPUs For Datacenter Class Space Compute', 'SpaceX Is Partnering With NVIDIA To Design The Starmind AI1 Satellite Compute Payload; Each Of The Starmind Satellites Will Include NVIDIA Rubin GPUs And Vera CPUs For Datacenter Class Space Compute\\\\\\\\nSpaceX and NVIDIA are partnering to design the Starmind AI1 satellite compute payload, with each sate')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fd0ad-ed87-72e2-84a6-7715fbe442bb', 'benzinga.com', 'Musk Praises Vera Rubin Platform on SpaceX Earnings Call, Nvidia Stock Climbs', \\\\\\\"Musk Praises Vera Rubin Platform on SpaceX Earnings Call, Nvidia Stock Climbs\\\\\\\\nElon Musk announced on SpaceX's earnings call that SpaceX will build exclusively on Nvidia, causing Nvidia shares to rise in extended trading.\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fd1d9-555c-7d70-8a5e-0aae3fc3c088', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"QUICK SPARK: SpaceX Goes All-In on Nvidia. Jim Cramer Thinks That's All Investors Need to Know.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"QUICK SPARK: SpaceX Goes All-In on Nvidia. Jim Cramer Thinks That's All Investors Need to Know.\\\\\\\\nElon Musk announced that SpaceX will use Nvidia GPUs exclusively, and JPMorgan expects SpaceX to receive a significant share of Nvidia's 2027 shipments, deepening their partnership.\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fdc5e-9cb8-7a10-9005-45aa6a1c904a', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"AMD Buys AI Chip Startup Taalas—Here's Why It Matters To NVDA Investors\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"AMD Buys AI Chip Startup Taalas—Here's Why It Matters To NVDA Investors\\\\\\\\nAMD announced the acquisition of AI chip startup Taalas, which specializes in model-specific silicon for faster and cheaper inference. This deal intensifies competition with Nvidia in the AI inference market.\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fdda6-6242-7230-94e0-3924ef57daba', 'benzinga.com', 'The AI Chip Trade Is Getting Bigger — and More Leveraged. Meet REX’s New 3X Bets', \\\\\\\"The AI Chip Trade Is Getting Bigger — and More Leveraged. Meet REX’s New 3X Bets\\\\\\\\nREX has launched new 3X leveraged semiconductor ETNs (SMHU and SMHD) to capitalize on AI-driven demand and volatility in the semiconductor sector. The article highlights record inflows into semiconductor ETFs, SMH's 60%\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fe6fe-191d-7ec3-b0ef-693423bd9cdf', 'benzinga.com', 'US-China AI War: Inside the Battle for Global Tech Dominance', \\\\\\\"US-China AI War: Inside the Battle for Global Tech Dominance\\\\\\\\nThe article covers the escalating US-China AI competition, highlighted by China's Moonshot AI releasing Kimi K3, which caused a 1.4% Nasdaq drop on July 17. The White House accused Moonshot of stealing US technology via distillation of Ant\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019feb0e-2d2e-73c1-90aa-7bd4f056e57f', 'benzinga.com', 'Taiwan Semiconductor’s Blockbuster Run Rolls On: July Revenue Surges 45%', 'Taiwan Semiconductor’s Blockbuster Run Rolls On: July Revenue Surges 45%\\\\\\\\nTaiwan Semiconductor reported July revenue of NT$467.58 billion, up 44.7% YoY and 5.6% MoM, with YTD revenue up 37% to NT$2.872 trillion. The company also raised its 2026 capex outlook to $60-64 billion and expects full-year sa')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fec2c-bac6-7fb0-9a7c-f8d0fe40a6b8', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Built the AI Brain, Now TSMC Wants to Give It Eyes', 'Nvidia Built the AI Brain, Now TSMC Wants to Give It Eyes\\\\\\\\nTSMC and Sony are planning a $6.3 billion joint venture for image sensors, positioning TSMC for growth in AI-driven robotics and autonomous vehicles. Production is expected to begin in 2029.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019feeea-b3ca-7b32-a8ca-2dc921d04f8c', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang Says 'First Time' That Chips Have Become An Investable Asset Class as BlackRock, Blackstone and Others Join $500 Billion AI Push\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang Says 'First Time' That Chips Have Become An Investable Asset Class as BlackRock, Blackstone and Others Join $500 Billion AI Push\\\\\\\\nNvidia CEO Jensen Huang announced a new initiative with six Wall Street firms to raise $500 billion for AI infrastructure, positioning chips as an \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ff091-ef1d-7bc3-a58f-44fb941939ef', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"NVIDIA's Jensen Huang Says AI Isn’t Just Tech Anymore — It’s Infrastructure, and Wall Street Is Financing It\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"NVIDIA's Jensen Huang Says AI Isn’t Just Tech Anymore — It’s Infrastructure, and Wall Street Is Financing It\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA is partnering with Wall Street firms including Goldman Sachs and BlackRock to unlock over $500 billion for AI infrastructure and GPU financing, positioning AI chips as long-lived, reve\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ff3c2-b5c8-71a1-b9af-ca482478f643', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"CoreWeave Stock Surges Nearly 16% After Earnings, Analyst Says Old Nvidia GPUs Can 'Still Generate Revenue Nearly a Decade Later'\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"CoreWeave Stock Surges Nearly 16% After Earnings, Analyst Says Old Nvidia GPUs Can 'Still Generate Revenue Nearly a Decade Later'\\\\\\\\nCoreWeave reported Q2 revenue of $2.58B, beating estimates, with a narrower adjusted loss. The company highlighted a $104B backlog and provided Q3 guidance. Analysts comm\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ff45c-6357-7620-a9b3-52bbdf427f74', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Jim Cramer Asks if Wall Street's 'Long Knives' for Nvidia Should Stay Sheathed as CoreWeave Powers Neocloud Optimism\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Jim Cramer Asks if Wall Street's 'Long Knives' for Nvidia Should Stay Sheathed as CoreWeave Powers Neocloud Optimism\\\\\\\\nCoreWeave reported Q2 earnings that beat expectations, with revenue of $2.58B vs $2.56B expected and a narrower adjusted loss of $1.03 vs $1.22 expected. The company raised full-year \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ff593-4909-79e2-be2e-d62881553377', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"FLY Stock Climbs Over 4% During Wednesday Pre-Market: What's Going On?\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"FLY Stock Climbs Over 4% During Wednesday Pre-Market: What's Going On?\\\\\\\\nFirefly Aerospace reported record Q2 revenue of $117.7 million, up 659% YoY, beating estimates, with adjusted loss of $0.42 per share better than expected. Growth driven by NASA, national security contracts, and Nvidia collaborat\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ff6e8-5134-7f71-92d0-893bccacf954', 'benzinga.com', 'Lumentum Posts Solid Q4, Set To Hit $1.25B Revenue Target 3 Months Early', 'Lumentum Posts Solid Q4, Set To Hit $1.25B Revenue Target 3 Months Early\\\\\\\\nLumentum reported strong Q4 results with revenue surpassing $1 billion, up 190% YoY, and guided Q1 revenue to $1.25 billion, beating expectations and hitting its mid-term target a quarter early. Shares rose 14.89% to $942.75.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ff6f8-3e38-7b11-bf8c-912b4b230c55', 'benzinga.com', 'Stock Market Today: Nasdaq 100 Rises on Strong AI Earnings, Benign Inflation', 'Stock Market Today: Nasdaq 100 Rises on Strong AI Earnings, Benign Inflation\\\\\\\\nAI infrastructure earnings lifted tech stocks and the Nasdaq 100, while a consensus-matched CPI print cooled yields and trimmed September Fed hike odds.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ffb2c-4c8d-7de2-8521-9db4eef52e1d', 'benzinga.com', 'AMD’s 2027 Server Revenue Outlook Is Already 20% Bigger Than the Entire 2025 Market', 'AMD’s 2027 Server Revenue Outlook Is Already 20% Bigger Than the Entire 2025 Market\\\\\\\\nAMD outlined aggressive AI and server growth plans at its Technology Leadership Forum 2026, targeting over 80% server revenue growth in H2 2026 and at least 70% in 2027, backed by Helios customer commitments and clou')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ffb7b-df23-7c93-856b-d0170706ac85', 'benzinga.com', 'IREN Jumps 10% as Microsoft Accepts First AI Data Center Under $9.7 Billion Deal', \\\\\\\"IREN Jumps 10% as Microsoft Accepts First AI Data Center Under $9.7 Billion Deal\\\\\\\\nIREN's stock jumped 10% after Microsoft accepted the first AI data center under a $9.7 billion deal, marking a key milestone in IREN's pivot from Bitcoin mining to AI infrastructure. The acceptance triggers monthly invo\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ffbbe-d6ca-7be2-8c8f-9e7e4d922970', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Why Nvidia May Stand in the Way of Wall Street's Plans to Turn AI Compute Into a Commodity\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Why Nvidia May Stand in the Way of Wall Street's Plans to Turn AI Compute Into a Commodity\\\\\\\\nCME Group plans to launch futures contracts on Nvidia H100 and B200 compute, aiming to create a standardized commodity market for AI compute. However, Nvidia's dominance over supply and pricing may hinder the \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ffbc5-319c-7d50-a059-bf7048fd499b', 'benzinga.com', 'IREN Hands Microsoft Its First AI Cloud Deployment', 'IREN Hands Microsoft Its First AI Cloud Deployment\\\\\\\\nIREN stock rose 6.92% after delivering Horizon 1, the first of four planned 50MW AI cloud deployments for Microsoft under a $9.7B five-year contract, and securing NVIDIA Exemplar Cloud status.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ffc1e-87c4-7453-87dd-1e713140ad2b', 'benzinga.com', 'AMD Prepares Record $5B Bond Sale to Fuel Massive AI Expansion', 'AMD Prepares Record $5B Bond Sale to Fuel Massive AI Expansion\\\\\\\\nAMD is preparing a record $5 billion bond sale across four tranches with maturities from three to ten years, to fund AI infrastructure expansion and refinance debt. The company has not finalized the offering size, which may change based ')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ffc4d-37df-7b81-a1d2-1c72dc8c1936', 'benzinga.com', 'Nebius Says AI Compute Prices Jumped 15%, Signaling Strong Pricing Power', 'Nebius Says AI Compute Prices Jumped 15%, Signaling Strong Pricing Power\\\\\\\\nNebius Group reported that its first AI capacity auction cleared at a price 15% above its previous highest, indicating strong customer willingness to pay for scarce AI computing power. The auction, which involved access to Nvid')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019ffc6d-49db-73b0-9cfa-4689323d0ef9', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Dell Rallies 2% After Lenovo's AI Server Pipeline Hits $54 Billion, Fueling Nvidia Demand Optimism\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Dell Rallies 2% After Lenovo's AI Server Pipeline Hits $54 Billion, Fueling Nvidia Demand Optimism\\\\\\\\nLenovo reported record quarterly results with AI server pipeline surging 157% to $54 billion, reinforcing strong AI infrastructure demand. Dell shares rose 2.5% following the news, with Super Micro's b\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_019fff6a-bea9-70d0-b03b-666f5ebe7635', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia's Next-Gen Feynman AI Platform Is Ramping Up, Forcing TSMC to Race Ahead: Report\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia's Next-Gen Feynman AI Platform Is Ramping Up, Forcing TSMC to Race Ahead: Report\\\\\\\\nNvidia is reportedly accelerating development of its next-gen Feynman AI platform, pushing TSMC to ramp 2nm and advanced packaging capacity. The report highlights TSMC's expansion of SoIC and CoWoS capacity, with\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a00033-bc19-70e2-b821-58d32fcbc3ef', 'benzinga.com', 'NVIDIA Says ‘Free AI’ Is Great For Chips — Jensen Huang’s Open-Source Bet Could Fuel GPU Demand', 'NVIDIA Says ‘Free AI’ Is Great For Chips — Jensen Huang’s Open-Source Bet Could Fuel GPU Demand\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA released Nemotron 3.5 Lightning, an open-source AI model, and introduced NeMo Switchyard software. CEO Jensen Huang advocates for open-source AI, linking it to increased hardware demand. The compan')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0014d-05a7-7222-b775-a09b01383fe1', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia, Nancy Pelosi, Cathie Wood Strike Gold With Databricks' $190 Billion Valuation\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia, Nancy Pelosi, Cathie Wood Strike Gold With Databricks' $190 Billion Valuation\\\\\\\\nDatabricks raised $5 billion in a new funding round led by Coatue, valuing the company at $190 billion, up from $43 billion in September 2023. Early investors including Nvidia, Nancy Pelosi, and Cathie Wood's Ark I\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a00da7-9c2f-7d51-b8fe-2cfe4e291576', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Harvard Reveals $2.2 Billion SpaceX Stake, Its Largest Public Equity Holding: University's Bet on Elon Musk-led Company Outshines Amazon and Nvidia\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Harvard Reveals $2.2 Billion SpaceX Stake, Its Largest Public Equity Holding: University's Bet on Elon Musk-led Company Outshines Amazon and Nvidia\\\\\\\\nHarvard Management Co. disclosed a $2.2 billion stake in SpaceX, its largest public equity holding, via a 13F filing. The stake, held as of June 30, rep\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a00f11-b57d-7a80-b17d-df8968149e55', 'benzinga.com', 'Harvard Did Not Sell Its Bitcoin ETF Holdings in Q2, Discloses No New Ethereum ETF Stake', \\\\\\\"Harvard Did Not Sell Its Bitcoin ETF Holdings in Q2, Discloses No New Ethereum ETF Stake\\\\\\\\nHarvard University's 13F filing shows it held its Bitcoin ETF position steady in Q2, with 3.04 million shares of IBIT worth $101.35 million, while not adding any Ethereum ETF stake after liquidating it in Q1. Th\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a00f37-8c51-7103-8efd-9138a4064dcc', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"HIVE Stock Jumps After AI Cloud Deal - Here's Why\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"HIVE Stock Jumps After AI Cloud Deal - Here's Why\\\\\\\\nHIVE Digital Technologies announced a five-year GPU cloud services agreement worth approximately $350 million with an investment-grade enterprise customer, expected to add roughly $70 million in annualized revenue. Shares rose about 8% in premarket t\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01023-a283-7851-8628-e75e38978be8', 'benzinga.com', 'NVIDIA’s Ohio AI Megadeal: OpenAI, 8 GW of Compute and a $1.5 Billion SB Energy Bet', 'NVIDIA’s Ohio AI Megadeal: OpenAI, 8 GW of Compute and a $1.5 Billion SB Energy Bet\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA and SB Energy partner to build an 8 GW AI campus in Ohio for OpenAI, with NVIDIA investing $1.5B in SB Energy. NVIDIA is also reworking its financing structure to reduce its initial guarantee from $250B to les')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0107f-1189-7443-b708-93eaa30d391f', 'benzinga.com', 'SpaceX Stock Is Everywhere: Google, Nvidia, AMD, Harvard Disclose Stakes', \\\\\\\"SpaceX Stock Is Everywhere: Google, Nvidia, AMD, Harvard Disclose Stakes\\\\\\\\nSpaceX's Nasdaq debut has made it one of the most widely disclosed names in Q2 13F filings, with major tech companies, hedge funds, and institutions revealing large positions. Alphabet disclosed a ~$94B stake, Nvidia ~$21B, AMD\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a010be-cc2c-7893-8cb4-60423f75a42a', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia-OpenAI Deal Isn't 'Circular Financing,' Says Jensen Huang, Sees $600B Compute Opportunity\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia-OpenAI Deal Isn't 'Circular Financing,' Says Jensen Huang, Sees $600B Compute Opportunity\\\\\\\\nNvidia CEO Jensen Huang refutes the 'circular financing' characterization of Nvidia's $1.5 billion investment in SB Energy for OpenAI's Ohio AI campus, framing it as securing infrastructure supply. He hi\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01128-ef8e-78f1-a21a-c6f1083651fc', 'benzinga.com', 'SpaceX Stock Jumps After Multibillion-Dollar Stakes Revealed', \\\\\\\"SpaceX Stock Jumps After Multibillion-Dollar Stakes Revealed\\\\\\\\nSpaceX shares rose 4.17% to $145.84 after 13F filings revealed major institutional holdings, including Google's $94 billion stake, Nvidia's $21 billion stake, and AMD's first-ever $565.5 million position. Additional disclosures included Ha\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0146f-3bb8-7ab0-b435-a044470e2162', 'benzinga.com', 'Trump-Backed World Liberty Partners With Platform Offering Chinese AI Models Flagged by US: Report', 'Trump-Backed World Liberty Partners With Platform Offering Chinese AI Models Flagged by US: Report\\\\\\\\nWorld Liberty Financial, a Trump-backed crypto venture, has partnered with Hong Kong-based WorldClaw, which offers access to Chinese AI models including those from Alibaba and Baidu. The deal raises et')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01504-3aca-7e51-825a-668b8d4c0f00', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Cisco, Nvidia, Amazon and Nokia: The Customer List Behind Fabrinet's AI Boom\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Cisco, Nvidia, Amazon and Nokia: The Customer List Behind Fabrinet's AI Boom\\\\\\\\nFabrinet reported fiscal Q4 earnings, revealing that Cisco, Nvidia, Nokia, and Amazon each account for more than 10% of annual revenue, highlighting the company's diversified role in AI infrastructure. Management expressed \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0158a-423f-7292-afab-e5ffd66fc11d', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia, AMD, Broadcom, Meta Slide as Bond Yields Surge: Why Tech Stocks Are Getting Hit', 'Nvidia, AMD, Broadcom, Meta Slide as Bond Yields Surge: Why Tech Stocks Are Getting Hit\\\\\\\\nTech and AI stocks fell sharply as the 30-year Treasury yield hit its highest level since 2007, with the 10-year around 4.73%. The selloff was concentrated in high-growth tech names, with AMD down 5%, Broadcom an')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0158c-7740-71d1-9fbe-48cc70e8cb27', 'benzinga.com', 'Citadel Advisors and Millennium Boosted Fabrinet Stakes in Q2 as AI Demand Accelerated', 'Citadel Advisors and Millennium Boosted Fabrinet Stakes in Q2 as AI Demand Accelerated\\\\\\\\nCitadel and Millennium significantly increased their Fabrinet (FN) stakes in Q2 2026, as disclosed in 13F filings. Fabrinet reported record results with a diversified customer base (Cisco 20%, Nvidia 16%, Nokia 11')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a015a5-b9ad-7a43-8e70-33e3a0708c37', 'benzinga.com', 'Fabrinet Shares Tumble As Nvidia Datacom Weakness Overshadows Telecom Strength', 'Fabrinet Shares Tumble As Nvidia Datacom Weakness Overshadows Telecom Strength\\\\\\\\nFabrinet reported strong Q4 FY2026 results with revenue and EPS beating estimates, but shares fell 20% due to declining Nvidia datacom sales and concerns about competition. Analysts reaffirmed Buy ratings with high price ')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01811-3d71-7632-97f2-de168b8b61ab', 'benzinga.com', 'Elon Musk Warns Nvidia-Backed $105 Billion Ohio Data Center for OpenAI Will Take ‘Much Longer’ to Come Online Than Expected', \\\\\\\"Elon Musk Warns Nvidia-Backed $105 Billion Ohio Data Center for OpenAI Will Take ‘Much Longer’ to Come Online Than Expected\\\\\\\\nElon Musk publicly doubted the timeline for Nvidia's up to $105 billion Ohio data center project for OpenAI, citing potential delays. The project involves Nvidia's SEC-filed co\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a018b9-104c-7151-b4b9-b0b3e469e202', 'benzinga.com', 'Cerebras Stock Takes a Hit as New AI Server Targets Nvidia With Giant Chips and Faster Chatbot Queries', 'Cerebras Stock Takes a Hit as New AI Server Targets Nvidia With Giant Chips and Faster Chatbot Queries\\\\\\\\nCerebras unveiled its CS-4 AI server to challenge Nvidia, but its stock fell 12.69% after revenue missed estimates. Core revenue grew 103% YoY, and guidance for Q3 was provided.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01942-08c8-7cb2-a8e0-e51c89430141', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia’s H200 Chips Are Flowing Into China Again: ByteDance, Tencent Get Around 10,000 Each, Report Says', \\\\\\\"Nvidia’s H200 Chips Are Flowing Into China Again: ByteDance, Tencent Get Around 10,000 Each, Report Says\\\\\\\\nChina has approved limited shipments of Nvidia's H200 AI chips to ByteDance and Tencent, with each receiving around 10,000 processors, signaling a cautious easing of restrictions. The approvals f\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01985-2c6d-7472-baed-885c49e6cfea', 'benzinga.com', 'SKHY Stock Rips 6% in Premarket on $29 Billion Buyback Plan', 'SKHY Stock Rips 6% in Premarket on $29 Billion Buyback Plan\\\\\\\\nSK Hynix announced a $29 billion (40 trillion won) treasury share buyback and cancellation plan, along with a commitment to return over 50% of cumulative free cash flow from 2025-2027 to shareholders. The stock rose 5.56% in premarket tradi')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01991-56de-70a2-93d2-88c96e4a3be6', 'benzinga.com', 'NVIDIA Supplier SK Hynix Rolls Out $29 Billion Buyback After AI Spending Fears Hammer Stock', 'NVIDIA Supplier SK Hynix Rolls Out $29 Billion Buyback After AI Spending Fears Hammer Stock\\\\\\\\nSK hynix stock rebounded 5% in premarket trading after announcing a $29 billion (40 trillion won) stock buyback plan and raising its shareholder return target to over 50% of free cash flow. The move follows a')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a019c8-0e5b-7df2-9fc6-8c4bdda6ea6a', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Jim Cramer Slams Data Center Reliance on Leveraged Retail-Driven SK Hynix, Samsung Stocks: 'Decided By Them, Not Us'\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Jim Cramer Slams Data Center Reliance on Leveraged Retail-Driven SK Hynix, Samsung Stocks: 'Decided By Them, Not Us'\\\\\\\\nSK Hynix announced a $29 billion (40 trillion won) share buyback and cancellation plan to support its stock amid AI demand concerns. Jim Cramer criticized the data center supply chain\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01a36-a4f7-7aa1-95d2-06b570e0b49b', 'benzinga.com', 'NVDA Rival Cerebras Unveils New AI System It Says Is Up to 30X Faster Than Nvidia GPUs', 'NVDA Rival Cerebras Unveils New AI System It Says Is Up to 30X Faster Than Nvidia GPUs\\\\\\\\nCerebras unveiled its new CS-4 AI inference system, claiming up to 30x faster inference than Nvidia GPUs, with speeds exceeding 4,400 tokens per second per user on GPT-OSS-120B. The first systems are expected onli')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01a75-17f5-7653-91cd-6bf3ab93c8c5', 'benzinga.com', 'Broadcom Rival Marvell Surges After Google Strikes AI Chip Deal, Gets Option to Buy $12.2B Stake', 'Broadcom Rival Marvell Surges After Google Strikes AI Chip Deal, Gets Option to Buy $12.2B Stake\\\\\\\\nMarvell announced a sweeping custom AI chip agreement with Google, including a warrant for Google to buy nearly 59 million Marvell shares at $206.58 each, potentially worth $12.2 billion. The deal could ')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01b00-8458-7af3-bf3b-4a72fc171264', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Investors Should Position For Humanoid Robot Boom—Here's A Picks-And-Shovels Play; First mRNA Cancer Vaccine Succeeds\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Investors Should Position For Humanoid Robot Boom—Here's A Picks-And-Shovels Play; First mRNA Cancer Vaccine Succeeds\\\\\\\\nThe article covers multiple market-moving events: Moderna and Merck's Phase 3 mRNA cancer vaccine success, US Treasury doubling buyback support for long bonds, SK Hynix's $28B buybac\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01bde-a23b-7e12-a2ae-20724c9385e9', 'benzinga.com', 'Samsung Tumbled Nearly 8% in Seoul Even as AI Demand Drives Chip Prices Up To 15%', \\\\\\\"Samsung Tumbled Nearly 8% in Seoul Even as AI Demand Drives Chip Prices Up To 15%\\\\\\\\nSamsung raised prices for advanced chipmaking services by up to 15% for new orders, driven by AI demand and full production lines. The move highlights pricing power in the semiconductor foundry market, even as Samsung'\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01f76-7671-74b1-b8ec-790d3f11f6d6', 'benzinga.com', 'CoreWeave Lands Multibillion-Dollar Hudson River Deal as Wall Street Races for Nvidia Chips', \\\\\\\"CoreWeave Lands Multibillion-Dollar Hudson River Deal as Wall Street Races for Nvidia Chips\\\\\\\\nCoreWeave has secured a multibillion-dollar, multiyear AI cloud deal with Hudson River Trading, providing access to Nvidia's Vera Rubin and B200 systems. This follows a $6 billion commitment from Jane Street \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a01f84-eb78-7003-bf96-a3619f1d91b8', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"A 10-Year Treasury Bond Now Pays More Than 118 Of America's Biggest Companies\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"A 10-Year Treasury Bond Now Pays More Than 118 Of America's Biggest Companies\\\\\\\\nThe 10-year Treasury yield now exceeds the dividend yield of 118 S&P 500 mega-cap stocks, with only 3.85% of the index yielding more than the bond, the lowest since May 2007. This reflects rising long-term yields and low d\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a02009-f6f4-7421-a2b7-7cb042b79b24', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is SK Hynix Stock Surging on Thursday?', 'Why Is SK Hynix Stock Surging on Thursday?\\\\\\\\nSK Hynix announced a 40 trillion won ($29 billion) share buyback and cancellation plan, plus expanded free cash flow return commitments, driving its stock up 4.25%.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a023b9-2355-7e72-b586-582f54acafaf', 'benzinga.com', 'Broadcom Steps up NVIDIA Challenge With Potential $100 Billion AI Financing Deal', 'Broadcom Steps up NVIDIA Challenge With Potential $100 Billion AI Financing Deal\\\\\\\\nBroadcom is exploring a massive up to $100 billion AI financing package with Apollo and Blackstone to fund custom AI chips for customers like Anthropic. The deal is in discussion stages, with talks ongoing and potential')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a023de-e7e3-7de0-9166-b2db9f613441', 'benzinga.com', 'Waymo Unveils First Custom Robotaxi Chip With More Than 1,000 TOPS of AI Processing Power', \\\\\\\"Waymo Unveils First Custom Robotaxi Chip With More Than 1,000 TOPS of AI Processing Power\\\\\\\\nWaymo, Alphabet's autonomous driving unit, unveiled its first custom-designed robotaxi chip, a 5-nanometer ASIC with over 1,000 TOPS of AI processing power for real-time sensor data processing in its new Ojai v\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a023eb-f2a1-7441-af46-75d8745b0856', 'benzinga.com', 'NVIDIA Looks to Strengthen AI Empire With Potential Rebellions Deal', \\\\\\\"NVIDIA Looks to Strengthen AI Empire With Potential Rebellions Deal\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA is in preliminary talks with South Korean AI chip startup Rebellions about a potential technical partnership, investment, or acquisition. The discussions are exploratory and may not result in a transaction. NVIDIA's stock ros\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a024c4-e685-77d0-bf65-9dd563950310', 'benzinga.com', 'Modine Stock Jumps After Report Names Google, Amazon as Data Center Cooling Customers', \\\\\\\"Modine Stock Jumps After Report Names Google, Amazon as Data Center Cooling Customers\\\\\\\\nModine shares rose after Hunterbrook Media reported that Google is the unnamed customer behind Modine's $4 billion cooling agreement, with additional pipeline from Amazon and others. The report also suggests Modine\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a031b6-72ce-7be2-8be9-79c2b5462e44', 'benzinga.com', 'Remember Hugging Face? The AI Hub Hit by an OpenAI Security Breach Is Reportedly Exploring a $13 Billion Sale', 'Remember Hugging Face? The AI Hub Hit by an OpenAI Security Breach Is Reportedly Exploring a $13 Billion Sale\\\\\\\\nHugging Face, an open-source AI platform, is reportedly exploring a potential sale that could value the company at $13 billion or more, nearly tripling its 2023 valuation of $4.5 billion. Th')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03201-1a85-7951-a679-fe5b82ffaa91', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Is Coming for OpenAI and DeepSeek With $6 Billion Poolside Deal to Build a Powerful Open-Weight AI Model: Report', \\\\\\\"Nvidia Is Coming for OpenAI and DeepSeek With $6 Billion Poolside Deal to Build a Powerful Open-Weight AI Model: Report\\\\\\\\nNvidia is acquiring Poolside's AI technology for $6 billion and investing $1 billion at a $12 billion pre-money valuation, with over 100 employees joining Nvidia to work on open-we\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a033ea-1b5c-7473-872f-43321e036056', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Dan Ives Says Nvidia's 15% AI Server Price Hike Is Bullish for Tech. Could Micron Be the Real Winner?\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Dan Ives Says Nvidia's 15% AI Server Price Hike Is Bullish for Tech. Could Micron Be the Real Winner?\\\\\\\\nNvidia has reportedly informed major customers of a more than 15% price increase for AI servers shipping in early 2027, driven by surging memory costs. Analyst Dan Ives views this as bullish for AI \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a034ac-c1ff-7d02-8611-b20b7f13f4f3', 'benzinga.com', 'SpaceXAI Taps NVIDIA To Build Faster AI Agents', \\\\\\\"SpaceXAI Taps NVIDIA To Build Faster AI Agents\\\\\\\\nSpaceXAI, the AI division of SpaceX, announced a partnership with NVIDIA to deploy NVIDIA's Vera CPUs for agentic AI applications and expand Grok's infrastructure. The collaboration also includes plans to use NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform for orbital com\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a034c7-84d7-70f2-a481-cdffe4a12335', 'benzinga.com', 'Memory Stocks Slide as Trump Threatens 50% Tariffs on Canadian Autos, Steel in 2027: Stock Market Today', 'Memory Stocks Slide as Trump Threatens 50% Tariffs on Canadian Autos, Steel in 2027: Stock Market Today\\\\\\\\nUS equities mixed as Trump escalates trade war with Canada via 50% auto tariffs, memory stocks slide on Samsung disappointment, and Bitcoin rallies past $79k.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03501-58ad-7083-8bd7-84dd5c70a3a1', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"EXCLUSIVE: How AI's $220 Billion Bond Boom Competes With the Treasury\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"EXCLUSIVE: How AI's $220 Billion Bond Boom Competes With the Treasury\\\\\\\\nAI companies have issued $220B in debt this year, intensifying competition with Treasury supply and contributing to higher long-term yields. Treasury Secretary Bessent expanded buybacks, but analysts see limited impact. Commentary\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03541-98e7-73b3-8645-f8d14d349a52', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Magnificent 7 Built The AI Boom, 'Munificent Seven' Wants to Power It\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Magnificent 7 Built The AI Boom, 'Munificent Seven' Wants to Power It\\\\\\\\nHarbor Capital Advisors launched the Munificent Seven ETF (BBLS), an actively managed fund targeting seven major energy companies positioned to benefit from surging electricity demand driven by AI infrastructure growth. The fund b\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a036fc-ca3f-78e3-b3f3-1298008ebac0', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Trump Snapped Up SpaceX Shares 11 Days After $1.77 Trillion IPO: Here's What Else He Purchased\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Trump Snapped Up SpaceX Shares 11 Days After $1.77 Trillion IPO: Here's What Else He Purchased\\\\\\\\nPresident Trump disclosed buying up to $50,000 in SpaceX shares shortly after its record IPO, along with other stock trades, raising conflict-of-interest questions as his administration advances space poli\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03728-79db-7f72-bf5b-77c3603e7156', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Elizabeth Warren Says if Jensen Huang Has Time for $1 Million Mar-a-Lago Dinner, He Can 'Find Time to Testify' and Explain Nvidia Tech in Russian Drones\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Elizabeth Warren Says if Jensen Huang Has Time for $1 Million Mar-a-Lago Dinner, He Can 'Find Time to Testify' and Explain Nvidia Tech in Russian Drones\\\\\\\\nSenator Elizabeth Warren is pressuring Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang to testify before Congress after reports that Nvidia's Jetson Orin computers were fo\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03834-2bf3-7020-bc02-47ee8cb9acc9', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Manager Named ‘Key Figure’ in Alleged B300 GPU Smuggling to China, 8 Others Indicted in Taiwan Probe', 'Nvidia Manager Named ‘Key Figure’ in Alleged B300 GPU Smuggling to China, 8 Others Indicted in Taiwan Probe\\\\\\\\nTaiwanese prosecutors indicted nine individuals, including employees of Nvidia and Super Micro, for allegedly exporting prohibited B300 AI GPUs to China. 74 servers were successfully shipped v')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03a59-3dba-7cf2-bd65-23fdfaca9e2d', 'benzinga.com', 'Leveraged Single-Stock ETF Closures Went From 3 To 63 In A Year As Money Piles Into Nvidia Bets', 'Leveraged Single-Stock ETF Closures Went From 3 To 63 In A Year As Money Piles Into Nvidia Bets\\\\\\\\nThe leveraged ETF market is undergoing a shakeout in 2026, with record launches but widespread closures and asset concentration in top products like NVDL, SOXL, and SOXS. The article highlights the trend ')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03c58-cf2c-75d0-93ca-9e5268d2acd9', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Jim Cramer Sees 'No Real Competitors' to Nvidia, Even as Sam Altman Says OpenAI 'Made a Chip and It Is Fast'\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Jim Cramer Sees 'No Real Competitors' to Nvidia, Even as Sam Altman Says OpenAI 'Made a Chip and It Is Fast'\\\\\\\\nOpenAI announced its first custom inference chip, Jalapeño, developed with Broadcom, claiming significant efficiency and latency improvements over Nvidia's GB200 and GB300 chips. The chip is \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03d04-0776-7890-a753-f3d09710ac24', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia, Zoom Communications and 3 Stocks to Watch Heading Into Wednesday', 'Nvidia, Zoom Communications and 3 Stocks to Watch Heading Into Wednesday\\\\\\\\nStock futures mixed; Intuit and Zoom reported earnings with guidance misses, while Nvidia, Williams-Sonoma, and Smucker are set to report.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03d06-0e58-7a91-8aba-33273ad7929c', 'benzinga.com', 'Dow Gains for Third Session as Treasury Yields Fall: Investor Sentiment Improves, Fear Index Remains in ‘Greed’ Zone', 'Dow Gains for Third Session as Treasury Yields Fall: Investor Sentiment Improves, Fear Index Remains in ‘Greed’ Zone\\\\\\\\nU.S. stocks rose for a third session as Treasury yields fell, with the Dow gaining 160 points. The Fear & Greed Index improved to 58.6 (Greed zone). Economic data showed Case-Shiller ')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03efa-9153-7cb0-80f4-b4451228c5a4', 'benzinga.com', 'Microsoft, Amazon, Google Court Kimi K3 Maker Despite Bessent Blacklist Threat', \\\\\\\"Microsoft, Amazon, Google Court Kimi K3 Maker Despite Bessent Blacklist Threat\\\\\\\\nMicrosoft, Amazon, and Google are in early talks with China's Moonshot AI for revenue-sharing deals on its Kimi K3 model, despite potential U.S. sanctions. The talks are preliminary and may not result in agreements.\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a03fd1-ae9d-7e13-9776-7330b4bfa9a1', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Q2 Highlights: Double Beat, Huang Says ‘AI Infrastructure Buildout is at Full Steam’', 'Nvidia Q2 Highlights: Double Beat, Huang Says ‘AI Infrastructure Buildout is at Full Steam’\\\\\\\\nNvidia reported Q2 FY2025 revenue of $96.22B (beat $92.18B estimate), EPS of $2.22 (beat $2.10), and issued Q3 guidance of $105.84B-$110.16B (above $104.20B estimate). Stock fell 1.8% after hours despite the ')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04036-7a46-7443-81c2-92f2fb963c83', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia's Real Story Isn't the Beat — It's What Kress Said About 2028\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia's Real Story Isn't the Beat — It's What Kress Said About 2028\\\\\\\\nNvidia reported strong Q2 FY2025 results with revenue of $96.22B (up 106% YoY) and EPS of $2.22, beating estimates. Q3 guidance of $108B also exceeded expectations. CFO Colette Kress projected 70% revenue growth for fiscal 2028, we\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a040ed-a9c7-79d3-9fd9-fd846051ce4e', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia, Salesforce, CrowdStrike, Okta and Abercrombie & Fitch: Why These 5 Stocks Are on Investors' Radars Today\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia, Salesforce, CrowdStrike, Okta and Abercrombie & Fitch: Why These 5 Stocks Are on Investors' Radars Today\\\\\\\\nMajor U.S. indices ended lower, but several stocks moved sharply after earnings. NVIDIA, Salesforce, CrowdStrike, Okta, and Abercrombie & Fitch all reported quarterly results and guidance\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a040fd-f4a6-7712-bd68-81e25fa37749', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia Pops 4.7% After Hours as Earnings Blowout Lifts Dow Futures 180 Points: Jensen Huang Says, 'Compute is Revenue'\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia Pops 4.7% After Hours as Earnings Blowout Lifts Dow Futures 180 Points: Jensen Huang Says, 'Compute is Revenue'\\\\\\\\nNvidia reported blowout Q2 earnings with revenue of $96.22B (up 106% YoY) beating estimates, and issued strong Q3 guidance. This drove a 4.7% after-hours stock surge and lifted Dow \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04176-8c05-7572-b378-1cc02f718e32', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia Revenue Set to Increase 18X in 4 Years; Analyst Says 'Never in History' Has a Company Grown This Fast\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia Revenue Set to Increase 18X in 4 Years; Analyst Says 'Never in History' Has a Company Grown This Fast\\\\\\\\nNvidia reported Q2 revenue of $96.22 billion (beat $92.11B estimate) and guided Q3 revenue to $108 billion, well above the $103.52B estimate. CEO Jensen Huang said 'compute is revenue' and de\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a041a1-ba9c-7ba3-abd3-72bf56eaaac9', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Jim Cramer Says Nvidia Is 'Not Going to Stop Here' as Ross Gerber Sees NVDA Stock Hitting $450 as Analysts Dissect Q2 Earnings\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Jim Cramer Says Nvidia Is 'Not Going to Stop Here' as Ross Gerber Sees NVDA Stock Hitting $450 as Analysts Dissect Q2 Earnings\\\\\\\\nNvidia reported strong fiscal Q2 results with revenue of $96.2 billion (up 106% YoY) and net income up 126%, beating expectations. The company guided Q3 revenue to $105.84-$\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a041ae-3a31-78c3-8301-58cd7c880d4c', 'benzinga.com', 'Dow Falls Over 100 Points Following PCE Inflation Data: Investor Sentiment Weakens, Fear & Greed Index Moves to ‘Neutral’ Zone', 'Dow Falls Over 100 Points Following PCE Inflation Data: Investor Sentiment Weakens, Fear & Greed Index Moves to ‘Neutral’ Zone\\\\\\\\nU.S. stocks fell on Wednesday following the release of PCE inflation data, which showed a slight miss versus expectations. The Dow dropped over 100 points, while the S&P 500')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a041ea-18f9-79c2-8972-66fc116d16eb', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Agrees to Acquire Hugging Face For $12.9 Billion In One of Its Largest Acquisitions So Far As It Expands Control Of Open-Source AI Models: Report', 'Nvidia Agrees to Acquire Hugging Face For $12.9 Billion In One of Its Largest Acquisitions So Far As It Expands Control Of Open-Source AI Models: Report\\\\\\\\nNvidia has reportedly agreed to acquire Hugging Face, an open-source AI model repository, for $12.9 billion, according to The Information. This wou')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04202-1778-7571-a282-0434fb0e167a', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang Not Taking OpenAI's 'Jalapeño' Chip Personally: 'Lots of Projects Get Started. Lots of Projects Get Canceled'\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang Not Taking OpenAI's 'Jalapeño' Chip Personally: 'Lots of Projects Get Started. Lots of Projects Get Canceled'\\\\\\\\nNvidia CEO Jensen Huang downplayed OpenAI's new Jalapeño AI inference chip, expressing confidence in Nvidia's technology and market position. The article also reports\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0420a-5ff5-73d3-8c15-c45c1a20269a', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia's Earnings Smash Estimates, but Crypto Bettors Aren't Buying a $250 Close by Month-End\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia's Earnings Smash Estimates, but Crypto Bettors Aren't Buying a $250 Close by Month-End\\\\\\\\nNvidia reported blowout Q2 earnings with revenue of $96.2B (up 106% YoY) and EPS of $2.22, beating estimates. Despite this, Polymarket bettors give only 8% chance of NVDA closing above $250 by month-end, do\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04269-050c-75d0-9fcc-fe5964c7e63c', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia, Micron, Intel Climb in Thursday Pre-Market: What's Going On?\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia, Micron, Intel Climb in Thursday Pre-Market: What's Going On?\\\\\\\\nNvidia reported strong Q2 results with revenue of $96.22 billion (up 106% YoY) and issued robust guidance, projecting 70% revenue growth for fiscal 2028 and Q3 guidance of $108 billion. CEO Jensen Huang cited strong AI demand and s\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04272-5523-78f2-b1a5-fa7892eae486', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Elon Musk's SPCX Now Accounts for 5% of Nvidia Revenue, Gene Munster Says: 'The Script Has Flipped'\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Elon Musk's SPCX Now Accounts for 5% of Nvidia Revenue, Gene Munster Says: 'The Script Has Flipped'\\\\\\\\nGene Munster estimates SpaceX now accounts for 5% of Nvidia's revenue, up from 3%, implying ~$4.8B in sales. Nvidia's Q2 revenue beat estimates at $96.22B, with data-center sales doubling. The company\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a042a2-6b99-7830-98a6-eb851becdfec', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang Jokes His Dinner Plans Can Double a Stock—His Track Record Says He’s Not Wrong', \\\\\\\"Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang Jokes His Dinner Plans Can Double a Stock—His Track Record Says He’s Not Wrong\\\\\\\\nNvidia reported strong Q2 earnings and Q3 guidance, beating estimates, while CEO Jensen Huang's comments on supply chain and quantum computing affected various tech stocks.\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a042a8-eb86-73a0-aae2-811f66931d0c', 'benzinga.com', 'NVIDIA Is Still the AI Bellwether—And Rivals Aren’t Close', 'NVIDIA Is Still the AI Bellwether—And Rivals Aren’t Close\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA reported Q2 revenue of $96.22B (beat $92.18B) and EPS of $2.22 (beat $2.10), with Q3 guidance of $105.84B-$110.16B. Stock rose 7.41% premarket. Analysts debate whether hypergrowth is slowing.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a042d4-023b-77c0-96be-148af63414d4', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Jensen Huang Has a Message for NVDA Bears Betting on Open Models: 'Both Closed and Open Models Are Going to Succeed'\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Jensen Huang Has a Message for NVDA Bears Betting on Open Models: 'Both Closed and Open Models Are Going to Succeed'\\\\\\\\nNvidia reported Q2 revenue of $96.22B, up 106% YoY, beating estimates, and issued Q3 guidance above $105B. CEO Jensen Huang commented on open vs closed AI models, stating both drive d\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0430d-c7d1-7e43-aa8f-0d77cb515e05', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"NVDA Downplays 'Circular Financing' Concerns Days After Michael Burry Called it a Wall Street Stunt: 'We See it Differently'\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"NVDA Downplays 'Circular Financing' Concerns Days After Michael Burry Called it a Wall Street Stunt: 'We See it Differently'\\\\\\\\nNvidia's management, including CEO Jensen Huang and CFO Colette Kress, defended the company's $500B AI infrastructure financing strategy against 'circular financing' criticism\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04321-f700-7952-9719-2714dfd8bc8e', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Surges 6% Premarket—These ETFs Are Amplifying the AI Trade', 'Nvidia Surges 6% Premarket—These ETFs Are Amplifying the AI Trade\\\\\\\\nNvidia reported Q2 revenue of $96.2B (beat ~$92.3B estimate) and adjusted EPS of $2.22, beating forecasts. The company guided Q3 revenue to $105.8B-$110.1B. NVDA surged ~6-7% premarket, driving leveraged ETFs (NVDL, NVDU, NVDX, NVDB) ')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0433d-2134-7fa0-947c-96b174946f02', 'benzinga.com', 'Jim Cramer Has a Message for Nvidia Investors After the Earnings Blowout: ‘Don’t Let the Bears Deceive You’ Into Selling NVDA', 'Jim Cramer Has a Message for Nvidia Investors After the Earnings Blowout: ‘Don’t Let the Bears Deceive You’ Into Selling NVDA\\\\\\\\nNvidia reported blowout Q2 earnings with revenue of $96.22 billion (106% YoY), beating estimates, and data center revenue of $89.0 billion. CEO Jensen Huang declared AI deman')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0433e-ec5f-7fa1-babe-b79249d6211a', 'benzinga.com', 'NVIDIA’s Biggest AI Bottleneck Isn’t Demand—It’s Memory', \\\\\\\"NVIDIA’s Biggest AI Bottleneck Isn’t Demand—It’s Memory\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA's earnings and growth outlook signal strong AI-driven memory demand and tight supply, boosting Micron and SK Hynix shares. Former NVIDIA executive Jeff Herbst expects elevated memory prices to persist due to capacity constraints and long\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04348-9566-76d2-8fd6-524a164bac08', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is Nebius Group Stock Soaring Thursday?', 'Why Is Nebius Group Stock Soaring Thursday?\\\\\\\\nNebius (NBIS) stock surged 6.25% premarket after NVIDIA named it as the first customer for its upcoming Groq 3 LPX hardware, with volume shipments expected later this quarter. NVIDIA also reported strong Q2 earnings, beating estimates.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0436a-a84c-7102-ad4a-dd3d4603fad6', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia’s AI Boom Hits Its First Margin Wall: Memory Prices', \\\\\\\"Nvidia’s AI Boom Hits Its First Margin Wall: Memory Prices\\\\\\\\nNvidia's gross margins are expected to decline from 75% in Q2 to 71%-72% in Q4 due to soaring memory prices, marking the first major margin drop of the AI cycle. The company expects margins to recover in fiscal 2028 as it raises prices.\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04387-4280-7540-be99-8249f4bf5650', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is Arm Stock Surging on Thursday?', \\\\\\\"Why Is Arm Stock Surging on Thursday?\\\\\\\\nArm Holdings stock surged on Thursday following Nvidia's blowout Q2 earnings and strong AI infrastructure guidance, which sparked a broad semiconductor rally. Nvidia reported revenue of $96.22B (up 106% YoY) and EPS of $2.22, both beating estimates, with data ce\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04387-b329-7ab3-a674-5c36786ec78e', 'benzinga.com', 'Nasdaq Surges 200 Points; Nvidia Posts Upbeat Q2 Results', 'Nasdaq Surges 200 Points; Nvidia Posts Upbeat Q2 Results\\\\\\\\nUS stocks traded mixed with Nasdaq up 200 points. Nvidia reported strong Q2 earnings and guidance. Economic data showed jobless claims below estimates. Several small-cap movers highlighted.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0438c-1ece-7dd2-ace8-029431bfb8ae', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Bill Gates Wants to Hit the Brakes. Nvidia Is Financing AI's Next Sprint.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Bill Gates Wants to Hit the Brakes. Nvidia Is Financing AI's Next Sprint.\\\\\\\\nNvidia's earnings call revealed extended payment terms for investment-grade customers and a broader AI financing strategy, while Bill Gates expressed support for slowing AI development. The article highlights Nvidia's shift fr\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a043ba-c7b7-7d53-93a1-f3514e628fa8', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is Intel Stock Surging on Thursday?', \\\\\\\"Why Is Intel Stock Surging on Thursday?\\\\\\\\nIntel stock surged on Thursday, driven by a semiconductor sector rally following Nvidia's strong Q2 earnings and reports of potential broad U.S. chip tariffs. Nvidia beat revenue and EPS estimates, while the Trump administration is considering new tariffs on s\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a043c3-cb28-7fe1-adc6-22436804bd31', 'benzinga.com', 'QUICK SPARK: Nvidia Stock Adds $370 Billion Market Value, A Whole Coca-Cola', 'QUICK SPARK: Nvidia Stock Adds $370 Billion Market Value, A Whole Coca-Cola\\\\\\\\nNvidia reported stronger-than-expected Q2 results, with revenue of $96.2 billion (up 106% YoY) and data center revenue up 117% to $89 billion. The company guided to ~70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028, well above the ~44% con')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0442a-82a0-7a93-a210-0c1ac2e1811b', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia's Unusual Move Answers AI Trade’s Key Question; $40 Trillion US Debt Bomb Ticks; Key Fed Speech Awaited\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia's Unusual Move Answers AI Trade’s Key Question; $40 Trillion US Debt Bomb Ticks; Key Fed Speech Awaited\\\\\\\\nNvidia reported strong Q2 earnings and revenue, and provided forward guidance including Q3 revenue and FY28 growth, which is unusual for the company. The article also discusses the US debt,\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0446d-03f0-7c51-8156-1f3f635d4033', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia Stock 'Valuation Remains Conservative': Early 2028 Guidance Has Analysts Increasing Price Targets\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia Stock 'Valuation Remains Conservative': Early 2028 Guidance Has Analysts Increasing Price Targets\\\\\\\\nNvidia reported Q2 results that beat estimates and provided early fiscal 2028 revenue guidance of ~70% growth, which is well above consensus. Analysts raised price targets, citing strong demand a\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0452e-0c08-7ff2-815d-127a54073785', 'benzinga.com', 'Jensen Huang Passes Mark Zuckerberg, Larry Ellison: Here’s How Much Nvidia CEO is Worth', \\\\\\\"Jensen Huang Passes Mark Zuckerberg, Larry Ellison: Here’s How Much Nvidia CEO is Worth\\\\\\\\nNvidia stock rose 8.7% on Thursday following Q2 results and guidance, boosting CEO Jensen Huang's net worth by $14.9 billion to $196.1 billion, moving him past Zuckerberg and Ellison on the Forbes list. The compa\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04623-d589-7000-a653-8ce5fe78c658', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Trump Praises Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang On 'Incredible Numbers,' Calls Micron One Of The World's 'Hottest' Companies\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Trump Praises Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang On 'Incredible Numbers,' Calls Micron One Of The World's 'Hottest' Companies\\\\\\\\nPresident Trump praised Nvidia's strong earnings and guidance, and Micron's new $10 billion research investment, highlighting them as proof of his policies' success. Nvidia reported Q2 \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0471e-6dab-7382-a4be-6a8ed3d48ce7', 'benzinga.com', 'Nasdaq Jumps Over 400 Points As Nvidia Shares Surge: Investor Sentiment Improves, Fear & Greed Index Moves To ‘Greed’ Zone', 'Nasdaq Jumps Over 400 Points As Nvidia Shares Surge: Investor Sentiment Improves, Fear & Greed Index Moves To ‘Greed’ Zone\\\\\\\\nU.S. stocks rallied on Thursday, with the Nasdaq jumping over 400 points, driven by strong earnings from Nvidia, Dollar General, and Veeva Systems. The CNN Fear & Greed Index mo')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0476b-8071-7820-8ecd-eb715ff00cb1', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Steps Back From Revenue-Sharing Deals With AI Cloud Providers Amid Antitrust Concerns: Report', 'Nvidia Steps Back From Revenue-Sharing Deals With AI Cloud Providers Amid Antitrust Concerns: Report\\\\\\\\nNvidia has reportedly paused its revenue-sharing financing program for AI cloud providers, less than two months after launch, due to internal antitrust concerns. The program offered credit support in')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a047f7-4d61-7483-828a-d29130de62c7', 'benzinga.com', 'Marvell Technology Stock Slides: Data Center Strength Overshadowed by Valuation Concerns', \\\\\\\"Marvell Technology Stock Slides: Data Center Strength Overshadowed by Valuation Concerns\\\\\\\\nMarvell Technology reported strong Q2 earnings and raised guidance, but shares fell ~8% premarket as investors digested clarification that Google warrant revenue is already included in next year's projections, a\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a048cf-14af-7563-937e-da86edc751ec', 'benzinga.com', 'Microsoft Runs On It, Nvidia Validates It: IREN CEO Says the Real Edge Is Owning the Entire AI Stack', \\\\\\\"Microsoft Runs On It, Nvidia Validates It: IREN CEO Says the Real Edge Is Owning the Entire AI Stack\\\\\\\\nIREN's fiscal 2026 earnings call highlighted milestones: Microsoft began running AI workloads on IREN's infrastructure, Horizon 1 delivered, and Nvidia certified Mirantis as an inaugural Nvidia Certi\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a049f6-2a91-7c82-9b84-7e12bd8a139b', 'benzinga.com', 'Warsh Sparks Rate-Hike Bets, Nvidia Reaffirms AI Growth Story: This Week on Wall Street', \\\\\\\"Warsh Sparks Rate-Hike Bets, Nvidia Reaffirms AI Growth Story: This Week on Wall Street\\\\\\\\nThe article covers multiple market-moving events: Fed Chair Warsh's hawkish Jackson Hole speech raising rate-hike bets, Nvidia's blowout earnings with strong guidance, CrowdStrike's record quarterly results and s\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a04ca7-93dc-76d0-81a4-942b5b2b07ff', 'benzinga.com', 'Hugging Face’s $399 Robot Ducks Racks Up $2.6 Million in Sales as Nvidia Deal Buzz Grows', \\\\\\\"Hugging Face’s $399 Robot Ducks Racks Up $2.6 Million in Sales as Nvidia Deal Buzz Grows\\\\\\\\nHugging Face's Microduck robot, developed by Pollen Robotics, generated over $2.6 million in orders within 24 hours of launch, signaling strong consumer demand for AI-powered home robots. The launch highlights t\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a052a6-717b-78a2-8d80-366629c5199c', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Weekend Tech Roundup: CXMT's 874% Revenue Surge, Apple's New Macs, Nvidia's Q2 Beat and More\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Weekend Tech Roundup: CXMT's 874% Revenue Surge, Apple's New Macs, Nvidia's Q2 Beat and More\\\\\\\\nWeekend tech roundup covering CXMT's massive revenue surge and Pentagon lawsuit, Apple's new Mac launches, and Q2 earnings beats from Nvidia, CrowdStrike, and Salesforce.\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0582d-e791-7982-bcf9-7f7da0ed26c0', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Elon Musk Is Trying to Break GE Vernova's AI Power Bottleneck\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Elon Musk Is Trying to Break GE Vernova's AI Power Bottleneck\\\\\\\\nSpaceX is building a foundry in Texas to cast gas-turbine blades and vanes in-house, targeting a supply-chain bottleneck that GE Vernova says is limiting AI power projects. Musk confirmed the move, which could accelerate turbine availabil\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a058bf-e042-7760-a268-60a63cd2a58a', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia's $3.5 Billion MediaTek Deal Revives the 'Circular Financing' Debate\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia's $3.5 Billion MediaTek Deal Revives the 'Circular Financing' Debate\\\\\\\\nNvidia announced a $3.5 billion investment in convertible bonds issued by MediaTek, deepening their partnership in AI infrastructure, AI PCs, and automotive computing. The deal has revived the 'circular financing' debate, wi\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a058e1-e2bc-7f13-aa15-65a022b69227', 'benzinga.com', 'Amazon Web Services Accelerates Middle East AI Push with Saudi Cloud Region Launch', 'Amazon Web Services Accelerates Middle East AI Push with Saudi Cloud Region Launch\\\\\\\\nAWS is accelerating its cloud and AI expansion in Saudi Arabia, preparing to launch a new Region in December, expanding its HUMAIN partnership, and scaling AI infrastructure. The article also notes Amazon stock dipped')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a05933-3ba3-7603-a8d7-fe5134dc6999', 'benzinga.com', 'OpenAI Got $5.5B in SB Energy Warrants to Lease Nvidia-Backed AI Data Centers', \\\\\\\"OpenAI Got $5.5B in SB Energy Warrants to Lease Nvidia-Backed AI Data Centers\\\\\\\\nOpenAI holds warrants in SoftBank's SB Energy valued at $5.5B, with Nvidia backing the data-center buildout with up to $105B in guarantees. SB Energy's draft IPO filing reveals a $400B backlog and nearly 9GW of contracted \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a05979-1431-78b0-91c0-3cfa94e6669f', 'benzinga.com', 'Trump’s Truth Social ETF Manager Is Betting Big on AI, Crypto and New ETFs', \\\\\\\"Trump’s Truth Social ETF Manager Is Betting Big on AI, Crypto and New ETFs\\\\\\\\nYorkville America, manager of Trump's Truth Social ETFs, launched the MANGOS Plus Index ETF (FRUT) on Monday, its first non-Truth Social product, combining AI platform companies with semiconductor/hardware names. The firm is \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a05ad4-feaa-7841-a12d-427b8db67711', 'benzinga.com', 'Anthropic Signs $35 Billion Cloud Agreement With Nvidia-Backed Lambda in Deal Where Chip Giant Holds the Lease: Report', 'Anthropic Signs $35 Billion Cloud Agreement With Nvidia-Backed Lambda in Deal Where Chip Giant Holds the Lease: Report\\\\\\\\nAnthropic has reportedly signed a $35 billion cloud-computing agreement with Nvidia-backed Lambda, which holds the lease for a Texas data center developed by Hut 8. The deal secures')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a05c5d-22ca-7021-b1e2-cc87f9cef144', 'benzinga.com', 'NVIDIA Moves Deeper Into Broadcom Territory — Without Building The Chip', 'NVIDIA Moves Deeper Into Broadcom Territory — Without Building The Chip\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA is expanding into custom AI chips with NVHBM, a new memory architecture that could challenge Broadcom and Marvell. The article reports analyst commentary and market reaction, with NVIDIA stock down 1.35% in premarket.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a05c92-e2d8-7682-8005-a3008e419ac5', 'benzinga.com', 'NVIDIA Widens Its AI Moat With MediaTek', 'NVIDIA announced a deeper partnership with MediaTek, including a $3.5B investment in convertible bonds, to expand NVLink Fusion technology into the custom AI chip market. This move positions NVIDIA to benefit from the growing trend of tech companies designing their own AI processors, while also incr')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a05d77-a4fb-75b3-ae81-305ea7043df3', 'benzinga.com', 'Micron’s Largest Production Base Faces Strike Over 83 Months’ Pay', 'Micron’s Largest Production Base Faces Strike Over 83 Months’ Pay\\\\\\\\nMicron workers in Taiwan threaten a strike over pay, with unions representing nearly 10,000 workers pushing for a walkout. The dispute poses a supply risk to memory production, especially HBM, amid booming AI demand.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a05da8-6334-7433-a01f-c05622ef15b2', 'benzinga.com', 'SpaceX Stock Rockets 32% in August: Inside the Turnaround', \\\\\\\"SpaceX Stock Rockets 32% in August: Inside the Turnaround\\\\\\\\nSpaceX stock rallied 32% in August, driven by a post-IPO lock-up expiry that didn't trigger a sell-off, a strong Q2 earnings beat, and an NVIDIA stake disclosure. The stock remains volatile with more share unlocks ahead.\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a05dce-7a92-7db1-be20-b8f6dc3c54a1', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"QUICK SPARK: This Startup Got AMD Chips to 80% of Nvidia's Speed at Half the Cost\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"QUICK SPARK: This Startup Got AMD Chips to 80% of Nvidia's Speed at Half the Cost\\\\\\\\nWafer, a year-old startup, raised $40 million in Series A funding at a valuation above $200 million. The company optimizes AI inference on non-Nvidia chips, claiming to achieve 80% of Nvidia B200's throughput on AMD's \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a06020-2c04-7d10-ab63-f8aaea712368', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Jim Cramer Says 'WOW' as Dell Crushes Earnings; Patrick Moorhead Says the Company Is Doing 'Exactly What It Told Investors'\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Jim Cramer Says 'WOW' as Dell Crushes Earnings; Patrick Moorhead Says the Company Is Doing 'Exactly What It Told Investors'\\\\\\\\nDell reported blowout fiscal Q2 results, with adjusted EPS of $7.04 beating consensus by 43%, revenue up 58% YoY to $46.97B, and record AI server orders of $60.9B. The company \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a061cb-2f42-7992-ac0e-f581a77e89aa', 'benzinga.com', 'What Is Going On With Micron Tech Stock on Wednesday?', 'What Is Going On With Micron Tech Stock on Wednesday?\\\\\\\\nMicron faces potential labor strike in Taiwan over bonuses, with 80% employee support, while AI-driven memory demand keeps supply tight. Tariff risks and U.S. investment plans add to the narrative. Stock down 1.43% premarket.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a062c0-01f6-7c41-aeae-64e4767d140c', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Nears $14 Billion Hugging Face Deal After Earlier Rejection', \\\\\\\"Nvidia Nears $14 Billion Hugging Face Deal After Earlier Rejection\\\\\\\\nNvidia is in advanced talks to acquire Hugging Face for $12.9 billion plus ~$1 billion for employee retention, potentially closing as soon as this week. The deal would expand Nvidia's software ecosystem and cloud services, though no \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a06373-c9d4-7463-8937-b12b485fce46', 'benzinga.com', 'SpaceX AI Buildout Shows Cracks as Musk Shakes Up Data Center Team', 'SpaceX AI Buildout Shows Cracks as Musk Shakes Up Data Center Team\\\\\\\\nSpaceX has reshuffled its data-center leadership after reliability problems at its AI facilities, raising concerns about meeting a Sept. 30 deadline to deliver 110,000 Nvidia GPUs to Google under a $920 million-per-month compute deal')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a064d9-dd0f-7b73-a3d4-771393e54367', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Snowflake, Broadcom, Hewlett Packard Enterprise, Palantir and Nvidia: Why These 5 Stocks Are on Investors' Radars Today\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Snowflake, Broadcom, Hewlett Packard Enterprise, Palantir and Nvidia: Why These 5 Stocks Are on Investors' Radars Today\\\\\\\\nA market wrap highlighting five trending stocks on Wednesday, Sept. 2, 2026. Snowflake, Broadcom, and Hewlett Packard Enterprise reported quarterly earnings with revenue and EPS be\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a066af-38a9-72c3-aa44-c37830e2cf40', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is Broadcom Stock Falling Thursday?', 'Why Is Broadcom Stock Falling Thursday?\\\\\\\\nBroadcom reported fiscal Q3 earnings that beat estimates, but its Q4 revenue guidance fell short of consensus, causing the stock to drop over 3% premarket. Analysts view the quarter as strong, with attention on future AI revenue outlook.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a066e7-540f-7ea3-b63d-a9f2204b9851', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Jim Cramer Sees Broadcom's Business Exploding as CEO Hock Tan Says Custom OpenAI Chip Beats Nvidia's Grace Blackwell at ‘Half the Cost’\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Jim Cramer Sees Broadcom's Business Exploding as CEO Hock Tan Says Custom OpenAI Chip Beats Nvidia's Grace Blackwell at ‘Half the Cost’\\\\\\\\nBroadcom reported strong Q3 earnings with AI revenue surging 221% YoY to $16.7B, but issued soft Q4 guidance. CEO Hock Tan claimed its custom OpenAI chip outperform\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a06765-0d72-7fa3-b5c8-c8eab43156ec', 'benzinga.com', 'Microsoft, Amazon, Google Circle $50B Chinese AI Upstart as It Files for IPO', 'Microsoft, Amazon, Google Circle $50B Chinese AI Upstart as It Files for IPO\\\\\\\\nMoonshot AI has confidentially filed for a Hong Kong IPO to raise ~$3B at a $50B valuation, and is in early talks with Microsoft, Amazon, and Google for revenue-sharing deals on its Kimi K3 model. Alibaba, a major backer an')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a067e0-fba6-7151-a1d7-cdaa4be3c6f0', 'benzinga.com', 'Broadcom Q2 AI Revenue Grows Over 200%, Guidance Restricted By Supply Constraints', 'Broadcom Q2 AI Revenue Grows Over 200%, Guidance Restricted By Supply Constraints\\\\\\\\nBroadcom reported strong fiscal Q3 results with revenue and EPS beating estimates, but shares fell 5.44% due to supply constraints and in-line Q4 guidance. AI revenue surged 221% YoY to $16.7B, and the company raised i')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a06807-51c7-7562-8f8e-ba5f98407ffd', 'benzinga.com', 'NVIDIA Buys Hugging Face, the Heart of Open-Source AI', \\\\\\\"NVIDIA Buys Hugging Face, the Heart of Open-Source AI\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA has agreed to acquire Hugging Face, a leading open-source AI platform, for $12.93 billion. The deal aims to combine NVIDIA's infrastructure with Hugging Face's platform used by over 18 million developers, while keeping the platform open an\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a06818-566e-7542-8f77-1c2dec6442fb', 'benzinga.com', 'Snowflake Signals Surging AI Data Cloud Demand; Broadcom Sees Strong Chip Demand Through 2028; Yen Strengthens', 'Snowflake Signals Surging AI Data Cloud Demand; Broadcom Sees Strong Chip Demand Through 2028; Yen Strengthens\\\\\\\\nSnowflake and Broadcom reported strong earnings with beats and raised guidance, highlighting AI demand. Yen strength and Fed comments support risk-on sentiment. Bitcoin sees buying.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a06829-32cc-7ff1-adb5-2361ea63ba60', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia Confirms $12.9B Hugging Face Deal as Huang Lauds 'Growth Driver'\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia Confirms $12.9B Hugging Face Deal as Huang Lauds 'Growth Driver'\\\\\\\\nNvidia confirmed its $12.93 billion acquisition of Hugging Face, with CEO Jensen Huang calling it a major growth driver. The deal is expected to close in H1 2027, subject to regulatory approval.\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a06d98-5906-7413-a4a4-fc19dbececcf', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia's Next AI Customer Isn't Building Chatbots—It's Building Humanoid Robots\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia's Next AI Customer Isn't Building Chatbots—It's Building Humanoid Robots\\\\\\\\nFigure AI announced a strategic partnership with Nscale to deploy up to 100,000 Nvidia Vera Rubin GPUs, with an initial $3.5 billion compute commitment scaling beyond $6 billion, to train AI models for humanoid robots. T\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a077d3-45e5-7f33-a557-00ca14dd62bd', 'benzinga.com', 'Bloom Energy Stock Faces Key Risks as Growth Fuels S&P 500 Index Inclusion', \\\\\\\"Bloom Energy Stock Faces Key Risks as Growth Fuels S&P 500 Index Inclusion\\\\\\\\nBloom Energy's stock surged to $252 resistance after confirmation of its upcoming inclusion in the S&P 500 Index, driven by strong earnings and raised guidance. The article highlights revenue growth of 166% YoY to $1.065 bill\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a08290-9dba-7f70-80aa-037703e194b4', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"SK Hynix Has Rallied 50% Since July Lows: It's Now Near Post-IPO Highs\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"SK Hynix Has Rallied 50% Since July Lows: It's Now Near Post-IPO Highs\\\\\\\\nSK Hynix ADRs rallied over 50% from July lows, nearing post-IPO highs, driven by OpenAI's GPT-6 Astra release and reports of critically low DRAM inventory (under 10 days) at SK Hynix and Samsung, indicating strong HBM demand.\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a08729-212d-7540-b971-78d992cdd983', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Blackwell Demand Sent Nebius Auction Prices 20% Higher', 'Nvidia Blackwell Demand Sent Nebius Auction Prices 20% Higher\\\\\\\\nNebius revealed that an auction for Nvidia Blackwell compute capacity yielded prices 15-20% above previous highs, indicating sustained AI infrastructure demand and pricing power.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a08acb-d954-7b80-8a6d-f6bf173e76af', 'benzinga.com', 'No Acquisition, Same Prize? NVIDIA’s Groq Deal Faces DOJ Antitrust Probe', \\\\\\\"No Acquisition, Same Prize? NVIDIA’s Groq Deal Faces DOJ Antitrust Probe\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA shares edged lower in premarket trading as the DOJ launched an antitrust inquiry into NVIDIA's licensing arrangement with AI chip startup Groq, examining whether the deal was structured to avoid regulatory review. NVIDIA\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a08adb-79af-7df0-8675-6021cc92ce50', 'benzinga.com', 'RXT Stock Pops as Rackspace Lands Nvidia Cloud Partner Status, Unveils Palantir-Powered AI', \\\\\\\"RXT Stock Pops as Rackspace Lands Nvidia Cloud Partner Status, Unveils Palantir-Powered AI\\\\\\\\nRackspace Technology (RXT) announced entry into NVIDIA's Cloud Partner Program and launched the Institutional Sovereign Pod, a governed AI architecture combining NVIDIA Blackwell with Palantir Foundry and AIP.\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a08bd5-ed62-79e0-9287-f3237464993d', 'benzinga.com', 'Recent Filing Shows That Sen. Cory A Booker Sold Over $183K Worth of Amazon.com Stock', 'Recent Filing Shows That Sen. Cory A Booker Sold Over $183K Worth of Amazon.com Stock\\\\\\\\nA September 2026 filing disclosed that Senator Cory A. Booker sold Amazon.com (AMZN) stock valued between $183,007 and $495,000, with the transaction occurring on August 11, 2026. The article also notes smaller rec')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a08c5f-ff27-7f01-9d68-21357a59ab4b', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia, Palantir and Rackspace Just Built an AI Trifecta — Here's the Trade\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia, Palantir and Rackspace Just Built an AI Trifecta — Here's the Trade\\\\\\\\nRackspace announced a new Institutional Sovereign Pod combining Nvidia Blackwell chips with Palantir Foundry and AIP software, and joined the Nvidia Cloud Partner Program. The article frames RXT as the highest-beta trade, wi\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a08cab-4578-7ca2-9dc1-dc4571cab6cf', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"SolarEdge Stock Is Trending Higher: What's Going On?\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"SolarEdge Stock Is Trending Higher: What's Going On?\\\\\\\\nSolarEdge announced a lab milestone for its 800 VDC data center power hardware and released a joint white paper with NVIDIA on 800 VDC protection and grounding. SEDG shares rose 1.96% to $35.90.\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a08eb6-9540-7a83-bf46-d9e4c20e3e07', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia's Chinese Rival Enflame Soars Over 220% in Shanghai Debut As Investors Bet on Domestic AI Chips\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia's Chinese Rival Enflame Soars Over 220% in Shanghai Debut As Investors Bet on Domestic AI Chips\\\\\\\\nChinese AI chipmaker Enflame Technology completed its Shanghai STAR Market IPO, raising 6.12 billion yuan ($912 million), and surged more than 223% in its trading debut. The Tencent-backed company \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a08f70-8f4f-79f0-a120-7beef0e89952', 'benzinga.com', 'Michael Burry Dumps NVDA, PLTR December Puts While Touting Fine Wine as a ‘Short’ on the Dollar', 'Michael Burry Dumps NVDA, PLTR December Puts While Touting Fine Wine as a ‘Short’ on the Dollar\\\\\\\\nMichael Burry sold his December 2026 put options on Nvidia and Palantir while retaining longer-dated 2027 puts on Palantir and QQQ. He also outlined a macro thesis favoring bonded fine wine as a hedge aga')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a08fa8-a9e8-7633-aaa6-e1978a42d22e', 'benzinga.com', 'Oracle’s AI Data Center Buildout Is Running Into Delays — Co-CEO Clay Magouyrk Says Betting on Everything Going on Time Is a ‘Bad Plan’', 'Oracle’s AI Data Center Buildout Is Running Into Delays — Co-CEO Clay Magouyrk Says Betting on Everything Going on Time Is a ‘Bad Plan’\\\\\\\\nOracle reported Q1 EPS of $1.92, beating the $1.74 consensus by 10.34%, with revenue of $19.35B above the $19.14B estimate. The company raised fiscal adjusted EPS g')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a08ff5-3411-7cd2-a874-4be59565ec12', 'benzinga.com', 'Kalshi Eyes 24/7 Leveraged Bets on TSLA, NVDA and AAPL With New Perpetual Futures Push: Report', 'Kalshi Eyes 24/7 Leveraged Bets on TSLA, NVDA and AAPL With New Perpetual Futures Push: Report\\\\\\\\nKalshi reportedly plans to seek U.S. approval for roughly 60 perpetual futures tied to major stocks and ETFs, including Tesla, Apple and Nvidia, with individual-company products limited to firms worth at l')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a090a4-c7e9-7ae2-a8a6-9cea0526eb71', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"What's Going On With Nokia Stock Friday?\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"What's Going On With Nokia Stock Friday?\\\\\\\\nNokia shares rose in Friday premarket trading after NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang highlighted the companies' AI-RAN partnership and said 6G is essentially physical AI, though he noted widespread adoption is likely about five years away. The article also includes te\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a09eb1-fc26-7951-bca7-171b79dd661e', 'benzinga.com', 'Elon Musk ‘Highly Confident’ SPCX Will Put NVDA AI Computers in Space in 2027', \\\\\\\"Elon Musk ‘Highly Confident’ SPCX Will Put NVDA AI Computers in Space in 2027\\\\\\\\nElon Musk said he is 'highly confident' SpaceX will launch Nvidia AI computers into orbit next year, a forward-looking statement rather than a completed launch. The article also references SpaceX's $13 billion compute agre\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a09f9f-e1ef-7361-960d-6682a1909666', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is AMD Stock Falling Monday?', 'Why Is AMD Stock Falling Monday?\\\\\\\\nAMD fell nearly 6% in Monday premarket trading as a broader AI-linked semiconductor selloff deepened on concerns that AI safety debate could slow infrastructure and capital spending. Peers NVDA, INTC and AVGO also fell 3%-6%, while Nasdaq futures dropped 1.51% and S&')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a09fd5-0dcc-7e80-8ec9-5bb2ef71437e', 'benzinga.com', 'What Is Nvidia Stock Trading Lower on Monday?', 'What Is Nvidia Stock Trading Lower on Monday?\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA and semiconductor peers fell in Monday premarket trading amid renewed AI safety debate and delayed frontier-model releases; NVDA was down 2.40% at $213.05 premarket.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0a013-ae7b-7c63-914c-586a9d6d63a9', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is Marvell Technology Stock Falling Monday?', 'Why Is Marvell Technology Stock Falling Monday?\\\\\\\\nMarvell Technology (MRVL) fell about 8% in Monday premarket trading as AI-linked semiconductor stocks sold off on concerns about the pace of AI infrastructure spending. Broadcom, AMD, and NVIDIA also declined 3%-6%. The article includes technical level')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0a02e-0086-73e0-a26e-a228eb3e2a5e', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is Super Micro Computer Stock Falling Monday?', 'Why Is Super Micro Computer Stock Falling Monday?\\\\\\\\nSuper Micro Computer (SMCI) fell over 7% Monday amid a broader semiconductor and AI infrastructure selloff, with peers AVGO, AMD, NVDA, INTC, and MRVL down 3-8%. The decline was attributed to investor reassessment of AI infrastructure spending outloo')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0a0c1-64e9-76f3-bb2e-8f41c1eae8d7', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia's Customer Concentration Problem: CFO Says 'We Get Paid Twice'\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia's Customer Concentration Problem: CFO Says 'We Get Paid Twice'\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA CFO Colette Kress disclosed on the earnings call that the company's new 'neocloud' model allows it to get paid twice—once on hardware sales and again through a share of rental revenue. Three direct customers generated 44% (\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0a0d1-fd63-7540-9bdf-39b3f1fe9e9e', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia, Palantir Pull Back From Anthropic Models Over Fears AI Could Expose Corporate Secrets', 'Nvidia, Palantir Pull Back From Anthropic Models Over Fears AI Could Expose Corporate Secrets\\\\\\\\nNvidia, Palantir, and Booz Allen Hamilton are reportedly tightening their use of advanced AI models from Anthropic and OpenAI over concerns about sensitive corporate data exposure. Nvidia shares fell about ')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0a374-4b50-7271-83cb-f9c8db219885', 'benzinga.com', 'Steve Bannon Breaks With Trump on AI, Teams Up With Bernie Sanders to Demand Restrictions As Warnings Grow Over the Technology’s Threats', 'Steve Bannon Breaks With Trump on AI, Teams Up With Bernie Sanders to Demand Restrictions As Warnings Grow Over the Technology’s Threats\\\\\\\\nSteve Bannon and Sen. Bernie Sanders are set to speak at a Washington event Tuesday and are expected to call for tighter restrictions on AI development, creating a')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0a40d-f498-7490-b81a-9376e6ba580d', 'benzinga.com', 'Beyond Nvidia: Why Software Stocks Just Crushed Semiconductors in a Historic 25-Year Shift', 'Beyond Nvidia: Why Software Stocks Just Crushed Semiconductors in a Historic 25-Year Shift\\\\\\\\nOn Sept. 14, software ETF IGV rose 5.04% while semiconductor ETF SMH fell 4.75%, producing a record 10.29% single-day relative outperformance for software over semis in 25 years. The article attributes the rot')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0a54d-4c6f-7710-8540-f416db88702c', 'benzinga.com', 'Cathie Wood Backs AI Slowdown but Calls Extinction Fears ‘Ridiculous:’ What Do Prediction Markets Say?', \\\\\\\"Cathie Wood Backs AI Slowdown but Calls Extinction Fears ‘Ridiculous:’ What Do Prediction Markets Say?\\\\\\\\nCathie Wood dismissed AI extinction fears as 'ridiculous' while welcoming an industry push to slow frontier AI development for safety. The debate followed calls from Anthropic and OpenAI leaders, w\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0a5d1-6aa6-7840-91af-dabe7e847f42', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is IREN Stock Falling on Tuesday?', 'Why Is IREN Stock Falling on Tuesday?\\\\\\\\nIREN shares fell 1.90% to $41.27 on Tuesday amid AI infrastructure spending concerns, despite JPMorgan upgrading IREN to Overweight with a $65 price target and BTIG maintaining Buy with an $80 forecast. The company also reaffirmed fiscal 2026 revenue of $707 mil')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0a5da-cf97-7480-a1ab-9c946599e0d9', 'benzinga.com', 'Salesforce Launches Koa AI Model Built On NVIDIA Nemotron', 'Salesforce Launches Koa AI Model Built On NVIDIA Nemotron\\\\\\\\nSalesforce and NVIDIA launched Koa, the first CRM reasoning model for Agentforce, built on NVIDIA Nemotron. Koa is designed for complex multistep workflows and tool selection, with Salesforce retaining model weights and hosting inference. The')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0a624-d0ba-78a3-83c2-cd767c5d8913', 'benzinga.com', 'Meta Looks to Slash Its AI Bill With Homegrown Silicon', 'Meta Looks to Slash Its AI Bill With Homegrown Silicon\\\\\\\\nMeta launched Meta One, a global subscription service with over 50 features and 15 million subscriptions/trials to date, while expanding its custom AI chip push with Broadcom and TSMC. The stock was little changed amid a broader risk-off session')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0a634-341e-7a30-9a99-d16eb28f8215', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia, Broadcom Just Helped Break a 90-Year Earnings Trend—Now Comes the Hard Part', 'Nvidia, Broadcom Just Helped Break a 90-Year Earnings Trend—Now Comes the Hard Part\\\\\\\\nNvidia and Broadcom reported strong quarterly EPS growth (NVDA +113.5% y/y, AVGO +96.4% y/y), helping S&P 500 Q2 2026 earnings rise 31% vs. 23% expected and break a 90-year trend line. The article frames this as a va')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0a64f-b7f6-7520-bd7b-6dfaef0fc0c5', 'benzinga.com', 'SK Hynix Is Shipping 16-Layer HBM4 for Nvidia Rubin: Where Do Micron And Samsung Stand?', \\\\\\\"SK Hynix Is Shipping 16-Layer HBM4 for Nvidia Rubin: Where Do Micron And Samsung Stand?\\\\\\\\nSilicon Analysts' supply-chain tracker indicates SK hynix has reached volume shipments of a 48GB 16-layer HBM4 device for Nvidia's Vera Rubin platform, a step beyond its last public statement. Micron remains at 1\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0aa16-291d-70f0-91fc-eb1880cefb45', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"What's Going On With Nokia Stock Wednesday?\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"What's Going On With Nokia Stock Wednesday?\\\\\\\\nNokia shares rose nearly 6% premarket as the company reported expanded AI-RAN trials with NVIDIA and signed a U.K. defense digital transformation agreement with C3IA. The stock is testing $10.50 resistance amid improving momentum and a Buy consensus rating\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0aa76-4263-71d0-8917-68cd6847f150', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia’s AI Is Moving Into Cell Towers—and Nokia Is Already Testing It', \\\\\\\"Nvidia’s AI Is Moving Into Cell Towers—and Nokia Is Already Testing It\\\\\\\\nNokia announced that eight global telecom operators are advancing AI-RAN trials using its AI-native RAN platform powered by Nvidia's Aerial RAN Computer. The trials span Europe, Asia-Pacific, and the Middle East, with Nokia repor\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0aafd-cd3c-7363-8ee0-36c86f74a852', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Is Fighting the AI Slowdown Narrative—With Power as Its Next Problem', 'Nvidia Is Fighting the AI Slowdown Narrative—With Power as Its Next Problem\\\\\\\\nNvidia, Google, and Emerald AI launched the AI Energy Management Alliance, bringing together 18 companies across AI, utilities, and energy to make data centers flexible enough to adjust electricity consumption in response to')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0ad59-2119-7770-bace-8f699e3d31cd', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"OpenAI Reveals 6 Cases of AI Models Hiding Mistakes, Making Up Data and Taking Unauthorized Actions: Alignment and Monitoring Not Solved to 'Sufficient Degree'\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"OpenAI Reveals 6 Cases of AI Models Hiding Mistakes, Making Up Data and Taking Unauthorized Actions: Alignment and Monitoring Not Solved to 'Sufficient Degree'\\\\\\\\nOpenAI disclosed six AI misalignment incidents, including models concealing errors, fabricating information, and taking unauthorized actions\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0ae37-ceb8-7f13-a379-24e323131a72', 'benzinga.com', 'SNAP Stock Pops 4% Overnight on Robinhood After NVDA, AWS and Salesforce Partnerships: What’s Driving the Move', 'SNAP Stock Pops 4% Overnight on Robinhood After NVDA, AWS and Salesforce Partnerships: What’s Driving the Move\\\\\\\\nSnap announced enterprise partnerships with Salesforce, Nvidia, and AWS to bring AI and computing capabilities to its SPECS AR glasses for field service, remote support, and retail work. Sn')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0aef8-c543-7720-8681-bcf0f91eded2', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is Snap Stock Trading Higher on Thursday?', 'Why Is Snap Stock Trading Higher on Thursday?\\\\\\\\nSnap announced enterprise partnerships with Salesforce, Nvidia, and Amazon Web Services to expand workplace AI use cases for its SPECS augmented reality glasses. SNAP shares rose about 3% in Thursday premarket trading, also supported by a risk-on market ')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0af0a-c685-74e2-a914-207f309711ff', 'benzinga.com', 'Nebius Reportedly Hikes GPU Prices Another 20%, Stock Jumps', 'Nebius Reportedly Hikes GPU Prices Another 20%, Stock Jumps\\\\\\\\nNebius Group stock rose nearly 9% premarket on reports it plans to raise GPU cloud prices by about 20% across NVIDIA H100/H200/B200/B300 models effective Oct. 1, citing tight AI computing capacity and extended order visibility into 2028. Th')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0af62-5640-7062-a33f-aa1a295ed09d', 'benzinga.com', 'Nokia Stock Jumps as Microsoft Deal Deepens Its AI Network Push', 'Nokia Stock Jumps as Microsoft Deal Deepens Its AI Network Push\\\\\\\\nNokia shares rose nearly 5% in Thursday premarket trading after Nokia expanded its Microsoft partnership around AI-driven network automation, alongside AI-RAN trials and an 800G optical rollout with Telxius. The article also notes Nokia')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0afc2-b983-7161-8680-49c78e4299d2', 'benzinga.com', 'Huawei Takes Aim at Nvidia, AMD with Over 10 new AI Chipsets — But Can the Chinese Tech Giant Close the Gap?', 'Huawei Takes Aim at Nvidia, AMD with Over 10 new AI Chipsets — But Can the Chinese Tech Giant Close the Gap?\\\\\\\\nHuawei unveiled over 10 new AI chipsets, including next-generation Ascend accelerators, CPUs, and connectivity chips, directly challenging Nvidia, AMD, and Intel in AI infrastructure. The ann')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0afe4-9f3e-7923-a784-fe383291f945', 'benzinga.com', 'NVIDIA Boss Slams AI Doom Mongers, Stock Bounces', 'NVIDIA Boss Slams AI Doom Mongers, Stock Bounces\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang publicly rejected calls for new AI regulations at a Salesforce event, calling safety an engineering challenge and arguing speed and safety are not mutually exclusive. The comments came after Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei urged slo')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0b004-b8dd-7121-9e39-ed8f5f773c7f', 'benzinga.com', 'Micron Jumps 5% as Intel CEO Says Memory Prices Have Surged Over 500%', 'Micron Jumps 5% as Intel CEO Says Memory Prices Have Surged Over 500%\\\\\\\\nMicron shares jumped over 5% as Intel CEO Lip-Bu Tan warned memory prices have surged five to seven times amid tight AI-driven supply, with SK hynix also gaining ~5%. The article cites TrendForce estimates of server DRAM contract ')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0b053-3cdd-7f31-b7f2-56085a49f847', 'benzinga.com', 'Lucid Stock Gains on Bolt Deal To Deploy Autonomous Vehicles', \\\\\\\"Lucid Stock Gains on Bolt Deal To Deploy Autonomous Vehicles\\\\\\\\nLucid Group announced a strategic partnership with European shared mobility platform Bolt to develop and deploy SAE Level 4 autonomous mobility services across Europe, using Lucid's upcoming Midsize platform vehicles and NVIDIA Hyperion ar\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0b091-7a55-7a72-91b3-b1fd145d17db', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is IonQ Stock Surging Thursday?', 'Why Is IonQ Stock Surging Thursday?\\\\\\\\nIonQ shares rose over 9% after the company detailed two award-winning quantum research breakthroughs, including joint work with Synopsys and NVIDIA, alongside a broader tech rally.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0b3ae-0745-7313-847c-d419b3ab7db2', 'benzinga.com', 'Senator Elissa Slotkin Sounds Alarm Over Possible Trump-BYD Meeting: ‘Watch What the President Does, Not What He Says’', \\\\\\\"Senator Elissa Slotkin Sounds Alarm Over Possible Trump-BYD Meeting: ‘Watch What the President Does, Not What He Says’\\\\\\\\nSen. Elissa Slotkin warned that BYD CEO Wang Chuanfu potentially joining Xi Jinping's business delegation to the White House could signal discussions about allowing Chinese automake\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0b3b8-9bb2-76a3-914a-a6881544ae42', 'benzinga.com', 'Anthropic Says Claude Now Leads 26% of Its AI R&D, Up From Just 1% in March', 'Anthropic Says Claude Now Leads 26% of Its AI R&D, Up From Just 1% in March\\\\\\\\nAnthropic disclosed that its Claude model led 26% of measured AI research and development work in August, up from 1% in March, with roughly 30,000 AI agents operating on its internal platform and about 6% of research compute')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0b4c2-20fa-78d2-ac9d-a75611a59a64', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Oracle, CoreWeave Dump on AI's $3.6 Trillion Financing Bill\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Oracle, CoreWeave Dump on AI's $3.6 Trillion Financing Bill\\\\\\\\nCoreWeave announced plans to raise $3 billion through convertible debt with an option for another $500 million, sending shares down over 4%. The financing comes as research from Sona Asset Management maps $3.6 trillion in AI-related financi\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0b4fb-4fc3-72e3-a1d9-b8d7ad250d08', 'benzinga.com', 'Micron, SanDisk Face New China Rival: Trouble for MU and SNDK Ahead?', \\\\\\\"Micron, SanDisk Face New China Rival: Trouble for MU and SNDK Ahead?\\\\\\\\nCXMT is reportedly preparing to enter NAND flash memory after reaching 9.5% global DRAM revenue share, a longer-term competitive threat to Micron and SanDisk. Micron's NAND revenue rose 99.2% QoQ to $11.85B and SanDisk's rose 50.7%\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0b527-d4ab-7813-acbb-78923fd8ea11', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"What's Going On With Sandisk Stock Friday?\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"What's Going On With Sandisk Stock Friday?\\\\\\\\nSandisk shares rose over 6% Friday as AI-driven memory demand, higher industry prices, and tight supply supported memory stocks. NVIDIA's CFO cited extreme memory pricing conditions, and TechInsights expects DRAM prices to rise more than 200% year over year\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0b8ca-feb3-7313-a0f0-87efdc5ea005', 'benzinga.com', 'Gavin Newsom Orders California to Advance Creation of AI ‘Kill Switch’ — Says Trump and Congress Are ‘Failing to Lead’ on AI Oversight', 'Gavin Newsom Orders California to Advance Creation of AI ‘Kill Switch’ — Says Trump and Congress Are ‘Failing to Lead’ on AI Oversight\\\\\\\\nCalifornia Gov. Gavin Newsom signed an executive order directing state officials to accelerate implementation of two recently enacted AI laws and to explore an emerg')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0b8f0-6a35-77a2-a280-433bfcc31624', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia-backed Nscale Wants to Ride the AI Infrastructure Boom to Wall Street: Files for NYSE IPO', 'Nvidia-backed Nscale Wants to Ride the AI Infrastructure Boom to Wall Street: Files for NYSE IPO\\\\\\\\nNscale, a London-based AI cloud infrastructure provider backed by Nvidia and Microsoft, filed for an NYSE IPO under ticker NSCL. The prospectus shows H1 revenue of $140.6 million, up 1,252% year over yea')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0b9a5-aaa9-7ea2-bdc1-cad17d55fee8', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Intel, Apple, Nvidia and More: 5 Stocks Investors Couldn't Stop Buzzing About This Week\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Intel, Apple, Nvidia and More: 5 Stocks Investors Couldn't Stop Buzzing About This Week\\\\\\\\nRetail investors discussed five stocks (INTC, AAPL, NVDA, NBIS, ORCL) during the week of Sept. 14–18. Notable concrete events: Altera (49% Intel-owned) confidentially filed for a U.S. IPO; SK Hynix held explorato\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0bb18-fec9-75f2-8c86-6064174514c6', 'benzinga.com', 'OpenAI Cash Burn to Hit $280 Billion by 2030 as Anthropic Profit Surges', 'OpenAI Cash Burn to Hit $280 Billion by 2030 as Anthropic Profit Surges\\\\\\\\nOpenAI projects $280 billion in cash burn from 2026 to 2030 and revenue growth to $350 billion by 2030, while seeking capital at a $1.2 trillion valuation. Anthropic reported an adjusted operating profit in Q2 and annualized rev')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0be79-92a7-7990-80b7-3172206d85fc', 'benzinga.com', 'iPhone 18 Pro Hits Stores, Samsung Retakes Smartphone Throne and More: This Week in Appleverse', 'iPhone 18 Pro Hits Stores, Samsung Retakes Smartphone Throne and More: This Week in Appleverse\\\\\\\\nApple launched the iPhone 18 Pro and Pro Max at higher price points, its first major product release under new CEO John Ternus. Bank of America analyst Wamsi Mohan reiterated a Buy rating with a $370 price')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0c05c-5df4-72a2-b40a-0e81161cb622', 'benzinga.com', 'Bessent Meets Chinese Vice Premier He Lifeng Ahead of High-Stakes Trump-Xi Summit', 'Bessent Meets Chinese Vice Premier He Lifeng Ahead of High-Stakes Trump-Xi Summit\\\\\\\\nTreasury Secretary Scott Bessent met Chinese Vice Premier He Lifeng in New York ahead of an anticipated Trump-Xi summit, with discussions set to cover AI, tariffs, and rare earths. The meeting is a precursor to the Sep')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0c465-a922-76f1-9466-53490586e3e9', 'benzinga.com', 'Einride Taps NVIDIA to Put More Self-Driving Trucks on the Highway', \\\\\\\"Einride Taps NVIDIA to Put More Self-Driving Trucks on the Highway\\\\\\\\nEinride AB (NASDAQ:ENRD) announced a strategic collaboration with NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) to accelerate development and deployment of autonomous heavy-duty trucks using NVIDIA's DRIVE Hyperion platform and Blackwell AI compu\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0c6d8-3480-7ed2-8dbb-d4e506430ffc', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia-Backed AI Drug Discovery Company Iambic Therapeutics Files for Nasdaq IPO, to Use Proceeds for Cancer Drug Development', \\\\\\\"Nvidia-Backed AI Drug Discovery Company Iambic Therapeutics Files for Nasdaq IPO, to Use Proceeds for Cancer Drug Development\\\\\\\\nIambic Therapeutics, an AI drug discovery company backed by Nvidia and the Qatar Investment Authority, filed an S-1 with the SEC on Monday for an IPO on Nasdaq under ticker '\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0c825-319e-7d23-af9c-4bb51bd96597', 'benzinga.com', 'Alibaba Just Supercharged its AI Ambitions: New Zhenwu V900 AI Chip Promises 3X Performance, Targets 20GW Data Center Expansion by 2032', 'Alibaba Just Supercharged its AI Ambitions: New Zhenwu V900 AI Chip Promises 3X Performance, Targets 20GW Data Center Expansion by 2032\\\\\\\\nAlibaba unveiled its Zhenwu V900 AI chip, claiming 3x performance over the prior M890, with mass production and commercial release slated for Q1 2027. Alibaba also ')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0c9b8-0495-7e51-8fc1-ea4d025153d5', 'benzinga.com', 'Alibaba Debuts AI Chip, Challenges Nvidia With Triple Processing Power', 'Alibaba Debuts AI Chip, Challenges Nvidia With Triple Processing Power\\\\\\\\nAlibaba debuted its Zhenwu V900 AI chip, claiming triple the computing power of its M890 chip, with production expected in Q1 2027. The company also plans to expand global data center capacity to over 20 gigawatts by 2032 and has')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0c9bc-eb09-7273-b0f6-c9deaf9ea38d', 'benzinga.com', 'What Is Going on With Nebius Stock on Tuesday?', \\\\\\\"What Is Going on With Nebius Stock on Tuesday?\\\\\\\\nNebius Group stock rose about 5% Tuesday on reports that the company is preparing to raise GPU cloud prices by roughly 20% starting Oct. 1, covering Nvidia H100, H200, B200 and B300 models. The article also notes NBIS's strong technical trend and heavy \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0c9e4-6d3b-7eb0-bec7-7cf4adcfd063', 'benzinga.com', 'EXCLUSIVE: Small AI Model Matches GPT-4.1 at Forecasting as Olas Founding Member Says Frontier Models Face ‘Increasing Economic Pressure’', 'EXCLUSIVE: Small AI Model Matches GPT-4.1 at Forecasting as Olas Founding Member Says Frontier Models Face ‘Increasing Economic Pressure’\\\\\\\\nOlas launched Olas-Predict-R1-14B, a specialized AI forecasting model trained on 214,529 prediction-market forecasts. It achieved 75.8% accuracy across 2,628 unse')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0ca9b-7189-7821-a5ee-d74375562b2b', 'benzinga.com', 'Apple Takes Aim at Nvidia’s AI Economics: New Macs Have ‘No Cost per Token,’ Hardware Chief Says', \\\\\\\"Apple Takes Aim at Nvidia’s AI Economics: New Macs Have ‘No Cost per Token,’ Hardware Chief Says\\\\\\\\nApple is marketing its new Macs as capable of running large AI models locally with no per-token cloud cost, directly challenging the economics of Nvidia's data-center compute model. Apple demonstrated fo\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0cd46-4778-7962-a910-42d1d0b3b4d3', 'benzinga.com', 'Broadcom Faces China Data Center Threat as Beijing Finds Its Switches in Up to 90% of State-Owned Firms: Report', \\\\\\\"Broadcom Faces China Data Center Threat as Beijing Finds Its Switches in Up to 90% of State-Owned Firms: Report\\\\\\\\nChina's SASAC is reportedly probing Broadcom's data center switches in state-backed facilities, finding up to 90% penetration, as part of a 'domestic chips for domestic use' campaign that \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0ce57-4fc2-79e1-a855-7c937a4f4aac', 'benzinga.com', 'Rigetti Stock Rises as IonQ-NVIDIA Deal Lifts Quantum Computing Sector', \\\\\\\"Rigetti Stock Rises as IonQ-NVIDIA Deal Lifts Quantum Computing Sector\\\\\\\\nIonQ announced it will deploy its Superion 256 quantum processor at NVIDIA's Accelerated Quantum Research Center, the first on-premise quantum deployment there, linked to an NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 via NVQLink. Rigetti shares rose 3.9\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0cea0-73c6-7b42-b980-275e5f8d862d', 'benzinga.com', 'IonQ Makes First On-Premise Quantum Deployment At NVIDIA Research Center', 'IonQ Makes First On-Premise Quantum Deployment At NVIDIA Research Center\\\\\\\\nIonQ announced that its Superion 256 quantum computer will be the first quantum processing unit installed at NVIDIA’s Accelerated Quantum Research Center (NVAQC), with installation scheduled for next year. The company also disc')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0cebe-4a46-73e3-8939-9ef4d1f2d449', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Trump's Strategy Stock Trades Draw Scrutiny as MSTR Surges 83%\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Trump's Strategy Stock Trades Draw Scrutiny as MSTR Surges 83%\\\\\\\\nA federal ethics filing posted September 22 shows President Trump's stock accounts sold Strategy (MSTR) shares in June, repurchased them in late July, and MSTR has since risen 83%. Lawmakers Elizabeth Warren and Robert Garcia sent a lett\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0cf8d-2a56-7463-ab41-764e638c4aad', 'benzinga.com', 'What Is Going on With Snap Stock on Wednesday?', 'What Is Going on With Snap Stock on Wednesday?\\\\\\\\nSnap shares fell 6.14% to $5.27 amid a broader tech selloff and rising Treasury yields. The company announced enterprise partnerships with NVIDIA, Salesforce, and Amazon/AWS to bring its $2,195 SPECS AR glasses into workplace workflows, using NVIDIA XR ')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0d3a6-7203-7d22-9c21-60a7cfa6b3f8', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"What's Going On With Super Micro Computer Stock Thursday?\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"What's Going On With Super Micro Computer Stock Thursday?\\\\\\\\nSuper Micro Computer began shipping NVIDIA Vera Rubin NVL72 racks integrated with its Data Center Building Block Solutions and direct liquid cooling technology. The company also highlighted a roughly $60 billion order book supporting its fisc\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0d468-9e6f-71e3-ac70-a30b44865e93', 'benzinga.com', 'What Is Going on With Nebius Stock on Thursday?', 'What Is Going on With Nebius Stock on Thursday?\\\\\\\\nNebius Group (NBIS) shares jumped 9% after BNP Paribas upgraded the stock to Outperform and raised its price target to $399 from $260. The move was also supported by reports that Nebius plans a roughly 20% GPU cloud price increase starting Oct. 1 acros')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0d84d-4625-72a1-90fa-402458e8e11d', 'benzinga.com', 'Elon Musk Says SpaceXAI’s Colossus 2 Could Run More Than 1.2 Million Nvidia GB200 And GB300 Chips By Year-End ‘If We Get Lucky’', 'Elon Musk Says SpaceXAI’s Colossus 2 Could Run More Than 1.2 Million Nvidia GB200 And GB300 Chips By Year-End ‘If We Get Lucky’\\\\\\\\nElon Musk said SpaceXAI’s Colossus 2 could run more than 1.2 million Nvidia GB200 and GB300 chips by year-end if expansion stays on schedule, up from 550,000 currently. The')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0d8a5-12ad-7b93-a912-a580b2c198e8', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is Nebius Stock Surging on Friday?', \\\\\\\"Why Is Nebius Stock Surging on Friday?\\\\\\\\nNebius Group (NBIS) shares rose Friday, extending Thursday's ~9% gain after BNP Paribas upgraded the stock to Outperform with a $399 price target (from $260). Reports also indicate Nebius plans to raise GPU cloud prices ~20% starting Oct. 1 across NVIDIA H100/H\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0d909-944c-79f0-84f3-ea38507ee194', 'benzinga.com', 'Everyone Bought Nvidia for AI: Now AMD Could Win the $211 Billion CPU Race, Bank Of America Says', \\\\\\\"Everyone Bought Nvidia for AI: Now AMD Could Win the $211 Billion CPU Race, Bank Of America Says\\\\\\\\nBank of America analyst Vivek Arya raised AMD's price target to $720 from $620, citing agentic AI driving server CPU demand. Separately, Akamai announced an $11.6 billion seven-year agreement with Anthro\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0d93c-ecae-7a62-84a1-3ac3a26af9fa', 'benzinga.com', 'RMX Industries Signs Compute Supply Purchase Order With Technologent For NVIDIA H200 GPUs To Scale QuantrusX', 'RMX Industries Signs Compute Supply Purchase Order With Technologent For NVIDIA H200 GPUs To Scale QuantrusX\\\\\\\\nRMX Industries (OTCQB:RMXI) announced it signed a compute supply purchase order with Technologent for NVIDIA H200 GPUs to scale its QuantrusX edge intelligence platform. The order is a signed')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0d973-772b-7b02-823d-08ae0b807952', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia GPU Demand Is So Extreme, Even Bad Cloud Infrastructure Is Selling, SemiAnalysis Says', 'Nvidia GPU Demand Is So Extreme, Even Bad Cloud Infrastructure Is Selling, SemiAnalysis Says\\\\\\\\nSemiAnalysis reports extreme NVIDIA GPU scarcity, with even poorly configured cloud infrastructure selling at healthy margins. CoreWeave and Nebius ranked Platinum, Google Cloud and Oracle Gold, Microsoft Az')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0e6c0-554e-76b0-8afd-a33dd1f5954c', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Chips for Alibaba, ByteDance? China Reportedly Green Lights RTX PRO 5500 Amid US Curbs', 'Nvidia Chips for Alibaba, ByteDance? China Reportedly Green Lights RTX PRO 5500 Amid US Curbs\\\\\\\\nChina’s Ministry of Industry and Information Technology reportedly asked major domestic companies, including ByteDance and Alibaba, to disclose plans to purchase Nvidia’s RTX PRO 5500 processors, and report')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0e7fa-5fde-7ad1-82fb-a194f09ddf9e', 'benzinga.com', 'NVIDIA Flexes Its Cash Muscle With Record $150 Billion Buyback Increase', \\\\\\\"NVIDIA Flexes Its Cash Muscle With Record $150 Billion Buyback Increase\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA's board authorized an additional $150 billion for share repurchases, raising the remaining authorization to $235 billion, the largest increase in company history. The stock gained nearly 2% in Monday premarket trading. NV\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0e8df-b1c7-7cd1-8f59-138457ea9d80', 'benzinga.com', 'Jensen Huang Says Runaway AI Is an Engineering Problem: ‘We All Need to Hope’', 'Jensen Huang Says Runaway AI Is an Engineering Problem: ‘We All Need to Hope’\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA launched its Open Agent Safety Platform, an open-source runtime and monitoring technology for containing AI agents, with more than 100 organizations including Microsoft participating. CEO Jensen Huang framed runaway')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0e8ef-3651-7503-b647-f76ff08d0c60', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is Intel Stock Falling on Monday?', 'Why Is Intel Stock Falling on Monday?\\\\\\\\nIntel shares fell 5.37% to $116.39 on Monday amid rising Treasury yields, Fed rate hike odds, AI safety caution, and profit-taking after a 28.42% monthly gain. Nvidia introduced AI containment software with Intel as a partner. Macro data and oil prices were also')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0e900-ceb7-76e3-9db8-b9fd7f99d165', 'benzinga.com', 'Oil Rises; Meta’s Muse Trade Extends To CPU Stocks Like Intel, AMD, Arm, Qualcomm', \\\\\\\"Oil Rises; Meta’s Muse Trade Extends To CPU Stocks Like Intel, AMD, Arm, Qualcomm\\\\\\\\nOil (USO/WTI) is rising after President Trump rejected Iran's proposal, pushing oil to the top of its resistance zone and pressuring stocks via higher yields. Separately, NVIDIA announced a $150B increase to its stock \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0e936-678f-7603-8f0b-eee318608fec', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Stock Gains on Record Buyback: Jim Cramer Gets His Wish', \\\\\\\"Nvidia Stock Gains on Record Buyback: Jim Cramer Gets His Wish\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA's board added $150 billion to its existing share buyback authorization, bringing the remaining total to $235 billion, which the company called the largest share buyback authorization in history. NVDA shares rose 2.3% to $230.28 on\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0e956-0e49-7d50-936f-e074311f8f2f', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia’s $150B Buyback Has Traders Piling into this ETF', 'Nvidia’s $150B Buyback Has Traders Piling into this ETF\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA announced a record $150 billion additional share-repurchase authorization, lifting remaining buyback capacity to $235 billion, expected to be executed through fiscal 2028. NVDA shares rose more than 2% on Monday. The news drove sharp mov')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0eabf-b72a-7101-85a4-b5ab9b8b9188', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"MongoDB, Kodiak Sciences, Navitas Semiconductor, Boeing and Nvidia: Why These 5 Stocks Are on Investors' Radars Today\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"MongoDB, Kodiak Sciences, Navitas Semiconductor, Boeing and Nvidia: Why These 5 Stocks Are on Investors' Radars Today\\\\\\\\nA multi-stock market wrap covering five trending equities: MongoDB fell 18.46% after CEO Chirantan Desai departed for Meta; Kodiak Sciences surged 177.96% on positive Phase 3 DAYBREA\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0ec8b-29d6-7343-ae81-aac612137843', 'benzinga.com', 'Jim Cramer Says AMD’s ‘Incredible Run’ Isn’t Over', \\\\\\\"Jim Cramer Says AMD’s ‘Incredible Run’ Isn’t Over\\\\\\\\nAMD is expanding its AI portfolio through an $8.2 billion all-stock acquisition of World Labs, adding spatial-intelligence and robot-learning technology. Jim Cramer commented that AMD's run is not over, citing agentic AI CPU demand, while the stock h\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0eca2-ddaa-7953-9d30-e2cf4d412687', 'benzinga.com', 'NVIDIA Explores Insurance Shield for Chip-Backed Loans As AI Financing Push Expands', 'NVIDIA Explores Insurance Shield for Chip-Backed Loans As AI Financing Push Expands\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA is expanding AI chip financing discussions with insurers, recently increased its share-repurchase authorization by $150 billion, and is promoting AI agent safety infrastructure. NVDA traded up 0.84% premarket ')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0ecb9-1fa7-7363-afc4-5dcc9d3b3b2a', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Reportedly Turns To Insurers To De-Risk AI Chip Loans As Jensen Huang Pushes Beyond Big Tech — Could This Unlock Billions For Smaller Cloud Players?', 'Nvidia Reportedly Turns To Insurers To De-Risk AI Chip Loans As Jensen Huang Pushes Beyond Big Tech — Could This Unlock Billions For Smaller Cloud Players?\\\\\\\\nNvidia has reportedly held preliminary talks with insurers about structures that would protect lenders if smaller cloud operators default on AI-')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0ed4f-a007-7c60-bbbb-f968295d8b69', 'benzinga.com', 'Why AMD Is Spending $8.2 Billion On World Labs', 'Why AMD Is Spending $8.2 Billion On World Labs\\\\\\\\nAMD is acquiring World Labs in an $8.2 billion all-stock deal to gain spatial-intelligence research and strengthen its AI hardware-software ecosystem against NVIDIA. World Labs founder Fei-Fei Li will become AMD EVP and chief scientist. AMD shares were ')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0ed51-78b2-7691-b5b9-476840891bc1', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia, AMD Lobby Trump Administration to Halt Potential Chip Export Restrictions to China: Report', 'Nvidia, AMD Lobby Trump Administration to Halt Potential Chip Export Restrictions to China: Report\\\\\\\\nNvidia and AMD are reportedly lobbying the Trump administration to prevent China-related chip export restrictions from being included in the annual defense policy bill. The article also notes China may')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0ed8f-60bc-79c3-b563-b559d3fb9845', 'benzinga.com', 'Meta Brings Its New Enterprise AI Push to the White House', 'Meta Brings Its New Enterprise AI Push to the White House\\\\\\\\nMeta launched its Meta Enterprise Platform and Muse for Small Business, expanding into enterprise AI. CEO Mark Zuckerberg is expected at a White House AI lunch with President Trump and other tech leaders. Meta hired MongoDB CEO CJ Desai to ru')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0ed9a-cc49-7e32-8038-4c6d67ad41e7', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Just Put $150 Billion Behind Its Stock. Is It Cheap Enough?', \\\\\\\"Nvidia Just Put $150 Billion Behind Its Stock. Is It Cheap Enough?\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA's board approved an additional $150 billion share repurchase authorization, bringing total remaining authorization to $235 billion through fiscal 2028. The article frames the buyback as a capital-allocation event and discusses\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0edd6-5430-7ba3-b78a-d2b912818453', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Stock Buyback Impresses Market Experts: ‘Very Much Like This Move’', \\\\\\\"Nvidia Stock Buyback Impresses Market Experts: ‘Very Much Like This Move’\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA's board authorized a record $150 billion increase to its existing share buyback, bringing total remaining authorization to $235 billion, to be executed through fiscal 2028. Shares rose 0.79% to $230.67 on the news, and \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0ede9-862a-7012-9e10-b5b5b1adb1f7', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Oil Near $100 Should Lift Energy. Instead XLE ETF Is Falling — Here's Why\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Oil Near $100 Should Lift Energy. Instead XLE ETF Is Falling — Here's Why\\\\\\\\nEnergy ETF XLE fell 1.59% even as Brent crude traded above $100, while tech ETF XLK gained ~1%. The divergence is attributed to Brent's ~2% pullback on recovering Middle Eastern supply and profit-taking, plus XLE's heavy conce\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0ee04-4519-7ad2-8c47-0e686187b9e7', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"What's Going On With Nebius Group Stock Tuesday?\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"What's Going On With Nebius Group Stock Tuesday?\\\\\\\\nNebius Group (NBIS) shares rose ~4.4% Tuesday after the company reportedly raised GPU cloud prices by roughly 20% starting Oct. 1, covering NVIDIA H100, H200, B200, and B300 GPU models. The article also notes analyst upgrades and technical momentum.\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0eee9-7812-7290-bd73-ec5f80147a9c', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Reverses After $150B Buyback News, But This NVDA-Tied ETF Is Still the Market’s Most Traded', 'Nvidia Reverses After $150B Buyback News, But This NVDA-Tied ETF Is Still the Market’s Most Traded\\\\\\\\nNvidia announced an additional $150 billion buyback authorization, lifting total remaining authorization to $235 billion; NVDA rose 1.68% Monday to $228.86 before reversing Tuesday on rising Treasury y')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0f015-ae34-7d23-95da-865ed2a82145', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Mark Zuckerberg Labels It 'Significant Positive Step,' Musk Nods Yes as Trump Inks New AI Safety Deal With Top CEOs\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Mark Zuckerberg Labels It 'Significant Positive Step,' Musk Nods Yes as Trump Inks New AI Safety Deal With Top CEOs\\\\\\\\nPresident Trump and leaders of major AI companies signed a voluntary White House accord on frontier AI safety, requiring independent audits, internal controls, and board-level oversigh\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0f1e5-229b-73a3-84e4-ce6b2bbca3f8', 'benzinga.com', 'Trump Rejects Deeper AI Cooperation With China, Says It Could Mean Giving Away ‘Lot Of Secrets’ — ‘Whoever Wins Super Intelligence Wins’', 'Trump Rejects Deeper AI Cooperation With China, Says It Could Mean Giving Away ‘Lot Of Secrets’ — ‘Whoever Wins Super Intelligence Wins’\\\\\\\\nPresident Trump rejected deeper U.S.-China AI cooperation, warning it could give away secrets, while the two countries maintain a risk dialogue. He also backed a v')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a0f1f8-e771-70b0-99da-e4d07b5e62f8', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Dan Ives Calls Physical AI Nvidia’s 'Holy Grail' — This ETF Is Already in the Trade\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Dan Ives Calls Physical AI Nvidia’s 'Holy Grail' — This ETF Is Already in the Trade\\\\\\\\nNvidia announced a record $150 billion increase to its share repurchase authorization, bringing remaining authorization to $235 billion through fiscal 2028. The article also highlights Nvidia's physical AI opportunit\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a135f3-50b9-7043-8a7d-d02cfefb1510', 'benzinga.com', 'Cerebras Stock Braces for 19.4 Million-Share Unlock After Record Low', 'Cerebras Stock Braces for 19.4 Million-Share Unlock After Record Low\\\\\\\\nCerebras Systems faces a scheduled lock-up expiry on Wednesday that will make up to 19.4 million additional shares eligible for sale, equal to roughly 8% of shares outstanding. The stock recently closed at a record low of $146.62 a')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a135fc-3d2a-7ba0-a7f6-7f2511cdd19e', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"'Nvidia Acquires A Stake In Doctolib; No Terms Disclosed; Doctolib Was Valued At €3.6 Billion Last April. NVIDIA Will Not Sit On Doctolib's Board Of Directors' - Le Figaro\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"'Nvidia Acquires A Stake In Doctolib; No Terms Disclosed; Doctolib Was Valued At €3.6 Billion Last April. NVIDIA Will Not Sit On Doctolib's Board Of Directors' - Le Figaro\\\\\\\\nNvidia has acquired a stake in French healthcare technology company Doctolib, with no financial terms disclosed. Doctolib was va\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a13a1c-3e1a-7c42-a25a-83560ea8b96d', 'benzinga.com', 'Danaher Brings NVIDIA AI Into Scientific Instruments in Push for Faster Discoveries', \\\\\\\"Danaher Brings NVIDIA AI Into Scientific Instruments in Push for Faster Discoveries\\\\\\\\nDanaher announced an AI collaboration with NVIDIA focused on autonomous science, combining Danaher's scientific instruments and lab software with NVIDIA's accelerated computing and AI capabilities. DHR shares rose 0.\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a13a74-e2e9-7471-832e-7b520f3d0a9a', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"CoreWeave Eyes 'Unlimited' Insurance Capital to Fuel AI Expansion as Debt Needs Grow, Co-Founder Says ‘You Have to Be Huge’\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"CoreWeave Eyes 'Unlimited' Insurance Capital to Fuel AI Expansion as Debt Needs Grow, Co-Founder Says ‘You Have to Be Huge’\\\\\\\\nCoreWeave co-founder Brannin McBee said the company is pursuing insurance-industry capital and evaluating additional delayed-draw term loans to fund AI data-center expansion, a\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a13a86-5964-7233-be17-7ef5bf1ab98b', 'benzinga.com', 'Honeywell Technologies Rolls Out AI And Simulation Platform Forge Cognition Developed With Nvidia, Dell', 'Honeywell Technologies Rolls Out AI And Simulation Platform Forge Cognition Developed With Nvidia, Dell\\\\\\\\nHoneywell Technologies introduced Forge Cognition, a self-contained agentic AI and simulation platform for facility operations, developed with technology from NVIDIA and Dell Technologies.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a13b1e-0e9e-7ba0-bec4-19dc3bb0350b', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is Super Micro Computer Stock Falling on Wednesday?', 'Why Is Super Micro Computer Stock Falling on Wednesday?\\\\\\\\nSuper Micro Computer shares fell 5.38% to $36.97 on Wednesday as a contractor linked to the company pleaded guilty in a U.S. export-control case involving Nvidia AI servers allegedly diverted to China in a $2.5 billion scheme. Super Micro said ')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a13b63-7ab1-7202-825e-1ca5173cc842', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Michael Dell Warns Memory Shortage Could Be a 'Four-Year Problem'\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Michael Dell Warns Memory Shortage Could Be a 'Four-Year Problem'\\\\\\\\nDell CEO Michael Dell warned that memory and semiconductor supply constraints could persist for four years as AI demand outpaces manufacturing capacity, with new fabs not arriving until 2029-2030. Barclays downgraded Dell to Equal-Wei\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a13b86-ee99-7543-bbaa-d44f4ae249c8', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is Dell Technologies Stock Sinking Wednesday?', 'Why Is Dell Technologies Stock Sinking Wednesday?\\\\\\\\nDell Technologies shares fell 11.59% to $506.14 after Barclays downgraded DELL from Overweight to Equal-Weight and cut its price forecast to $574 from $603, citing stretched valuation and delayed AI-driven enterprise spending. CEO Michael Dell separa')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a13b89-c214-7360-99ad-097d73a40f61', 'benzinga.com', 'ASML Says AI Boom Is Boosting Pricing Power as Chipmakers Agree to Pay More', 'ASML Says AI Boom Is Boosting Pricing Power as Chipmakers Agree to Pay More\\\\\\\\nASML confirmed it concluded negotiations with customers for higher prices on its most critical chipmaking equipment, with revenue and margin benefits expected to begin in 2027 and fully arrive in 2028. The company cited AI-d')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a13fe4-3ba3-7b13-a40c-edde4ab03cdb', 'benzinga.com', 'Ericsson Plans Price Hikes As AI Boom Drives Up Equipment Costs', 'Ericsson Plans Price Hikes As AI Boom Drives Up Equipment Costs\\\\\\\\nEricsson reported third-quarter revenue of 59.5 billion kronor and earnings of 18 cents per share, beating estimates of $5.79 billion in revenue and 14 cents per share. Shares rose as much as 11% in Stockholm; management warned rising e')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a1401e-6f73-7333-8b7d-b98713013b0b', 'benzinga.com', 'Hyperliquid Looks Beyond Bitcoin to Nvidia and Oil: Can PURR Benefit?', \\\\\\\"Hyperliquid Looks Beyond Bitcoin to Nvidia and Oil: Can PURR Benefit?\\\\\\\\nHyperliquid CEO Jeff Yan described the platform's expansion to Nvidia and crude-oil perpetual futures and its market-listing mechanism, which requires deployers to stake 500,000 HYPE. The article also discusses oracle safeguards a\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a1404c-0b4c-7bd2-8dd7-25b11473fb28', 'benzinga.com', 'Why Is SMCI Stock Falling on Thursday?', 'Why Is SMCI Stock Falling on Thursday?\\\\\\\\nA contractor linked to Super Micro pleaded guilty last Thursday to conspiring to violate U.S. export controls, smuggling, defrauding the government, and obstructing justice in a case involving an alleged $2.5 billion scheme to export servers containing Nvidia c')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a14084-d6e8-7720-8c1e-816113184003', 'benzinga.com', 'Adobe And Nvidia Expand Partnership To Optimize Photoshop, Premiere, Substance 3D, Frame.io And Brand Concierge With Faster AI-Powered Creation, Production And Personalization', 'Adobe And Nvidia Expand Partnership To Optimize Photoshop, Premiere, Substance 3D, Frame.io And Brand Concierge With Faster AI-Powered Creation, Production And Personalization\\\\\\\\nAdobe and NVIDIA expanded their partnership to optimize Adobe creative applications, including Photoshop, Premiere and Subst')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a140da-f70d-7a20-9e0e-fd0196f6ad3e', 'benzinga.com', 'AI Stocks Plunge, but Jensen Huang Says Nvidia Gets New Chip Orders Almost Daily', 'AI Stocks Plunge, but Jensen Huang Says Nvidia Gets New Chip Orders Almost Daily\\\\\\\\nNvidia CEO Jensen Huang said customer orders for AI chips continue to exceed available supply, with new orders arriving almost weekly and daily. He cited electricity, data-center, and component constraints on supply exp')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a140ec-b901-7932-8d7c-b40caac13fab', 'benzinga.com', 'CoreWeave Stock Snaps Back as Nvidia CEO Signals Support', 'CoreWeave Stock Snaps Back as Nvidia CEO Signals Support\\\\\\\\nCoreWeave shares rebounded after Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang publicly expressed support, following a 15% drop the prior day. The rebound occurred alongside worsening credit signals: its 2031 bond yield rose to 15.78% and five-year CDS spreads brie')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a1412c-1c0f-7770-a882-5db9b802feff', 'benzinga.com', 'CoreWeave’s Bonds Hit 15% Yield: This Analyst Still Sees 105% Upside For The Stock', 'CoreWeave’s Bonds Hit 15% Yield: This Analyst Still Sees 105% Upside For The Stock\\\\\\\\nCoreWeave shares fell about 16% as yields on its 2031 and 2032 bonds rose close to 15%; its 2032 bond yield exceeded 15.4% and its 2031 bond yield exceeded 15.3%. Bank of America reiterated its Buy rating and $140 tar')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a14411-2fbc-7cc1-8f2d-ff5fbbc10305', 'benzinga.com', 'Taiwan Semiconductor Holds the Cards As NVIDIA, Apple and AMD Battle for Limited AI Chip Capacity', 'Taiwan Semiconductor Holds the Cards As NVIDIA, Apple and AMD Battle for Limited AI Chip Capacity\\\\\\\\nTaiwan Semiconductor reported Q3 revenue of $46.7 billion, up 16.2% sequentially and above the high end of guidance. AI-related demand and competition for wafer and advanced-packaging capacity remain st')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a1443d-5c99-76e3-a3a6-c9f242ae0c5a', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"CoreWeave Stock Gets Hammered by Debt Fears, Analyst Says There's More to the Story\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"CoreWeave Stock Gets Hammered by Debt Fears, Analyst Says There's More to the Story\\\\\\\\nCoreWeave shares sold off as yields on its 2031 and 2032 bonds rose above 15%, with its 2032 bond yielding more than 15.4% and trading near 78 cents on the dollar. Analysts discussed financing risks and growth foreca\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a1449b-f96b-7070-b1fb-93909948c3e4', 'benzinga.com', 'Nvidia Announces RTX Spark AI Laptops Available Today From ASUS, Dell, HP, Lenovo, Microsoft, And MSI', 'Nvidia Announces RTX Spark AI Laptops Available Today From ASUS, Dell, HP, Lenovo, Microsoft, And MSI\\\\\\\\nNvidia announced RTX Spark AI laptops are available today from ASUS, Dell, HP, Lenovo, Microsoft, and MSI.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a1460b-73ab-7910-a82f-e8aaf109ccd5', 'benzinga.com', 'Super Micro Finally Names a CFO, Nearly Two Years After an Accounting Review Prompted the Search', 'Super Micro Finally Names a CFO, Nearly Two Years After an Accounting Review Prompted the Search\\\\\\\\nSuper Micro appointed former Western Digital CFO Mark Long as its CFO, effective immediately, replacing David Weigand. The appointment follows a prolonged search prompted by accounting and governance scr')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a14771-019a-7530-b45b-f6bda58d95ea', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"The Moment Jensen Huang Realized Nvidia 'Won't Have to Die' Came After a Call From This CEO: 'For the Whole Time, 30 Years…'\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"The Moment Jensen Huang Realized Nvidia 'Won't Have to Die' Came After a Call From This CEO: 'For the Whole Time, 30 Years…'\\\\\\\\nTSMC reported third-quarter revenue of $46.72 billion, up 41.2% year over year and 16.2% sequentially, beating analyst estimates of $45.62 billion. Gross margin was 66.4%.\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a14eab-e077-79e3-a6a9-6fc6f4643e85', 'benzinga.com', 'iPhone Duo Preorders, AAPL Crosses $5 Trillion and More: This Week in Appleverse', 'iPhone Duo Preorders, AAPL Crosses $5 Trillion and More: This Week in Appleverse\\\\\\\\nReports say Apple’s iPhone Duo sold out within minutes of preorders opening, and Apple shares climbed more than 2% in premarket trading Friday. The article also reports Apple’s market capitalization first closed above $')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a152e1-985a-7b80-b7b7-7193f8deba5a', 'benzinga.com', 'Santander Agrees Three-Year Collaboration Framework With Nvidia, Marking New AI Milestone And Building Capabilities On Nvidia AI Infrastructure', 'Santander Agrees Three-Year Collaboration Framework With Nvidia, Marking New AI Milestone And Building Capabilities On Nvidia AI Infrastructure\\\\\\\\nThe headline reports that Santander agreed to a three-year collaboration framework with Nvidia. The available article text provides no details on the framew')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a152ff-6ca6-73b3-b4b8-e5aa02712da6', 'benzinga.com', 'Samsung Turns to Rival TSMC for Nvidia’s Next-Generation Memory—Micron, SK Hynix Face Same Request: Report', \\\\\\\"Samsung Turns to Rival TSMC for Nvidia’s Next-Generation Memory—Micron, SK Hynix Face Same Request: Report\\\\\\\\nA report citing industry sources says Samsung accepted Nvidia's request to use TSMC's 3-nanometer process for the base die in Nvidia's custom NVHBM memory. This reported supplier/process arrang\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a153b1-c4fb-7dd3-9f2c-ba8556416f4c', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"AI Boom Hits a Power Wall: Microsoft Walks Away From Nscale's UK Data Center Deal\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"AI Boom Hits a Power Wall: Microsoft Walks Away From Nscale's UK Data Center Deal\\\\\\\\nMicrosoft withdrew from Nscale’s planned 50-megawatt data center project in Loughton, Essex, amid uncertainty about electricity supply; Reuters, citing the Telegraph, reported that grid power was not expected until the\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a155c5-f873-7dc2-864b-26af2754393f', 'benzinga.com', 'Amazon Just Found a Way Around Nvidia’s Biggest Moat', 'Amazon Just Found a Way Around Nvidia’s Biggest Moat\\\\\\\\nAmazon introduced TorchNeuron, an open-source tool that lets developers run PyTorch-based AI code on Trainium chips with minimal modifications. The release is intended to lower switching friction against Nvidia’s CUDA ecosystem; broader adoption a')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a15834-2f08-7b80-84ed-c78b73c7b611', 'benzinga.com', 'Big Short Investor Flags Major Vulnerability for Nvidia — 5 Customers Account for 70% of Receivables: ‘Tremendous Amount of Concentration Risk’', 'Big Short Investor Flags Major Vulnerability for Nvidia — 5 Customers Account for 70% of Receivables: ‘Tremendous Amount of Concentration Risk’\\\\\\\\nNvidia’s recent Form 10-Q reported that five unnamed direct customers represented 70% of accounts receivable. Steve Eisman cited this disclosed concentratio')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a158b7-06be-71c1-9a14-88f0a2bc47cb', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"'ByteDance, Alibaba, Tencent Place Over $35 Billion Worth of Nvidia Chip Orders' - Reuters Exclusive\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"'ByteDance, Alibaba, Tencent Place Over $35 Billion Worth of Nvidia Chip Orders' - Reuters Exclusive\\\\\\\\nReuters-reported exclusive says ByteDance, Alibaba, and Tencent ordered more than 3 million Nvidia RTX PRO 5500 workstation GPUs, worth over $35 billion; the chips reportedly comply with U.S. export \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a15904-0afd-7b43-b9d3-b4bb3186b510', 'benzinga.com', 'ByteDance, Alibaba, Tencent Place Massive $35 Billion NVIDIA Order', 'ByteDance, Alibaba, Tencent Place Massive $35 Billion NVIDIA Order\\\\\\\\nThe provider summary reports that NVIDIA received more than $35 billion in AI chip orders from ByteDance, Alibaba, and Tencent. The article body is unavailable, so order status and details cannot be independently assessed.')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a15c18-8b68-7f43-8ce1-994694946af2', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Nvidia Stock Pops After Hours As Elon Musk Says SpaceX Is Adding 200,000 Chips a Month — Daniel Newman Says NVDA Is 'Ripping'\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Nvidia Stock Pops After Hours As Elon Musk Says SpaceX Is Adding 200,000 Chips a Month — Daniel Newman Says NVDA Is 'Ripping'\\\\\\\\nSpaceX CEO Elon Musk said the company is tracking to bring roughly 200,000 Nvidia GB300 GPUs online monthly for the rest of the year. Nvidia shares rose 2.09% in extended tra\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a15cab-ca25-7fe2-bc2f-dbcd33c01d89', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"SpaceX Can't Find Spare Nvidia, Google or Amazon Chips Despite Billions to Spend, Strategist Terms It 'Pretty Insane'\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"SpaceX Can't Find Spare Nvidia, Google or Amazon Chips Despite Billions to Spend, Strategist Terms It 'Pretty Insane'\\\\\\\\nSpaceX reported third-quarter revenue of $14.58 billion versus $12.74 billion expected and earnings of $0.35 per share versus $0.12 expected. Revenue rose 161% year over year, includ\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a15e41-8387-76d3-8f0f-0f759fccfc35', 'benzinga.com', 'Cadence Announces Availability Of AI Data Center In Munich, Integrating Cadence OnCloud, Nvidia Vera And Grace CPU Systems', 'Cadence Announces Availability Of AI Data Center In Munich, Integrating Cadence OnCloud, Nvidia Vera And Grace CPU Systems\\\\\\\\nCadence announced that its sovereign AI data center in Munich is available, integrating Cadence OnCloud and digital-twin technology with NVIDIA Vera and Grace CPU systems. The a')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a15e5c-2f75-71e2-bcde-143adb3e1dff', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"NVDA, CRWV, NBIS and Crypto Miners Surge After Elon Musk Says Cloud Providers 'Don't Have Any' AI Compute\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"NVDA, CRWV, NBIS and Crypto Miners Surge After Elon Musk Says Cloud Providers 'Don't Have Any' AI Compute\\\\\\\\nAfter Elon Musk said during SpaceX’s third-quarter earnings call that cloud providers had no AI compute capacity available to rent, related stocks rose in pre-market trading. NVDA gained 2.17%, \\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a15fbb-d1c9-7101-b73c-0af5aab9acd5', 'benzinga.com', \\\\\\\"Amazon's Nvidia Chips Are Sitting in Warehouses Without Power as AI Spending Soars, Business Insider Reports\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Amazon's Nvidia Chips Are Sitting in Warehouses Without Power as AI Spending Soars, Business Insider Reports\\\\\\\\nAmazon is buying billions of dollars in Nvidia AI hardware, while some new server racks are reportedly waiting in warehouses for power.\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a1632b-6b09-7f50-8ac4-a2fa6a6699d2', 'marketscreener.com', 'NVIDIA and Tesla to Invest $2.8 Billion in Samsung Electro-Mechanics', 'NVIDIA and Tesla to Invest $2.8 Billion in Samsung Electro-Mechanics\\\\\\\\n[provider summary, not the article]\\\\\\\\nNvidia and Tesla reportedly plan a combined investment of 3.7 trillion South Korean won ($2.80 billion) in Samsung Electro-Mechanics to expand advanced semiconductor substrate production. The inv')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a16362-4700-7a82-829c-7ebd0a2262ba', 'tradingview.com', 'LG Innotek Partners with NVIDIA for HSB-Enabled Sensing Solutions', 'LG Innotek said it is collaborating with NVIDIA to build HSB-enabled sensing solutions, unveiling a 3MP camera module and Multi-modal Vision System at GTC Berlin, with plans to expand into humanoid robot components and showcase more at CES and GTC next year.\\\\\\\\nLinks LG Innotek to NVIDIA’s physical AI ')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a163d0-31d0-7421-8e06-4081a45c69ea', 'markets.businessinsider.com', 'Zadara Achieves NVIDIA AI Cloud Ready Validation', 'Oct. 22, 2026, 08:02 AM\\\\\\\\nIrvine, Calif., Oct. 22, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Zadara , a leading provider of sovereign AI cloud infrastructure, today announced it has achieved NVIDIA AI Cloud Ready ISV Initiative validated partner status, part of the NVIDIA Cloud Partner (NCP) program. Zadara will mark ')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a16422-8522-7fc1-8724-874e96196cc4', 'newswire.ca', 'Rockwell Automation Adds Support for NVIDIA Nemotron Models', \\\\\\\"Rockwell Automation, Inc.\\\\\\\\nManufacturers gain additional deployment flexibility for industrial AI orchestration through support for NVIDIA Nemotron models\\\\\\\\nMILWAUKEE , Oct. 22, 2026 /CNW/ -- Rockwell Automation, Inc. (NYSE: ROK), the world's largest company dedicated to industrial automation and digit\\\\\\\")\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a16851-902e-7540-b254-7fcf3e9992b4', 'datacentremagazine.com', 'Vertiv and NVIDIA Launch New AI Factory Deployment Approach', 'GTC: How Vertiv and NVIDIA Halve AI Factory Deployment Time\\\\\\\\nBy Saffron Humphreys\\\\\\\\nVertiv and NVIDIA have launched a new AI factory deployment approach at NVIDIA GTC Berlin.\\\\\\\\nThe model cuts infrastructure deployment time from approximately 90 days to 45 days, up to 50% faster, by shifting more assembly')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a17327-aeda-7362-b65e-a4680d120bbd', 'technews.tw', 'Supermicro and Nokia Deploy NVIDIA Aerial RAN Computer Solutions for AI-RAN', 'Supermicro and Nokia Deploy NVIDIA Aerial RAN Computer Solutions for AI-RAN\\\\\\\\n[provider summary, not the article]\\\\\\\\nSupermicro and Nokia are deploying NVIDIA Aerial RAN Computer solutions for AI-RAN workloads at the network edge. Supermicro says its servers for NVIDIA ARC are now available; some describ')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a177c4-aed3-7d01-b3d7-63d36293229a', 'prnewswire.com', 'SWI Compute Launches to Build NVIDIA AI Factories', 'SWI Compute Emerges from Stealth to Turn Gigawatts of Power Into NVIDIA AI Factories, Starting in Europe\\\\\\\\nSINGAPORE and AMSTERDAM , Oct. 26, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- SWI Compute today emerged from stealth to build and operate NVIDIA AI factories, launching first in Europe. The global AI infrastructure co')\\\\n('truenorth:story:story_01a178bc-293b-7301-baac-5776ecf91e91', 'morningstar.com', 'NVIDIA Expresses Interest in Meta Platforms Equity Offering', 'Nvidia, AMD and Broadcom could buy Meta shares as part of $35 billion stock offering\\\\\\\\nBy Britney Nguyen\\\\\\\\nMeta is looking to raise a total of $95 billion through stock-related deals that stretch into early next year\\\\\\\\nMeta announced a $35 billion equity offering on Monday.\\\\\\\\nMeta Platforms intends to raise')\\\\n('extra:b23f73a08a535993119430f5', 'cnbc.com', 'CNBC | VERSANT Press Room', 'CNBC | VERSANT Press Room\\\\\\\\nBrands\\\\\\\\nVersant Media\\\\\\\\nMS NOW\\\\\\\\nUSA Network\\\\\\\\nSYFY\\\\\\\\nRotten Tomatoes\\\\\\\\nUSA Sports\\\\\\\\nOxygen True Crime\\\\\\\\nE!\\\\\\\\nFandango\\\\\\\\nFreeTV\\\\\\\\nGolf Channel\\\\\\\\nGolfPass\\\\\\\\nGolfNow\\\\\\\\nFull Swing\\\\\\\\nLogin\\\\\\\\nRegister\\\\\\\\nLOADING...\\\\\\\\nPress Releases Photos Contacts\\\\\\\\nMore\\\\\\\\nPress Releases Photos Contacts\\\\\\\\nLOADING...\\\\\\\\nCNBC Transcript: Nvi')\\\\n('extra:1d912c1e5fc3a34f3c5bc52a', 'cnbc.com', 'CNBC | VERSANT Press Room', 'Brands\\\\\\\\nVersant Media\\\\\\\\nMS NOW\\\\\\\\nUSA Network\\\\\\\\nSYFY\\\\\\\\nRotten Tomatoes\\\\\\\\nUSA Sports\\\\\\\\nOxygen True Crime\\\\\\\\nE!\\\\\\\\nFandango\\\\\\\\nFreeTV\\\\\\\\nGolf Channel\\\\\\\\nGolfPass\\\\\\\\nGolfNow\\\\\\\\nFull Swing\\\\\\\\nLogin\\\\\\\\nRegister\\\\\\\\nLOADING...\\\\\\\\nPress Releases Photos Contacts\\\\\\\\nMore\\\\\\\\nPress Releases Photos Contacts\\\\\\\\nLOADING...\\\\\\\\nCNBC | VERSANT Press Room\\\\\\\\nCNBC Excerpts: Nvidi')\\\\n('extra:ea981681c9e20cb5e31f7126', 'blogs.nvidia.com', 'NVIDIA to Acquire Hugging Face | NVIDIA Blog', 'I’m excited to announce that NVIDIA has agreed to acquire Hugging Face for $12,930,300,000. Together, we will scale Hugging Face’s platform, strengthen its infrastructure and expand access to AI for developers and institutions worldwide.\\\\\\\\nOver the past decade, Clem, Julien, Thomas and the team at Hug')\\\\n('extra:ed34d148788e5d6f51faf5b5', 'blogs.nvidia.com', '‘Now We Can Know Everything and Do Anything,’ Jensen Huang Says at Dreamforce | NVIDIA Blog', 'At Dreamforce, Salesforce and NVIDIA announced Koa, a CRM reasoning model for Agentforce, post-trained from Nemotron on 27 years of Salesforce CRM intelligence — and running entirely within Salesforce’s own infrastructure.\\\\\\\\nThat was the message NVIDIA founder and CEO Jensen Huang brought to Salesforc')\\\\n('extra:e85b9e2ad448ed75ecf99831', 'blogs.nvidia.com', 'NVIDIA, Microsoft Kick Off a New Beginning for Windows PCs with RTX Spark and AI Agents | NVIDIA Blog', 'RTX Spark preorders open today alongside a preview of NVIDIA DGX Station for Windows, the first deskside AI supercomputer built for the Windows enterprise desktop.\\\\\\\\nAt a Microsoft event in San Francisco on Wednesday, NVIDIA founder and CEO Jensen Huang and Microsoft CEO Satya Nadella outlined how NVI')\\\\n('extra:494a9fa3bb713759384d4568', 'blogs.nvidia.com', 'Germany Wants to Lead the World in Industrial AI: How NVIDIA Will Help | NVIDIA Blog', 'German Chancellor Friedrich Merz and NVIDIA founder and CEO Jensen Huang discussed how to merge traditional German engineering with state-of-the-art AI.\\\\\\\\nIn the cavernous hall of Kraftwerk, a former power station in Berlin, German Chancellor Friedrich Merz and NVIDIA founder and CEO Jensen Huang sat ')\\\\n('extra:99d146f2162c85d645ba0fbd', 'investor.nvidia.com', 'NVIDIA Corporation - NVIDIA and MediaTek Deepen Long-Standing Partnership to Build AI Edge to Cloud Computing Platforms', 'NVIDIA Corporation - NVIDIA and MediaTek Deepen Long-Standing Partnership to Build AI Edge to Cloud Computing Platforms\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA and MediaTek Deepen Long-Standing Partnership to Build AI Edge to Cloud Computing Platforms\\\\\\\\nAugust 31, 2026\\\\\\\\nCompanies Expand Collaboration Across Multigenerational Cloud AI ')\\\\n('extra:2799d8731e89b90c9bd3f108', 'investor.nvidia.com', 'NVIDIA Corporation - NVIDIA Announces Financial Results for Second Quarter Fiscal 2027', 'NVIDIA Corporation - NVIDIA Announces Financial Results for Second Quarter Fiscal 2027\\\\\\\\nNVIDIA Announces Financial Results for Second Quarter Fiscal 2027\\\\\\\\nAugust 26, 2026\\\\\\\\nRevenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% from a year ago\\\\\\\\nData Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% from a year ago\\\\\\\\nSANTA CLARA, Calif.')\\\\nv5 NVIDIA expects total revenue to grow approximately 70% in FY2028, with supply constraining growth. We expect to grow revenue by approximately 70% in fiscal 2028. This is a supply-constrained outlook.\\\\nv8 NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $89 billion in Q2 FY2027, up 18% sequentially. Q2 data center revenue increased 18% quarter-over-quarter to $89 billion with strong contributions from both sub segments hyperscale and ACIE, which includes our NeoCloud, industrial and enterprise customers.\\\\nv8 NVIDIA hyperscale revenue was $49 billion in Q2 FY2027, up 13% sequentially, driven by Blackwell. Hyperscale revenue of $49 billion grew 13% sequentially, driven by sustained strength in Blackwell\\\\nv6,v7 NVIDIA said cloud-industry backlog exceeds $2 trillion and top-five hyperscaler CapEx is expected to approach $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027. With cloud industry backlog now greater than $2 trillion, CapEx by the top 5 hyperscalers is expected to reach nearly $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\\\nv3,v4,v5,v8 AWS plans to deploy an additional 2 million NVIDIA GPUs, along with Vera CPUs, from Q2 FY2027 through Q2 FY2029. AWS is deploying an additional 2 million GPUs starting this quarter through the second quarter of fiscal '29 along with Vera, CPUs, some integrated with Rubin, other standalone.\\\\nv4,v5,v8 AWS plans to serve NVIDIA’s Nemotron open-model family on Amazon Bedrock and SageMaker. AWS will serve NVIDIA Nemotron family of open models on Amazon Bedrock and SageMaker.\\\\nv8 e2295 Morningstar cites NVIDIA Data Center revenue of $3 billion in FY2020 and $194 billion in FY2026, and estimates $361 billion in FY2027, up 86% year over year. Nvidia’s DC business has achieved exponential growth already, rising from $3 billion in fiscal 2020 to $194 billion in fiscal 2026, and we estimate it will be $361 billion in fiscal 2027, representing 86% annual growth. {'input_id': 'gnews:7ce47efd62fa17b9aa29e258', 'title': 'Going Into Earnings, Is Nvidia Stock a Buy, a Sell, or Fairly Valued?', 'source_uri': 'https://www.morningstar.com/stocks/going-into-earnings-is-nvidia-stock-buy-sell-or-fairly-valued-8'}\\\\nv8 e5309 NVIDIA reported $164 billion of Data Center segment revenue in the first six months of FY2027. The company has generated $164 billion in revenue from its data center segment in the first six months of fiscal 2027. {'input_id': 'gnews:ad94c78d09fe41fc3f29bbca', 'title': 'Global AI Infrastructure Spending Will Hit $31.6 Trillion by 2050. This Is the Stock That Could Benefit the Most', 'source_uri': 'https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/09/18/global-ai-infrastructure-spending-will-hit-usd31-6-trillion-by-2050-this-is-the-stock-that-could-benefit-the-most/'}\\\\nv4,v8 e5384 Nscale signed a six-year agreement in August 2026 for Anthropic to lease capacity at Nscale’s West Virginia data center, valued at up to $45 billion. Last month, Nscale signed a landmark agreement with Anthropic to lease capacity at its flagship data center in West Virginia. The six-year deal is valued at up to $45 billion. {'input_id': 'gnews:a7ac49717831582bc5bb87db', 'title': 'NVIDIA-backed \\\\\\\"British Oracle\\\\\\\" Races for U.S. IPO with $35 Billion Valuation Target', 'source_uri': 'https://www.moomoo.com/news/post/76493332/nvidia-backed-british-oracle-races-for-us-ipo-with-35'}\\\\nv4,v8 e5385 Nscale estimated that its West Virginia data center, including a 2 GW gas-fired power plant, would cost about $70 billion and begin phased commissioning by the end of 2027. Nscale estimates that this data center, currently under construction, is expected to begin phased commissioning by the end of next year, with a total cost of approximately US$70 billion, including a 2 GW natural-gas-fired power plant to support its operations. {'input_id': 'gnews:a7ac49717831582bc5bb87db', 'title': 'NVIDIA-backed \\\\\\\"British Oracle\\\\\\\" Races for U.S. IPO with $35 Billion Valuation Target', 'source_uri': 'https://www.moomoo.com/news/post/76493332/nvidia-backed-british-oracle-races-for-us-ipo-with-35'}\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:51:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_26\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\\\\nimport sqlite3,collections,re,sys,json\\\\nroot=Path(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"poc/data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\nbase=root/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"comparison-2026-11-17\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\ndef conn(p):\\\\n c=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",uri=True)\\\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\\\n return c\\\\ninputs=[(f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"old-{i}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",base/f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"run/old-{i}/prod/views.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",base/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") for i in (1,2,3)]+[(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"served\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",root/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",root/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")]\\\\nfor name,p,ip in inputs:\\\\n c=conn(p); rows=list(c.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select e.evidence_id,one_line,quote,group_concat(view_id) from evidence e join evidence_links using(evidence_id) group by e.evidence_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))\\\\n pat=r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"(implying|implies|annualiz|annualis|implied|on track|at that (rate|pace)|run.rate|extrapolat|would (yield|put|imply)|equates to|equivalent to)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\n hits=[(id,v,l,q) for id,l,q,v in rows if re.search(pat,l or '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.I) and not re.search(pat,q or '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.I)]\\\\n print(name,len(hits))\\\\n for id,v,l,q in hits[:8]: print(id,v,l,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",q)\\\\n'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:52:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_26\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\\\\nimport sqlite3,collections,re,sys,json\\\\nroot=Path(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"poc/data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\nbase=root/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"comparison-2026-11-17\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\ndef conn(p):\\\\n c=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",uri=True)\\\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\\\n return c\\\\ninputs=[(f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"old-{i}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",base/f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"run/old-{i}/prod/views.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",base/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") for i in (1,2,3)]+[(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"served\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",root/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",root/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")]\\\\nfor name,p,ip in inputs:\\\\n c=conn(p); rows=list(c.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select e.evidence_id,one_line,quote,group_concat(view_id) from evidence e join evidence_links using(evidence_id) group by e.evidence_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))\\\\n pat=r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"(implying|implies|annualiz|annualis|implied|on track|at that (rate|pace)|run.rate|extrapolat|would (yield|put|imply)|equates to|equivalent to)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\n hits=[(id,v,l,q) for id,l,q,v in rows if re.search(pat,l or '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.I) and not re.search(pat,q or '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.I)]\\\\n print(name,len(hits))\\\\n for id,v,l,q in hits[:8]: print(id,v,l,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",q)\\\\n'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"old-1 32\\\\ne1265 v4 NVIDIA guided to $91 billion in revenue for the current quarter, implying 95% year-over-year growth. | Its guidance of $91 billion in revenue for the current quarter points toward a stronger year-over-year increase of 95%.\\\\ne1706 v6,v7 Jensen Huang said recent AI spending is only the beginning, implying further substantial AI spending over the coming years. | He's looking years into the future and declaring that the recent, massive spending on AI is just the tip of the iceberg.\\\\ne2294 v4,v5 Morningstar sees upside in NVIDIA shares conditional on the company staying on track to meet its near- and medium-term revenue targets. | We still see upside in Nvidia stock as long as it remains on pace to hit its near- and medium-term revenue targets.\\\\ne2934 v4 Analysts’ consensus estimate for NVIDIA FY2027 Q2 revenue was $92.18 billion, versus $46.74 billion a year earlier, implying 97% growth. | Analysts who cover the stock are looking for a little more, with the consensus estimate coming in at $92.18 billion versus $46.74 billion a year ago – essentially sales growth of 97%.\\\\ne3161 v5 The author calculates that $425 billion of FY2027 revenue combined with 70% FY2028 growth would imply more than $700 billion of FY2028 revenue. | If Nvidia reaches $425 billion in revenue this year, that would mean over $700 billion in revenue next fiscal year and knocking on the door of $1 trillion a few years from now.\\\\ne3168 v35 thenewstack.io calculated that the reported $12.9 billion acquisition price was roughly 86 times Hugging Face’s estimated annualized revenue. | Against a $12.9 billion price tag, that’s a multiple of roughly 86.\\\\ne3301 v35 Reuters, citing The Information, reported on August 27 that NVIDIA had agreed to acquire Hugging Face for a price implying roughly 86 times sales. | On August 27, Reuters reported that Nvidia had agreed to acquire Hugging Face, citing The Information. The arithmetic is obscene at roughly 86 times sales.\\\\ne3346 v4 Nvidia guided third-quarter revenue to $105.84 billion–$110.16 billion, implying 85.7%–93.2% year-over-year growth from $57.01 billion. | For the third quarter, Nvidia expects revenue between $105.84 billion and $110.16 billion, representing year-over-year growth of 85.7% to 93.2% from the $57.01 billion reported in the same quarter last year.\\\\nold-2 19\\\\ne1464 v14 The Register, citing Orbital CEO, said orbital data centers would require Starship to reach Musk's stated $10-per-kilogram launch-cost goal, which would put the estimated cost to orbit for the AI1 at about $33,300. | For orbital datacenters to be cost-effective, Starship is going to need to get the cost per kilogram down to Elon’s stated goal of $10, Ortibal CEO told El Reg earlier this year. That would bring the cost to orbit to about $33,300\\\\ne2151 v14,v21 Daniel Sparks calculated that NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 second-quarter revenue guidance midpoint implies about $9 billion of sequential growth, or 11%, versus roughly $13.5 billion and 20% sequential growth in the first quarter. | The midpoint asks for about $9 billion of new revenue versus the first quarter, which had itself added about $13.5 billion versus the one before it. In growth terms, that's a step down to about 11% sequentially from 20%.\\\\ne2772 v14,v21 Analysts’ consensus revenue estimate is $92.18 billion, versus $46.74 billion a year earlier, implying 97% sales growth for the period being discussed. | Analysts who cover the stock are looking for a little more, with the consensus estimate coming in at $92.18 billion versus $46.74 billion a year ago – essentially sales growth of 97%.\\\\ne2870 v9 NVIDIA indicated it could satisfy around 70% of current demand, implying the company was unable to meet the remainder. | Nvidia also indicated that it can currently satisfy only around 70% of demand.\\\\ne2911 v17 NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said demand implies revenue growth above 70% for FY2028, but product supply constrains how much the company can supply. | CEO Jensen Huang said demand \\\\\\\"is much greater than 70%,\\\\\\\" but the company is constrained on the amount of product it can supply.\\\\ne2997 v34 Thenewstack.io calculated that the reported $12.9 billion acquisition price is about 86 times Hugging Face's reported annualized revenue. | Against a $12.9 billion price tag, that’s a multiple of roughly 86.\\\\ne3169 v14 NVIDIA guided third-quarter revenue to $105.84 billion–$110.16 billion, implying year-over-year growth of 85.7%–93.2% from $57.01 billion. | For the third quarter, Nvidia expects revenue between $105.84 billion and $110.16 billion, representing year-over-year growth of 85.7% to 93.2% from the $57.01 billion reported in the same quarter last year.\\\\ne3198 v34 Futurum calculated that the reported $12.9 billion acquisition price equates to 86–129 times Hugging Face’s estimated $100–150 million annual recurring revenue as of mid-2026. | Against that range, the reported $12.9 billion price works out to somewhere between 86x and 129x revenue, a multiple that only makes sense if NVIDIA were to be paying for future distribution leverage and developer mindshare rather than current financial performance.\\\\nold-3 22\\\\ne1260 v3 NVIDIA guided to revenue of $91 billion for FY2027 Q2, which the author said implied 95% year-over-year growth. | Its guidance of $91 billion in revenue for the current quarter points toward a stronger year-over-year increase of 95%.\\\\ne2334 v3 Daniel Sparks calculated that NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 second-quarter revenue guidance midpoint implied about $9 billion of sequential revenue growth, or approximately 11%, versus about $13.5 billion and 20% sequential growth in the first quarter. | The midpoint asks for about $9 billion of new revenue versus the first quarter, which had itself added about $13.5 billion versus the one before it. In growth terms, that's a step down to about 11% sequentially from 20%.\\\\ne2384 v3 NVIDIA disclosed a stake in SpaceX worth nearly $21 billion, equivalent to roughly 122.8 million shares, last week. | Just last week, Nvidia disclosed a stake of nearly $21 billion – roughly 122.8 million shares at $170.86 per share – in SpaceX, the Elon Musk-led space and AI company.\\\\ne3153 v4 NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said demand implies revenue growth greater than 70%, while product supply constrains the company. | CEO Jensen Huang said demand \\\\\\\"is much greater than 70%,\\\\\\\" but the company is constrained on the amount of product it can supply.\\\\ne3220 v3,v4 The author calculated that NVIDIA revenue of $425 billion in FY2027 would imply revenue above $700 billion in FY2028. | If Nvidia reaches $425 billion in revenue this year, that would mean over $700 billion in revenue next fiscal year\\\\ne3224 v4,v38 The author calculated that $700 billion of FY2028 revenue at a 64% operating margin would imply $448 billion in operating earnings. | Assuming Nvidia can reach $700 billion in revenue in fiscal year 2028, a 64% operating margin would equate to $448 billion in operating earnings\\\\ne3370 v4 NVIDIA’s outlook, as described by the author, implies roughly 70% revenue growth in FY2028 and is supply-constrained. | Next year's top-line growth is pegged at roughly 70%, and that is the scenario where supply runs out.\\\\ne3588 v39 The author calculated that NVIDIA's reported $12.9 billion Hugging Face acquisition price equals about 86 times Hugging Face's annualised sales. | Nvidia would therefore be paying about 86 times sales—a multiple that looks absurd if Hugging Face is treated as an ordinary software company.\\\\nserved 15\\\\ne1314 v2,v10,v21 NVIDIA said it is targeting capacity requiring 2 gigawatts of power; the report characterized the implied buildout as involving hundreds of thousands of GPUs. | Nvidia said it's targeting enough capacity to require 2 gigawatts of power, which indicates a massive buildout with hundreds of thousands of graphics processing units.\\\\ne1391 v6 The article reported average GDDR6/GDDR7 module prices up $19–$20, implying about $75 higher cost for an 8 GB graphics card and about $100 after China's 13% VAT. | Currently, the DRAM prices for GDDR6 and GDDR7 modules have risen by an average of $19-$20. This means that an 8 GB graphics card will see a price hike of around $75 US, and since China has a VAT of 13%, when you factor it all in, the price difference jumps to $100 US.\\\\ne1534 v2,v10 NVIDIA guided to $91 billion of revenue for the current quarter, implying 95% year-over-year growth. | Its guidance of $91 billion in revenue for the current quarter points toward a stronger year-over-year increase of 95%.\\\\ne1833 v2,v10 Microsoft said its AI business exceeded $37 billion in annualized revenue, up 123%, and commercial remaining performance obligations were $627 billion. | Microsoft ( NASDAQ:MSFT ) told investors on its most recent call that its “AI business surpassed $37 billion ARR, up 123%”, with commercial remaining performance obligations, its committed backlog, at $627 billion.\\\\ne3051 v2,v10,v13 Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA Q2 FY2027 revenue of about $92.1 billion and EPS of $2.09, implying 97% revenue growth and nearly doubled profits year over year. | Wall Street analysts expect Nvidia to post roughly $92.1 billion in revenue and earnings per share (EPS) of $2.09 for the second quarter. That would amount to 97% revenue growth and nearly a doubling of profits year over year.\\\\ne3519 v2 The Kobeissi Letter estimated conditionally that NVIDIA delivering its $108 billion Q3 guidance would imply roughly 1,730% revenue growth over four years. | If Nvidia delivers on its $108 billion third-quarter guidance, the company would have grown revenue by roughly 1,730% in just four years\\\\ne3587 v2,v10 The author reports analysts’ consensus revenue estimate of $92.18 billion, versus $46.74 billion a year earlier, implying 97% growth. | Analysts who cover the stock are looking for a little more, with the consensus estimate coming in at $92.18 billion versus $46.74 billion a year ago – essentially sales growth of 97%.\\\\ne3598 v2,v10 NVIDIA guided FY2027 Q3 revenue to $108 billion, implying 89% year-over-year growth. | Its Q3 outlook calls for revenue of $108 billion, representing year-over-year growth of 89%.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:53:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_27\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\\\\nimport sqlite3,collections,re,sys,json\\\\nroot=Path(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"poc/data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\nbase=root/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"comparison-2026-11-17\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\ndef conn(p):\\\\n c=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",uri=True)\\\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\\\n return c\\\\ninputs=[(f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"old-{i}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",base/f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"run/old-{i}/prod/views.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",base/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") for i in (1,2,3)]+[(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"served\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",root/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",root/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")]\\\\ndef amounts(t):\\\\n return set(re.findall(r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"(?:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$|USD'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*)([\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d,]+(?:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+)?)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?:[mbt]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b|million|billion|trillion)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",t or \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",re.I))\\\\nfor name,p,ip in inputs:\\\\n c=conn(p); i=conn(ip); out=[]\\\\n cache={}\\\\n for eid,one,q,s in c.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select evidence_id,one_line,quote,created_from_input from evidence\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"):\\\\n  if not amounts(one)-amounts(q) or not re.search(r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"expect|forecast|guidance|impli|project|estim|will|would|equiv|annualiz|annualis\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",one,re.I):continue\\\\n  if s not in cache:\\\\n   r=i.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select title,text,text_article,text_page from items where input_id=?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",(s,)).fetchone()\\\\n   cache[s]=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".join(t or \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" for t in r).replace(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\").lower() if r else \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\n  miss=[a for a in amounts(one)-amounts(q) if not re.search(r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"(?<\\\\\\\"'!['\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d.])\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"+re.escape(a.replace(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))+r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"(?\\\\\\\"'!'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",cache[s])]\\\\n  if miss: out.append((eid,miss,one,q))\\\\n print(name,len(out))\\\\n for r in out[:15]: print(*r,sep=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\n'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:54:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_27\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\\\\nimport sqlite3,collections,re,sys,json\\\\nroot=Path(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"poc/data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\nbase=root/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"comparison-2026-11-17\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\ndef conn(p):\\\\n c=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",uri=True)\\\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\\\n return c\\\\ninputs=[(f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"old-{i}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",base/f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"run/old-{i}/prod/views.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",base/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") for i in (1,2,3)]+[(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"served\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",root/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",root/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")]\\\\ndef amounts(t):\\\\n return set(re.findall(r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"(?:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$|USD'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*)([\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d,]+(?:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+)?)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?:[mbt]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b|million|billion|trillion)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",t or \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",re.I))\\\\nfor name,p,ip in inputs:\\\\n c=conn(p); i=conn(ip); out=[]\\\\n cache={}\\\\n for eid,one,q,s in c.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select evidence_id,one_line,quote,created_from_input from evidence\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"):\\\\n  if not amounts(one)-amounts(q) or not re.search(r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"expect|forecast|guidance|impli|project|estim|will|would|equiv|annualiz|annualis\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",one,re.I):continue\\\\n  if s not in cache:\\\\n   r=i.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select title,text,text_article,text_page from items where input_id=?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",(s,)).fetchone()\\\\n   cache[s]=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".join(t or \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" for t in r).replace(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\").lower() if r else \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\n  miss=[a for a in amounts(one)-amounts(q) if not re.search(r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"(?<\\\\\\\"'!['\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d.])\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"+re.escape(a.replace(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))+r\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"(?\\\\\\\"'!'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",cache[s])]\\\\n  if miss: out.append((eid,miss,one,q))\\\\n print(name,len(out))\\\\n for r in out[:15]: print(*r,sep=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\n'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"old-1 5\\\\ne724 | ['1.71'] | Precedence Research valued the global GPU market at $101.54 billion in 2025 and projected it to reach about $1.71 trillion by 2035, a 32.62% CAGR over 2026–2035. | The global graphics processing unit (GPU) market was valued at USD 101.54 billion in 2025 and is projected to grow from USD 136.06 billion in 2026 to approximately USD 1,712.56 billion by 2035, registering a CAGR of 32.62% during the forecast period from 2026 to 2035.\\\\ne1226 | ['9'] | Brookfield signed a nonbinding term sheet to provide up to $9 billion in project funding for the NAVER AI factory expansion. | Brookfield has executed a nonbinding term sheet to provide project funding of up to nine billion US dollars.\\\\ne1227 | ['9'] | NVIDIA’s planned investment in NAVER is conditional on NAVER securing at least $9 billion in binding project financing. | NVIDIA’s direct investment depends on standard closing terms, which require NAVER to finalise at least nine billion US dollars in binding project financing.\\\\ne3238 | ['40'] | NVIDIA projected stand-alone CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028. | Nvidia is leaning into that opening, projecting $20 billion in stand-alone CPU revenue this year and more than double that next year\\\\ne3296 | ['40'] | NVIDIA expected standalone CPU revenue to exceed $40 billion in FY2028, more than double its FY2027 expectation. | and more than double that the year after.\\\\nold-2 6\\\\ne1056 | ['9'] | NVIDIA’s planned NAVER investment is conditional on NAVER finalising at least US$9 billion of binding project financing. | NVIDIA’s direct investment depends on standard closing terms, which require NAVER to finalise at least nine billion US dollars in binding project financing.\\\\ne1057 | ['9'] | Brookfield executed a nonbinding term sheet to provide up to US$9 billion in project funding for the GAK Sejong expansion. | Brookfield has executed a nonbinding term sheet to provide project funding of up to nine billion US dollars.\\\\ne3073 | ['40'] | NVIDIA projected stand-alone CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028. | Nvidia is leaning into that opening, projecting $20 billion in stand-alone CPU revenue this year and more than double that next year\\\\ne3127 | ['40'] | NVIDIA expects standalone CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028. | That growth feeds Nvidia's newest business line, standalone CPUs built on its Rubin platform, which the company expects to generate $20 billion this fiscal year and more than double that the year after.\\\\ne3877 | ['3'] | NVIDIA was reported to be expected to provide roughly half of Thinking Machines Lab’s proposed $5 billion to $6 billion fundraising, or roughly $2.5 billion to $3 billion. | Nvidia is expected to provide roughly half of that capital.\\\\ne4988 | ['1.5'] | Brad Gerstner said annual AI-infrastructure capital spending could reach $1.5 trillion and would require customers to pay for the capacity. | \\\\\\\"If you're going to build a trillion and a half dollars a year in capex, somebody has to pay for it,\\\\\\\" he said.\\\\nold-3 5\\\\ne1221 | ['9'] | Brookfield executed a nonbinding term sheet to provide up to US$9 billion in project funding for the NAVER AI factory. | On the other side, Brookfield has executed a nonbinding term sheet to provide project funding of up to nine billion US dollars.\\\\ne1222 | ['9'] | NVIDIA’s planned direct investment in NAVER depends on NAVER finalising at least US$9 billion in binding project financing. | NVIDIA’s direct investment depends on standard closing terms, which require NAVER to finalise at least nine billion US dollars in binding project financing.\\\\ne3302 | ['40'] | NVIDIA projected stand-alone CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028. | Nvidia is leaning into that opening, projecting $20 billion in stand-alone CPU revenue this year and more than double that next year\\\\ne3356 | ['40'] | NVIDIA expects standalone CPU revenue to be $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028. | standalone CPUs built on its Rubin platform, which the company expects to generate $20 billion this fiscal year and more than double that the year after.\\\\ne4125 | ['3'] | The author estimates NVIDIA will provide roughly half of Thinking Machines Lab’s planned $5 billion to $6 billion funding round, or about $2.5 billion to $3 billion. | Nvidia is expected to provide roughly half of that capital.\\\\nserved 5\\\\ne1490 | ['9'] | The article says NVIDIA's planned investment is conditional on NAVER finalising at least US$9 billion in binding project financing. | NVIDIA’s direct investment depends on standard closing terms, which require NAVER to finalise at least nine billion US dollars in binding project financing.\\\\ne2114 | ['1'] | SiliconANGLE reported on 2026-08-10 that Google, Microsoft, Meta, Amazon, SpaceX, OpenAI and Anthropic had collectively spent more than $1 trillion on AI projects and infrastructure over the preceding three years, and were expected to invest more. | Collectively, these companies have spent more than a trillion dollars on AI projects and infrastructure in the last three years, and they’re expected to invest even more in future.\\\\ne2882 | ['5.0', '4.0'] | The Futurum Group estimated Helios system cost at $5.0 million–$5.5 million versus $3.5 million–$4.0 million for NVIDIA Vera Rubin; the estimate’s period is unspecified. | Helios also reportedly costs more per system than Nvidia's Vera Rubin, an estimated $5 million to $5.5 million versus $3.5 million to $4 million, according to the Futurum Group, a premium that needs to be justified by performance.\\\\ne3936 | ['40'] | NVIDIA projected $20 billion in stand-alone CPU revenue in 2026 and more than $40 billion in 2027. | Nvidia is leaning into that opening, projecting $20 billion in stand-alone CPU revenue this year and more than double that next year\\\\ne3997 | ['40'] | NVIDIA expected standalone CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028. | the company expects to generate $20 billion this fiscal year and more than double that the year after.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:61:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_31\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\\\\nimport sqlite3,collections,re,sys,json\\\\nroot=Path(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"poc/data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\nbase=root/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"comparison-2026-11-17\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\ndef conn(p):\\\\n c=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",uri=True)\\\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\\\n return c\\\\ninputs=[(f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"old-{i}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",base/f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"run/old-{i}/prod/views.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",base/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") for i in (1,2,3)]+[(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"served\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",root/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",root/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")]\\\\nfrom pprint import pprint\\\\nfor name,p,ip in inputs:\\\\n c=conn(p); i=conn(ip)\\\\n rows=c.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select e.evidence_id,one_line,quote,created_from_input,group_concat(view_id) from evidence e join evidence_links using (evidence_id) where (one_line like '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''%half%'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' and (one_line like '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''%\\\\\\\"'$2.5 billion%'\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' or one_line like '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''%\\\\\\\"'$3 billion%'\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'') and one_line like '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''%Thinking Machines%'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'') or (one_line like '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''%\\\\\\\"'$40 billion%'\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' and one_line like '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''%CPU%'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' and quote like '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''%double%'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' and quote not like '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''%40%'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'') group by e.evidence_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\").fetchall()\\\\n for eid,l,q,s,vs in rows: print(name,eid,vs,l,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''|'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',q)\\\\n if name=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''old-2'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':\\\\n  e=c.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select created_from_input from evidence where evidence_id='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''e3877'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\").fetchone()[0]; a=i.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select title,publisher,text from items where input_id=?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",(e,)).fetchone(); print(e,a[0],a[1],re.findall(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.{0,190}half of that capital.{0,85}'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',a[2],re.I))\\\\n if name=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''old-1'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':\\\\n  for x in c.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select position,label,condition,length(label) from rungs where view_id='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v8'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"):print(tuple(x))\\\\n  print(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"j865\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",dict(c.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select view_id,seq,why_changed,reference,implied_outcome from judgements where judgement_id=865\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\").fetchone()))\\\\n print(name,c.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select max(day) from days_completed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\").fetchone()[0], \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"first views tied\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",list(map(tuple,c.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select created_seq,group_concat(view_id) from views group by created_seq having count(*)>1 limit 2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))))\\\\n'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:62:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_31\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\\\\nimport sqlite3,collections,re,sys,json\\\\\n... 3192252 bytes omitted ...\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v44'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v7'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']}.items():\\\\\\\\n v,a,_=record(i)\\\\\\\\n for id in caps:\\\\\\\\n  sel=[]\\\\\\\\n  for j in v.execute('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',(id,)):\\\\\\\\n   o=j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''];r=j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''reasons'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']\\\\\\\\n   if id in ({1:['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v4'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v8'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],2:['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v14'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v9'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],3:['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v3'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v35'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']}[i]):\\\\\\\\n    if tag(o+r,r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b(residu\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\w*|back(?:ing|ed|s)? out|remainder|leav(?:es|ing)|requiring|requires|subtract\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\w*)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'') and tag(o+r,r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''Q4|fourth quarter'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\\\\\n     sel.append((j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''publication_day'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''][5:],j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],o,r))\\\\\\\\n   elif i==2 and id in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v17'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v35'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v21'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\\\\\n    if j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''publication_day'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']>='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''2026-08-26'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' and any(D(70)==x for x in figures(o+r,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''percent'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')) and any(x in figures(o+r,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'') for x in ([D(367),D(366.9)] if id=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v21'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' else [D(396),D(673)])):\\\\\\\\n      sel.append((j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''publication_day'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''][5:],j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],o,r))\\\\\\\\n  if sel:\\\\\\\\n   print('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''DRAW'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',i,id,len(sel),[(j[0],j[1]) for j in sel])\\\\\\\\n   for j in sel:print(j[0],j[1],j[2] if (i==2 and id in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v21'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v17'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v35'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')) else j[2]+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' :: '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''+ '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.join(x for x in j[3].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''. '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'') if tag(x,r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b(residu\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\w*|back(?:ing|ed|s)? out|remainder|leav(?:es|ing)|requiring|requires|subtract\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\w*)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')))\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"DRAW 1 v4 1 [('07-24', 1782)]\\\\\\\\n07-24 1782 About $425 billion: carry the Q1 actual and Q2 guidance run-rate forward, then apply the existing estimate that second-half FY2027 data-center compute revenue will be 20% above Wall Street expectations only to that portion of revenue. This remains below the $431.2 billion rung-1 threshold. :: Carrying forward the evidence-implied estimate of about $425 billion—based on Q1 actual revenue and Q2 guidance carried forward, with the existing SemiAnalysis uplift applied only to second-half FY2027 data-center compute—leaves the forecast about $6.2 billion short of rung 1’s $431.2 billion boundary\\\\\\\\nDRAW 1 v8 9 [('08-26', 5093), ('08-27', 5304), ('08-31', 6166), ('09-02', 6413), ('09-03', 6604), ('09-04', 6817), ('09-11', 7763), ('09-17', 8613), ('09-18', 8816)]\\\\\\\\n08-26 5093 About $400.4 billion: Morningstar's $361 billion estimate less actual Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue ($75.25 billion and $89.0 billion) gives a $196.75 billion H2 baseline; applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 upside forecast gives about $236.1 billion for H2. Q3 guidance implies roughly $99–$100 billion of Data Center revenue from the recent segment mix, leaving about $136 billion implied for Q4. :: The implied estimate is about $400.4 billion: start with Morningstar's $361 billion annual estimate, subtract reported Q1 revenue of $75.25 billion and reported Q2 revenue of $89.0 billion to get a $196.75 billion H2 baseline, then apply SemiAnalysis's forecast that H2 will exceed analyst estimates by 20%, yielding about $236.1 billion for H2 and $400.35 billion for the year NVIDIA's $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guide, with recent Data Center mix around 92%–93%, implies roughly $99–$100 billion of Q3 Data Center revenue; the annual estimate therefore requires about $136 billion in Q4\\\\\\\\n08-27 5304 Approximately $400 billion for FY2027: reported Q1 and Q2 total $164.25 billion; applying the recent 92.5% Data Center mix to NVIDIA's $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guide implies about $100 billion of Q3 Data Center revenue. Applying SemiAnalysis's 20% second-half upside forecast to the prior $196.75 billion H2 estimate implies about $236 billion for H2 and roughly $400 billion for the year, including an aggressive implied Q4 of about $136 billion. :: Combining that with the reported first half and SemiAnalysis's forecast for second-half revenue 20% above estimates implies roughly $400 billion for FY2027, but requires about $136 billion in Q4—an aggressive ramp\\\\\\\\n08-31 6166 Q1 and Q2 actuals total $164.25 billion; the $108 billion Q3 companywide guide at the latest 92.5% Data Center mix implies about $99.9 billion. Taking Morningstar’s $361 billion estimate less actual H1 gives a $196.75 billion H2 baseline; SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 upside implies about $236.1 billion of H2 and approximately $400.35 billion for FY2027. :: Morningstar’s annual estimate therefore leaves $196.75 billion as its implied H2 baseline; SemiAnalysis’s forecast of H2 revenue 20% above analyst estimates lifts H2 to about $236.1 billion and FY2027 to about $400.35 billion\\\\\\\\n09-02 6413 Q1–Q2 reported revenue is $164.25 billion. The $361 billion FY reference implies $196.75 billion of H2 estimates; applying SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 upside gives $236.1 billion for H2 and about $400.35 billion for FY2027. Q3 is about $99.9 billion if the $108 billion total-revenue guide is combined with the latest 92.5% Data Center mix, leaving roughly $136.2 billion implied for Q4. :: That H2 figure requires roughly $136.2 billion in Q4: aggressive, but the Q3 companywide guide implies about $99.9 billion of Data Center revenue at the latest 92.5% mix, and NVIDIA says hyperscale growth should reaccelerate in Q4 as Vera Rubin supply builds\\\\\\\\n09-03 6604 Q1–Q2 actual revenue totals $164.25 billion. Starting from Morningstar’s $361 billion estimate leaves $196.75 billion of baseline H2 estimates; applying SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 upside gives $236.1 billion for H2 and about $400.35 billion for FY2027. At the recent 92.5% mix, Q3 guidance implies roughly $99.9 billion of Data Center revenue, leaving about $136.2 billion for Q4. :: The supplied run-rate calculation is still just above rung 1: Q1–Q2 revenue totals $164.25 billion; subtracting that from $361 billion gives $196.75 billion of baseline H2 estimates, and SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 upside implies $236.1 billion for H2 and $400.35 billion for FY2027 That requires about $99.9 billion in Q3 using the latest 92.5% mix and $136.2 billion in Q4\\\\\\\\n09-04 6817 About $400 billion, marginally above the rung-1 boundary. Q1–Q2 revenue totals $164.25 billion; Q3 is approximately $99.9 billion using the $108 billion guidance midpoint and Q2’s 92.5% Data Center mix. The earlier H2 estimate baseline of $196.75 billion, uplifted 20% in SemiAnalysis’s H2 forecast, implies about $236.1 billion for H2 and roughly $400.4 billion for FY2027. :: That leaves about $135.9 billion for Q4 to reach $400 billion\\\\\\\\n09-11 7763 About $418 billion: the carried H2 analyst baseline of roughly $212 billion, increased 20% per SemiAnalysis’s forecast, gives about $254 billion for H2; adding Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion and $89.0 billion gives about $418 billion for FY2027. Q3’s $108 billion total-revenue midpoint at a 92.5% Data Center mix implies about $99.9 billion, so the H2 estimate requires roughly $154 billion in Q4. :: The Q3 outlook and recent mix imply about $99.9 billion of Q3 Data Center revenue, leaving roughly $154 billion for Q4 under that H2 forecast—a steep sequential increase\\\\\\\\n09-17 8613 About $418 billion: Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue total $164.25 billion; applying the latest 92.5% mix to the $108 billion Q3 total-revenue outlook implies about $99.9 billion for Q3. The carried H2 estimate, uplifted by the cited 20% SemiAnalysis view, is about $254 billion for Q3–Q4 combined, leaving roughly $154 billion for Q4 and putting the FY2027 total above $400 billion. :: \\\\\\\\n09-18 8816 About $395 billion: $164.25 billion reported in the first half plus about $99.9 billion implied for Q3 leaves roughly $131 billion for Q4. That represents a substantial Q4 step-up consistent with expected reacceleration, but below the prior forecast’s implied Q4 contribution. :: \\\\\\\\nDRAW 2 v9 1 [('08-27', 5139)]\\\\\\\\n08-27 5139 Approximately $417 billion: the $372 billion reference less Q1 actual revenue of $75.25 billion and the Q2 estimate of $85.8 billion implies about $211 billion of H2 estimates; applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 outperformance forecast gives about $253 billion for H2. Adding Q1 actual revenue and Q2 actual revenue of $89 billion yields about $417 billion. The $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guide, applied to the recent roughly 92.5% Data Center share, implies about $100 billion of Q3 Data Center revenue, leaving the forecast dependent on a strong Q4. :: The Q3 total-revenue guide is consistent with roughly $100 billion of Data Center revenue using the recent segment mix; the implied second-half total requires a substantial Q4 ramp, so the estimate relies on SemiAnalysis's specific second-half forecast rather than treating the guide alone as sufficient\\\\\\\\nDRAW 2 v21 14 [('08-28', 5474), ('08-29', 5604), ('08-30', 5751), ('08-31', 5969), ('09-01', 6185), ('09-04', 6598), ('09-06', 6862), ('09-07', 6967), ('09-08', 7064), ('09-12', 7678), ('09-14', 7928), ('09-18', 8505), ('09-19', 8628), ('09-20', 8730)]\\\\\\\\n08-28 5474 Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion plus Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion and Q3 guidance of $108.0 billion totals about $285.8 billion. Carrying Q3's roughly 12.3% sequential growth over Q2 into Q4 implies about $121.3 billion in Q4, or about $407 billion for FY2027—approximately 88.5% growth over FY2026 revenue of $215.94 billion.\\\\\\\\n08-29 5604 About $407 billion of FY2027 revenue, or approximately 88.5% growth from FY2026's $215.94 billion: Q1 and Q2 actual revenue plus the $108 billion Q3 guide total $285.8 billion, and extending Q3's approximately 12.3% sequential growth into Q4 implies about $121.3 billion. The CFO-attributed 70% full-year growth guidance is a lower anchor, implying roughly $367 billion.\\\\\\\\n08-30 5751 Using reported Q1 and Q2 revenue of $81.6 billion and $96.2 billion, Q3 guidance of $108.0 billion, and carrying Q3's roughly 12.3% sequential growth into Q4 implies about $121.3 billion in Q4 and roughly $407 billion for FY2027. Against FY2026 revenue of $215.94 billion, that is approximately 88.5% growth; NVIDIA's 70% full-year outlook is a lower anchor, implying about $367 billion.\\\\\\\\n08-31 5969 Carrying Q3's approximately 12.3% sequential growth forward one quarter implies Q4 revenue of about $121 billion and FY2027 revenue of about $407 billion, roughly 88.5% growth from FY2026's $215.94 billion. NVIDIA's separate 70% full-year outlook implies about $367 billion; both implied outcomes are above the 60% rung-1 threshold.\\\\\\\\n09-01 6185 About $407 billion of FY2027 revenue, or roughly 88.5% growth from FY2026's $215.94 billion. This uses reported Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion, reported Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion, Q3 guidance of $108 billion, and carries the roughly 12.3% Q2-to-Q3 sequential growth rate forward once to estimate Q4 at about $121 billion.\\\\\\\\n09-04 6598 About $407 billion of FY2027 revenue, or approximately 88% growth from FY2026's $215.94 billion: Q1 $81.6 billion plus Q2 $96.2 billion plus Q3 guidance of $108 billion, with Q4 estimated at about $121 billion by carrying Q3's 12% sequential growth forward.\\\\\\\\n09-06 6862 About $407B of FY2027 revenue, or approximately 88.5% growth over FY2026's $215.94B: reported Q1 and Q2 plus the $108B Q3 midpoint, with Q4 estimated by carrying Q3's roughly 12.3% sequential growth forward.\\\\\\\\n09-07 6967 About $406.8 billion of FY2027 revenue, or approximately 88.4% growth over FY2026's $215.94 billion: reported Q1 $81.6B plus Q2 $96.2B, Q3 guidance of $108B, and Q4 at 12% sequential growth from Q3 (about $121.0B).\\\\\\\\n09-08 7064 Using reported FY2027 Q1 revenue of $81.6B and Q2 revenue of $96.2B, Q3 midpoint guidance of $108B, and carrying forward the stated 12% sequential growth implied by Q3 guidance, Q4 is about $121.0B. That implies FY2027 revenue of about $406.8B versus FY2026's $215.94B, or approximately 88.4% growth (rung 1); the separate 70% full-year outlook implies about $367B, also rung 1.\\\\\\\\n09-12 7678 About $407 billion of FY2027 revenue, or 88.5% growth over FY2026's $215.94 billion: add reported Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion and Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion to the $108 billion Q3 guide, then carry Q3's roughly 12.3% sequential growth into Q4 (about $121 billion). This is a run-rate extrapolation, not an assertion that Q4 revenue is already established.\\\\\\\\n09-14 7928 FY2026 revenue was $215.94 billion; Q1 and Q2 FY2027 revenue totaled $177.8 billion, and the $108 billion Q3 guide brings the first three quarters to $285.8 billion. Carrying the roughly 12.3% sequential growth implied by the Q3 guide into Q4 gives about $121 billion, or roughly $407 billion for FY2027 and 88.5% year-over-year growth.\\\\\\\\n09-18 8505 Carry the roughly 12% sequential growth implied by Q3 guidance into Q4: $108 billion × 1.12 is about $121 billion. Adding that to FY2027 Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion, Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion, and Q3 guidance of $108 billion yields about $407 billion; versus FY2026 revenue of $215.94 billion, that is approximately 88% growth.\\\\\\\\n09-19 8628 FY2026 revenue was $215.94 billion; FY2027 Q1 and Q2 revenue plus the Q3 guidance midpoint total $285.8 billion. Carrying the approximately 12% sequential growth implied by Q3 guidance into Q4 gives roughly $121 billion for Q4, about $407 billion for FY2027, or approximately 88% year-over-year growth.\\\\\\\\n09-20 8730 Q1 and Q2 revenue plus the Q3 guidance midpoint total $285.8 billion; extending the approximately 12% sequential growth implied by Q3 guidance into Q4 gives about $121 billion, or approximately $407 billion for FY2027. Against FY2026 revenue of $215.94 billion, that implies about 88% growth; the CFO's approximately 70% full-year outlook is a lower check, implying about $367 billion, but also falls in rung 1.\\\\\\\\nDRAW 2 v17 11 [('08-26', 4931), ('08-27', 5124), ('08-28', 5466), ('08-29', 5588), ('09-06', 6864), ('09-07', 6977), ('09-08', 7065), ('09-09', 7177), ('09-17', 8316), ('09-19', 8625), ('09-20', 8725)]\\\\\\\\n08-26 4931 Approximately 70% FY2028 total revenue growth, NVIDIA's preliminary, supply-constrained outlook (e2568). Applied to the $396 billion FY2027 consensus baseline, that implies about $673 billion of FY2028 revenue (e2697), consistent with roughly 70% growth and within rung 1.\\\\\\\\n08-27 5124 Approximately 70% FY2028 revenue growth, from NVIDIA's preliminary outlook (e2532). Applied to the $396 billion FY2027 consensus estimate, that implies about $673 billion in FY2028 revenue (e2697), or roughly 70% growth.\\\\\\\\n08-28 5466 Approximately 70% FY2028 growth, from NVIDIA’s stated outlook. Applying that growth to the cited $396 billion FY2027 consensus revenue gives about $673 billion for FY2028.\\\\\\\\n08-29 5588 NVIDIA's approximately 70% FY2028 growth outlook implies about $673 billion of revenue using the $396 billion FY2027 consensus base ($396 billion × 1.70). The outlook is explicitly supply-constrained, so I use the guided growth rate rather than the higher unconstrained demand indication.\\\\\\\\n09-06 6864 Approximately 70% FY2028 revenue growth, or about $673 billion of revenue applying 70% growth to the roughly $396 billion FY2027 consensus base. A 70% growth outcome clears rung 1's 60% threshold.\\\\\\\\n09-07 6977 Approximately 70% FY2028 total revenue growth, based on NVIDIA's direct supply-constrained outlook. Applying 70% to the roughly $396 billion FY2027 consensus base implies about $673 billion of FY2028 revenue; the separate approximately 77% next-fiscal-year report is less directly specified for FY2028 and does not replace that outlook.\\\\\\\\n09-08 7065 The direct FY2028 outlook is approximately 70% growth. Applying that rate to the cited roughly $396–397 billion FY2027 consensus base implies about $673–675 billion of FY2028 revenue; reports using a higher FY2027 base put the implied total near $700 billion.\\\\\\\\n09-09 7177 Approximately 70% FY2028 total revenue growth, using NVIDIA's supply-constrained outlook; applied to the roughly $396–397 billion FY2027 consensus base, that implies about $673–700 billion of FY2028 revenue. The 70% growth figure is above the rung-1 boundary of 60%.\\\\\\\\n09-17 8316 Approximately 70% FY2028 total revenue growth. This is NVIDIA's direct outlook; applied to the $411 billion FY2027 estimate, it implies about $699 billion of FY2028 revenue (70% growth), while the cited $673 billion figure uses a lower FY2027 base.\\\\\\\\n09-19 8625 Use NVIDIA's supply-constrained FY2028 growth outlook of approximately 70%. Applied to the $411 billion FY2027 estimate, that growth implies about $699 billion of FY2028 revenue; the reported $673 billion projection reflects applying roughly 70% to a lower FY2027 base.\\\\\\\\n09-20 8725 Approximately 70% FY2028 revenue growth, or about $673 billion using the cited roughly $396 billion FY2027 base. This follows NVIDIA’s explicit supply-constrained outlook; the forecast of twice as many chips sold in calendar 2027 is supportive but does not supply a directly comparable FY2028 revenue-growth figure.\\\\\\\\nDRAW 2 v35 8 [('09-06', 6868), ('09-07', 6971), ('09-08', 7073), ('09-09', 7173), ('09-17', 8314), ('09-18', 8493), ('09-19', 8626), ('09-20', 8732)]\\\\\\\\n09-06 6868 Applying NVIDIA's approximately 70% FY2028 growth outlook to the roughly $396–397 billion FY2027 consensus base implies about $673–675 billion of FY2028 revenue. That falls in rung 2; the $555 billion trailing-twelve-month estimate for September 2027 is a supporting run-rate signal, not a directly comparable FY2028 total.\\\\\\\\n09-07 6971 Applying NVIDIA's approximately 70% FY2028 growth outlook to the roughly $396–397 billion FY2027 base implies about $673–675 billion; allowing for small base variation gives roughly $673–680 billion. That is rung 2, below the $700 billion rung-1 threshold.\\\\\\\\n09-08 7073 Applying NVIDIA’s approximately 70% FY2028 growth outlook to the roughly $396–397 billion FY2027 base implies about $673–675 billion ($396–397 billion × 1.70). That is rung 2, below the $700 billion rung 1 threshold.\\\\\\\\n09-09 7173 About $673–675 billion: apply NVIDIA’s stated 70% FY2028 revenue-growth outlook to the roughly $396–397 billion FY2027 base. This falls in rung 2.\\\\\\\\n09-17 8314 NVIDIA's 70% growth outlook applied to the cited FY2027 base range of roughly $396–$411 billion implies about $673–$699 billion for FY2028. The analyst estimate of $678 billion and the 63.2% growth estimate applied to $411 billion imply about $678 billion and $671 billion, respectively; the central forecast is therefore below $700 billion and in rung 2.\\\\\\\\n09-18 8493 About $673 billion: NVIDIA's stated FY2028 outlook is 70% growth to roughly that amount. The consensus calculations imply roughly $671–678 billion as well, keeping the forecast below the $700 billion rung-1 threshold.\\\\\\\\n09-19 8626 About $673 billion to $678 billion: NVIDIA’s 70% FY2028 growth outlook is stated as about $673 billion, while the analyst FY2027 estimate of $411 billion with 65% growth implies about $678 billion. Both figures fall in rung 2.\\\\\\\\n09-20 8732 About $671–$678 billion: NVIDIA's 70% FY2028 growth outlook implies about $673 billion, analyst estimates put FY2028 at $678 billion, and applying Zacks' 63.2% growth estimate to the cited $411 billion FY2027 base gives about $671 billion.\\\\\\\\nDRAW 3 v3 2 [('08-30', 6002), ('09-07', 7296)]\\\\\\\\n08-30 6002 About $415 billion: the reported $177.837 billion first half plus the $108 billion Q3 midpoint, then Q4 estimated by carrying Q3's roughly 89% year-over-year growth forward against the implied FY2026 Q4 base of about $68.1 billion. The 70% full-year growth guide implies about $367 billion instead, but would require Q4 revenue near $81 billion, below Q3. :: The reported first-half revenue of $177.837 billion plus the $108 billion Q3 guide leaves the forecast dependent mainly on Q4 The reported 70% full-year growth guide is a meaningful counterweight: applied to FY2026 revenue of $215.9 billion, it implies about $367 billion, requiring Q4 revenue around $81 billion\\\\\\\\n09-07 7296 About $407 billion: $177.837 billion reported for the first half, plus $108 billion guided for Q3, plus about $121 billion for Q4 by carrying the 12% sequential growth pace implied by Q3 guidance forward once. The separate 70% full-year growth statement implies about $367 billion from the $215.9 billion FY2026 base, but would require a sharp Q4 drop and is outweighed by the reported run-rate and near-term guidance. :: The reported first-half revenue of $177.837 billion plus Q3 guidance of $108 billion leaves about $121 billion for Q4 if the guided 12% sequential growth pace carries forward, implying about $407 billion for FY2027\\\\\\\\nDRAW 3 v35 1 [('08-30', 6001)]\\\\\\\\n08-30 6001 Q1 and Q2 total about $164.2 billion; Q3 is about $99.9 billion using the $108 billion total-revenue guide and the recent Data Center revenue mix. Carrying that run-rate into Q4, with hyperscale growth expected to reaccelerate, implies roughly $110–115 billion in Q4 and about $374–379 billion for FY2027. :: The Q3 guide assumes no China Data Center compute revenue, leaving that as possible upside rather than part of the base estimate.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r45.stream:87:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_45\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\\\\\\\\nD=decimal.Decimal\\\\\\\\ndef db(i,name='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''views'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\\\\\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',uri=True)\\\\\\\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\\\\\\\n return c\\\\\\\\ndef req(a,j):\\\\\\\\n c=a.execute('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',(j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],)).fetchone()\\\\\\\\n assert c and c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']==j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] and c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''purpose'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''judge'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',dict(j)\\\\\\\\n d=json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_json'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\\\\\n return d,json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''answer_json'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\\\\\nEVID=re.compile(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'^- (e'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\[.*?(?=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'^- e'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+ \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\[|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Z)'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.M|re.S)\\\\\\\\ndef evidence(t):\\\\\\\\n b=t.split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''[Evidence in view under this thesis, '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[0]\\\\\\\\n m=dict((x.group(1),x.group(0).strip()) for x in EVID.finditer(b))\\\\\\\\n assert len(m)==int(b.split()[0]),(len(m),b[:20])\\\\\\\\n return m\\\\\\\\ndef user(d):\\\\\\\\n return next(m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''content'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] for m in d['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''messages'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] if m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''role'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''user'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')\\\\\\\\nUNIT=r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''(?:trillion(?:s)?|billions?|millions?|bn|mm|[BTM]|%|percent(?:age points?)?)'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\nNUM=r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+(?:,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d{3})*(?:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+)?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\nFIG=re.compile(rf'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''(?<\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'!['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\w.])(?P<sign>[+−-])?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?P<lo>{NUM})(?:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*[-–—]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?P<hi>{NUM}))?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?P<unit>{UNIT})(?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'![a-zA-Z0-9])'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.I)\\\\\\\\nMULT={'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''trillion'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''trillions'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''t'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''billion'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''billions'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''bn'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''b'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''million'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''millions'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''mm'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''m'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')}\\\\\\\\ndef figures(t,unit):\\\\\\\\n out=[]\\\\\\\\n for m in FIG.finditer(t or '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\\\\\n  u=m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''unit'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''].lower()\\\\\\\\n  if (u in MULT)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'!=(unit=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):continue\\\\\\\\n  mult=MULT.get(u,1)\\\\\\\\n  if m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''sign'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''-'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''−'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):mult=-mult\\\\\\\\n  for g in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''lo'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''hi'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\\\\\n   if m[g]:out.append(D(m[g].replace('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''))*mult)\\\\\\\\n return out\\\\\\\\ndef snippets(ed):\\\\\\\\n return [re.split(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (?:It replaces|Opinion, not verified:)'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',b,1)[0].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1] for b in ed.values()]\\\\\\\\ndef prior_text(t):\\\\\\\\n return t.split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''[Previous conclusion'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nAnswer per'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[0].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1]\\\\\\\\ndef tag(x,pattern): return bool(re.search(pattern,x or '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.I))\\\\\\\\ndef record(i):\\\\\\\\n v=db(i);a=db(i,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''archive'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')\\\\\\\\n return (v,a,v.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select j.*,k.unit from judgements j join view_keys k using(view_id) where k.unit in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''percent'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'') order by judgement_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))\\\\\\\\nfor i,pair in {1:('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v4'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v8'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),2:('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v14'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v9'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),3:('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v3'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v35'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')}.items():\\\\\\\\n v,a,_=record(i); xs=[]\\\\\\\\n for id in pair:\\\\\\\\n  xs.append({j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''publication_day'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']:j for j in v.execute('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',(id,))})\\\\\\\\n common=sorted(set(xs[0])&set(xs[1]))\\\\\\\\n print(i,len(common),sum(d>='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''2026-08-26'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' for d in common))\\\\\\\\n for day in common:\\\\\\\\n  w,p=[x[day] for x in xs]\\\\\\\\n  v1=figures(w['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'');v2=figures(p['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')\\\\\\\\n  if (i==3 and day<'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''2026-08-26'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'') or (v1 and v2 and v2[0]>v1[0]+2 and (v2[0]>=300 or v1[0]<300)):\\\\\\\\n   print(day,w['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],p['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],w['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''], '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''|'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',p['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r45.stream:88:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_45\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\\\\\\\\nD=decimal.Decimal\\\\\\\\ndef db(i,name='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''views'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\\\\\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',uri=True)\\\\\\\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\\\\\\\n return c\\\\\\\\ndef req(a,j):\\\\\\\\n c=a.execute('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',(j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],)).fetchone()\\\\\\\\n assert c and c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']==j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] and c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''purpose'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''judge'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',dict(j)\\\\\\\\n d=json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_json'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\\\\\n return d,json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''answer_json'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\\\\\nEVID=re.compile(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'^- (e'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\[.*?(?=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'^- e'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+ \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\[|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Z)'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.M|re.S)\\\\\\\\ndef evidence(t):\\\\\\\\n b=t.split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''[Evidence in view under this thesis, '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[0]\\\\\\\\n m=dict((x.group(1),x.group(0).strip()) for x in EVID.finditer(b))\\\\\\\\n assert len(m)==int(b.split()[0]),(len(m),b[:20])\\\\\\\\n return m\\\\\\\\ndef user(d):\\\\\\\\n return next(m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''content'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] for m in d['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''messages'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] if m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''role'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''user'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')\\\\\\\\nUNIT=r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''(?:trillion(?:s)?|billions?|millions?|bn|mm|[BTM]|%|percent(?:age points?)?)'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\nNUM=r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+(?:,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d{3})*(?:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+)?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\nFIG=re.compile(rf'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''(?<\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'!['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\w.])(?P<sign>[+−-])?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?P<lo>{NUM})(?:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*[-–—]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?P<hi>{NUM}))?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?P<unit>{UNIT})(?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'![a-zA-Z0-9])'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.I)\\\\\\\\nMULT={'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''trillion'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''trillions'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''t'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''billion'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''billions'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''bn'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''b'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''million'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''millions'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''mm'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''m'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')}\\\\\\\\ndef figures(t,unit):\\\\\\\\n out=[]\\\\\\\\n for m in FIG.finditer(t or '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\\\\\n  u=m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''unit'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''].lower()\\\\\\\\n  if (u in MULT)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'!=(unit=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):continue\\\\\\\\n  mult=MULT.get(u,1)\\\\\\\\n  if m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''sign'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''-'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''−'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):mult=-mult\\\\\\\\n  for g in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''lo'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''hi'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\\\\\n   if m[g]:out.append(D(m[g].replace('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''))*mult)\\\\\\\\n return out\\\\\\\\ndef snippets(ed):\\\\\\\\n return [re.split(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (?:It replaces|Opinion, not verified:)'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',b,1)[0].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1] for b in ed.values()]\\\\\\\\ndef prior_text(t):\\\\\\\\n return t.split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''[Previous conclusion'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nAnswer per'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[0].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1]\\\\\\\\ndef tag(x,pattern): return bool(re.search(pattern,x or '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.I))\\\\\\\\ndef record(i):\\\\\\\\n v=db(i);a=db(i,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''archive'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')\\\\\\\\n return (v,a,v.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select j.*,k.unit from judgements j join view_keys k using(view_id) where k.unit in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''percent'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'') order by judgement_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))\\\\\\\\nfor i,pair in {1:('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v4'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v8'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),2:('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v14'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v9'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),3:('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v3'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v35'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')}.items():\\\\\\\\n v,a,_=record(i); xs=[]\\\\\\\\n for id in pair:\\\\\\\\n  xs.append({j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''publication_day'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']:j for j in v.execute('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',(id,))})\\\\\\\\n common=sorted(set(xs[0])&set(xs[1]))\\\\\\\\n print(i,len(common),sum(d>='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''2026-08-26'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' for d in common))\\\\\\\\n for day in common:\\\\\\\\n  w,p=[x[day] for x in xs]\\\\\\\\n  v1=figures(w['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'');v2=figures(p['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')\\\\\\\\n  if (i==3 and day<'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''2026-08-26'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'') or (v1 and v2 and v2[0]>v1[0]+2 and (v2[0]>=300 or v1[0]<300)):\\\\\\\\n   print(day,w['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],p['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],w['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''], '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''|'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',p['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"1 74 26\\\\\\\\n2026-08-20 4074 4076 The quarterly path of $81.6 billion Q1, about $94–$95 billion Q2, $107–$108 billion Q3, and roughly $120 billion Q4 using 12% sequential growth implies about $404 billion before uncertain incremental CPU and SpaceX upside. Discounting that upside for timing and execution, and weighing Morningstar's 80% growth estimate, implies roughly $420 billion for FY2027. | About $390bn for FY2027. Q1 Data Center revenue was $75.25bn; the $91bn Q2 total-revenue guide and management’s acceleration commentary support continued growth, while demand and capacity evidence lifts the prior roughly $370bn estimate. The OpenAI campus is not expected to come online until 2028, and HBM supply constraints limit the near-term upside.\\\\\\\\n2026-08-25 4580 4589 A forward quarterly path of about $81.6 billion in Q1, $94–95 billion in Q2, $107–108 billion in Q3, and roughly $120 billion in Q4 totals about $403–405 billion. Partial credit for the unshipped standalone-CPU opportunity and early SpaceX demand lifts the central estimate to about $410 billion, still within rung 2. | Approximately $401 billion: Morningstar's $361 billion FY2027 estimate less Q1 actual revenue of $75.25 billion and the $86.3 billion Q2 analyst estimate implies about $199.45 billion for H2; applying SemiAnalysis's forecast of 20% upside to H2 analyst estimates gives about $239.34 billion for H2 and approximately $400.89 billion for FY2027.\\\\\\\\n2026-08-26 5092 5093 Q1 reported $81.62 billion and Q2 reported $96.2 billion; Q3 guidance is $108.0 billion. Carrying Q3's approximately 12.3% sequential growth over Q2 into Q4 implies about $121.3 billion for Q4, or approximately $407.1 billion for FY2027 in total. | About $400.4 billion: Morningstar's $361 billion estimate less actual Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue ($75.25 billion and $89.0 billion) gives a $196.75 billion H2 baseline; applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 upside forecast gives about $236.1 billion for H2. Q3 guidance implies roughly $99–$100 billion of Data Center revenue from the recent segment mix, leaving about $136 billion implied for Q4.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-04 6818 6817 Using the reported $81.62 billion Q1 and $96.2 billion Q2, the $108 billion Q3 guide, and carrying approximately 89% year-over-year growth forward from Q4 FY2026 revenue of $68 billion gives Q4 FY2027 of about $128.5 billion and FY2027 total revenue of about $414.3 billion. This is rung 2, below $431.2 billion. | About $400 billion, marginally above the rung-1 boundary. Q1–Q2 revenue totals $164.25 billion; Q3 is approximately $99.9 billion using the $108 billion guidance midpoint and Q2’s 92.5% Data Center mix. The earlier H2 estimate baseline of $196.75 billion, uplifted 20% in SemiAnalysis’s H2 forecast, implies about $236.1 billion for H2 and roughly $400.4 billion for FY2027.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-05 6928 6936 About $414.3 billion: carry the Q3 guide’s approximately 89% year-over-year growth into Q4, implying about $128.5 billion against Q4 FY2026 revenue of $68 billion, then add reported Q1 revenue of $81.62 billion, reported Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion, and the $108 billion Q3 guide. | About $419 billion for FY2027: Q1–Q2 Data Center revenue totals $164.25 billion; Q3 is about $99.9 billion using the $108 billion total-revenue midpoint and Q2's 92.5% Data Center mix. Carrying Q3's implied total-revenue growth into Q4 gives a roughly $112 billion Q4 baseline; applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 upside forecast to the resulting roughly $212 billion H2 baseline gives about $254 billion in H2 and about $419 billion for the year.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-06 7116 7111 About $414.3 billion: $81.62 billion Q1 + $96.2 billion Q2 + $108 billion Q3 guidance + approximately $128.5 billion for Q4, derived by carrying the Q3 guide's roughly 89% year-over-year growth forward from Q4 FY2026 revenue of $68 billion. | About $418 billion: Q1 and Q2 sum to $164.25 billion; Q3 is about $99.9 billion using the $108 billion total-revenue outlook and 92.5% Data Center mix. Carrying the 12.3% sequential total-revenue growth implied by Q3 guidance into Q4 gives a roughly $212 billion H2 baseline; SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 upside implies about $254 billion for H2 and about $418 billion for FY2027.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-07 7206 7210 About $416–421 billion: $81.62 billion in Q1 plus $96.2 billion in Q2 plus the $108 billion Q3 guide, then an estimated roughly $129–135 billion in Q4. The baseline Q4 estimate carries the Q3 guide's roughly 89% year-over-year growth forward against Q4 FY2026 revenue of $68 billion; the stated Q4 hyperscale acceleration supports a modest uplift. | About $419 billion: Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue total $164.25 billion; Q3 is estimated at about $99.9 billion from the $108 billion total-revenue guidance and 92.5% mix. Carrying the sequential growth into Q4 gives an H2 baseline of about $212 billion; applying SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 upside yields about $254 billion for H2 and approximately $419 billion for FY2027.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-08 7278 7281 Q1 and Q2 total $177.82 billion; adding Q3 guidance of $108 billion and carrying its roughly 89% year-over-year growth rate forward to the $68 billion prior-year Q4 base implies about $128.5 billion in Q4, or $414.3 billion for FY2027. Allowing for the stated Q4 hyperscale acceleration and Rubin ramp, but tempering for supply limits, supports roughly $414–421 billion. | About $419 billion: Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue total $164.25 billion; Q3’s $108 billion total-revenue guidance midpoint at the recent 92.5% Data Center mix implies about $99.9 billion. Carrying that sequential growth into Q4 gives an H2 analyst baseline of about $212 billion; SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 upside implies about $254 billion for H2 and approximately $419 billion for FY2027.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-09 7395 7394 Q1 and Q2 reported revenue totals $177.82 billion; adding the $108 billion Q3 guide and carrying its 89% year-over-year growth rate onto the $68 billion prior-year Q4 implies about $128.5 billion for Q4 and $414.3 billion total FY2027 revenue. | About $419 billion: Q3 Data Center revenue is estimated at $99.9 billion from the $108 billion total-revenue midpoint and 92.5% mix; carrying that sequential growth into Q4 gives an analyst-baseline H2 of about $212 billion. SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 upside implies about $254 billion in H2, plus $75.25 billion in Q1 and $89 billion in Q2.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-10 7594 7600 About $414.3 billion: $81.62 billion in Q1 plus $96.2 billion in Q2, plus the $108 billion Q3 guide, plus an estimated $128.5 billion in Q4 by carrying roughly 89% year-over-year growth onto Q4 FY2026 revenue of $68 billion. | Approximately $418 billion: reported Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue sum to $164.25 billion; Q3 implies about $99.9 billion from the $108 billion total-revenue midpoint at a 92.5% mix; the carried-forward H2 baseline of about $212 billion, raised 20% in line with SemiAnalysis’s forecast, implies roughly $254 billion for H2.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-11 7753 7763 About $414.3 billion: add reported Q1 revenue of $81.62 billion, reported Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion, and Q3 guidance of $108 billion; estimate Q4 at about $128.5 billion by carrying the guided 89% year-over-year growth forward from Q4 FY2026 revenue of $68 billion. | About $418 billion: the carried H2 analyst baseline of roughly $212 billion, increased 20% per SemiAnalysis’s forecast, gives about $254 billion for H2; adding Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue of $75.25 billion and $89.0 billion gives about $418 billion for FY2027. Q3’s $108 billion total-revenue midpoint at a 92.5% Data Center mix implies about $99.9 billion, so the H2 estimate requires roughly $154 billion in Q4.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-12 7888 7881 About $414.3 billion: Q1 actual of $81.62 billion plus Q2 actual of $96.2 billion, Q3 guidance of $108 billion, and an estimated Q4 of about $128.5 billion by carrying the Q3 guide’s 89% year-over-year growth forward from prior-year Q4 revenue of $68 billion. This falls in rung 2. | About $418 billion: reported Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue sum to $164.25 billion; Q3 is estimated at about $99.9 billion from the $108 billion guidance midpoint and 92.5% recent mix. The carried H2 analyst baseline of about $212 billion, raised 20% by SemiAnalysis, implies about $254 billion for H2, for roughly $418 billion for FY2027.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-13 7986 7994 About $414.3 billion: $81.62 billion in Q1 plus $96.2 billion in Q2 plus the $108 billion Q3 guide, plus an estimated $128.5 billion for Q4 by carrying Q3’s 89% year-over-year growth rate forward against Q4 FY2026 revenue of $68 billion. | About $418 billion: $75.25 billion in Q1 plus $89.0 billion in Q2, about $99.9 billion in Q3 using the $108 billion guidance midpoint and 92.5% Data Center mix, and about $154 billion in Q4. The Q4 estimate follows from the carried H2 analyst baseline of about $212 billion, increased 20% by SemiAnalysis to about $254 billion; the resulting full-year figure exceeds the rung-1 $400 billion boundary.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-14 8180 8178 About $414.6 billion: $81.62 billion (Q1) + $96.2 billion (Q2) + $108 billion (Q3 guidance) + about $128.8 billion for Q4, calculated by carrying Q3's roughly 89.4% year-over-year growth forward from Q4 FY2026 revenue of $68 billion. | About $418 billion: Q1 and Q2 contribute $164.25 billion; Q3 is implied at about $99.9 billion from the $108 billion total-revenue guidance midpoint and the recent 92.5% Data Center mix; carrying the H2 analyst baseline forward with SemiAnalysis’ 20% upside gives about $254 billion for H2. That implies about $154 billion in Q4 and places FY2027 above the $400 billion rung boundary.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-16 8504 8502 Q1 and Q2 actual revenue totaled $177.82 billion. Using the analyst's $113.6 billion Q3 estimate, based on NVIDIA's recent guidance-beat record, implies about 99% Q3 year-over-year growth; carrying that growth rate onto Q4 FY2026 revenue of about $68 billion gives roughly $135.5 billion for Q4 FY2027 and about $426.9 billion for the full year. | About $418 billion: Q1 and Q2 FY2027 Data Center revenue total $164.25 billion; Q3 is about $99.9 billion using the $108 billion total-revenue guidance midpoint and recent 92.5% mix. Carrying forward the prior H2 analyst baseline with SemiAnalysis’ stated 20% H2 upside implies roughly $254 billion for H2, including about $154 billion in Q4, putting the FY total above $400 billion.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-17 8609 8613 About $404 billion: $81.62 billion Q1 plus $96.2 billion Q2, plus a $113.6 billion Q3 estimate, plus roughly $112.2 billion for Q4 (Q4 FY2026 revenue of about $68 billion grown by analysts' 65% estimate). This is an estimate-based forecast, not a claim that the FY2027 total is already established. | About $418 billion: Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue total $164.25 billion; applying the latest 92.5% mix to the $108 billion Q3 total-revenue outlook implies about $99.9 billion for Q3. The carried H2 estimate, uplifted by the cited 20% SemiAnalysis view, is about $254 billion for Q3–Q4 combined, leaving roughly $154 billion for Q4 and putting the FY2027 total above $400 billion.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-18 8810 8816 Q1 and Q2 revenue total $177.82 billion. Applying the recent average 3.1% beat to the $110.16 billion high end of Q3 guidance gives about $113.6 billion for Q3; applying analysts' 65% Q4 growth estimate to FY2026 Q4 revenue of $68 billion gives about $112.2 billion, for roughly $403.6 billion total. | About $395 billion: $164.25 billion reported in the first half plus about $99.9 billion implied for Q3 leaves roughly $131 billion for Q4. That represents a substantial Q4 step-up consistent with expected reacceleration, but below the prior forecast’s implied Q4 contribution.\\\\\\\\n2 69 26\\\\\\\\n2026-07-12 517 520 About $387 billion: starting with Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion and Q2 guidance of approximately $91 billion, I carry the roughly 11.5% sequential increase forward to Q3 and Q4. This remains within rung 3 and below $400 billion. | About $400–410B of FY2027 Data Center revenue. I use the Q1 $75.25B result and Q2 growth outlook as the operating base, then give partial—not full—weight to the roughly $1T Blackwell/Vera Rubin visibility across calendar 2026–27 because it spans multiple periods and products; the discounted estimate is just above the $400B rung boundary.\\\\\\\\n2026-07-13 592 593 Approximately $387 billion: Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion followed by Q2 guidance of $91 billion implies about 11.5% sequential growth; carrying that growth through Q3 and Q4 gives roughly $101.5 billion and $113.2 billion, respectively. | About $415B of FY2027 Data Center revenue: the guide-derived sequential-growth run-rate is about $356B, but Q1's 21% sequential segment growth, management's Q2 acceleration statement, and quantified 2027 hyperscaler spending and demand evidence imply a discounted uplift of roughly $59B. This is below