imately 12.3% sequential growth ($108.0 billion × $108.0 billion / $96.2 billion ≈ $121.3 billion), implies FY2027 revenue of about $407.1 billion. | Approximately $422 billion for FY2027: $164.25 billion from Q1–Q2 plus an implied roughly $99.9 billion in Q3 and the carried roughly $115 billion Q4 estimate gives an H2 baseline near $215 billion; applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 outperformance estimate yields about $422 billion for the year.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-02 6219 6218 FY2027 revenue of about $407.1 billion: $81.6 billion reported in Q1, $96.2 billion reported in Q2, $108.0 billion guided for Q3, and approximately $121.3 billion for Q4 if Q3's roughly 12.3% sequential growth carries forward. | About $422 billion for FY2027: $164.25 billion reported in Q1–Q2, about $99.9 billion implied for Q3 from the $108 billion total-revenue guide at the latest 92.5% Data Center mix, and the carried Q4 baseline of about $115 billion make an H2 analyst baseline near $215 billion. Applying SemiAnalysis's estimate that H2 Data Center revenue will exceed analyst estimates by 20% gives about $258 billion for H2 and roughly $422 billion for FY2027.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-03 6392 6405 Q1 $81.6 billion + Q2 $96.2 billion + Q3 guided midpoint $108.0 billion + implied Q4 about $121.3 billion = approximately $407.1 billion. Q4 is derived by carrying forward the Q2-to-Q3 sequential growth rate of about 12.3%. | About $422 billion: Q1 and Q2 total $164.25 billion; Q3 is estimated at about $99.9 billion by applying the reported 92.5% Q2 Data Center mix to the $108 billion total-revenue outlook; with the carried Q4 baseline of about $115 billion, H2 is about $215 billion. Applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 upside to estimates gives roughly $258 billion for H2 and $422 billion for FY2027.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-04 6590 6599 About $407.1 billion: $81.6 billion Q1 plus $96.2 billion Q2 plus $108 billion Q3 guidance, with Q4 estimated at about $121.3 billion by carrying forward the roughly 12.3% Q2-to-Q3 sequential growth rate. | About $422 billion for FY2027: $164.25 billion actual in Q1–Q2, about $99.9 billion implied for Q3 from the $108 billion total-revenue guide at a 92.5% Data Center mix, and a carried Q4 baseline of about $115 billion yield an H2 baseline near $215 billion. Applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 outperformance estimate gives roughly $258 billion for H2 and about $422 billion for the year.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-05 6715 6702 About $407.1 billion: reported Q1 and Q2 revenue total $177.8 billion; adding Q3 guidance of $108 billion and carrying the Q2-to-Q3 sequential growth rate (about 12.3%) into Q4 implies about $121.3 billion. The resulting FY2027 total is approximately $407.1 billion. | About $422 billion for FY2027: $164.25 billion of Q1–Q2 actuals, approximately $99.9 billion for Q3 from the $108 billion total-revenue guidance at a 92.5% Data Center mix, and a carried Q4 baseline of about $115 billion produce a roughly $215 billion H2 baseline; SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 upside forecast implies about $258 billion for H2.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-07 6966 6975 Approximately $407 billion: FY2027 Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion plus Q2's $96.2 billion plus Q3 guidance of $108.0 billion totals $285.8 billion; carrying Q3's roughly 12.3% sequential growth forward implies Q4 of about $121.3 billion. The total is about $407.1 billion, within rung 2. | About $414 billion: Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue total $164.25 billion; Q3 is estimated at about $100 billion by applying the latest reported 92.5% Data Center mix to the $108 billion total-revenue guide. The $372 billion reference implies about $208 billion in H2; SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 upside implies about $249 billion in H2 and approximately $414 billion for FY2027.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-08 7058 7072 About $407 billion: Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion plus Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion plus Q3 midpoint guidance of $108 billion, with Q4 estimated at about $121.3 billion by carrying forward Q3's 12.3% sequential growth once. This is an extrapolation rather than Q4 guidance, and it falls in rung 2. | About $414 billion: Q1 and Q2 actual Data Center revenue sum to $164.25 billion; the H2 analyst baseline of about $208 billion, derived from the carried FY2027 reference, rises to roughly $249 billion under SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 upside forecast. The $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guide and latest Data Center mix imply roughly $100 billion for Q3, consistent with—not additional to—that H2 estimate.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-09 7169 7178 About $407 billion: $81.6 billion Q1 plus $96.2 billion Q2, plus the $108 billion Q3 midpoint, plus an estimated $121.3 billion Q4 by carrying forward the 12.3% sequential growth implied by Q3 guidance. | About $413–414 billion: Q1–Q2 total $164.25 billion; Q3 is roughly $100 billion from the $108 billion total-revenue guide at the latest 92.5% Data Center mix; the carried H2 baseline of about $208 billion, raised 20% by SemiAnalysis, is about $249–250 billion. The Q3 estimate is included within H2, not added again.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-10 7396 7400 About $407.1 billion: $81.6 billion in Q1 plus $96.2 billion in Q2 plus the $108 billion Q3 guide, then approximately $121.3 billion for Q4 by carrying forward the roughly 12.3% sequential growth implied by the Q3 midpoint. | About $413–414 billion: $164.25 billion of reported FY2027 H1 Data Center revenue plus approximately $249–250 billion implied for H2 by the prior roughly $208 billion baseline and SemiAnalysis's 20% upside estimate. The approximately $99.9 billion Q3 calculation is included within H2, not added separately.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-11 7568 7562 About $407.1 billion: $81.6 billion (Q1) + $96.2 billion (Q2) + $108 billion (Q3 guidance) + approximately $121.3 billion for Q4, carrying forward the roughly 12.3% sequential growth implied by Q2-to-Q3 guidance. | About $414 billion: $75.25 billion in Q1 plus $89.0 billion in Q2 equals $164.25 billion for H1; applying SemiAnalysis's 20% uplift to the carried-forward roughly $208 billion H2 baseline implies about $249.6 billion in H2, or about $413.9 billion for FY2027.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-12 7684 7670 About $407.1 billion: $81.6 billion Q1 + $96.2 billion Q2 + $108.0 billion Q3 guidance midpoint + approximately $121.3 billion for Q4, carrying forward the 12.3% sequential growth implied from Q2 to Q3. | Approximately $414 billion: Q1 plus Q2 Data Center revenue is $164.25 billion; Q3 is estimated at about $99.9 billion from the $108 billion company revenue guide and the latest 92.5% Data Center mix. The prior H2 baseline of about $208 billion, raised 20% in line with SemiAnalysis’s H2 estimate, implies about $249.6 billion for H2 and roughly $414 billion for the year.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-13 7776 7770 About $407.1 billion: $81.6 billion (Q1) + $96.2 billion (Q2) + $108 billion (Q3 guidance midpoint) + about $121.3 billion for Q4, carrying forward the 12.3% sequential growth implied by Q2-to-Q3 guidance. This is rung 2. | About $414 billion: $164.25 billion from Q1 and Q2 plus approximately $249.6 billion for H2, using the carried $208 billion H2 analyst baseline increased 20% by SemiAnalysis. The Q3 guide and current Data Center mix imply about $100 billion for Q3, which is part of H2, not an additional amount.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-14 7934 7939 About $407.1 billion: $81.6 billion in Q1, $96.2 billion in Q2, and $108 billion at the Q3 guidance midpoint, plus an estimated $121.3 billion in Q4 by extending the roughly 12.3% Q2-to-Q3 sequential growth rate. This is above $400 billion and below $450 billion. | Approximately $414 billion: FY2027 Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue total about $164.25 billion; the $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guide implies about $100 billion of Data Center revenue at the latest reported mix. Carrying forward the prior H2 baseline of about $208 billion and applying SemiAnalysis’s 20% above-estimates forecast gives about $249.6 billion for H2, including Q3, and about $414 billion for FY2027.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-17 8312 8319 Using Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion and Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion, estimate Q3 at about $113.6 billion by applying the reported 3.1% average beat to the $110.16 billion high end of the $108 billion guidance. Carrying forward the roughly 12.3% sequential growth implied by Q2-to-Q3 guidance gives Q4 of about $127.6 billion, or approximately $419 billion for FY2027. | About $382 billion: Q1 and Q2 total approximately $164.25 billion; applying the recent 92.5% Data Center mix to the $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guide implies about $99.9 billion for Q3; carrying that run rate forward with Q4 hyperscale reacceleration implies roughly $115–120 billion for Q4.\\\\\\\\n3 32 25\\\\\\\\n2026-08-19 4048 4033 Q1 actual revenue of $81.6 billion, Q2 guidance of $91 billion, the Q3 estimate of $103.1 billion, and about 12% sequential growth into Q4 imply a baseline around $391–$392 billion. Applying the carried estimate of 20% upside to second-half Data Center compute adds roughly $40 billion, implying total FY2027 revenue around $431–$433 billion. | $361 billion for FY2027: Morningstar explicitly estimates that figure, citing FY2026 data-center revenue of $194 billion and 86% annual growth. The estimate sits exactly at rung 2’s lower boundary and below rung 1’s $400 billion threshold.\\\\\\\\n2026-08-20 4101 4100 Roughly $434–$437 billion: carry forward the prior $391–$392 billion quarterly baseline plus about $40 billion from the estimated 20% second-half Data Center compute upside, then add about $3–$4 billion for BofA’s $94–$95 billion Q2 forecast versus the $91 billion guide midpoint. The higher Q3 expectation is not added separately because it overlaps the second-half tracking uplift. | Around $361 billion with an unquantified modest upward tilt: the China shipment reports add potential revenue, but give no sales value from which to calculate a larger increment. That remains below the $400 billion rung-1 threshold.\\\\\\\\n2026-08-21 4186 4180 Approximately $432–436 billion: applying the roughly $40 billion implied second-half Data Center compute upside from SemiAnalysis to the roughly $392 billion annual reference, with BofA's Q2 estimate adding about $3–4 billion versus guidance, while avoiding a separate overlapping Q3 addition. | Around the high-$300 billions, anchored on Morningstar’s $361 billion estimate with some upside from reported China shipments and demand evidence. The supplied evidence does not quantify an FY2027 increase of at least $39 billion, so the implied figure remains below $400 billion.\\\\\\\\n2026-08-22 4222 4216 About $432–436 billion: apply SemiAnalysis's 20% upside to second-half FY2027 Data Center compute, implying roughly $40 billion above the $392 billion consensus, then include about $3–4 billion for BofA's $94–95 billion Q2 forecast versus the roughly $91 billion guide/consensus. This is a forecast, not an established result, and sits just above the $431.2 billion rung-1 boundary. | About $372 billion: apply the reported 92% Q1 FY2027 year-over-year growth rate to the cited $194 billion FY2026 revenue base ($194B × 1.92).\\\\\\\\n2026-08-23 4298 4288 About $438–440 billion: start from the $392 billion FY2027 estimate, add roughly $40 billion implied by SemiAnalysis’s 20% second-half Data Center compute upside, and allow about $6–8 billion for BofA’s Q2 and following-quarter estimates above the respective consensus figures. | About $372 billion for FY2027: carry the reported 92% year-over-year Q1 FY2027 growth forward across the $194 billion FY2026 base ($194 billion × 1.92).\\\\\\\\n2026-08-24 4510 4507 Approximately $438–440 billion: the Q1 reported revenue of $81.6 billion and Q2 guide of $91 billion anchor the run-rate; above-consensus Q2/Q3 outlooks and the roughly $40 billion implied upside from SemiAnalysis’s 20%-above-consensus second-half Data Center compute projection lift the estimate above $431.2 billion. | Carrying the reported 92% Q1 FY2027 year-over-year growth forward from the cited $194 billion FY2026 data-center revenue implies approximately $372 billion for FY2027. The Q2 consensus of $85.14 billion, up about 107% year over year, is consistent with strong growth but does not establish an estimate above $400 billion.\\\\\\\\n2026-08-25 4665 4667 About $436 billion: start from the $396 billion FY2027 estimate and carry forward the existing roughly $40 billion uplift implied by SemiAnalysis's forecast that second-half FY2027 Data Center compute revenue will exceed consensus by 20% (e60, e1116). | Approximately $387 billion: applying an indicative 99.5% FY2027 growth rate—the midpoint of reported Q1 growth of 92% and the Q2 consensus growth estimate of 107%—to the cited $194 billion FY2026 base.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-01 6457 6454 First-half revenue was $177.837 billion; the $108 billion Q3 guide implies roughly 89% year-over-year growth. Carrying that growth into Q4, whose FY2026 comparison is about $68.1 billion ($215.9 billion FY2026 revenue less $90.805 billion first-half revenue and $57.01 billion FY2026 Q3 revenue), implies roughly $129 billion for Q4 and about $415 billion for FY2027. | About $374–379 billion: Q1 and Q2 sum to about $164.2 billion; Q3 is estimated at about $99.9 billion by applying Q2’s 92.5% Data Center mix to management’s $108 billion total-revenue guide; the carried Q4 estimate is about $110–115 billion with hyperscale growth reaccelerating.\\\\\\\\n2026-09-12 8046 8045 The first-half reported revenue of $177.837 billion, plus Q3 guidance of $108 billion and a 12% sequential carry into Q4, implies about $406.8 billion before the SemiAnalysis forecast of second-half data-center compute revenue 20% above consensus. Applying a discounted uplift only to that portion supports an approximate FY2027 outcome of $435 billion. | About $376 billion: Q1 and Q2 total about $164.2 billion; the roughly $108 billion Q3 total-revenue outlook at the 92.5% Data Center mix implies about $99.9 billion; carrying the guided 12.3% sequential growth forward implies roughly $112 billion in Q4.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r45.stream:89:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_46\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\\\\\\\\nD=decimal.Decimal\\\\\\\\ndef db(i,name='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''views'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\\\\\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',uri=True)\\\\\\\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\\\\\\\n return c\\\\\\\\ndef req(a,j):\\\\\\\\n c=a.execute('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',(j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],)).fetchone()\\\\\\\\n assert c and c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']==j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] and c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''purpose'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''judge'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',dict(j)\\\\\\\\n d=json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_json'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\\\\\n return d,json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''answer_json'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\\\\\nEVID=re.compile(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'^- (e'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\[.*?(?=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'^- e'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+ \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\[|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Z)'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.M|re.S)\\\\\\\\ndef evidence(t):\\\\\\\\n b=t.split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''[Evidence in view under this thesis, '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[0]\\\\\\\\n m=dict((x.group(1),x.group(0).strip()) for x in EVID.finditer(b))\\\\\\\\n assert len(m)==int(b.split()[0]),(len(m),b[:20])\\\\\\\\n return m\\\\\\\\ndef user(d):\\\\\\\\n return next(m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''content'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] for m in d['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''messages'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] if m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''role'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''user'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')\\\\\\\\nUNIT=r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''(?:trillion(?:s)?|billions?|millions?|bn|mm|[BTM]|%|percent(?:age points?)?)'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\nNUM=r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+(?:,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d{3})*(?:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+)?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\nFIG=re.compile(rf'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''(?<\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'!['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\w.])(?P<sign>[+−-])?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?P<lo>{NUM})(?:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*[-–—]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?P<hi>{NUM}))?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?P<unit>{UNIT})(?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'![a-zA-Z0-9])'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\