\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''dep cites'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',v.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select count(*) from judgements where json_array_length(cited_views_json)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'!=0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\").fetchone()[0])\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"8734 e2620 - e2620 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000075:nvda-20260726.htm 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported $99 billion of equity investments and $25 billion of equity investment commitments as of 2026-07-26.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: These include equity investments of $99 billion and equity investment commitments of $25 billion as of July 26, 2026.\\\\\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2929, e3258, e3477, e3889, e3917; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\\\\\n8734 e2889 - e2889 [party_statement; Business Insider, reporting NVIDIA's statement; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:aec1fae1b903de5c43ba7fdf 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said on Wednesday that it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the remainder of its fiscal year, in addition to $47.9 billion held in private companies.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: The company said Wednesday that it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest of its fiscal year, on top of $47.9 billion it already holds in private companies.\\\\\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2960; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\\\\\n8734 e3474 - e3474 [fact; insidermonkey.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:baa07a74334dc91adc7d85bc 2026-08-31] NVIDIA is investing $3.5 billion in MediaTek through convertible bonds.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ: NVDA ) is investing $3.5 billion in Taiwan-based MediaTek through convertible bonds, taking an existing AI partnership a step further.\\\\\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3558; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\\\\\n8734 e3934 - e3934 [rumour; finance.yahoo.com; original source finance.yahoo.com ; from gnews:67a905d722fae62095fd741e 2026-09-04] NVIDIA is reportedly discussing an approximately $2.5 billion investment in Thinking Machines Lab; no completion date is stated.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: Nvidia is separately in discussions to invest approximately $2.5 billion\\\\\\\\n8734 e4648 - e4648 [rumour; Calcalist Tech, citing Reuters; original source Unnamed people familiar with the discussions cited by Reuters ; from gnews:767d795fbdf40bc90ce11e15 2026-09-14] People familiar with discussions told Reuters that Nvidia could invest up to $10 billion in Anthropic’s potential IPO.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: Nvidia could invest as much as $10 billion\\\\\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4669; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\\\\\n8734 e4729 - e4729 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:6261d9e9a1fe8d22c05f5e82 2026-09-15] NVIDIA spent more than $42 billion buying equity stakes in other companies in the first half of FY2027, versus about $1.2 billion in the prior-year first half.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: Nvidia spent more than $42 billion buying equity stakes in other companies in the first half of the fiscal year, up from about $1.2 billion a year earlier.\\\\\\\\n8595 e1786 - e1786 [third_party_view; Patrick Sanders, The Motley Fool; original source Amazon, Meta Platforms, Microsoft, and Alphabet ; from gnews:c8ac167e2356a75994ebc26f 2026-08-13] Amazon, Meta Platforms, Microsoft, and Alphabet indicated they expect combined AI-infrastructure spending to exceed $730 billion in calendar 2026 and increase in calendar 2027.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: Amazon , Meta Platforms , Microsoft , and Alphabet have indicated they will spend more than $730 billion combined on AI infrastructure this year, and they expect that number to increase next year.\\\\\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1583, e1925; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\\\\\n8595 e1926 - e1926 [third_party_view; uk.finance.yahoo.com, citing Bank of America; original source Bank of America ; from gnews:1219126db2e6631aa1264142 2026-08-16] Bank of America said analyst consensus for hyperscalers’ calendar 2027 spending rose from $480 billion in August 2025 to $1.08 trillion in August 2026, an increase of about 127%.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: What analysts expect the hyperscalers to spend in 2027 alone has more than doubled in the space of a year, from a consensus of $480 billion (€416bn) in August 2025 to $1.08 trillion (€943bn) this month, a rise of about 127%, according to Bank of America.\\\\\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1559, e2008; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\\\\\n8595 e2535 - e2535 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said cloud-industry backlog exceeded $2 trillion and top-five hyperscaler capital expenditures were expected to approach $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: With cloud industry backlog now greater than $2 trillion, CapEx by the top 5 hyperscalers is expected to reach nearly $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\\\\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e465, e3124, e3306, e3307, e3372, e3401, e3405, e3485, e4112; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\\\\\n8730 e3108 - e3108 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Colette Kress 2026-08-26; from gnews:b39d8c4b1f73b622347a66e4 2026-08-28] CFO Colette Kress guided to 70% growth for NVIDIA revenue for the full fiscal year; the article says this was ahead of analyst estimates.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: As if this weren't enough, Kress guided 70% growth for the full fiscal year, which was ahead of analyst estimates.\\\\\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4226, e4227, e4386, e4400, e4913; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\\\\\n8730 e4900 - e4900 [party_statement; crn.com; original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 2026-09-18] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said NVIDIA expected revenue to grow approximately 70% next year because of supply constraints.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: we expect to grow approximately 70 percent as we are supply constrained.\\\\\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4400; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\\\\\ne3108 extract 5149 29715 nt marked 138% annual growth to sit at $40.3 billion. This growth suggested that the firm's business was not solely dependent on hyperscaler orders and was diversifying. As if this weren't enough, Kress guided 70% growth for the full fiscal year, which was ahead of analyst estimates.\\\\\\\\nYet, digging deeper, all might not be well at NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA). The firm's free cash flow in the quarter dropped to $21.3 billion in the second quarter f\\\\\\\\ne2532 extract 4491 29034 rastructure buildout, supported by an expanding and diverse set of growth opportunities, spanning hyperscalers, AI labs, AI natives, enterprises and sovereign customers. We expect to grow revenue by approximately 70% in fiscal 2028. This is a supply-constrained outlook. Q2 data center revenue increased 18% quarter-over-quarter to $89 billion with strong contributions from both sub segments hyperscale and ACIE, which includes our NeoClou\\\\\\\\ne2889 extract 4778 27523 as fielding takeover interest.\\\\\\\\nNvidia and Hugging Face did not respond to requests for comment.\\\\\\\\nNvidia has increasingly ramped up dealmaking with its enormous cash pile. The company said Wednesday that it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest of its fiscal year, on top of $47.9 billion it already holds in private companies.\\\\\\\\nMicrosoft also met with Hugging Face, but the person familiar and a second person said talks are not ongoing.\\\\\\\\nNvidia already has a relationship with Hugging Face. The ch\\\\\\\\n[]\\\\\\\\n1 views 47 judgements 1609 dep cites 0\\\\\\\\n2 views 43 judgements 1616 dep cites 0\\\\\\\\n3 views 49 judgements 1707 dep cites 0\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r45.stream:91:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_47\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\\\\\\\\nD=decimal.Decimal\\\\\\\\ndef db(i,name='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''views'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\\\\\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',uri=True)\\\\\\\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\\\\\\\n return c\\\\\\\\ndef req(a,j):\\\\\\\\n c=a.execute('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',(j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],)).fetchone()\\\\\\\\n assert c and c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']==j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] and c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''purpose'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''judge'\\\