\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)\\\\\\\\n p=p[1].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[0] if len(p)==2 else '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''none'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n print(j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''publication_day'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''view_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''rung'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],p[:390])\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-07-14 v14 8752 3 About $387 billion: $81.6 billion in Q1 and $91 billion guided for Q2 imply roughly 11.5% sequential growth; carrying that growth forward gives approximately $101.5 billion in Q3 and $113.2 billion in Q4, totaling about $387 billion. \\\\\\\\n- v8 (open; first_is_bullish) How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?: now rung 3 Neutral, judged 2026-07-14\\\\\\\\n    Comparison point stated by that judgement: NVIDIA's forecast of $20 billion in stand-alone CPU sales for FY2027 is the market/company reference and sits at the lower boundary of rung 2.\\\\\\\\n    The system's forecast for it (our own judgement, n\\\\\\\\n2026-07-15 v14 8756 2 Carrying the sequential growth from Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion to Q2 guidance of $91 billion forward implies about $101.5 billion in Q3 and $113.2 billion in Q4, or roughly $387 billion for FY2027. Adding the dependency's approximately $19.5 billion stand-alone CPU forecast gives about $407 billion. \\\\\\\\n- v8 (open; first_is_bullish) How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?: now rung 3 Neutral, judged 2026-07-15\\\\\\\\n    Comparison point stated by that judgement: NVIDIA’s FY2027 stand-alone CPU sales forecast of $20 billion; this reference is at the lower boundary of rung 2.\\\\\\\\n    The system's forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): About $19.5 bil\\\\\\\\n2026-07-16 v14 8759 2 About $407 billion: $81.6 billion in Q1 plus $91 billion guided for Q2, with Q2's sequential growth carried into Q3 and Q4, implies roughly $387 billion; adding the dependency's approximately $19.5 billion stand-alone CPU forecast gives about $407 billion. \\\\\\\\n- v8 (open; first_is_bullish) How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?: now rung 3 Neutral, judged 2026-07-16\\\\\\\\n    Comparison point stated by that judgement: NVIDIA's $20 billion FY2027 stand-alone CPU sales forecast is the market/company reference and sits at rung 2, the $20 billion lower boundary.\\\\\\\\n    The system's forecast for it (our own judgement, n\\\\\\\\n2026-07-17 v14 8763 2 Q1 revenue of $81.615 billion followed by Q2 guidance of $91 billion implies about $387 billion for FY2027 if Q2's sequential growth rate carries through Q3 and Q4. Adding the dependency's approximately $19 billion stand-alone CPU estimate as incremental implies about $406 billion. \\\\\\\\n- v8 (open; first_is_bullish) How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?: now rung 3 Neutral, judged 2026-07-17\\\\\\\\n    Comparison point stated by that judgement: NVIDIA’s approximately $20 billion FY2027 stand-alone CPU sales forecast is the market reference and sits at the lower boundary of rung 2.\\\\\\\\n    The system's forecast for it (our own judgement, not e\\\\\\\\n2026-07-18 v14 8766 2 Applying the Q1-to-Q2 sequential growth rate (about 11.5%) to Q2's $91 billion guidance for Q3 and Q4 gives approximately $387 billion for FY2027. Adding the dependency's approximately $19 billion stand-alone CPU estimate gives an implied total of about $406 billion, in rung 2. \\\\\\\\n- v8 (open; first_is_bullish) How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?: now rung 3 Neutral, judged 2026-07-17\\\\\\\\n    Comparison point stated by that judgement: NVIDIA’s approximately $20 billion FY2027 stand-alone CPU sales forecast is the market reference and sits at the lower boundary of rung 2.\\\\\\\\n    The system's forecast for it (our own judgement, not e\\\\\\\\n2026-07-20 v14 8770 3 Using Q1 FY2027 revenue of $81.615 billion and Q2 guidance of $91 billion, the 11.5% sequential increase carried forward gives approximately $101.5 billion for Q3 and $113.2 billion for Q4, or about $387 billion for FY2027. The approximately $19 billion stand-alone CPU estimate is included within, not added to, total company revenue. \\\\\\\\n- v8 (open; first_is_bullish) How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?: now rung 3 Neutral, judged 2026-07-20\\\\\\\\n    Comparison point stated by that judgement: NVIDIA's $20 billion FY2027 stand-alone CPU sales target; it sits at the lower boundary of rung 2. No separate market-consensus figure is supplied.\\\\\\\\n    The system's forecast for it (our own judgeme\\\\\\\\n2026-09-20 v9 9024 3 About $388 billion: v14's approximately $419 billion total-revenue forecast, based on reported first-half results, Q3 guidance adjusted for the reported beat history, and carried-forward sequential growth into Q4, multiplied by the latest 92.5% Data Center mix. This is below the $400 billion rung-2 boundary. \\\\\\\\n- v14 (open; first_is_bullish) How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?: now rung 2 Bullish, judged 2026-09-20\\\\\\\\n    Comparison point stated by that judgement: Wall Street analysts expect about $411 billion of FY2027 revenue (rung 2). Zacks’ 87.4% growth estimate against FY2026 revenue of about $215.9 billion implies about $404.5 billion, also rung 2.\\\\\\\\n    The system's forecas\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r45.stream:101:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_52\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\\\\\\\\nD=decimal.Decimal\\\\\\\\ndef db(i,name='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''views'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\\\\\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',uri=True)\\\\\\\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\\\\\\\n return c\\\\\\\\ndef req(a,j):\\\\\\\\n c=a.execute('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',(j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],)).fetchone()\\\\\\\\n assert c and c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']==j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] and c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''purpose'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''judge'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',dict(j)\\\\\\\\n d=json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_json'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\\\\\n return d,json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''answer_json'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\\\\\nEVID=re.compile(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'^- (e'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\[.*?(?=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'^- e'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\