\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\\\\\n  if id in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v7'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v37'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'') and i\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'!=2:\\\\\\\\n   for key,x in ed.items():\\\\\\\\n    if key in raw['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''cites'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] and tag(x,r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''Oracle|72%|1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.3 trillion'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\\\\\n     print(x.split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    Opinion'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')[0][:680])\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"1 v28 9016 09-20 The company-based reference is about $43 billion ($25 billion of commitments as of July 26 plus $18 billion committed for the rest of FY2027), which is rung 2. No dated market consensus is supplied. About $75 billion outstanding at the FY2027 annual report: use Bank of America’s approximately $70 billion commitment estimate as the anchor and allow a modest net increase for later disclosed deals, discounted for overlap and funding before the report.\\\\\\\\n1 v7 8890 09-19 BofA's $1.08 trillion 2027 consensus estimate covers five companies. Subtracting the carried Oracle estimate of roughly $100–$150 billion gives about $930–$980 billion for the four companies in this question, which is rung 3. About $1.15–$1.20 trillion, centered near $1.16 trillion: NVIDIA's $1.3 trillion top-five forecast less the carried roughly $100–$150 billion Oracle estimate. This is in rung 4.\\\\\\\\n- e2685 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said cloud-industry backlog exceeds $2 trillion and top-five hyperscaler CapEx is expected to approach $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: With cloud industry backlog now greater than $2 trillion, CapEx by the top 5 hyperscalers is expected to reach nearly $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\\\\\\\n- e3281 [third_party_view; insidermonkey.com; original source Steve Eisman 2026-08-13; from gnews:afc4112f1dd4c804f27af950 2026-08-28] Steve Eisman estimated on August 13 that OpenAI and Anthropic generate roughly 70% of Microsoft, Amazon, Google, and Oracle’s AI-related revenue and 25%–35% of their cloud revenue.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Big Short\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" investor Steve Eisman warned on CNBC's \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Fast Money\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" on August 13 that OpenAI and Anthropic account for roughly 70% of AI-related revenue at Microsoft, Amazon, Google, and Oracle, and as much as 25% to 35% of those companies' cloud revenue.\\\\\\\\n- e4256 [party_statement; fool.com (Manali Pradhan); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:49351bd6de4706de524baf5f 2026-09-05] NVIDIA expects the top five hyperscalers' combined capital expenditures to approach $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: Nvidia also expects the combined capital expenditures of the top five hyperscalers to approach $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\\\\\\\n- e5031 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com (analyst), citing Reuters’ account of BofA Global Research estimates; original source BofA Global Research ; from gnews:ca2f580191a4509ac38bc1cf 2026-09-15] BofA Global Research estimated that Microsoft, Alphabet, Amazon, Meta and Oracle would spend roughly $795 billion on capital expenditures in calendar 2026 and $1.08 trillion in calendar 2027, a 36% increase year over year.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: Reuters cited BofA Global Research estimates showing Microsoft, Alphabet ( NASDAQ:GOOG ), Amazon ( NASDAQ:AMZN ), Meta ( NASDAQ:META ) and Oracle ( NYSE:ORCL ) could collectively pour roughly $795 billion into capital expenditures in 2026 before pu\\\\\\\\n- e5046 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:5adb2372d28f9339f479435d 2026-09-15] NVIDIA said the top five hyperscalers are expected to spend nearly $800 billion on capital expenditures in calendar 2026 and $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: The company said the top five hyperscalers are expected to spend nearly $800 billion on capital expenditures in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\\\\\\\n- e5076 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-09-16; from gnews:8cdef40aebf24cdc89f530ff 2026-09-16] The top five hyperscalers’ annual capital spending is expected to reach $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: The figure is expected to increase to $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\\\\\\\n- e5086 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com author; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:3f21db1f9791e20f80909da8 2026-09-16] NVIDIA management pegged top-five hyperscaler capital expenditures at nearly $800 billion in calendar 2026 and $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: top-five hyperscaler CapEx management pegged at nearly $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\\\\\\\n- e5155 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4fbadb3b4cb5846297a34b0a 2026-09-16] NVIDIA estimates that the top five hyperscalers’ capital expenditures could reach $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027, up from $800 billion in 2026.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: Nvidia, for instance, estimates that the capex of the top five hyperscalers could increase to $1.3 trillion in 2027, up from $800 billion this year.\\\\\\\\n- e5308 [party_statement; Harsh Chauhan, fool.com, paraphrasing NVIDIA; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ad94c78d09fe41fc3f29bbca 2026-09-18] NVIDIA projected that the top five U.S. hyperscalers’ capital expenditures will total $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: Even better, Nvidia projects that this figure will jump to $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\\\\\\\n- e5328 [party_statement; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4ee5d8f73b7bcfc2f2111ad1 2026-09-19] The projected data center capital expenditures of the five largest AI hyperscalers rise to $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: Next year, that figure is projected to rise to $1.3 trillion.\\\\\\\\n2 v16 8735 09-20 NVIDIA’s approximately $20 billion FY2027 standalone CPU outlook is the reference; $20 billion falls at rung 3. Approximately $25 billion or slightly more for FY2027: about $20 billion from Vera standalone CPU sales plus a roughly $5 billion Grace contribution, using Grace’s reported greater-than-$5-billion trailing-12-month revenue as the recent run-rate proxy.\\\\\\\\n2 v29 8734 09-20 Bank of America's roughly $70 billion estimate of NVIDIA's equity investments in ecosystem partners; this is rung 3 ($50 billion to below $75 billion). Its period and whether it measures outstanding commitments are unclear. About $53 billion: $25 billion of commitments reported as of July 26 plus $18 billion committed for the remainder of FY2027, then the $3.5 billion MediaTek investment announced after that remainder-of-year figure and a risk-adjusted contribution from the $10 billion Anthropic and $2.5 billion Thinking Machines discussions.\\\\\\\\n2 v6 8595 09-19 Calendar-2027 hyperscaler spending consensus is about $1.08 trillion (e1926), in rung 3 ($900 billion to below $1.1 trillion). About $1.19 trillion for the four named hyperscalers: apply the prior approximate $730 billion/$800 billion four-to-five share proxy to NVIDIA’s $1.3 trillion top-five calendar-2027 CapEx estimate (e2535; repeated in e4756 and later reports).\\\\\\\\n2 v9 8737 09-20 The market reference supplied by the previous conclusion is approximately $414 billion for FY2027, which sits at rung 2 ($400 billion to below $450 billion). Approximately $410 billion: $164 billion reported in the first half, about $100 billion implied for Q3 from the $108 billion total-revenue guide and recent Data Center mix, and roughly $146 billion estimated for Q4. The Q4 estimate reflects management's expected hyperscale reacceleration and Rubin ramp, with a discounted contribution from SemiAnalysis's forecast that second-half Data Center revenue would exceed analyst estimates by 20%.\\\\\\\\n3 v14 9182 09-20 NVIDIA’s roughly $20 billion FY2027 standalone CPU outlook is the relevant company reference and sits at rung 2 ($20 billion to less than $25 billion); it is not a total-CPU figure. Just above $25 billion: carry the approximately $20 billion FY2027 standalone CPU outlook forward and add Grace’s reported trailing-12-month revenue run-rate of more than $5 billion.\\\\\\\\n3 v3 9183 09-20 Wall Street analysts expect about $411 billion for FY2027 (e4360, e5406), placing the reference in rung 2. About $446 billion: $177.837 billion in first-half revenue, approximately $113.6 billion for Q3 using the guidance midpoint and the cited average beat, and approximately $127 billion for Q4 by carrying forward 12% sequential growth, then adding about $27–28 billion for the estimated 20% second-half data-center-compute uplift.\\\\\\\\n3 v33 9175 09-20 The company-based reference is approximately $43 billion: $25 billion of commitments as of July 26 plus $18 billion committed for the rest of FY2027. That reference sits in rung 3 ($30 billion to less than $50 billion). Approximately $40–45 billion, centered near $43 billion: carry forward the reported $25 billion commitment balance together with the stated $18 billion remainder-of-FY2027 commitment, without adding later deal headlines that may overlap or count unfulfilled obligations as completed investments. This remains below the $50 billion rung-4 threshold.\\\\\\\\n3 v37 9173 09-20 NVIDIA management's FY2028 gross-margin guidance is 72%–73%. The range spans rung 3 at 72% and rung 2 above 72% through 73%; its midpoint of 72.5% lies in rung 2. About 72.0% for FY2028: I place the result at the floor of management's 72%–73% guidance because negotiated Q1 price increases support recovery, while rising memory prices and persistent supply constraints weigh against exceeding 72%.\\\\\\\\n- e2788 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA forecast Q3 FY2027 GAAP and non-GAAP gross margins of 73.5%–74.5%, Q4 FY2027 margins of 71%–72%, and FY2028 margins of 72%–73%.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: For Q3, we expect GAAP and non-GAAP gross margins to be 74% plus or minus 50 basis points. We expect margins to bottom in Q4 in the 71% to 72% range before settling at 72% to 73% in fiscal year '28, as executed price increases take effect in Q1.\\\\\\\\n3 v41 9166 09-20 NVIDIA management’s stated expectation that FY2028 CPU revenue will more than double the $20 billion FY2027 expectation implies more than $40 billion, which is rung 2. Roughly $38–39 billion for FY2028: the stated more-than-double expectation points above $40 billion, but is discounted for a forward Vera target without shipment volume in hand, with the competitive evidence adding execution risk.\\\\\\\\n3 v7 9044 09-19 Bank of America's reported analyst consensus of $1.08 trillion for 2027 hyperscaler capital spending (e2080) is the market reference and sits in rung 3 ($900 billion to below $1.1 trillion). The separate $1.08 trillion BofA estimate includes Microsoft, Alphabet, Amazon, Meta, and Oracle (e5056), so it is not an exact match for this four-company, data-center-only question. About $1.1 trillion, marginally above the rung-4 boundary. This is a judgmental scope-adjusted synthesis: NVIDIA's $1.3 trillion top-five 2027 capex forecast (e2759) is discounted for the fifth company and non-data-center capex, with the lower $1.08 trillion estimate (e5056) and execution constraints tempering it; no supplied evidence directly quantifies that discount.\\\\\\\\n- e2759 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said the five largest hyperscalers’ capital expenditures are expected to total nearly $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: With cloud industry backlog now greater than $2 trillion, CapEx by the top 5 hyperscalers is expected to reach nearly $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\\\\\\\n- e5056 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source BofA Global Research ; from gnews:ca2f580191a4509ac38bc1cf 2026-09-15] BofA Global Research estimated that Microsoft, Alphabet, Amazon, Meta and Oracle could spend $1.08 trillion collectively on capital expenditures in calendar 2027, about 36% more than in 2026.\\\\\\\\n    Quote: before pushing that figure to $1.08 trillion in 2027. That would represent an increase of about 36% in a single year\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r46.stream:14:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_7\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '3049,3083p;10957,11016p;2476,2483p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; cat .claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"## D186 · 2026-10-26 · Asset-thesis rungs describe business outcomes; the favourable end is registered per thesis\\\\n\\\\n- Alex chose option C (\\\\\\\"可以\\\\\\\"): rungs of an asset thesis state the business outcome (above, near or below guidance), and each thesis registers which end is favourable for the company, as a theme thesis's dependants already state a direction. Reason: results and direction separate (NVDA beat four quarters and fell; capital spending can build capacity or hurt returns). Recorded; not implemented in this slice: it changes `check_ladder`, the writer, judging, the UI adapter and the Idea route (value × reader), so it is its own slice with its own measurement.\\\\n\\\\n## D187 · 2026-10-26 · A company's own quantity sits under that company's object, private companies included\\\\n\\\\n- Alex chose option C (\\\\\\\"可以\\\\\\\"): any company's own quantity is a thesis under that company (SpaceX's compute capacity under SpaceX, Alphabet's capital spending under GOOGL), consistent with 06-views rule 5 (\\\\\\\"company figures use the fiscal year\\\\\\\"); a macro theme opens only when a thesis depends on it. Recorded; not implemented in this slice: it needs a private-company object kind in the universe and the one switch (01-universe), its own slice. Until then the gold accepts the Codex reading (evidence to NVDA data-center revenue) for SpaceX.\\\\n\\\\n## D260 · 2026-11-02 · A judgement is a forecast against a reference: the rung the evidence in force makes most likely, judged against what the market expects; the answer states the reference and the implied outcome (judging-v6)\\\\n\\\\n- Alex, 2026-11-02, asked whether the judge's stance should stay an absolute-band lookup (the current reading) or be judged relative to expectations: \\\\\\\"门槛没有标准，按照你作为 hedge fund analyst 的认识来定\\\\\\\". Decided by Claude under that delegation: the definition below is Claude's analyst judgement, recorded as such, not Alex's words.\\\\n- Mechanism (arm 4 draw 1, all 356 judgements read, `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/review-2026-11-02.md` §7 and `proof-judging-v6.txt`): 8 of 314 later judgements moved a rung and 320 of 356 reasons say \\\\\\\"remains\\\\\\\"; the FY2027 total revenue question was judged 12 times at neutral while its upward pushes grew from 1 to 35, every reason \\\\\\\"the $392 billion estimate is inside the band … does not establish $400 billion\\\\\\\"; the gross-margin judgement wrote \\\\\\\"leans toward rung 2 but does not warrant moving\\\\\\\"; the 2027 hyperscaler-capex theme stayed below the band management's own forecast names because the forecast \\\\\\\"is not fact\\\\\\\". The judging-v5 prompt asked the judge to \\\\\\\"be precise about what is established\\\\\\\" and said only fact can establish a rung: the model read \\\\\\\"established\\\\\\\" as the bar for leaving a rung and the consensus figure as the anchor. A second cause stays open: the ladder's neutral band is written at opening without naming what it compares against (PRD 06 ladder rule 2 asks for it); that is the extraction's rule and is not changed here.\\\\n- Decided, the analyst's rule: (1) the rung is a forecast, the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved; \\\\\\\"not established\\\\\\\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. (2) The reference is what the market expects: consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline; a consensus or guidance figure alone keeps the judgement at the reference's rung and, once other evidence has arrived, is never the reason to stay. (3) The judge derives the outcome the evidence implies (reported figures and guidance give a run-rate; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it), checks it against the dependencies' conclusions (a part cannot exceed its whole; a figure spanning several periods or products gives the question only its share), compares it with the rung boundaries and moves when it crosses one. (4) Weight follows tier and novelty: fact fixes what is known; party statements are the strongest forecast input; third-party views and rumours move the forecast in proportion to their specificity; a repeat, another outlet or an opinion with no new fact or calculation moves nothing. (5) The answer states `reference` and `implied_outcome` as required fields from `judging-v6` (`judging.schema_for`; code refuses an empty one; stored beside the rung in `judgements.reference` / `implied_outcome`; a ledger written before v6 gains the columns at its first write), so the D3 stance gold can read the reasoning, not only the rung. Written where the judgement is specified: PRD 06 State rules (`docs/system-design/new-facts.js` STATE_RULES, the generated block) and this record.\\\\n- Proof (`proof-judging-v6.txt`, `proof-judging-v6b.txt`: the last stored judgement request of 14 theses of arm 4 draw 1 re-sent once each under v6 and read beside the stored v5 answers, about a cent): every answer names the reference and derives the implied outcome. Six rungs moved against the stored ones: non-GAAP gross margin 3 → 2 (Q1 reported 75% and Q2 guided 75% sit on the rung-2 boundary), 2027 hyperscaler capex 4 → 5 (management's own \\\\\\\"more than $1 trillion\\\\\\\"), China accelerator share 4 → 5 (share \\\\\\\"fallen to zero\\\\\\\"), China H200 authorization No → Yes (a reported plan to permit named firms and reported progress in reviews, six months before the deadline), Data Center revenue 2 → 3 ($355–360 billion derived from Q1 and the total-revenue proxy, below the $360 billion boundary), Blackwell+Rubin revenue 2 → 1 in the first send by annualising a two-year \\\\\\\"$1 trillion visibility\\\\\\\" figure to $545 billion, a part above its whole: clause (3)'s consistency check was added for it and the re-send gives rung 2 ($320–360 billion, a share of the Data Center segment). Total revenue stays at 3 with the arithmetic shown (H1 $172.6 billion from Q1 and the Q2 guide; $400 billion needs more than $227 billion in H2). Prompt 2,453 → 3,782 characters: the request defined neither what a rung means nor a reference and its \\\\\\\"established\\\\\\\" wording forced the defect; the two sentences that carried it were cut. Configuration `poc-v90` (poc-v89 with judging-v6); the default stays `poc-v69`. Tests: `tests/test_stance_fields.py`. Measured by re-sent stored requests, not by an arm (Alex: \\\\\\\"不要再跑这些有的没的臂了\\\\\\\").\\\\n\\\\n## D261 · 2026-11-02 · A ruler or gold that is built and reviewed is never changed again\\\\n\\\\n- Alex, 2026-11-02, while the judgement ruler (D3) was being built: \\\\\\\"你的尺子做出来和金标真的不能再动了，已经造成了3天的各种漂移，非常的严重，我需要你记录到我们的决策和原则里面，我们做完的review过的尺子金标不能再动了\\\\\\\".\\\\n- The drift he names, counted: the extraction ruler went from the first standard (D229, 2026-10-29) to the signed page version 3 (D243, the same day) to version 5 (D250, 2026-10-31), the gold was re-derived from version 3 to version 5 with 62 recorded changes, and every score between D248 and 2026-10-31 had been read against the version-3 gold (the \\\\\\\"假的测量\\\\\\\" of 2026-10-31); the judgement step had no ruler at all until today. Three days of numbers that cannot be compared with each other.\\\\n- Decided (his words; written at the decision it governs, AGENTS §7.1): once a ruler and its gold have been reviewed (readers who did not write them read them against the decisions; Alex signed), neither the definition nor the gold changes again. A defect found later is a dated correction record beside the gold (`corrections-*.json`), printed with every score and never merged in. A new definition is a new version that only his decision opens, with its own gold derived from scratch; old scores stay as they were and are never compared with the new. A ruler under construction is edited only until that review, and nothing is scored against it before.\\\\n- What is locked by this record: the extraction standard page (`docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html`, version 3 signed D243, with D250's four boundaries and counting unit) and `golden-v5/` (sha256 in `golden-v5.sha256`): no version 6; the loop's desk ruler (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/README.md`, D1–D3). What is still under construction and locks at his review: the judgement ruler `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/ruler-v1.md`, its reader brief, question list and gold `gold-v1.json` (the sign-off is a separate record).\\\\n\\\\n## D262 · 2026-11-02 · The judgement ruler (D3) and its gold are fixed: the gold is reader B's answers; frozen at sha256 636c056d1e4252fa…\\\\n\\\\n- Alex, 2026-11-02, after reading the two readers' reasoning on every disagreement (readers A and B differed on 3 of 23 questions by range or yes/no and on 12 of 20 direction labels; the system disagreed with the draft on the total revenue and Vera CPU questions in every draw): \\\\\\\"那就不要理A了；我们就go with B 好吧，定下尺子金表\\\\\\\".\\\\n- Fixed by that decision: the ruler `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/ruler-v1.md` (unit: a gold question at the window end 2026-07-14; material: golden-v5's 309 items by sha; a numeric question agrees when the gold's implied range overlaps the band of the rung the judge chose, a yes/no question when the answers match; the two null baselines printed with every score); the question list and the must_open mapping as built (`questions-v1.json`, 22 seeds + the Ohio guarantee); the gold `gold-v1.json` = reader B's 23 answers verbatim (B: a fresh-context Claude reader, model-authored, 3 questions marked no material: CoWoS capacity, semiconductor growth, SK Telecom), sha256 `636c056d1e4252fa759660803067e6ccd67a81067b012905e918aa9dec4005f2` in `gold-v1.sha256` and in `score_judgement.py`, which refuses any other. Reader A (Codex) stays beside it as the control record (`reader-A.json`, `reconcile-v1.md`): its distance from B is the stick's own noise. Claude's two proposals of the afternoon (a three-level score when readers split; toss-up questions excluded) were not adopted: one range per question, every question counts. From here D261 applies: nothing in the ruler or the gold changes; a defect is a dated record in `corrections-v1.json`.\\\\n- First measurement on the frozen gold (`score-r4-identity.txt`, arm 4, three draws, judging-v5): judged questions agreeing 13/19, 15/18, 12/17; the lookup baseline (the rung containing the gold's reference figure) 9/15, 8/14, 8/14; always-neutral 5/11, 5/10, 5/10. Disagreeing in every draw: FY2027 total revenue (gold $400–435 billion, judge neutral by consensus lookup) and Vera CPU revenue (gold $8–18 billion, judge the top rung on management's $20 billion at face value); in two of three: the financing-commitments total (gold $25–60 billion, judge $10–20 billion). Never judged in any draw: NVIDIA's own capex (q12); the operating margin in two draws (q10): evidence never reached them, counted apart as \\\\\\\"no judgement\\\\\\\". The new judge (`judging-v6`, D260) has no run to score yet; a run on `poc-v90` is Alex's call.\\\\n\\\\n## D263 · 2026-11-02 · The judge is written to the frozen gold's own reasoning (judging-v7, poc-v91); a gap to the gold is closed in the judge, not re-measured\\\\n\\\\n- Alex, after the first score on the frozen gold was reported as the system being \\\\\\\"wrong\\\\\\\" on some questions: \\\\\\\"不是啊什么叫错？我不是和你说了就按照claude的标准来就好了嘛\\\\\\\". The gold is Claude's (reader B's) standard by D262; a disagreement is the distance between the judge and that standard, to be closed in the judge's rule, not a verdict to be measured again.\\\\n- What reader B does that judging-v6 did not, read from B's answers on the questions that differed (`judgement-gold/reconcile-v1.md`, `gold-v1.json`): carries the guided growth forward rather than annualising the last quarter flat (Data Center, total revenue); discounts a management target for a product with no shipments by default (Vera CPU: two selling quarters, four million units at $5,000, the company's own choice of another CPU); sizes an announced but unsized commitment from its disclosed comparable (the Firmus backstop from Sharon's); derives a figure no one states from the accounting identities in the evidence (capex from operating less free cash flow); keeps linked conclusions consistent (China share against the H200 authorization theme). Written into `judging-v7.txt` as five clauses (v6 3,782 → 4,924 characters; reason: each clause is a behaviour of the frozen standard the judge lacked), named by `poc-v91`; schema and code unchanged.\\\\n- Proof on the stored requests of the questions whose arm-4 judgement differed from the gold (`proof-judging-v7a.txt`, `proof-judging-v7.txt`; one send each, cents): total revenue rung 3 → 2 (about $421 billion from the guided growth on FY2026's base; gold $400–435 billion), Data Center 3 → 2 (about $372 billion; gold $370–400 billion), Vera CPU 1 → 2 ($12 to below $20 billion, the target discounted for the volume not in hand; gold $8–18 billion), DRAM prices 3 → 2 (about +15%; gold +10–35%), financing total stays 4 ($33.5–39.8 billion; gold $25–60 billion), the Ohio guarantee stays Yes; China share stays below 1% in draw 1, consistent with that draw's H200 theme judged No (the gold has the authorization likely and the share 1–8%; the consistency clause ties the share to the theme, so it moves with it). Six of the seven re-sent questions now land in the gold's band; the end-to-end agreement under judging-v7 needs a run on `poc-v91`, which is Alex's call. A placement gap seen on the way: the Vera CPU question never held the fall-launch statement (filed under the Rubin launch questions), so the judge could not count selling quarters from evidence; the default-discount clause covers it, the filing is a D2 class to count.\\\\n\\\\n## D264 · 2026-11-02 · The extraction reads the day's open questions with their takes lines and files the statements itself (extraction v72, poc-v92): the one-decider architecture Alex chose is built and measured against poc-v91 on the frozen ruler\\\\n\\\\n- Alex, 2026-11-02 evening, after asking why the open library was never adopted as the extraction's context (\\\\\\\"你为什么架构上没有采纳我说的开的库作为step 2 context\\\\\\\"; the answer traced the chain from his 10-31 instruction through the one-draw v82 replay I judged \\\\\\\"不采用\\\\\\\" myself to the D256 proposal left waiting): \\\\\\\"我们非常专注的验证这个架构选择：我们有金标和尺子frozen可以比；我们这个架构设计的核心就是透过适当的Prompt 和引入已经开的题，和题的叙述来决定抽取；现在最新的prompt有修改了很多小毛病，你看是不是用最新最好的prompt + v72这边告诉模型怎么用读取开题库的prompt 来做新的实验prompt。充分理解我的ask然后get it worked out\\\\\\\". This is his choice of the one-decider architecture (review-2026-11-02.md §4 way (i), the D256 proposal) and of its base prompt.\\\\n- Built (design: `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/design-v72.md`, the four tables of AGENTS §2, predictions frozen at sha256 `aec1bb40…` in `predictions-v72.sha256` before any send): extraction version 72, named by `poc/config/poc-v92.json` (= poc-v91 with T*-v72 and no placement setting). The request shows the questions open at the start of the item's day (D251's snapshot) each with the code-written takes line the placer read (`placement.question_lines`, one writer for both requests); the schema defines the evidence field `links` by the same rule (`placement.FILING_RULE`, the placer's v4 system-prompt rule restated beside the field: the narrowest open question whose takes line covers the statement, whoever says it, with or without a period or amount, plus the answer's own candidates, else empty); `role-v72.txt` is `role-v66.txt` with its first paragraph pointing at [Open questions] and the links field (the latest extraction prompt on the frozen extraction gold: v53 → v65 gold-rejected kept per draw about 109 → 59 with core and supporting flat, v66 = v65 + R3's boundary, `r3-final-scores-Y6.txt`); `categories-v72.json` and `review-v72.txt` are v66's. The extraction's links file each statement: one linked to an open question is filed there, one linked only to its candidates follows them, one linked to nothing is dropped as 'no home' (D209; the handover's reason is the same word, so `e2e_funnel` and `dropped_census` read it); no placement call exists for v72 (`extraction.one_decider`, `places` ends at v71). v71's `new_in_it` and `moves` fields are not asked (`MOVES_FIELDS_VERSIONS`). Settled by me under the delegation of 2026-11-01, and said so: the candidate rules stay v66's (propose when the item raises it; code owns identity and folds a duplicate of an open question, D258), not v71's \\\\\\\"only for a matter no open question covers\\\\\\\", which halved the candidates and the homes in v82; it is one sentence to tighten if the questions ruler says so.\\\\n- Two wirings of D251's snapshot were wrong and are fixed in the same change, each with a test that fails on its mutant (`tests/test_one_decider.py`): (1) before the first completed day the snapshot was empty, so the seeds (seq 0, D253) were invisible to every first-day item while the placer of poc-v91 saw them (`store.day_start_seq` is 0 before the first completed day); (2) the takes line prints a question's group names and aliases, which D257's alias merges change within a day, so the request bytes would have changed mid-day, the parallel day would have re-sent every waiting request, and two items of one day would have seen different lists (`store.groups_of_view_at` reads memberships and aliases at the snapshot's seq). Version gates: v53's and v71's request bytes are unchanged (tests); 274 tests pass; `scripts/preflight.py` over arm 4 draw 1 replays 243 stored answers through the current checks with the same 22 refusals as before (`preflight-v72-prep.txt`).\\\\n- Proof before the run (cents; `harness/resend_extract_v72.py`, `proof-v72-links.txt`: the four rack-delay articles of 2026-07-05/06 rebuilt under v72 from arm 4 draw 1's day-start snapshots, three sends each; the stored outcome of the same run as the control). The statements that name nothing (\\\\\\\"Our roadmap is intact\\\\\\\", the scrapped backup plan, NVL72x2 back-to-back racks), which the placer dropped or filed under same-day duplicate questions in every arm since 10-31, are filed under the seed question v18 (Rubin Ultra / Kyber NVL144 shipping) in 3/3 sends of the SemiAnalysis article (both statements), 3/3 of the Tom's Hardware article (NVL72x2; the denial 2/3 with one send's quote refused), 3/3 of the Cramer article (to v18, v2 or v31 by send), while in the Asian-suppliers article the NVL72x2 statement went once to no home and twice to the revenue questions (v1/v2, v2/v20: a sink link; the Kyber question v33 the control's placer used was opened that same day and is outside the snapshot). Zero candidates in 27 sends over nine matched articles against the control's four, all four Kyber duplicates of v18 (the list shown does the deduplication the matching step did after the fact). Request size 22–38K characters (27–44 open questions) against the control's mean 19.8K.\\\\n- The measurement, launched 2026-11-02 18:05 at his \\\\\\\"get it worked out\\\\\\\": `arms/r6-one-decider-v92/d1..3` against `arms/r6-control-v91/d1..3` (the acceptance run he stopped at 17:27, now the control, since arm 4 and v92 are separated by D258, D259 and D263 as well), 2026-07-01..14, seeds v2, eight extraction workers each, cap $3 a draw; scored on the frozen ruler (`e2e_funnel.py`, `score_judgement.py`), regressions first, every number, in `log.md` row 12 and `design-v72.md` §8. Whether poc-v92 becomes the default is his call after the numbers.\\\\n- Measured (six draws finished 19:40; `e2e-funnel-r6-v72.txt`, `judgement-gold/score-r6-*`, `matter-states-r6-v72.txt`, `probe-v72-sink.txt`; three-draw means, v91 → v92). Regressions first: core matters reaching judgement 76.3 → 73.7 of 86 (predicted ≥ +2, the null is ±2), core dropped for no home 4.0 → 5.7, article-opened questions 11.7 → 3.0 (candidates 65 → 6.7: the list shown suppresses proposals even with the candidate rule unchanged; must_open 28/28 and may_open 40/42 in both arms because the seeds cover them, the Ohio guarantee being the one visible loss), supporting not extracted 25.3 → 46.0. Held: supporting reaching 94.0 → 90.0 (at the −4 line), noise reaching 89.2 → 56.9 (−36%), judgement agreement 17/19, 17/18, 17/19 → 15/18, 16/17, 17/18 against lookup 8–9/14–15, cost $1.15 → $0.88 a draw with model time −36% and wall clock 95 → 46 minutes for three draws, zero re-sent requests. Two mechanisms, both in sentences and neither in the architecture: (1) the sink is back: 60–62% of links on the three company-wide revenue questions against v91's 34–40%, 190–208 statements a draw under both total and Data Center revenue against 5–6; the model's own account in three of three cases cites the figure-line takes clause D259 added (\\\\\\\"what makes that figure more or less likely: the demand, supply, competition and pricing behind it\\\\\\\") and concedes the links field's \\\\\\\"narrowest only\\\\\\\" should have excluded the broader question or the link altogether; (2) role-v66's end-of-request check removes 21 supporting matters a draw that v53 keeps (20 matters extracted in v91 in at least two draws and in v92 in at most one: third parties' actions and views, named hires and partners, product milestones, standard §5.1 kinds 2–3), a loss the extraction bench's \\\\\\\"supporting in at least two draws\\\\\\\" count had hidden. Verdict: as built, v72 is neither better nor worse than v91 on the desk's counts and is cleaner, cheaper and faster; it does not become the default and no further arm is sent before the two mechanisms are fixed at their owners with $0 proofs: the root/driver pair collapsed to the narrower question by code (identity, D207's rule), the figure-line clause reworded and proved on re-sent stored v92 requests, and the base text (v53 against v66 under the architecture) put to Alex.\\\\n\\\\n## D725 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 45/45b: the number answers fail because related numbers have no shared, checked calculation; one judge version and one test recommended to Alex\\\\n\\\\n- **Alex's words** (2026-11-22): \\\\\\\"work with counsel and have a look at the traces of this problem … what is wrong with the system design\\\\n  overall … look at the code, look at the traces, deeply battle it out with counsel … because I think it's the most important thing\\\\n  that we don't hallucinate with the numbers, and I want you to get this right\\\\\\\".\\\\n- **The record:** `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/` (`RESULT.md`).\\\\n  - Claude's reflection was written before Codex's.\\\\n  - Codex ran an independent investigation (fresh thread `01a20501…`) and a challenge round.\\\\n  - Consensus. One wording point stays open: the $146B is arithmetically a residual, but the order of the judge's choices is unknown.\\\\n- **Diagnosis:**\\\\n  1. Answers are prose; code ties no figure to a source and recomputes nothing. The production check passes contradictory or invented\\\\n     figures.\\\\n  2. Related questions compute the same quantities separately. The unit is one question, with 0 dependencies.\\\\n  3. Filing and the evidence in view split their inputs. The previous conclusion carries figures without provenance.\\\\n  4. Opening's bands amplify an error.\\\\n- **Measured:**\\\\n  - Data Center Q4 above company Q4 on at least 13 of 26 days in old-1;\\\\n  - Data Center's full year above the total's on 20 consecutive days in old-2;\\\\n  - different Q3 bases on 17 of 18 paired days;\\\\n  - shared evidence between total and Data Center 8% in old-2;\\\\n  - 17 of the 24 double-rejected answers from unchecked arithmetic.\\\\n- **Recommended design** (a new judge version, Alex's to open):\\\\n  - one judging call per related family, each question keeping its answer from one calculation;\\\\n  - figures labelled by the judge (source, calculation, assumption; scope and period);\\\\n  - code checks only identity and arithmetic (figure in quote, recompute, part within whole, one value per shared quantity, a sourced\\\\n    reference);\\\\n  - unreconciled forecasts shown as unresolved;\\\\n  - extraction unchanged;\\\\n  - families declared for the test.\\\\n- **Interim for a first release:** number questions shown as \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\" until they pass the checks.\\\\n- **The test:** a $0 gate (hand reconstructions of five stored cases, four gold controls, three planted errors), then a paid gate\\\\n  (36 calls; joint against separate on the three draws' 09-20 pair, plus O, S and E singletons). Pass and stop lines are in `RESULT.md`.\\\\n- **Not done:** nothing built, sent or changed.\\\\n\\\\n## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\" as the first-release interim\\\\n\\\\n- **The questions** (after D725):\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"要不要开一个新的判官版本来试修法（相关的题合在一次里算，每个数字标明出处，程序检查算术和出处）？\\\\\\\" Options: 开，先做 0 元那一关\\\\n    (recommended: the format and checks designed and through the council, then the $0 gate on five stored cases, four gold controls and\\\\n    three planted errors; the paid gate asks Alex for its ceiling); 先不开.\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"第一版上线前的过渡：数字题只显示问题和来源，档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'，等通过检查再放出来。你同意这个做法吗？\\\\\\\" Options: 同意\\\\n    (recommended); 暂不定.\\\\n- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \\\\\\\"开，先做 0 元那一关 (推荐)\\\\\\\"; \\\\\\\"同意 (推荐)\\\\\\\".\\\\n- **Decided (Alex):**\\\\n  - A new judge version is opened for the bounded test of D725: related number questions judged together, with labelled figures and\\\\n    code checks of identity and arithmetic. It is designed and reviewed at $0, then the $0 gate runs. The paid gate needs Alex's\\\\n    ceiling.\\\\n  - Until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \\\\\\\"Forecast unavailable\\\\\\\": the band, the\\\\n    forecast text and its history withheld together. It is built with the release work, which is not started.\\\\n- poc-v118 stays the product.\\\\n---\\\\nname: prompt-audit\\\\ndescription: After every measurement of an extraction configuration, and before any prompt change, map each failure class in the stored draws to the sentence of the request that produced it, check that sentence against the frozen standard and the prompt principles, and write the audit table. Alex, 2026-11-02 - \\\\\\\"你应该看着prompt，然后对比失败的trace，然后仔细的根据尺子做对比，并且我们prompt的principle也要带入，是尝试教他general hedge fund analyst skill，不是要hardcode或是benchmark farming；你把这个写成一个skill以后固定跑\\\\\\\".\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n# Prompt audit: failures → the request's sentences → the standard → the principle\\\\n\\\\nRun this after every measured configuration (three draws scored on the frozen ruler) and before any edit to a prompt file, a schema\\\\ndescription or a takes line. A measurement without this audit is a score without a diagnosis (AGENTS §7.2, §6). The audit is read,\\\\nnot scripted: the scripts below only produce the lists to read.\\\\n\\\\n## 0. Inputs\\\\n\\\\n- The arm's run folders (`docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/arms/<arm>/d1..3`) and the baseline's.\\\\n- The frozen ruler (AGENTS §7.1): the extraction standard `docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html` (version 3, D243, with D250's\\\\n  boundaries), golden-v5, the questions standard, the judgement gold. Never edited; every disagreement is a gap in the system.\\\\n- The prompt principles (AGENTS §6 and §8): the prompt carries the standard and no new rule; it teaches a general hedge-fund\\\\n  analyst, so every sentence and example reads the same for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip maker, names no covered\\\\n  company, product or number, and takes no example from a test article; a classification is a closed set with examples; never grow a\\\\n  prompt to fix quality without cutting as much elsewhere; a field's definition sits in the schema beside the field; code owns\\\\n  identity, never importance.\\\\n\\\\n## 1. Dump the request as the model reads it\\\\n\\\\nOne stored request of the configuration (any article), printed whole: the system text (the role), every user block before the item\\\\n(category block, subjects, research reference, open questions with their takes lines, research groups), the closing sentence, the\\\\nend-of-request check, and every schema field description (evidence and candidates). Read it top to bottom once. List every\\\\ninstruction that decides keep, reject, link, open, or a field value, with its location (role paragraph, check row, schema field,\\\\ntakes line, category block). This list is the thing the failures are mapped onto.\\\\n\\\\n```sh\\\\npython3 - <<'PY'\\\\nimport sqlite3, json\\\\na = sqlite3.connect('file:<run folder>/archive.sqlite?mode=ro', uri=True)\\\\nreq = json.loads(a.execute(\\\\\\\"select request_json from model_calls where purpose='extract' and request_json like '%<title fragment>%' order by call_id desc limit 1\\\\\\\").fetchone()[0])\\\\nprint(req['messages'][0]['content']); print(req['messages'][1]['content'].split('[Item]')[0]); print(req['messages'][1]['content'].rsplit('\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n', 2)[-2:])\\\\nprint(json.dumps({k: v.get('description') for k, v in req['response_format']['json_schema']['schema']['properties']['evidence']['items']['properties'].items() if v.get('description')}, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))\\\\nPY\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## 2. Produce the failure lists (all at no model cost, on the stored draws)\\\\n\\\\n| List | Script | What it gives |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| Matter states across draws | `harness/matter_states.py arm=d1,d2,d3 base=d1,d2,d3` | every gold core/supporting matter: extracted or reaching in 3/2/1/0 draws; the systematic misses (0 of 3) and the coin flips (1 of 3) |\\\\n| Written noise by the standard's row | the `rows_all` count in `design-v72.md` §10 (the gold's `not_kept[].row`) | which row of the standard the written noise falls under, with examples |\\\\n| No-home drops | `harness/dropped_census.py d1 d2 d3` | gold matters written but dropped, with the questions open at the time |\\\\n| Where links go | `harness/links_by_question.py d1 d2 d3 --sample 20` | the pile per question, the revenue-sink share, statements under several questions, noise under revenue |\\\\n| Quote refusals | the `dropped` reasons of the handovers (`quote not in item`), each diffed against its closest source window | paraphrase against a word or two off |\\\\n| Question recall | `harness/question_recall.py d1 d2 d3` | must_open / may_open covered by seeds and by article-opened questions |\\\\n| Fields | 15 random stored statements with speaker, original_who, original_day, tier | read against the quote and the item's day and publisher |\\\\n\\\\nFor every list, read the items, not the counts: the raw answer beside the article for every systematic miss (a miss the scorer reports\\\\nmay be the matter written in other words: check before counting it), a sample of twenty for every pile.\\\\n\\\\n## 3. Map each failure class to the request\\\\n\\\\nFor each class with more than a handful of cases, fill one row:\\\\n\\\\n| Failure class (count, share) | The sentence(s) of the request that produced it, quoted | The standard's line on the same case (section, decision) | Verdict | The model's own account (when the sentence is not obvious) |\\\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\\\n\\\\nVerdicts, one of: **contradiction** (two sentences of the request pull opposite ways, or a request sentence removes what the standard\\\\nkeeps, D240), **missing** (no sentence decides the case; the model guesses, a coin flip per send), **abstract** (a clause without an\\\\nexample, read differently each send), **misread** (the sentence is right, the model does not apply it; needs the model's own account\\\\nbefore any change), **not the prompt** (code, scorer or sampler).\\\\n\\\\nThe model's own account: continue the stored conversation with one question about one case (`harness/probe_v72_link.py`,\\\\n`probe_v72_missing.py`), a cent a case, for every \\\\\\\"misread\\\\\\\" and for any class whose sentence is not obvious from reading.\\\\n\\\\n## 4. Check every proposed fix against the principles before writing it\\\\n\\\\n- It is written from the standard's line, not from the failing article: the example comes from another domain, names no covered\\\\n  company, product or number, and reads the same for every industry. A fix that only recovers the bench's misses is benchmark\\\\n  farming and is not written.\\\\n- It removes a contradiction, supplies a missing definition at its owner (schema field, takes line, check row, category block), or\\\\n  replaces an abstract clause with a closed set and examples. It never adds a rule the standard does not hold.\\\\n- It cuts at least as much as it adds, or the growth has a written reason; report characters before and after.\\\\n- One class per change; the change is proved on the stored requests of that class, three sends as stored against three changed,\\\\n  with the noise guards of the same articles; the whole bench accepts it (three draws) only when Alex asks for a run.\\\\n\\\\n## 5. Output\\\\n\\\\nWrite the table and the verdicts into the arm's design document (a numbered section), one row per class, in the order of the loss;\\\\nthe report to Alex states each class in a reader's words (what the system does wrong, which sentence makes it do that, what the\\\\nstandard says), never in the loop's own words (AGENTS, \\\\\\\"Authority and scope\\\\\\\": explain as to a sixteen-year-old).\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r65.stream:33:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_17\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'd=docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers; nl -ba $d/blind_rules.py | head -110; rg -n -i '\\\\\\\"'volume in hand|taken in full|selling quarter|discount.*target' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | head -55; nl -ba AGENTS.md | rg -i 'mechanism draws|closed set with examples|no case-fitted|abstract clause|council decides'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"     1\\\\t\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"The one source of the defect definitions and the writer's format material for judging-v13s blind readers and adjudicators (D744).\\\\n     2\\\\t\\\\n     3\\\\tReaders and adjudicators get the same text: the writer's system text, every schema description, and these definitions, so that what\\\\n     4\\\\tthe format rules permit is never marked as a defect by one and cleared by the other.\\\\n     5\\\\t\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n     6\\\\timport json\\\\n     7\\\\tfrom pathlib import Path\\\\n     8\\\\t\\\\n     9\\\\tDEFINITIONS = \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Definitions (judge each against the passages and the format rules the writer was given, shown below; what the format rules permit is\\\\n    10\\\\tnot a defect):\\\\n    11\\\\t- supported: the forecast follows from the shown passages and the answer's stated assumptions; a reader could check it against them.\\\\n    12\\\\t  For a forecast, the assumption that decides the band must rest on the passages in one of three ways: its size, a bound that\\\\n    13\\\\t  justifies the rung, or, when the passages do not give the asked quantity, a related figure that the answer explains. An explained\\\\n    14\\\\t  related figure satisfies this requirement even though the other side of the line remains possible. It is explained when the\\\\n    15\\\\t  answer says why the comparison applies to the companies, the period and the quantity asked, and why, under the answer's own stated\\\\n    16\\\\t  assumptions, the chosen side of the line is more likely; an answer that does not explain this is not supported (a ruling). For an unresolved\\\\n    17\\\\t  member, supported means its reason holds: after the strongest relevant passages, a gap remains that keeps the rung unsettled (a\\\\n    18\\\\t  ruling).\\\\n    19\\\\t- number misread: a source figure's number, scale, sign or qualifier differs from what its passage's quote writes, allowing what the\\\\n    20\\\\t  format rules permit.\\\\n    21\\\\t- wrong arithmetic: a computed figure does not equal its operation on its inputs, within the tolerance the format rules state.\\\\n    22\\\\t- part above or added into its whole: a segment is larger than the total it belongs to, or is added again into a total that already\\\\n    23\\\\t  includes it (directly or through an intermediate figure or an estimate).\\\\n    24\\\\t- two forecasts of one quarter: two different figures are used as the value of one quantity and period. A growth rate computed from\\\\n    25\\\\t  guidance and used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate is not a second value, when one figure supplies the quarter in the\\\\n    26\\\\t  calculation (a ruling). Look through any rate or multiple, including inside a stated assumption, for a second dollar value of the\\\\n    27\\\\t  quarter.\\\\n    28\\\\t- own estimate passed off as the market's reference: a figure marked as the market's reference is, or rests on, the writer's own\\\\n    29\\\\t  estimate or forecast. A reference that applies a past period's reported share or multiple to another period (a quarter's mix\\\\n    30\\\\t  applied to the year) is our comparison estimate, not the market's (a ruling).\\\\n    31\\\\t- broken structure: a link that does not resolve, a figure that depends on itself, a missing or doubled answer, an outcome that is not\\\\n    32\\\\t  the question's quantity, or a rung whose band does not hold the outcome. For a range outcome, the format allows \\\\\\\"a band it overlaps,\\\\n    33\\\\t  with the reason in reasons\\\\\\\": such a rung is not broken structure; a band the range does not reach is. A total used for a narrower\\\\n    34\\\\t  quantity (total capital expenditure for data-center spending) without a stated deduction or a supported bound is an outcome not of\\\\n    35\\\\t  the question's quantity (a ruling).\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    36\\\\t\\\\n    37\\\\t\\\\n    38\\\\tdef descriptions(schema, path=''):\\\\n    39\\\\t    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Every description in the schema, keyed by its field path.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    40\\\\t    found = {}\\\\n    41\\\\t    if isinstance(schema, dict):\\\\n    42\\\\t        if isinstance(schema.get('description'), str):\\\\n    43\\\\t            found[path.strip('/') or 'answer'] = schema['description']\\\\n    44\\\\t        for key, value in schema.items():\\\\n    45\\\\t            if key != 'description':\\\\n    46\\\\t                step = '' if key in ('properties', 'items', 'anyOf') else key\\\\n    47\\\\t                found.update(descriptions(value, f'{path}/{step}' if step else path))\\\\n    48\\\\t    elif isinstance(schema, list):\\\\n    49\\\\t        for value in schema:\\\\n    50\\\\t            found.update(descriptions(value, path))\\\\n    51\\\\t    return found\\\\n    52\\\\t\\\\n    53\\\\t\\\\n    54\\\\tdef allowed_qualifiers(schema):\\\\n    55\\\\t    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"The qualifier values the writer's own schema allowed (D747: an older run's schema, not today's list).\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    56\\\\t    options = schema['properties']['figures']['items']['properties']['qualifier']['anyOf']\\\\n    57\\\\t    found = [o['enum'] for o in options if isinstance(o, dict) and 'enum' in o]\\\\n    58\\\\t    if len(found) != 1:\\\\n    59\\\\t        raise SystemExit('the schema does not hold exactly one qualifier list')\\\\n    60\\\\t    return found[0]\\\\n    61\\\\t\\\\n    62\\\\t\\\\n    63\\\\tdef format_material(case_folder):\\\\n    64\\\\t    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"The writer's system text and every schema description, as shown to readers and adjudicators.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    65\\\\t    case_folder = Path(case_folder)\\\\n    66\\\\t    schema = json.loads((case_folder / 'schema.json').read_text())\\\\n    67\\\\t    return '\\\\\\\\n'.join(['# The system text the writer was given', (case_folder / 'system.txt').read_text(), '',\\\\n    68\\\\t                      '# The format rules the writer was given (schema descriptions)',\\\\n    69\\\\t                      json.dumps(descriptions(schema), indent=1, ensure_ascii=False), '',\\\\n    70\\\\t                      'The qualifier values the format allows (a qualifier not in this list cannot be recorded): '\\\\n    71\\\\t                      + ', '.join(allowed_qualifiers(schema)) + '.'])\\\\n3072:- What reader B does that judging-v6 did not, read from B's answers on the questions that differed (`judgement-gold/reconcile-v1.md`, `gold-v1.json`): carries the guided growth forward rather than annualising the last quarter flat (Data Center, total revenue); discounts a management target for a product with no shipments by default (Vera CPU: two selling quarters, four million units at $5,000, the company's own choice of another CPU); sizes an announced but unsized commitment from its disclosed comparable (the Firmus backstop from Sharon's); derives a figure no one states from the accounting identities in the evidence (capex from operating less free cash flow); keeps linked conclusions consistent (China share against the H200 authorization theme). Written into `judging-v7.txt` as five clauses (v6 3,782 → 4,924 characters; reason: each clause is a behaviour of the frozen standard the judge lacked), named by `poc-v91`; schema and code unchanged.\\\\n3073:- Proof on the stored requests of the questions whose arm-4 judgement differed from the gold (`proof-judging-v7a.txt`, `proof-judging-v7.txt`; one send each, cents): total revenue rung 3 → 2 (about $421 billion from the guided growth on FY2026's base; gold $400–435 billion), Data Center 3 → 2 (about $372 billion; gold $370–400 billion), Vera CPU 1 → 2 ($12 to below $20 billion, the target discounted for the volume not in hand; gold $8–18 billion), DRAM prices 3 → 2 (about +15%; gold +10–35%), financing total stays 4 ($33.5–39.8 billion; gold $25–60 billion), the Ohio guarantee stays Yes; China share stays below 1% in draw 1, consistent with that draw's H200 theme judged No (the gold has the authorization likely and the share 1–8%; the consistency clause ties the share to the theme, so it moves with it). Six of the seven re-sent questions now land in the gold's band; the end-to-end agreement under judging-v7 needs a run on `poc-v91`, which is Alex's call. A placement gap seen on the way: the Vera CPU question never held the fall-launch statement (filed under the Rubin launch questions), so the judge could not count selling quarters from evidence; the default-discount clause covers it, the filing is a D2 class to count.\\\\n    41\\\\t- **While Alex is not active, the council decides (D439).** A choice or a next step that would go to Alex, including opening a new\\\\n    85\\\\t- When one mechanism draws findings round after round, stop answering findings: propose one structural rule.\\\\n   114\\\\t- **No case-fitted fix.** A hand list, a special path or a rule fitted to the case in view fixes that case and breaks the next. First ask\\\\n   227\\\\t- **A classification the model must make is written as a closed set with examples:** two or three examples per class, the procedure\\\\n   229\\\\t  items\\\\\\\"). An abstract clause (\\\\\\\"a material statement\\\\\\\") is a coin flip per send. The examples are not growth to avoid; the abstract clause\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r65.stream:36:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_18\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r65.md; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3068,3074p'; nl -ba docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md | head -44\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"     1\\\\t# Council round 65: Claude's reflection on the D749 writer test, written before Codex's read\\\\n     2\\\\t\\\\n     3\\\\tAlex is asleep. His standing direction for tonight (the /goal of 2026-11-23): converge the remaining problems with the council,\\\\n     4\\\\tno scope drift, read the log so no mistake repeats, measure and settle, and head toward production. D439 governs while he is away:\\\\n     5\\\\t- the council decides reversibly;\\\\n     6\\\\t- no paid send (D439's ceiling is spent);\\\\n     7\\\\t- nothing is committed.\\\\n     8\\\\t\\\\n     9\\\\t## Result\\\\n    10\\\\t`BLIND5-RESULT.md`: INCONCLUSIVE, with one support split (X05, E Claude, rung 2 by taking guidance in full). No line failed:\\\\n    11\\\\t- the E Codex writer answered a justified unresolved;\\\\n    12\\\\t- both S forecasts and both P-v8 forecasts are supported;\\\\n    13\\\\t- both controls were caught;\\\\n    14\\\\t- there is no fresh defect and no refusal.\\\\n    15\\\\t\\\\n    16\\\\t## What I take from it\\\\n    17\\\\t1. **The repair worked where it was aimed.** The writer type that invented cuts twice (third run, targeted test) now withholds with\\\\n    18\\\\t   a specific gap, and both families accept it. S converged too.\\\\n    19\\\\t2. **The one split is resolvable on fact against an existing rule.** Bullet 2 says a not-yet-shipping target \\\\\\\"is taken in full only\\\\n    20\\\\t   when the evidence shows the volume in hand\\\\\\\".\\\\n    21\\\\t   - None of E's 15 passages shows shipments, revenue to date or orders.\\\\n    22\\\\t   - X05's premise (\\\\\\\"already selling at volume\\\\\\\") is an inference from a reaffirmed outlook.\\\\n    23\\\\t   - It is not a gap in D747. The two families differ on whether an outlook counts as volume in hand.\\\\n    24\\\\t3. **Log check: is this the same E mechanism again?**\\\\n    25\\\\t   - The earlier E failures were invented cuts. This one is the opposite: no discount, by asserting volume in hand.\\\\n    26\\\\t   - The request's clause \\\\\\\"the evidence shows the volume in hand\\\\\\\" has no closed definition, and AGENTS §6 says \\\\\\\"a classification\\\\n    27\\\\t     the model must make is written as a closed set with examples\\\\\\\".\\\\n    28\\\\t   - The smallest structural fix is a closed definition at its owner (bullet 2): volume in hand means reported shipments or revenue\\\\n    29\\\\t     to date, or orders with units, prices or dates in the passages. A company's own outlook or a \\\\\\\"will be deployed\\\\\\\" is not volume\\\\n    30\\\\t     in hand.\\\\n    31\\\\t   - This defines an existing term. It adds no new rule. Its source is the system text's own discount principle and D749 (\\\\\\\"if it can\\\\n    32\\\\t     say only that sales might fall short, answer can't tell\\\\\\\").\\\\n    33\\\\t\\\\n    34\\\\t## My position (to be challenged)\\\\n    35\\\\t- **Option 1, my lean.** Make the closed definition, a few dozen characters at bullet 2. Run the $0 checks (cases, rehearsal, plan\\\\n    36\\\\t  hash), then the cheapest proof (AGENTS §1.4):\\\\n    37\\\\t  - fresh writers on E only, two per family, plus fresh readers;\\\\n    38\\\\t  - and only if a fresh E reply still splits on this point, stop and put it to Alex as his ruling.\\\\n    39\\\\t  - If clean, ask Alex in the morning to authorize the paid re-send. The registered D749 result stays INCONCLUSIVE and is disclosed.\\\\n    40\\\\t    The E-only test is a separate, smaller registered test.\\\\n    41\\\\t- **Option 2.** Go straight to Alex in the morning for the paid re-send with X05 disclosed, and change nothing. It is cheaper\\\\n    42\\\\t  tonight, but it leaves a known ambiguity in the request that luna will meet on E and on every not-yet-shipping target in\\\\n    43\\\\t  production.\\\\n    44\\\\t- **Option 3.** Put \\\\\\\"is a reaffirmed outlook volume in hand?\\\\\\\" to Alex as a ruling. This is a definitional question his existing words\\\\n    45\\\\t  already answer (\\\\\\\"taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand\\\\\\\"). I lean that the council can settle it reversibly\\\\n    46\\\\t  tonight under D439.\\\\n    47\\\\t- **Process lesson applied.** The E-only test's registered lines must not demand settlement on boundary answers beyond what the\\\\n    48\\\\t  record shows readers deliver (D748's error). The decisive line is narrow: no fresh E reply takes a not-yet-shipping target in full,\\\\n    49\\\\t  or invents a cut, with settled support, and controls hold.\\\\n    50\\\\t- **What would change my mind.** The council finds the definition wider or narrower than the standard (D745, D747, D749), or finds\\\\n    51\\\\t  that E's passages do show volume in hand.\\\\n  3068\\\\t\\\\n  3069\\\\t## D263 · 2026-11-02 · The judge is written to the frozen gold's own reasoning (judging-v7, poc-v91); a gap to the gold is closed in the judge, not re-measured\\\\n  3070\\\\t\\\\n  3071\\\\t- Alex, after the first score on the frozen gold was reported as the system being \\\\\\\"wrong\\\\\\\" on some questions: \\\\\\\"不是啊什么叫错？我不是和你说了就按照claude的标准来就好了嘛\\\\\\\". The gold is Claude's (reader B's) standard by D262; a disagreement is the distance between the judge and that standard, to be closed in the judge's rule, not a verdict to be measured again.\\\\n  3072\\\\t- What reader B does that judging-v6 did not, read from B's answers on the questions that differed (`judgement-gold/reconcile-v1.md`, `gold-v1.json`): carries the guided growth forward rather than annualising the last quarter flat (Data Center, total revenue); discounts a management target for a product with no shipments by default (Vera CPU: two selling quarters, four million units at $5,000, the company's own choice of another CPU); sizes an announced but unsized commitment from its disclosed comparable (the Firmus backstop from Sharon's); derives a figure no one states from the accounting identities in the evidence (capex from operating less free cash flow); keeps linked conclusions consistent (China share against the H200 authorization theme). Written into `judging-v7.txt` as five clauses (v6 3,782 → 4,924 characters; reason: each clause is a behaviour of the frozen standard the judge lacked), named by `poc-v91`; schema and code unchanged.\\\\n  3073\\\\t- Proof on the stored requests of the questions whose arm-4 judgement differed from the gold (`proof-judging-v7a.txt`, `proof-judging-v7.txt`; one send each, cents): total revenue rung 3 → 2 (about $421 billion from the guided growth on FY2026's base; gold $400–435 billion), Data Center 3 → 2 (about $372 billion; gold $370–400 billion), Vera CPU 1 → 2 ($12 to below $20 billion, the target discounted for the volume not in hand; gold $8–18 billion), DRAM prices 3 → 2 (about +15%; gold +10–35%), financing total stays 4 ($33.5–39.8 billion; gold $25–60 billion), the Ohio guarantee stays Yes; China share stays below 1% in draw 1, consistent with that draw's H200 theme judged No (the gold has the authorization likely and the share 1–8%; the consistency clause ties the share to the theme, so it moves with it). Six of the seven re-sent questions now land in the gold's band; the end-to-end agreement under judging-v7 needs a run on `poc-v91`, which is Alex's call. A placement gap seen on the way: the Vera CPU question never held the fall-launch statement (filed under the Rubin launch questions), so the judge could not count selling quarters from evidence; the default-discount clause covers it, the filing is a D2 class to count.\\\\n  3074\\\\t\\\\n     1\\\\t# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\\\\n     2\\\\t\\\\n     3\\\\t> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \\\\\\\"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\\\\\\\".\\\\n     4\\\\t> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\\\\n     5\\\\t> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\\\\n     6\\\\t> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\\\\n     7\\\\t> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \\\\\\\"go\\\\\\\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \\\\\\\"also file under the other party's question\\\\\\\" and puts two\\\\n     8\\\\t> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\\\\n     9\\\\t> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\\\\n    10\\\\t> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\\\\\\\"不，用英文吧\\\\\\\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\\\\\\\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\\\\\\\").\\\\n    11\\\\t\\\\n    12\\\\t## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \\\\\\\"每次开始前都需要revisit\\\\\\\")\\\\n    13\\\\t\\\\n    14\\\\tBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\\\\n    15\\\\t\\\\n    16\\\\t1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\\\\n    17\\\\t2. Check against §3, \\\\\\\"not in scope\\\\\\\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\\\\n    18\\\\t3. Check against §4, \\\\\\\"constraints\\\\\\\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\\\\n    19\\\\t   word for it is already given.\\\\n    20\\\\t4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\\\\n    21\\\\t   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\\\\n    22\\\\t5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\\\\n    23\\\\t   AGENTS, \\\\\\\"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\\\\\\\").\\\\n    24\\\\t\\\\n    25\\\\t## 1. Goal (end to end)\\\\n    26\\\\t\\\\n    27\\\\tEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\\\\n    28\\\\tnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\\\\n    29\\\\tany one step's own score.\\\\n    30\\\\t\\\\n    31\\\\t## 2. The core blocker (proven)\\\\n    32\\\\t\\\\n    33\\\\t**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \\\\\\\"states exactly this question's own figure\\\\\\\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\\\\n    34\\\\t\\\\n    35\\\\tThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \\\\\\\"two problems\\\\\\\"):\\\\n    36\\\\t\\\\n    37\\\\t- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\\\\n    38\\\\t  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\\\\n    39\\\\t  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\\\\n    40\\\\t  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\\\\n    41\\\\t  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\\\\n    42\\\\t- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\\\\n    43\\\\t  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \\\\\\\"below $40 billion\\\\\\\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\\\\n    44\\\\t  nothing at all and were never judged.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72b.stream:32:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_16\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"PYTHONPATH=src python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,glob,collections\\\\nfrom hivemind import service\\\\nfrom hivemind.views import store, identity\\\\nfor f in sorted(glob.glob('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-?/prod/views.sqlite'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''))+glob.glob('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''poc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0815/views.sqlite'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')+glob.glob('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''poc/data/english-v23-jev-2026-10-25/views.sqlite'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\n c=sqlite3.connect('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''file:'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''+f+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',uri=True);c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\\\n cnt=collections.Counter(); labels=collections.Counter()\\\\n print(f)\\\\n for v in c.execute('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''select * from views order by rowid'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\n  i=v['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''view_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']; r=store.rungs_of(c,i); k=store.view_key(c,i) or {}; labs=tuple(x['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''label'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] for x in r); ls={l.lower().strip() for l in labs}; bands,error=service.ladder_bands(r)\\\\n  event=k.get('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''measure'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'') in identity.EVENT_MEASURES\\\\n  yn=len(labs)==2 and ls in ({'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''yes'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''no'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''},{'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''是'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''否'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''})\\\\n  category='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''event'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' if event else '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''binary'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' if yn else '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''amount'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' if bands else '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''unhandled-key'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' if k else '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''ambiguous'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\n  cnt[category]+=1;labels[labs]+=1\\\\n  if f.find('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''english-v23'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')\\\\\\\"'!=-1:\\\\n   if i=='\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v37'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'': print(i,k.get('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''measure'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),r)\\\\n  elif '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''sealed'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' in f or category in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''unhandled-key'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''ambiguous'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'') or event and (bands or len(labs)\\\\\\\"'!=2) or not event and yn or '\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''old-1'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' in f:\\\\n   print(i,category,k.get('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''measure'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''/'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.join(labs),v['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''question'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\n print(cnt,labels)'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite\\\\nv1 amount financing_amount Strongly bullish/Bullish/Neutral/Bearish/Strongly bearish How much credit support for AI clouds will NVIDIA have committed at the end of FY2027?\\\\nv2 amount financing_amount Strongly bullish/Bullish/Neutral/Bearish/Strongly bearish What total amount of NVIDIA’s credit-support and capacity-purchase obligations will be outstanding at the FY2027 annual report?\\\\nv3 event event Yes/No Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Rubin platform by December 31, 2026?\\\\nv4 amount total_revenue Strongly bullish/Bullish/Neutral/Bearish/Strongly bearish What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\\\\nv5 amount total_revenue Strongly bullish/Bullish/Neutral/Bearish/Strongly bearish What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2028?\\\\nv6 amount spend_total Below $500 billion/$500 billion to below $600 billion/$600 billion to below $700 billion/$700 billion to below $800 billion/$800 billion or more How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?\\\\nv7 amount spend_total Below $800 billion/$800 billion to below $900 billion/$900 billion to below $1.1 trillion/$1.1 trillion to below $1.2 trillion/$1.2 trillion or more How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\\\\nv8 amount segment_revenue Strongly bullish/Bullish/Neutral/Bearish/Strongly bearish How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\\\\nv9 event policy_event No/Yes Will China authorize purchases of Nvidia H200 chips by AI companies by January 31, 2027?\\\\nv10 event event Yes/No Will NVIDIA complete an investment in Firmus Technologies’ preference shares by December 31, 2026?\\\\nv11 amount gross_margin Strongly bullish/Bullish/Neutral/Bearish/Strongly bearish What gross margin will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\\\\nv12 event event Yes/No Will the French competition authority conclude its antitrust investigation into NVIDIA by January 31, 2027?\\\\nv13 event event Yes/No Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Kyber NVL144 next-generation AI rack system by December 31, 2028?\\\\nv14 amount financing_amount Strongly bullish/Bullish/Neutral/Bearish/Strongly bearish How much will NVIDIA’s supply-chain purchase commitments outstanding be at the end of FY2027?\\\\nv15 amount product_revenue Strongly bullish/Bullish/Neutral/Bearish/Strongly bearish How much total CPU revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\\\\nv16 event policy_event Yes/No Will the U.S. Senate pass the Remote Access Security Act by December 31, 2026?\\\\nv17 event event Yes/No Will NVIDIA complete its planned $1 billion investment in NAVER Corp. by December 31, 2026?\\\\nv18 amount financing_amount Strongly bullish/Bullish/Neutral/Bearish/Strongly bearish How much financing will NVIDIA have provided or committed to Amkor under the packaging expansion agreement by the FY2027 annual report?\\\\nv19 event event Yes/No Will NVIDIA agree to provide the reported financing guarantee for OpenAI's southern Ohio data center project by January 31, 2027?\\\\nv20 event event Yes/No Will NVIDIA agree to finance OpenAI chip purchases for the southern Ohio data center project by January 31, 2027?\\\\nv21 event event Yes/No Will NVIDIA launch its Rosa next-generation CPU by December 31, 2028?\\\\nv22 even