, '$700 billion to below $800 billion', '$800 billion or more'): 1, ('Below $500 billion', '$500 billion to below $600 billion', '$600 billion to below $800 billion', '$800 billion to below $1 trillion', '$1 trillion or more'): 1, ('Below guidance', 'Lower guidance range', 'Guidance midpoint', 'Above guidance', 'Well above guidance'): 1, ('Below $800 billion', '$800 billion to below $900 billion', '$900 billion to below $1.1 trillion', '$1.1 trillion to below $1.3 trillion', '$1.3 trillion or more'): 1, ('Below $800 billion', '$800 billion to under $900 billion', '$900 billion to under $1.1 trillion', '$1.1 trillion to under $1.2 trillion', '$1.2 trillion or more'): 1, ('Below $600 billion', '$600 billion to below $650 billion', '$650 billion to below $730 billion', '$730 billion to below $800 billion', '$800 billion or more'): 1, ('Below $800 billion', '$800 billion to below $950 billion', '$950 billion to below $1.05 trillion', '$1.05 trillion to below $1.2 trillion', '$1.2 trillion or more'): 1, ('Below $320 billion', '$320 billion to below $380 billion', '$380 billion to below $420 billion', '$420 billion to below $480 billion', '$480 billion or more'): 1, ('Below prior estimate', 'Near prior estimate', 'Near current projection', 'Above projection', 'At least $250 billion'): 1, ('Below 3.5%', '3.5% to below 3.9%', 'Near the July 2026 reading', '4.3% to below 4.7%', '4.7% or higher'): 1, ('Below 1.5 GW', '1.5 to below 1.9 GW', 'Near the stated expectation', '2.1 to below 2.5 GW', 'At least 2.5 GW'): 1, ('Lowest range', 'Lower range', 'Near forecast', 'Higher range', 'Highest range'): 1, ('Below $100 billion', '$100 billion to below $300 billion', '$300 billion to below $500 billion', '$500 billion to below $700 billion', '$700 billion or more'): 1, ('Below $650 billion', '$650 billion to below $700 billion', '$700 billion to below $790 billion', '$790 billion to below $850 billion', '$850 billion or more'): 1, ('Below $400 billion', '$400 billion to below $500 billion', '$500 billion to below $700 billion', '$700 billion to below $800 billion', '$800 billion or more'): 1, ('Below $450 billion', '$450 billion to below $550 billion', '$550 billion to below $650 billion', '$650 billion to below $750 billion', '$750 billion or more'): 1, ('Below $800 billion', '$800 billion to below $900 billion', '$900 billion to below $1 trillion', '$1 trillion to below $1.1 trillion', '$1.1 trillion or more'): 1, ('Below 4 GW', '4 GW to below 5 GW', '5 GW to below 10 GW', '10 GW to below 12 GW', '12 GW or more'): 1})\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72b.stream:57:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_29\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,glob,re\\\\nfor f in sorted(glob.glob('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-?/prod/views.sqlite'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')):\\\\n c=sqlite3.connect('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''file:'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''+f+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',uri=True)\\\\n print(f)\\\\n pat=re.compile(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.{0,150}(?:capex|hyperscaler|capital spending|infrastructure spending|capital expenditure).{0,200}'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.I)\\\\n found=[]\\\\n for vid,jid,day,reason,why in c.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select j.view_id,j.judgement_id,j.publication_day,j.reasons,j.why_changed from judgements j join view_keys k using(view_id) where k.measure in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''event'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''policy_event'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"):\\\\n  for m in pat.finditer((reason or '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''+(why or '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')):\\\\n   if re.search(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$|billion|trillion|rung [345]|range|band|position [345]'\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',m[0],re.I):\\\\n    found.append((vid,jid,day,m[0]))\\\\n print(len(found));print(*found[:18],sep='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')\\\\n'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite\\\\n12\\\\n('v20', 499, '2026-08-13', 'undary to rung 1. The rung remains Yes and the reported $350 billion discussion is not a new independent confirmation. However, the updated v6 and v7 capex theme conclusions strengthen the demand backdrop supporting the same forecast; the repeated reports themselves do not change it.')\\\\n('v25', 548, '2026-08-15', ' outlets are treated as one claim, not independent confirmation. The rung and the core $350 billion financing-report basis are unchanged. The updated hyperscaler capex conclusions add relevant support for the scale of chip demand behind the proposed financing, changing the supporting rationale without changing the forecast rung.')\\\\n('v31', 653, '2026-08-19', 'argely restate the same plan and do not establish closing or provide a closing schedule, so the forecast remains uncertain rather than proven. The AI-capex themes modestly support project execution; the chip-export-control themes do not bear on this investment. The rung and the key supporting fact remain the same: NVIDIA announced the $1.5 billion plan,')\\\\n('v30', 737, '2026-08-23', 'ompletion. The repeated reports add no independent closing information, and the expected chip purchases provide only modest strategic support. The AI-capex themes modestly reinforce the project context but do not change the binary forecast. The forecast remains rung 1 with the same implied $1.5 billion completion by December 31, 2026. The additional rep')\\\\n('v17', 762, '2026-08-24', 'd NAVER’s expansion plan, do not establish that the investment has closed or that the financing condition will be met by the deadline. The broader AI-capex outlook supports the project’s prospects somewhat, but does not remove this specific closing condition. The rung and key supporting facts are unchanged: the planned $1 billion investment remains cond')\\\\n('v10', 865, '2026-08-28', 'ta-center capex at rung 4 and 2027 capex at rung 4, strengthening the contextual support for Firmus financing and changing the supporting outlook, without changing the implied completion date.')\\\\n('v29', 1022, '2026-09-03', 'artnership remains at the MOU stage with limited detail, plus a reported potential $125 billion backstop whose details are not final. Updated 2026–27 hyperscaler capex conclusions also strengthen the demand backdrop. These change the supporting risk and demand picture without moving the forecast across the binary rung boundary.')\\\\n('v29', 1037, '2026-09-04', 'eing negotiated and NVIDIA cautioned that the MOUs may not lead to definitive agreements, but roughly a year remains to complete them. The updated AI-capex themes also support continuing demand for infrastructure financing. These factors leave completion by the deadline as the more likely outcome, without treating the $500 billion target as proof that a')\\\\n('v29', 1037, '2026-09-04', 'greements are complete. The rung remains Yes, but the updated AI-capex themes add a stronger demand backdrop than the previous judgement had, changing the key support for the same forecast. Recent filings and reports reiterate that the arrangements remain MOUs or prelim')\\\\n('v10', 1049, '2026-09-04', 'O later in 2026, makes completion by the deadline more likely than non-completion, though the reported interest is not a confirmed commitment. The AI-capex themes modestly support the commercial context, but do not establish that the investment will close. The rung and its key transaction facts are unchanged: the same report of approximately US$500 mill')\\\\n('v31', 1060, '2026-09-04', \\\\\\\"nce now includes SB Energy's reported $3.2 billion first-half 2026 net loss and $139 million revenue, mostly from its legacy business. The updated AI-capex outlook also supports the project backdrop; neither changes the most likely completion outcome.\\\\\\\")\\\\n('v10', 1080, '2026-09-05', 'fact remain as in the previous conclusion: the specific but unconfirmed report of about US$500 million of interest tied to a 2026 IPO. The updated AI-capex themes reinforce the commercial context but do not change the implied outcome or rung.')\\\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite\\\\n4\\\\n('v3', 175, '2026-07-20', ' The reported up-to-$500 billion is the possible full-build cost, not the size or terms of NVIDIA’s guarantee. The rung remains 2, but the updated AI-capex theme conclusion reinforces the forecast that the lease-related guarantee may proceed; it does not change the implied binary outcome or establish a guarantee amount.')\\\\n('v31', 1024, '2026-09-01', 'y still make completion by the deadline more likely than non-completion, so the binary rung does not change. The rung remains Yes, but the updated AI-capex themes add relevant support for the scale and continuation of the data-center buildout. They do not establish that the specific $1.5 billion investment has closed or change the implied completion out')\\\\n('v31', 1209, '2026-09-08', 'ut. The implied outcome therefore remains on the Yes side of the binary boundary. The rung and the core completion forecast are unchanged, but the AI-capex themes were updated since the prior judgement and now provide additional support for execution of the project. The specific $3 billion report is not a new supporting fact relative to the prior conclu')\\\\n('v31', 1463, '2026-09-16', 'and project-investment figures are not themselves evidence that this specific investment has been paid. The rung remains Yes, but the updated 2027 AI-capex theme adds support for the underlying data-center build and thus for completion of the investment; the report of a $3 billion agreement is part of the existing support, not a newly established transf')\\\\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/views.sqlite\\\\n5\\\\n('v21', 468, '2026-08-11', 'reement to be signed; the evidence therefore supports Yes as the forecast, not as an already-proven outcome. The rung remains Yes, but the updated AI-capex themes reinforce the infrastructure-demand backdrop supporting the forecast. The newer $125 billion figure is an option across potential deals, not a confirmed Ohio-specific guarantee; repeated repor')\\\\n('v36', 799, '2026-08-25', 'e past the binary rung boundary. The rung remains Yes, and the shipment-testing evidence is unchanged. The updated 2027 AI-capex theme now points to spending around $1 trillion, refreshing and strengthening the demand support for the same forecast without supplying a shipment date.')\\\\n('v34', 945, '2026-08-30', ' or delay. Completion is still a forecast, not an established fact, and the repeated reports do not independently confirm a transfer of funds. The AI-capex themes support the project backdrop but do not establish completion. The rung and implied outcome are unchanged from the previous conclusion. The evidence reiterates the $1.5 billion plan and the pre')\\\\n('v34', 1382, '2026-09-12', 'ot confirm that funds have transferred or clarify how it relates to the original $1.5 billion, but it strengthens the commitment case; the updated AI-capex outlook also modestly supports execution. The implied outcome remains on the Yes side of the binary boundary. The rung and implied completion outcome are unchanged, but the updated 2027 AI-capex outl')\\\\n('v34', 1498, '2026-09-15', 'larger commitment, but its mention that SB Energy is seeking a Nasdaq listing to fund the project also leaves execution and timing unresolved. The AI-capex outlook supports the project backdrop, not proof of completion. The rung remains Yes, but e4452 adds a newly reported $3 billion investment agreement and Nasdaq-listing funding context, changing the ')\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r67.stream:50:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_25\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n -i 'product (that |is )?(has |hasn.t |had |is )?not (yet |already )?shipp|product with no shipments|not-yet shipping|volume in hand' docs/system-design docs/prd docs/DECISIONS-log.md | head -30 | cut -c1-950\\\\nnl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '11342,11368p'\\\\nrg -n 're-send|same.*lines|singletons|gain' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md | head -22\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3072:- What reader B does that judging-v6 did not, read from B's answers on the questions that differed (`judgement-gold/reconcile-v1.md`, `gold-v1.json`): carries the guided growth forward rather than annualising the last quarter flat (Data Center, total revenue); discounts a management target for a product with no shipments by default (Vera CPU: two selling quarters, four million units at $5,000, the company's own choice of another CPU); sizes an announced but unsized commitment from its disclosed comparable (the Firmus backstop from Sharon's); derives a figure no one states from the accounting identities in the evidence (capex from operating less free cash flow); keeps linked conclusions consistent (China share against the H200 authorization theme). Written into `judging-v7.txt` as five clauses (v6 3,782 → 4,924 characters; reason: each clause is a behaviour of the frozen standard the judge lacked), named by `po\\\\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11674:  - Claude's closed list of \\\\\\\"volume in hand\\\\\\\" was rejected: it was wider and narrower than the standard at once.\\\\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11676:    puts the required volume in hand for the period\\\\\\\".\\\\n 11342\\\\t    - apply the rulings, in the reader brief and in code only where the structure decides them;\\\\n 11343\\\\t    - verify both reader families on the stored boundary replies;\\\\n 11344\\\\t    - re-run the registered blind test once with fresh writers and readers, then the paid re-send request.\\\\n 11345\\\\t\\\\n 11346\\\\t## D741 · 2026-11-22 · Alex rules the three reader questions of D740\\\\n 11347\\\\t\\\\n 11348\\\\t- **The questions** (after D740), each with its options; the recommended option is listed first:\\\\n 11349\\\\t  - 【增速参考】\\\\\\\"写手用公司指引的三季度 1080 亿算出“指引隐含增速约 12%”，参考它定四季度增速 13%，再套在自己预测的三季度 1136 亿上。进入收入计算的三季度数只有 1136 亿这一个。这算不算“同一季度用了两个数”的错？\\\\\\\" Options: 不算错 (推荐); 算错.\\\\n 11350\\\\t  - 【市场参照】\\\\\\\"分析师预期公司全年总收入 4110 亿，最近一个季度数据中心占 92.5%，乘出来约 3800 亿。能不能把这 3800 亿叫作“市场对数据中心全年的预期”？\\\\\\\" Options: 不能 (推荐); 能.\\\\n 11351\\\\t  - 【总开支当数据中心开支】\\\\\\\"问题问四大云厂商“数据中心资本开支”，原文只给了“总资本开支”（并说大部分投向 AI 基础设施）。一份答案直接拿总开支当数据中心开支，没扣非数据中心的部分。可以吗？\\\\\\\" Options: 必须写明扣多少 (推荐); 可以直接用.\\\\n 11352\\\\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \\\\\\\"不算错 (推荐)\\\\\\\"; \\\\\\\"不能 (推荐)\\\\\\\"; \\\\\\\"必须写明扣多少 (推荐)\\\\\\\".\\\\n 11353\\\\t- **Decided (Alex):**\\\\n 11354\\\\t  1. **Not a defect:** a growth rate computed from guidance and used only as a stated benchmark for an estimate, when one figure\\\\n 11355\\\\t     supplies the quarter in the revenue calculation.\\\\n 11356\\\\t  2. **Not the market's reference:** consensus for a total × a past quarter's reported share. That figure is our comparison estimate.\\\\n 11357\\\\t     Only an outside figure for the member's own quantity (for example Morningstar's direct segment estimate), or a calculation that\\\\n 11358\\\\t     carries no past period's reported share or multiple to another period, is the market's reference.\\\\n 11359\\\\t  3. **A total used for a narrower quantity** (total capex for data-center capex) must state the deduction as its own figure, or give\\\\n 11360\\\\t     a supported bound that shows where the narrower quantity lands.\\\\n 11361\\\\t- **How they are applied (D738):**\\\\n 11362\\\\t  - Ruling 2's carried share is structural, so S5 refuses it.\\\\n 11363\\\\t  - Rulings 1 and 3 go in the request and in the reader brief, because they turn on what a label or an estimate means.\\\\n 11364\\\\t  - Then three steps:\\\\n 11365\\\\t    1. fix the S1 \\\\\\\"from … to …\\\\\\\" range (D740);\\\\n 11366\\\\t    2. check that both reader families apply the rulings the same way to the stored boundary replies;\\\\n 11367\\\\t    3. re-run the registered blind test once with fresh writers and readers.\\\\n 11368\\\\t\\\\n23:| bounds and their propagation (C2 bound direction, C3/C6 open ends) | a source's qualifier is checked against the quote and shown to readers; computed figures are points or ranges |\\\\n152:  than today's (17 figure fields against 23, shorter descriptions than v2).\\\\n253:- **INCOMPLETE** is judged against the inventory of 12 first replies and 24 readings plus the third readings due.\\\\n260:  answer, accepted or refused, against the shown passages. For each answer they record:\\\\n276:**A clean result** goes to Alex as the request for the paid re-send: the same 36 requests rebuilt in v13s, under a new decision with\\\\n300:  - only a complete run that meets every line goes to Alex for the paid re-send.\\\\n323:  - A clean re-read goes to Alex for the paid re-send, beside the third run's record and its disclosures.\\\\n329:  1. check quotes and calculations against the format rules;\\\\n341:  | K-unsupported | E's Claude reply, 140% growth that its own reasons argue against | supported = no |\\\\n348:  - A clean result goes to Alex for the paid re-send.\\\\n383:  - a clean result supports asking Alex to authorize the 36-request paid re-send.\\\\n436:    $0 writer test, then Alex for the paid re-send.\\\\n444:  `ac707fa9…`, checked by `blind5.py build` against every built system text). This is the wording after council round 64\\\\n497:  - Either outcome goes back to the council, and the paid re-send stays on hold.\\\\n498:  - Only a clean pass supports asking Alex to authorize the paid re-send.\\\\n518:  checked by `blind6.py build` against every built system text). Bullet 2's \\\\\\\"it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the\\\\n529:  - the same pass, fail and inconclusive lines.\\\\n534:  - a clean pass supports asking Alex to authorize the paid re-send;\\\\n538:  `blind5.py`, shared by `blind6.py`, gains three changes:\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r67.stream:61:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_31\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n 'def publish_decision|def _s5|reference_unavailable' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py | tail -14\\\\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md | sed -n '456,491p'\\\\nnl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3049,3054p;3069,3073p'\\\\nrg -n 'indirect|already selling|2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.1x' poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/E/answers/claude.json | cut -c1-100\\\\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND6-RESULT.md | sed -n '36,49p'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"185:        outs, refs, reason = outcome_for.get(v, []), reference_for.get(v, []), _text(a.get('reference_unavailable'))\\\\n188:                errors.append(('S7', f'{v}: an unresolved answer has why, rung and reference_unavailable null, and no figure marked for it'))\\\\n199:                errors.append(('S5', f'{v}: needs exactly one of a figure marked as its reference or reference_unavailable'))\\\\n782:def publish_decision(family, calc, result):\\\\n   456\\\\t      wider);\\\\n   457\\\\t    - D749: decide the band before sizing, else unresolved, naming the unknown;\\\\n   458\\\\t    - D745's ruling: a justified unresolved answer is usable.\\\\n   459\\\\t  - Size: 4,540 → 4,794 characters, 910 → 961 tokens (o200k_base). The writer's request now carries the same routes the readers judge\\\\n   460\\\\t    by, and the decision order Alex approved.\\\\n   461\\\\t  - Checks at $0: cases 111 of 111, rehearsal 19 of 19, and the pinned v13 plan unchanged (`paid-plan.sha256`). The schema and the code\\\\n   462\\\\t    are unchanged.\\\\n   463\\\\t- **Scope** (`blind5.py`; run folder `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/`):\\\\n   464\\\\t  - cases S, E and P-v8, built from the repaired request;\\\\n   465\\\\t  - one fresh Claude subagent and one fresh read-only Codex session per case, 6 writers, each reading only `system.txt`, `user.txt` and\\\\n   466\\\\t    `schema.json`.\\\\n   467\\\\t- **Readers.** 8 blinded packets, shuffled X01–X08, with the key in `reader-key.json`:\\\\n   468\\\\t  - the 6 fresh replies;\\\\n   469\\\\t  - 2 controls carried unchanged from the targeted test, each shown with the request it was written for;\\\\n   470\\\\t  - each packet read by one fresh Claude and one fresh Codex reader under the D747 definitions.\\\\n   471\\\\t\\\\n   472\\\\t  Where they disagree, on support or on any defect, two adjudicators read the packet, one per family. The reasons behind every\\\\n   473\\\\t  settled vote are recorded by Claude as compatible or not (`reasons.json`). Matching votes with incompatible reasons go to\\\\n   474\\\\t  adjudication.\\\\n   475\\\\t\\\\n   476\\\\t  | Control | Built from | Expected reading |\\\\n   477\\\\t  |---|---|---|\\\\n   478\\\\t  | K-invented-cut | blind4 U05, E Codex: 90% of $40B with no order size or shipment pace | not supported |\\\\n   479\\\\t  | K-impossible-floor | blind4 U02, S Claude: \\\\\\\"more than $730B\\\\\\\" called a floor above its own $720B total | \\\\\\\"part above or added into its whole\\\\\\\" on F12, settled; its support is not scored |\\\\n   480\\\\t- **Pass:**\\\\n   481\\\\t  - every fresh S and E reply has a settled yes, on its forecast or on its unresolved reason;\\\\n   482\\\\t  - both fresh P-v8 replies have a settled yes on a forecast;\\\\n   483\\\\t  - every fresh reply is accepted and publishable by the code;\\\\n   484\\\\t  - no settled defect on a fresh reply;\\\\n   485\\\\t  - both controls read as expected.\\\\n   486\\\\t- **Otherwise (tally rules after council 64):**\\\\n   487\\\\t  - **Fail:**\\\\n   488\\\\t    - a fresh reply refused or held by the code (decided before any reading; an unreadable reply builds no packet);\\\\n   489\\\\t    - a fresh P-v8 reply that is not a forecast (decided from its shape alone);\\\\n   490\\\\t    - a settled no on a fresh reply;\\\\n   491\\\\t    - a settled defect on a fresh reply;\\\\n  3049\\\\t## D260 · 2026-11-02 · A judgement is a forecast against a reference: the rung the evidence in force makes most likely, judged against what the market expects; the answer states the reference and the implied outcome (judging-v6)\\\\n  3050\\\\t\\\\n  3051\\\\t- Alex, 2026-11-02, asked whether the judge's stance should stay an absolute-band lookup (the current reading) or be judged relative to expectations: \\\\\\\"门槛没有标准，按照你作为 hedge fund analyst 的认识来定\\\\\\\". Decided by Claude under that delegation: the definition below is Claude's analyst judgement, recorded as such, not Alex's words.\\\\n  3052\\\\t- Mechanism (arm 4 draw 1, all 356 judgements read, `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/review-2026-11-02.md` §7 and `proof-judging-v6.txt`): 8 of 314 later judgements moved a rung and 320 of 356 reasons say \\\\\\\"remains\\\\\\\"; the FY2027 total revenue question was judged 12 times at neutral while its upward pushes grew from 1 to 35, every reason \\\\\\\"the $392 billion estimate is inside the band … does not establish $400 billion\\\\\\\"; the gross-margin judgement wrote \\\\\\\"leans toward rung 2 but does not warrant moving\\\\\\\"; the 2027 hyperscaler-capex theme stayed below the band management's own forecast names because the forecast \\\\\\\"is not fact\\\\\\\". The judging-v5 prompt asked the judge to \\\\\\\"be precise about what is established\\\\\\\" and said only fact can establish a rung: the model read \\\\\\\"established\\\\\\\" as the bar for leaving a rung and the consensus figure as the anchor. A second cause stays open: the ladder's neutral band is written at opening without naming what it compares against (PRD 06 ladder rule 2 asks for it); that is the extraction's rule and is not changed here.\\\\n  3053\\\\t- Decided, the analyst's rule: (1) the rung is a forecast, the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved; \\\\\\\"not established\\\\\\\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. (2) The reference is what the market expects: consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline; a consensus or guidance figure alone keeps the judgement at the reference's rung and, once other evidence has arrived, is never the reason to stay. (3) The judge derives the outcome the evidence implies (reported figures and guidance give a run-rate; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it), checks it against the dependencies' conclusions (a part cannot exceed its whole; a figure spanning several periods or products gives the question only its share), compares it with the rung boundaries and moves when it crosses one. (4) Weight follows tier and novelty: fact fixes what is known; party statements are the strongest forecast input; third-party views and rumours move the forecast in proportion to their specificity; a repeat, another outlet or an opinion with no new fact or calculation moves nothing. (5) The answer states `reference` and `implied_outcome` as required fields from `judging-v6` (`judging.schema_for`; code refuses an empty one; stored beside the rung in `judgements.reference` / `implied_outcome`; a ledger written before v6 gains the columns at its first write), so the D3 stance gold can read the reasoning, not only the rung. Written where the judgement is specified: PRD 06 State rules (`docs/system-design/new-facts.js` STATE_RULES, the generated block) and this record.\\\\n  3054\\\\t- Proof (`proof-judging-v6.txt`, `proof-judging-v6b.txt`: the last stored judgement request of 14 theses of arm 4 draw 1 re-sent once each under v6 and read beside the stored v5 answers, about a cent): every answer names the reference and derives the implied outcome. Six rungs moved against the stored ones: non-GAAP gross margin 3 → 2 (Q1 reported 75% and Q2 guided 75% sit on the rung-2 boundary), 2027 hyperscaler capex 4 → 5 (management's own \\\\\\\"more than $1 trillion\\\\\\\"), China accelerator share 4 → 5 (share \\\\\\\"fallen to zero\\\\\\\"), China H200 authorization No → Yes (a reported plan to permit named firms and reported progress in reviews, six months before the deadline), Data Center revenue 2 → 3 ($355–360 billion derived from Q1 and the total-revenue proxy, below the $360 billion boundary), Blackwell+Rubin revenue 2 → 1 in the first send by annualising a two-year \\\\\\\"$1 trillion visibility\\\\\\\" figure to $545 billion, a part above its whole: clause (3)'s consistency check was added for it and the re-send gives rung 2 ($320–360 billion, a share of the Data Center segment). Total revenue stays at 3 with the arithmetic shown (H1 $172.6 billion from Q1 and the Q2 guide; $400 billion needs more than $227 billion in H2). Prompt 2,453 → 3,782 characters: the request defined neither what a rung means nor a reference and its \\\\\\\"established\\\\\\\" wording forced the defect; the two sentences that carried it were cut. Configuration `poc-v90` (poc-v89 with judging-v6); the default stays `poc-v69`. Tests: `tests/test_stance_fields.py`. Measured by re-sent stored requests, not by an arm (Alex: \\\\\\\"不要再跑这些有的没的臂了\\\\\\\").\\\\n  3069\\\\t## D263 · 2026-11-02 · The judge is written to the frozen gold's own reasoning (judging-v7, poc-v91); a gap to the gold is closed in the judge, not re-measured\\\\n  3070\\\\t\\\\n  3071\\\\t- Alex, after the first score on the frozen gold was reported as the system being \\\\\\\"wrong\\\\\\\" on some questions: \\\\\\\"不是啊什么叫错？我不是和你说了就按照claude的标准来就好了嘛\\\\\\\". The gold is Claude's (reader B's) standard by D262; a disagreement is the distance between the judge and that standard, to be closed in the judge's rule, not a verdict to be measured again.\\\\n  3072\\\\t- What reader B does that judging-v6 did not, read from B's answers on the questions that differed (`judgement-gold/reconcile-v1.md`, `gold-v1.json`): carries the guided growth forward rather than annualising the last quarter flat (Data Center, total revenue); discounts a management target for a product with no shipments by default (Vera CPU: two selling quarters, four million units at $5,000, the company's own choice of another CPU); sizes an announced but unsized commitment from its disclosed comparable (the Firmus backstop from Sharon's); derives a figure no one states from the accounting identities in the evidence (capex from operating less free cash flow); keeps linked conclusions consistent (China share against the H200 authorization theme). Written into `judging-v7.txt` as five clauses (v6 3,782 → 4,924 characters; reason: each clause is a behaviour of the frozen standard the judge lacked), named by `poc-v91`; schema and code unchanged.\\\\n  3073\\\\t- Proof on the stored requests of the questions whose arm-4 judgement differed from the gold (`proof-judging-v7a.txt`, `proof-judging-v7.txt`; one send each, cents): total revenue rung 3 → 2 (about $421 billion from the guided growth on FY2026's base; gold $400–435 billion), Data Center 3 → 2 (about $372 billion; gold $370–400 billion), Vera CPU 1 → 2 ($12 to below $20 billion, the target discounted for the volume not in hand; gold $8–18 billion), DRAM prices 3 → 2 (about +15%; gold +10–35%), financing total stays 4 ($33.5–39.8 billion; gold $25–60 billion), the Ohio guarantee stays Yes; China share stays below 1% in draw 1, consistent with that draw's H200 theme judged No (the gold has the authorization likely and the share 1–8%; the consistency clause ties the share to the theme, so it moves with it). Six of the seven re-sent questions now land in the gold's band; the end-to-end agreement under judging-v7 needs a run on `poc-v91`, which is Alex's call. A placement gap seen on the way: the Vera CPU question never held the fall-launch statement (filed under the Rubin launch questions), so the judge could not count selling quarters from evidence; the default-discount clause covers it, the filing is a D2 class to count.\\\\n1:{\\\\\\\"figures\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"F1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"what\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"population\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"NVIDIA\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"measure\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"revenue\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"CPU\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"period\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"F\\\\n    36\\\\t## 2. The E record across the four runs (same case, same passages)\\\\n    37\\\\t\\\\n    38\\\\t| Run | Codex writer | Claude writer |\\\\n    39\\\\t|---|---|---|\\\\n    40\\\\t| third run (D742 request) | 85% realisation, $34B; settled no | 1.85x bracket, $37B; yes in re-read 2, split under D747 |\\\\n    41\\\\t| targeted test (D745) | 90% realisation, $36B; settled no | 1.8x × 90% share, $32.4B; split, then no under D747 |\\\\n    42\\\\t| D749 | unresolved, specific gap; settled yes | 2.1x in full, $42B, asserting \\\\\\\"already selling at volume\\\\\\\"; split |\\\\n    43\\\\t| D750 | unresolved, specific gap; settled yes | 1.75x bracket midpoint, $35B; settled no |\\\\n    44\\\\t\\\\n    45\\\\t- **The Codex writer.** The repair (D749, D750) moved it from invented cuts to a justified unresolved, twice.\\\\n    46\\\\t- **The Claude writer.** It forecasts every time, by a different route each time, and has never been settled supported under the\\\\n    47\\\\t  current definitions.\\\\n    48\\\\t- **S** converged over D749 and D750: all four fresh forecasts are supported. Only defect marks on one answer remain split.\\\\n    49\\\\t- **P-v8** has been supported throughout.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r45.stream:59:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_30\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\\\\nD=decimal.Decimal\\\\ndef db(i,name='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''views'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',uri=True)\\\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\\\n return c\\\\ndef req(a,j):\\\\n c=a.execute('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',(j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],)).fetchone()\\\\n assert c and c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']==j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] and c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''purpose'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''judge'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',dict(j)\\\\n d=json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_json'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\n return d,json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''answer_json'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\nEVID=re.compile(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\"'^- (e'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\[.*?(?=\\\\\\\"'^- e'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+ \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\[|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Z)'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.M|re.S)\\\\ndef evidence(t):\\\\n b=t.split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''[Evidence in view under this thesis, '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[0]\\\\n m=dict((x.group(1),x.group(0).strip()) for x in EVID.finditer(b))\\\\n assert len(m)==int(b.split()[0]),(len(m),b[:20])\\\\n return m\\\\ndef user(d):\\\\n return next(m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''content'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] for m in d['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''messages'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] if m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''role'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''user'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')\\\\nUNIT=r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''(?:trillion(?:s)?|billions?|millions?|bn|mm|[BTM]|%|percent(?:age points?)?)'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\nNUM=r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+(?:,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d{3})*(?:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+)?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\nFIG=re.compile(rf'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''(?<\\\\\\\"'!['\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\w.])(?P<sign>[+−-])?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?P<lo>{NUM})(?:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*[-–—]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?P<hi>{NUM}))?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?P<unit>{UNIT})(?\\\\\\\"'![a-zA-Z0-9])'\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.I)\\\\nMULT={'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''trillion'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''trillions'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''t'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''billion'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''billions'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''bn'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''b'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''million'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''millions'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''mm'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''m'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')}\\\\ndef figures(t,unit):\\\\n out=[]\\\\n for m in FIG.finditer(t or '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\n  u=m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''unit'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''].lower()\\\\n  if (u in MULT)\\\\\\\"'!=(unit=='\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):continue\\\\n  mult=MULT.get(u,1)\\\\n  if m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''sign'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''-'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''−'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):mult=-mult\\\\n  for g in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''lo'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''hi'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\n   if m[g]:out.append(D(m[g].replace('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''))*mult)\\\\n return out\\\\ndef snippets(ed):\\\\n return [re.split(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (?:It replaces|Opinion, not verified:)'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',b,1)[0].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1] for b in ed.values()]\\\\ndef prior_text(t):\\\\n return t.split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''[Previous conclusion'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nAnswer per'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[0].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1]\\\\ndef tag(x,pattern): return bool(re.search(pattern,x or '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.I))\\\\ndef record(i):\\\\n v=db(i);a=db(i,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''archive'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')\\\\n return (v,a,v.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select j.*,k.unit from judgements j join view_keys k using(view_id) where k.unit in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''percent'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'') order by judgement_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))\\\\nfor i in (1,2,3):\\\\n v,a,rows=record(i)\\\\n C=collections.Counter(); first={}; prior={}; explicit=[]; matches={}\\\\n def tick(k,day):\\\\n  C[k]+=1\\\\n  first.setdefault(k,day)\\\\n def near(x,ys):\\\\n  return any(abs(x-y)<=D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.005'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')*max(abs(x),abs(y),D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.00000001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')) for y in ys)\\\\n for j in rows:\\\\n  d,raw=req(a,j);t=user(d);e=evidence(t);u=j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''unit'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']; dy=j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''publication_day'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''];id=j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''view_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']; key=(id,dy)\\\\n  assert all(raw[k]==j[k] for k in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''rung'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''reference'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')) and set(raw['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''cites'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])<=set(e), (i,j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\n  vals=figures(j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],u); ref=figures(j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''reference'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],u)\\\\n  s=snippets(e); shown=figures('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.join(s),u); quotes=figures('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.join(s1.split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    Quote: '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1] for s1 in s),u)\\\\n  tick('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''all-'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''+u,dy)\\\\n  if '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''[Not shown:'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' in t:tick('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''hidden'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\\\n  if vals:\\\\n   tick('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''parsed-'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''+u,dy)\\\\n   if not near(vals[0],shown):tick('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''lead no nearby-'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''+u,dy)\\\\n   if not near(vals[0],quotes):tick('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''lead no quote nearby-'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''+u,dy)\\\\n   if not any(near(x,shown) for x in vals):tick('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''no nearby at all-'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''+u,dy)\\\\n   if any(not near(x,shown) for x in vals):tick('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''at least one new-'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''+u,dy)\\\\n  if id in prior:\\\\n   tick('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''previous'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\\\n   if ref:\\\\n    tick('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''parsed-ref'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\\\n    own=bool(prior[id]) and near(ref[0],prior[id][:1])\\\\n    no=not near(ref[0],shown)\\\\n    carried=tag(j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''reference'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b(?:previous|prior|carried)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')\\\\n    prev=near(ref[0],figures(prior_text(t),u))\\\\n    if own and no:tick('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''own and no evidence'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\\\n    if carried and no:tick('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''carried and no evidence'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\\\n    if carried and prev and no:\\\\n     tick('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''carried prev no evidence'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\\\n     explicit.append((id,dy,j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''reference'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']))\\\\n    if carried and own and no:tick('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''carried own no evidence'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',dy)\\\\n    if i==2 and id=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v9'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' and dy in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''2026-09-15'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):assert no and prev and (own if dy.endswith('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''15'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'') else carried)\\\\n  prior[id]=vals\\\\n  if (i,id,dy) in ((2,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v9'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),(2,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v14'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),(2,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v29'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),(2,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v6'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''2026-09-19'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),(3,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v41'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')):\\\\n   print('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''control'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',i,id,dy,vals,[(str(x),near(x,shown)) for x in vals],ref)\\\\n print(i,dict(C),first)\\\\n print('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''carried'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',explicit[:14],explicit[-4:])\\\\n'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"1 {'all-USD': 737, 'parsed-USD': 736, 'lead no nearby-USD': 345, 'lead no quote nearby-USD': 389, 'no nearby at all-USD': 27, 'at least one new-USD': 524, 'previous': 821, 'parsed-ref': 798, 'hidden': 611, 'all-percent': 103, 'parsed-percent': 103, 'at least one new-percent': 66, 'own and no evidence': 4, 'lead no nearby-percent': 42, 'lead no quote nearby-percent': 42, 'carried and no evidence': 17, 'carried prev no evidence': 16, 'carried own no evidence': 1} {'all-USD': '2026-07-01', 'parsed-USD': '2026-07-01', 'lead no nearby-USD': '2026-07-01', 'lead no quote nearby-USD': '2026-07-01', 'no nearby at all-USD': '2026-07-01', 'at least one new-USD': '2026-07-01', 'previous': '2026-07-02', 'parsed-ref': '2026-07-02', 'hidden': '2026-07-07', 'all-percent': '2026-07-08', 'parsed-percent': '2026-07-08', 'at least one new-percent': '2026-07-08', 'own and no evidence': '2026-07-16', 'lead no nearby-percent': '2026-07-18', 'lead no quote nearby-percent': '2026-07-18', 'carried and no evidence': '2026-07-26', 'carried prev no evidence': '2026-07-26', 'carried own no evidence': '2026-08-02'}\\\\ncarried [('v2', '2026-07-26', 1919, 'No market consensus or NVIDIA guidance for the FY2027 outstanding total is supplied. The closest quantified disclosed baseline is $8.38 billion from the $3.5 billion added guarantee and Sharon AI’s $4.88 billion backstop, which sits in rung 4; the previous carried estimate including Firmus was about $11.5 billion, rung 5.'), ('v8', '2026-07-27', 2159, 'The carried-forward market-reference proxy is about $372.5 billion, in rung 2 ($350 billion to below $400 billion).'), ('v8', '2026-07-28', 2315, 'The carried-forward estimate is about $372.5 billion, in rung 2 ($350 billion to below $400 billion).'), ('v8', '2026-07-29', 2429, 'The carried-forward market estimate is about $372.5 billion, which is rung 2 ($350 billion to below $400 billion).'), ('v8', '2026-07-30', 2541, 'The carried-forward market estimate is about $372.5 billion, in rung 2 ($350 billion to less than $400 billion).'), ('v8', '2026-07-31', 2630, 'The carried-forward market estimate is about $372.5 billion, which sits in rung 2 ($350 billion to less than $400 billion).'), ('v1', '2026-08-02', 2692, 'No aggregate market consensus or NVIDIA guidance is supplied, so there is no external reference figure to place on the ladder. The carried base case of roughly $10–11 billion is in rung 4.'), ('v8', '2026-08-02', 2694, 'Analyst consensus is the reference; no numeric consensus is supplied in the current evidence. The carried comparison places it below the implied outcome, most consistently on rung 2 ($350bn to below $400bn).'), ('v1', '2026-08-03', 2728, 'No aggregate market consensus or NVIDIA guidance for total FY2027 credit-support obligations is supplied. The carried base estimate of about $10–11 billion is the available reference and sits in rung 4; the reported $250 billion Ohio proposal is not itself an established reference for committed obligations.'), ('v1', '2026-08-05', 2808, 'No aggregate market consensus or NVIDIA guidance for total FY2027 credit-support commitments is supplied. The carried base estimate of about $10–11 billion is rung 4; the reported $250 billion Ohio guarantee headline, if fully committed, would be in rung 5, but is not the most reliable reference for the committed amount by the due date.'), ('v8', '2026-08-05', 2805, 'Analyst consensus; no numeric figure is supplied in this view. The carried comparison places the reference most consistently in rung 2 ($350bn to below $400bn).'), ('v1', '2026-08-06', 2871, 'No explicit market consensus or aggregate NVIDIA guidance is supplied. The carried non-Ohio estimate of about $10–11 billion is rung 4; the carried estimate including a discounted Ohio contribution is about $20–21 billion, rung 5. The reported $250 billion Ohio figure, if taken in full, would also be rung 5 but is not the reference forecast used here.'), ('v8', '2026-08-09', 2975, 'Analyst consensus, as described in the previous conclusion, is $350bn to below $400bn: rung 2. No exact consensus estimate is supplied.'), ('v8', '2026-08-25', 4589, \\\\\\\"The carried-forward analyst-consensus reference is $350 billion to below $400 billion, rung 2. Morningstar's FY2027 estimate of $361 billion is likewise rung 2.\\\\\\\")] [('v8', '2026-08-09', 2975, 'Analyst consensus, as described in the previous conclusion, is $350bn to below $400bn: rung 2. No exact consensus estimate is supplied.'), ('v8', '2026-08-25', 4589, \\\\\\\"The carried-forward analyst-consensus reference is $350 billion to below $400 billion, rung 2. Morningstar's FY2027 estimate of $361 billion is likewise rung 2.\\\\\\\"), ('v8', '2026-08-26', 5093, \\\\\\\"Analyst consensus carried forward from the previous judgement is $350 billion to below $400 billion, rung 2. Morningstar's $361 billion FY2027 estimate is also in rung 2.\\\\\\\"), ('v8', '2026-08-27', 5304, \\\\\\\"The carried-forward market consensus is $350 billion to below $400 billion, which is rung 2; Morningstar's specific $361 billion FY2027 estimate is also rung 2.\\\\\\\")]\\\\ncontrol 2 v6 2026-09-19 [Decimal('1190.00'), Decimal('730'), Decimal('800'), Decimal('1300.0')] [('1190.00', False), ('730', True), ('800', True), ('1300.0', True)] [Decimal('1080.00'), Decimal('900'), Decimal('1100.0')]\\\\ncontrol 2 v14 2026-09-20 [Decimal('419'), Decimal('81.6'), Decimal('96.2'), Decimal('113.5'), Decimal('110.16'), Decimal('127')] [('419', False), ('81.6', True), ('96.2', True), ('113.5', True), ('110.16', True), ('127', False)] [Decimal('411'), Decimal('400'), Decimal('450'), Decimal('215.9'), Decimal('405')]\\\\ncontrol 2 v9 2026-09-20 [Decimal('410'), Decimal('164'), Decimal('100'), Decimal('108'), Decimal('146')] [('410', False), ('164', True), ('100', True), ('108', True), ('146', False)] [Decimal('414'), Decimal('400'), Decimal('450')]\\\\ncontrol 2 v29 2026-09-20 [Decimal('53'), Decimal('25'), Decimal('18'), Decimal('3.5'), Decimal('10'), Decimal('2.5')] [('53', False), ('25', True), ('18', True), ('3.5', True), ('10', True), ('2.5', True)] [Decimal('70'), Decimal('50'), Decimal('75')]\\\\n2 {'all-USD': 664, 'parsed-USD': 664, 'lead no nearby-USD': 378, 'lead no quote nearby-USD': 378, 'no nearby at all-USD': 27, 'at least one new-USD': 522, 'previous': 823, 'parsed-ref': 764, 'hidden': 595, 'all-percent': 176, 'parsed-percent': 175, 'at least one new-percent': 112, 'carried and no evidence': 29, 'carried prev no evidence': 29, 'lead no nearby-percent': 69, 'lead no quote nearby-percent': 69, 'no nearby at all-percent': 15, 'own and no evidence': 9, 'carried own no evidence': 1} {'all-USD': '2026-07-01', 'parsed-USD': '2026-07-01', 'lead no nearby-USD': '2026-07-01', 'lead no quote nearby-USD': '2026-07-01', 'no nearby at all-USD': '2026-07-01', 'at least one new-USD': '2026-07-01', 'previous': '2026-07-02', 'parsed-ref': '2026-07-02', 'hidden': '2026-07-07', 'all-percent': '2026-07-17', 'parsed-percent': '2026-07-17', 'at least one new-percent': '2026-07-21', 'carried and no evidence': '2026-07-22', 'carried prev no evidence': '2026-07-22', 'lead no nearby-percent': '2026-07-22', 'lead no quote nearby-percent': '2026-07-22', 'no nearby at all-percent': '2026-07-22', 'own and no evidence': '2026-08-29', 'carried own no evidence': '2026-09-09'}\\\\ncarried [('v9', '2026-07-22', 1453, \\\\\\\"No full-year FY2027 Data Center consensus or company guidance is supplied. The available annual run-rate reference is about $372B (FY2026 Data Center revenue of $193.7B carried forward at Q1 FY2027's 92% year-over-year growth), which sits in rung 3. NVIDIA's approximately $91B Q2 total-revenue guidance, assuming no China Data Center revenue, is a near-term reference, not a full-year estimate.\\\\\\\"), ('v9', '2026-07-24', 1649, \\\\\\\"Approximately $372B, in rung 3, using FY2026 Data Center revenue of $193.7B carried forward at FY2027 Q1's 92% year-over-year growth rate; no separate consensus estimate is supplied.\\\\\\\"), ('v9', '2026-07-25', 1717, \\\\\\\"No explicit consensus estimate is supplied. The reference is about $372B, calculated as FY2026 Data Center revenue of $193.7B carried forward at FY2027 Q1's 92% year-over-year growth rate; this is rung 3.\\\\\\\"), ('v9', '2026-07-26', 1787, \\\\\\\"Market reference: about $372 billion, in rung 3, based on FY2026 Data Center revenue of $193.7 billion carried forward at FY2027 Q1's 92% year-over-year growth rate.\\\\\\\"), ('v9', '2026-07-27', 2013, 'About $372 billion, in rung 3, using FY2026 Data Center revenue of $193.7 billion carried forward at the 92% year-over-year growth reported for FY2027 Q1. No separate consensus figure is supplied.'), ('v9', '2026-08-17', 3608, \\\\\\\"About $372B, in rung 3: FY2026 Data Center revenue of $193.7B carried forward at FY2027 Q1's 92% year-over-year growth; this is the run-rate reference, not the forecast.\\\\\\\"), ('v9', '2026-08-18', 3747, 'Approximately $372B, the market expectation stated in the previous conclusion; that lies in rung 3 ($350B to below $400B).'), ('v9', '2026-08-19', 3874, 'Approximately $372B, in rung 3 ($350B to below $400B), as the market/reference estimate carried forward from FY2026 Data Center revenue at the reported FY2027 Q1 year-over-year growth rate.'), ('v9', '2026-08-21', 3993, 'Approximately $372B, as carried from the prior conclusion; that reference sits in rung 3 ($350B to below $400B).'), ('v9', '2026-08-22', 4029, 'Approximately $372B, based on FY2026 Data Center revenue of $193.7B carried forward at 92% growth; this reference is in rung 3.'), ('v9', '2026-08-24', 4283, 'The market reference carried from the previous judgement is approximately $372B, derived there from FY2026 Data Center revenue of $193.7B carried forward at the reported 92% growth rate; this sits in rung 3 ($350B to below $400B). No new FY2027 consensus figure is supplied.'), ('v9', '2026-08-25', 4437, 'The carried market expectation is approximately $372B for FY2027 Data Center revenue, which is rung 3 ($350B to below $400B).'), ('v9', '2026-08-26', 4944, 'The carried market reference is approximately $372B for FY2027 Data Center revenue, at rung 3 ($350B to below $400B).'), ('v9', '2026-08-27', 5139, 'The carried market reference is approximately $372 billion, on rung 3 (Neutral: $350 billion to below $400 billion).')] [('v9', '2026-09-13', 7770, 'Approximately $372 billion, the market reference carried from the prior conclusion; this sits at rung 3.'), ('v9', '2026-09-14', 7939, 'The market reference carried from the previous judgement is approximately $372 billion, which sits in rung 3 ($350 billion to below $400 billion).'), ('v9', '2026-09-16', 8206, 'The approximately $414 billion FY2027 expectation carried from the previous conclusion is the reference; it sits at rung 2 ($400 billion to below $450 billion).'), ('v9', '2026-09-20', 8737, 'The market reference supplied by the previous conclusion is approximately $414 billion for FY2027, which sits at rung 2 ($400 billion to below $450 billion).')]\\\\ncontrol 3 v41 2026-09-20 [Decimal('38'), Decimal('39'), Decimal('40')] [('38', False), ('39', False), ('40', False)] [Decimal('20'), Decimal('40')]\\\\n3 {'all-USD': 641, 'parsed-USD': 641, 'at least one new-USD': 463, 'previous': 731, 'parsed-ref': 699, 'lead no nearby-USD': 283, 'lead no quote nearby-USD': 286, 'no nearby at all-USD': 25, 'hidden': 495, 'all-percent': 108, 'parsed-percent': 108, 'lead no nearby-percent': 36, 'lead no quote nearby-percent': 56, 'no nearby at all-percent': 3, 'at least one new-percent': 45, 'own and no evidence': 8} {'all-USD': '2026-07-01', 'parsed-USD': '2026-07-01', 'at least one new-USD': '2026-07-01', 'previous': '2026-07-02', 'parsed-ref': '2026-07-02', 'lead no nearby-USD': '2026-07-03', 'lead no quote nearby-USD': '2026-07-03', 'no nearby at all-USD': '2026-07-04', 'hidden': '2026-07-07', 'all-percent': '2026-08-06', 'parsed-percent': '2026-08-06', 'lead no nearby-percent': '2026-08-06', 'lead no quote nearby-percent': '2026-08-06', 'no nearby at all-percent': '2026-08-06', 'at least one new-percent': '2026-08-06', 'own and no evidence': '2026-09-04'}\\\\ncarried [] []\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72b.stream:67:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_34\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"ls poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/manifests | head; rg -n -m1 '2026-08-28' poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/replay.log | cut -c1-200; ls poc/mock | head -40; nl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '448,454p'; nl -ba poc/ui/src/adapters/bundle.js | sed -n '50,78p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '302,314p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"day-2026-07-01.json\\nday-2026-07-02.json\\nday-2026-07-03.json\\nday-2026-07-04.json\\nday-2026-07-05.json\\nday-2026-07-06.json\\nday-2026-07-07.json\\nday-2026-07-08.json\\nday-2026-07-09.json\\nday-2026-07-10.json\\n60:2026-08-28 | items  50 extracted  49 merged  1 skipped  0 failed  0 | evidence 275 new views  0 judged  31 changed  19 closed 0 | open views 35 | day $0.23 total $4.30 calls 5663\\ndata.en.json\\ndata.json\\nindex.html\\nindex.template.html\\nlibrary-preview-20261026.html\\ntranslations.json\\ntranslations.shard-0.json\\ntranslations.shard-1.json\\ntranslations.shard-2.json\\ntranslations.shard-3.json\\n   448\\t**The one next task: when release work opens, a $0 check of the reader's screen for number questions (D756).** On a stored number\\n   449\\tquestion that has a forecast and history, the reader must see only the question, its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\".\\n   450\\t\\n   451\\t- **Alex closed the v13s judge line at its STOP** (D756: end the line, release with \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"). Nothing from it enters the\\n   452\\t  product, and poc-v118 stays the product.\\n   453\\t- **No release work is open yet.** No other task is queued on the number-answer line.\\n   454\\t\\n    50\\t    const labels = view.rungs.map((r) => (r.label || '').trim());\\n    51\\t    if (!EVENT_OUTCOMES.includes(labels.join('|')))\\n    52\\t      throw new ContractError(\\n    53\\t        `${path}/rungs`,\\n    54\\t        \\\"an event's choices must be Yes/No or Yes/Ruled out/Still open\\\",\\n    55\\t      );\\n    56\\t    return labels;\\n    57\\t  }\\n    58\\t  if (view.answer_shape === 'unrecorded' || view.favourable_end === 'n/a')\\n    59\\t    return view.rungs.map((r, i) => String(i + 1)); // a position, not a score: the ladder states no direction\\n    60\\t  if (view.rungs.every((r) => r.score)) return view.rungs.map((r) => r.score);\\n    61\\t  if (view.rungs.length === 2) {\\n    62\\t    // a yes/no ladder may list No first: each rung shows its own outcome; other two-rung labels keep their order\\n    63\\t    const own = view.rungs.map((r) => YES_NO[(r.label || '').trim()]);\\n    64\\t    return own.includes('Yes') && own.includes('No') ? own : ['Yes', 'No'];\\n    65\\t  }\\n    66\\t  if (KINDS[view.kind] === 'Theme thesis') {\\n    67\\t    const first = representative(view.rungs[0]);\\n    68\\t    const last = representative(view.rungs.at(-1));\\n    69\\t    if (last > first) return [...ORDINAL].reverse();\\n    70\\t  }\\n    71\\t  return ORDINAL;\\n    72\\t}\\n    73\\tfunction source(value = {}, day = null) {\\n    74\\t  return {\\n    75\\t    title: value.title || '',\\n    76\\t    publisher: value.publisher || '',\\n    77\\t    category: value.category || '',\\n    78\\t    uri: value.uri || value.source_uri || null,\\n   302\\t        errors.append(f'rung moved from {last[\\\"rung\\\"]} to {data[\\\"rung\\\"]} but changed is false')\\n   303\\t    return errors\\n   304\\t\\n   305\\t\\n   306\\tdef _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer):\\n   307\\t    data = vocabulary.judgement_answer(answer.data)\\n   308\\t    judgement_id = store.insert(conn, 'judgements', view_id=view_id, seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'], rung=data['rung'],\\n   309\\t                                reasons=data['reasons'], cited_evidence_json=json.dumps(data['cites']), cited_views_json=json.dumps(data['cites_views']),\\n   310\\t                                pushes_json=json.dumps(data['pushes'], ensure_ascii=False), changed=1 if data['changed'] else 0,\\n   311\\t                                theme_pushes_json=json.dumps(data.get('theme_pushes', []), ensure_ascii=False),\\n   312\\t                                reference=data.get('reference'), implied_outcome=data.get('implied_outcome'),\\n   313\\t                                why_changed=data['why_changed'], config_checksum=cfg.checksum, call_id=answer.call_id,\\n   314\\t                                request_sha256=answer.request_sha256, publication_day=item['publication_day'])\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72b.stream:74:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_38\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"1. **Revision 2 leaves a confirmed forecast leak through Yes/No answers.** In `old-3`, the August 25 explanation for a shipment question (`v36`, judgement 799) says that the 2027 spending forecast is “around $1 trillion.” In `old-1`, the August 28 explanation for the Firmus investment (`v10`, judgement 865) gives the selected band for **both** the 2026 and 2027 spending questions. I read both explanations through `service.history()`. The judge receives related questions’ selected bands and reasons, and history returns the resulting text. Revision 2 promises to return Yes/No records exactly as they are today. Those requirements conflict on stored data. Preserve the Yes/No outcome, and specify how release readers handle explanations that disclose another question’s forecast. Use these two records as acceptance cases. [Design:95](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:95) · [judging.py:208](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:208) · [service.py:263](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:263) · [bundle.py:120](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/bundle.py:120)\\n\\n2. **Identity works on the four stores if the Yes/No test uses the stored vocabulary.** I checked every question. The three comparison stores split into **19 number / 28 event**, **17 / 26**, and **18 / 31**. All 85 event questions have an `event` or `policy_event` measure. In the sealed ledger, 43 of 94 questions parse as money, 21 further number questions are safely withheld by the fallback, and 30 are Yes/No. All 30 use `是` and `否`. A literal English test would withhold all 30 incorrectly. Specify exactly two labels, canonicalized with the existing vocabulary, in either order. With that reading I found no wrong show-or-withhold result in the four stores. I also verified both round-72 counterexamples directly. Sealed revenue `v3` parses from its conditions. Xbox `v37` has the `growth_rate` measure and bounds around zero, but its two answers are explicitly Yes and No. [Design:30](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:30) · [identity.py:10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/identity.py:10) · [vocabulary.py:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24) · [test_service.py:90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:90) · [test_service.py:119](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:119) · [Xbox store manifest:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-10-25-english/data-manifest.md:20)\\n\\n3. **The ambiguity rule still has a gap for a record with a key.** Section 2 limits its fallback to records with *no key*. The opening check accepts a ladder with every bound null. I cleared only the bounds on an in-memory copy of `old-1/v8` and ran its five original English conditions through the service parser. All five were refused. The `segment_revenue` key still exists, so this supported shape reaches no stated outcome. Withhold and list every unresolved record, whether or not it has a key. That closes the gap without extending the money parser to every language and unit. [Design:34](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:34) · [extraction.py:493](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:493) · [service.py:422](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:422) · [service.py:499](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:499)\\n\\n4. **The idea card has a second path that restores hidden bands.** Revision 2 covers candidate summaries, related questions, evaluation, and `/ideas` with either bundle setting. But the configured idea-summary version reads the ladder directly from storage when building its answer format, and the summary call adds it to the input again. I passed `v8` through that helper with its judgement removed. It added back “at least $400 billion” and “less than $250 billion.” Exclude withheld ladders from both reads and inspect the actual summary request in the test. A clean `judged` field alone does not establish that the idea prose is clean. [Design:69](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:69) · [poc-v118-idea.json:94](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/config/poc-v118-idea.json:94) · [idea.py:350](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:350) · [idea_composite.py:255](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea_composite.py:255) · [idea_composite.py:281](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea_composite.py:281)\\n\\n5. **The approved screen, `claim_position`, search ranking, processing dates, closing text, and fixed setting are addressed in the design.** The question page keeps the question, its sources and “Forecast unavailable,” including amounts a source actually quoted. Evaluation returns only the marker. Assessment counts and dates are omitted, and a closing record can say “closed” without its final band. Search ranks possible outcomes without reading the selected one. The design also identifies the browser’s separate assessment-date sort and fixes the release setting at `withheld`. These provisions match Alex’s decision and the cited readers. [D756:11833](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11833) · [Design:46](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:46) · [Design:65](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:65) · [Design:81](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:81) · [search.py:275](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/search.py:275) · [library.js:32](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/model/library.js:32) · [service.py:553](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:553)\\n\\n6. **The main exports are named, but a clean HTML file can reload unrestricted data.** The page opens its embedded snapshot, then automatically fetches `/library` from an API that defaults to `127.0.0.1:8788`. It replaces the snapshot after checking only that the response is a complete library. The idea page fetches its bundles from the same address. Since revision 2 explicitly leaves the existing POC setting open, a release HTML file opened beside that POC can show its forecasts. Bind the release page to the release service or have it refuse unrestricted responses. Apply the same content check to prepared JSON before embedding it. The static builder also embeds `--composite-trials` separately from the main dataset, and the translated `data.en.json` export retains judgement prose. Keep those inputs outside the release package unless checked. [Design:72](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:72) · [bootstrap.js:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:20) · [bootstrap.js:193](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:193) · [bootstrap.js:254](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:254) · [mock_build.py:61](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_build.py:61) · [mock_translate.py:114](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_translate.py:114)\\n\\n7. **The acceptance check selects the right question, but cannot prove the closing case as written.** `old-1/v8` has 75 judgements, 69 rows marked changed, and 9 actual moves between bands. Its only stored switch is `open=1, reason=created`. Round 72 generated the closing sentence by calling the formatter. There is no closing sentence on this question for the release page to hide. Keep `v8` for the page and same-sources check. Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real stored closing switch, and first verify that the unrestricted response exposes its final band. For the $0 idea check, use a recorded or test transport and inspect the composed request as well as the delivered card. [Design:109](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:109) · [pull.py:11](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/pull.py:11) · [service.py:280](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:280) · [service.py:356](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:356) · [idea.py:218](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:218)\\n\\n**Verdict — not ready.** An unchanged Yes/No explanation already discloses a number forecast in the stored data. Revision 2 needs to resolve that conflict and close the idea, identity, and export gaps before Alex opens release work. This review was read-only and cost $0.\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74e.stream:18:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: revision 5, for council round 74e. No code yet.** Release work was opened by the council under D439 (D758). The behaviour is\\n     4\\tfixed by D726, D756 and `FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4). This page holds the AGENTS §2 tables for the first slice.\\n     5\\t\\n     6\\t**Revision 2 answers `codex-r74.md`** (see `claude-r74.md`):\\n     7\\t- the pass condition is an origin check of every field against its stored source, not a string sweep;\\n     8\\t- a missing source item is refused;\\n     9\\t- the package is checked before it is moved into place;\\n    10\\t- the manifest is a closed set;\\n    11\\t- the bound is validated as a date;\\n    12\\t- narrow reads;\\n    13\\t- size and speed budgets;\\n    14\\t- tests that separate every branch;\\n    15\\t- `object`, `kind` and groups dropped;\\n    16\\t- no idea submission.\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\tThe evidence summary stays as extraction stored it (§8, disputed in `claude-r74.md`).\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\t**Revision 3 answers `codex-r74b.md`.**\\n    21\\t- The checker derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package: the date, each question's class, the records and their counts.\\n    22\\t- A missing source item refuses `check` too.\\n    23\\t- The files must be two regular, non-symlink files, with no duplicate JSON member names.\\n    24\\t- The staging folder has one owner.\\n    25\\t- The builder's refusal is tested through the builder.\\n    26\\t- The diagnostics read only the columns a store has.\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\t**Revision 4 answers `codex-r74c.md`.**\\n    29\\t- One date rule for build and `check`.\\n    30\\t- Questions are ordered by `created_seq, rowid`.\\n    31\\t- (Superseded in revision 5.) The build claimed its output folder before staging.\\n    32\\t- Cleanup sits where the staging path is known.\\n    33\\t- A report failure after publication has its own outcome.\\n    34\\t- The builder's refusal is proved through the real command on a scratch copy.\\n    35\\t- Tests 9, 13, 14 and 15 are sharpened.\\n    36\\t\\n    37\\t**Revision 5 answers `codex-r74d.md` with one structural rule** (AGENTS §1: the publication mechanism drew findings in 74b, 74c and\\n    38\\t74d). Staging is private, and the only public step is one atomic move that refuses any existing destination. There is no public\\n    39\\tclaim, so nothing public is created early or cleaned up. Staging is removed in a `finally` covering its whole life, so any error,\\n    40\\tdatabase errors included, leaves nothing at `--out`.\\n    41\\t\\n    42\\t## 0. Scope\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\t- **Slice 1 (this page), $0:**\\n    45\\t  - the exporter `release_export` and its self-check;\\n    46\\t  - the package writer, the package check and the origin check;\\n    47\\t  - the release builder, which calls the exporter directly;\\n    48\\t  - tests and mutants;\\n    49\\t  - the $0 release check on stored stores.\\n    50\\t- **Slice 2, next.** The release page reads only the package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite\\n    51\\t  trials, no idea submission control or route. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen, which completes D756's screen check.\\n    52\\t- **No idea submission in the release** (council 74). The idea path (`idea.py`) reads the ledger at every step and calls a paid model\\n    53\\t  per idea. The design's §5 idea acceptance (an idea card backed only by `v8`, and its composed request) is carried forward as pending\\n    54\\t  for the first idea-enabled slice.\\n    55\\t- **Not in scope:**\\n    56\\t  - the POC, its API, MCP and page (unchanged);\\n    57\\t  - colleagues' page;\\n    58\\t  - frozen pieces, extraction included;\\n    59\\t  - any model call;\\n    60\\t  - commit, publish, deploy.\\n    61\\t\\n    62\\t## 1. What is built\\n    63\\t\\n    64\\t`src/hivemind/release.py` is the one owner, beside `service.py`.\\n    65\\t\\n    66\\t- **Constants:**\\n    67\\t  - `FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'`;\\n    68\\t  - `ALLOW_LIST = 'release-allow-list/1'`;\\n    69\\t  - `FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE = 'Forecast unavailable'`;\\n    70\\t  - `PACKAGE_FILES = {'manifest.json', 'release-data.json'}`.\\n    71\\t- **`ALLOWED`:** the closed key set per record type.\\n    72\\t\\n    73\\t  | Record | Keys |\\n    74\\t  |---|---|\\n    75\\t  | envelope | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `questions` |\\n    76\\t  | number question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (= `number`), `forecast` (= the marker), `evidence` |\\n    77\\t  | event or Yes/No question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (`event` or `yes_no`), `answers` (the two stored rung labels, in position order), `answer` (the stored label of the latest judgement's rung on or before the bound, or null), `evidence` |\\n    78\\t  | evidence in force at the bound | `id`, `one_line`, `quote`, `tier`, `speaker`, `original_who`, `original_day`, `sources` |\\n    79\\t  | source recorded on or before the bound | `title`, `publisher`, `day`, `uri` |\\n    80\\t  | manifest | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `data_sha256` |\\n    81\\t\\n    82\\t- **`question_class(views_db, view_id, labels)`** (design §3):\\n    83\\t  - `event` when the view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES`. The key is read as `select measure from view_keys`, and\\n    84\\t    only when the table exists;\\n    85\\t  - `yes_no` when there are exactly two labels which, through `vocabulary.canonical('label', …)`, are `Yes` and `No` in either order;\\n    86\\t  - `number` otherwise: a view with no key, or one whose bands cannot be resolved.\\n    87\\t- **`release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None)`:**\\n    88\\t  - pins both connections (`bundle.read_snapshot`);\\n    89\\t  - resolves the bound with `service.resolve_bound`, refuses a store with no default day, and validates the bound with\\n    90\\t    `date.fromisoformat`;\\n    91\\t  - exports every view that exists at the bound (`service.view_exists`), closed ones included, in `created_seq, rowid` order;\\n    92\\t  - builds each record field by field from the table above, with column-limited SQL:\\n    93\\t    - `select view_id, question, created_seq from views order by created_seq, rowid`;\\n    94\\t    - `select position, label from rungs`;\\n    95\\t    - `select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1`;\\n    96\\t    - `service.is_open_as_of`, which reads only `open` and `after_seq`;\\n    97\\t  - takes evidence in force from `service.evidence` and its fields from that record;\\n    98\\t  - looks up each source's `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri` in the items database by `input_id`. A visible source whose item is\\n    99\\t    missing raises `ReleaseRefused` (there is no fallback to the id);\\n   100\\t  - calls `check_export` on its own result before returning (AGENTS §3: the writer refuses).\\n   101\\t- **`check_export(data)`:** the closed-set check.\\n   102\\t  - Every dict at every level has exactly its record type's keys.\\n   103\\t  - Value checks:\\n   104\\t    - `format` and `allow_list` equal the constants, and `as_of` is an ISO date;\\n   105\\t    - `class` is in its set;\\n   106\\t    - a number record's `forecast` is the marker;\\n   107\\t    - `answers` is two strings, and `answer` is one of them or null;\\n   108\\t    - `open` is a bool and every text field is a string.\\n   109\\t  - It returns the counts it judged: questions per class, evidence, sources.\\n   110\\t- **`check_origins(views_db, items_db, data, expected_as_of)`:** the pass condition. It is independent of the exporter's code path.\\n   111\\t  It derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package.\\n   112\\t  - **The bound: one rule for both commands.** `expected_as_of` is given by the caller.\\n   113\\t    - The builder passes the bound it resolved: `service.resolve_bound` on the requested day, or the default when none is given; an\\n   114\\t      omitted day with no default is refused.\\n   115\\t    - `check` passes the package's `as_of` through the same `service.resolve_bound`, which refuses a day after a store's last\\n   116\\t      completed day. A legacy ledger with no completed days accepts any valid date in both commands alike.\\n   117\\t    - The package's `as_of` must equal `expected_as_of`.\\n   118\\t  - **The class** of each question is derived from the stored measure and labels (`question_class`). The permitted keys and values\\n   119\\t    are then chosen from that class, never from the package's `class` field.\\n   120\\t  - **Order and counts.** The questions are compared as an ordered list in `created_seq, rowid` order, as `bundle.library` orders\\n   121\\t    them (`old-2/v2` and `v3` share sequence 8). Each question's evidence is compared in link order (`evidence_links.id`), and its\\n   122\\t    sources in row order (`evidence_sources.id`). A duplicate question, evidence record or source therefore fails.\\n   123\\t\\n   124\\t  It compares every field with its permitted stored source at the bound, by direct SQL:\\n   125\\t  - the question set equals the views visible at the bound, with `question` equal to `views.question`;\\n   126\\t  - `open` equals the latest visible switch's `open`;\\n   127\\t  - for `event` and `yes_no`: `answers` equal the rung labels in position order, and `answer` equals the label of the latest judgement\\n   128\\t    rung on or before the bound, or null;\\n   129\\t  - for `number`: only the marker;\\n   130\\t  - the evidence id set equals the links visible at the bound, minus those whose latest replacement is visible, computed in its own\\n   131\\t    SQL. Each evidence field equals the `evidence` row's column;\\n   132\\t  - each source list starts from every visible `evidence_sources` row, in row order, with `day` taken from\\n   133\\t    `evidence_sources.publication_day`. Each row needs a matching `items` row for `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri`; a row with no\\n   134\\t    item raises `ReleaseRefused` (a left join, so a missing item is never silently dropped).\\n   135\\t\\n   136\\t  Any difference raises `ReleaseRefused`, naming the question, the field and the evidence id. It returns the number of fields\\n   137\\t  compared.\\n   138\\t- **`stage(out_dir)`:** creates a private staging folder with a name unique to this invocation, `tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=out_dir.parent,\\n   139\\t  prefix='.<name>.staging-')`. Creation is exclusive, so only this invocation owns it. It returns the path.\\n   140\\t- **`write_package(data, staged)`:** writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` into the staging folder. It creates nothing\\n   141\\t  else.\\n   142\\t- **`publish(staged, out_dir)`:** one atomic move that refuses any existing destination, empty or not:\\n   143\\t  - on macOS, `renamex_np(staged, out_dir, RENAME_EXCL)` through `ctypes`. Verified on this Mac: onto a free path it succeeds; onto\\n   144\\t    an existing empty or non-empty folder it fails with `EEXIST`, and both folders stay as they were;\\n   145\\t  - on Linux, `renameat2(AT_FDCWD, staged, AT_FDCWD, out_dir, RENAME_NOREPLACE)`;\\n   146\\t  - where neither call exists, or the filesystem lacks support (`ENOTSUP`, `EINVAL`), it raises `ReleaseRefused`.\\n   147\\t\\n   148\\t  It never replaces, creates or removes anything at `out_dir` except by that one move.\\n   149\\t- **`check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None)`:**\\n   150\\t  - the directory holds exactly `PACKAGE_FILES`, each a regular file and not a symbolic link (`os.lstat`), with no subdirectories;\\n   151\\t  - both files parse as JSON with no duplicate member name at any level (an `object_pairs_hook` that refuses a repeated key);\\n   152\\t  - the manifest has exactly its four keys, and its `format`, `allow_list` and `as_of` equal the data's;\\n   153\\t  - its sha256 equals the data file's;\\n   154\\t  - the data passes `check_export`, and, when the stores are given, `check_origins` with the expected bound;\\n   155\\t  - it returns the counts.\\n   156\\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`** is for the report only. It lists the number questions whose `service.ladder_bands(rungs)`\\n   157\\t  returns `(None, reason)`, with the reason and whether the view has a key. Its output never enters the package.\\n   158\\t\\n   159\\t`scripts/release_build.py`:\\n   160\\t- **`build --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:**\\n   161\\t  1. refuse an existing `--out` early, as a convenience; `publish` holds the guarantee;\\n   162\\t  2. resolve the bound once (`service.resolve_bound`, `date.fromisoformat`);\\n   163\\t  3. `stage(--out)`. From here a `finally` removes this staging folder if it still exists;\\n   164\\t  4. `release_export` at that bound;\\n   165\\t  5. `write_package` into the staging folder;\\n   166\\t  6. `check_package` on the staged folder, with the stores and the resolved bound;\\n   167\\t  7. `publish` to `--out`;\\n   168\\t  8. write `<out>.report.json` beside the package, through a temporary file and `os.replace`.\\n   169\\t\\n   170\\t  The failure outcomes:\\n   171\\t  - **Before publication** (steps 2–7): any exception, whether `ReleaseRefused`, `OSError`, `sqlite3.Error` or another, prints the\\n   172\\t    reason and exits 1. The `finally` removes this build's staging folder; nothing exists at `--out` from this build. A corrected\\n   173\\t    retry at the same `--out` succeeds.\\n   174\\t  - **After publication** (step 8 fails): the package is final and checked. Exit 2 with \\\"package published and checked; report not\\n   175\\t    written; run `check` to regenerate it\\\".\\n   176\\t\\n   177\\t  It has no input path for prepared or translated JSON, and it takes no clock reading; the folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\\n   178\\t- **`check <out> --ledger --items`:** re-runs `check_package` on an existing package, with the stores, the package's `as_of`\\n   179\\t  validated against the store (above), and the regular-file and duplicate-key checks. It leaves the package in place and rewrites\\n   180\\t  `<out>.report.json`. This is also the retry after a report write failed. Its report gives `check_seconds` and marks\\n   181\\t  `export_seconds` as not measured.\\n   182\\t- **The report:**\\n   183\\t  - the store path and the bound;\\n   184\\t  - counts per class;\\n   185\\t  - the unresolved list;\\n   186\\t  - the fields compared;\\n   187\\t  - bytes;\\n   188\\t  - `export_seconds` (build only) and `check_seconds`.\\n   189\\t\\n   190\\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\\n   191\\t\\n   192\\t| State / event | What happens | What is written | Day used |\\n   193\\t|---|---|---|---|\\n   194\\t| Store's first day still in progress | `FirstDayNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | none |\\n   195\\t| Store with no completed day and no judgement, `--as-of` omitted | refused: \\\"no default day; supply --as-of\\\" | nothing | none |\\n   196\\t| `--as-of` not a valid date (`2026-08-99`) | refused by `date.fromisoformat` | nothing | none |\\n   197\\t| `--as-of` after the last completed day | `BoundNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | requested day |\\n   198\\t| `--as-of` valid, before the first visible question | empty `questions`; the report says 0 | package | bound |\\n   199\\t| `--as-of` omitted | last completed day (a legacy ledger: its last judgement day) | package | resolved bound |\\n   200\\t| View created after the bound | not exported | — | bound |\\n   201\\t| View closed on or before the bound | `open: false`, with no reason and no day | — | bound |\\n   202\\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\\n   203\\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\\n   204\\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\\n   205\\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\\n   206\\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded | — | bound |\\n   207\\t| Visible source with no row in the items database | `ReleaseRefused`, naming the evidence and input id | nothing final | bound |\\n   208\\t| Store written by a live run | not supported. The builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9), and both connections are pinned | — | — |\\n   209\\t| `--out` exists, empty or not, at the start | refused early; `publish` would also refuse | nothing | — |\\n   210\\t| `check_export`, `check_package` or `check_origins` refuses | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\\n   211\\t| A write, check or move fails, or a database error (`sqlite3.Error`, such as an items database with no `items` table) | exit 1; the `finally` removes this build's staging; a corrected retry at the same `--out` succeeds | nothing | — |\\n   212\\t| A folder, empty or not, appears at `--out` after staging | `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`; that folder is untouched; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing of this build | — |\\n   213\\t| The filesystem has no atomic no-replace move | `publish` refuses; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing | — |\\n   214\\t| Crash while staging | a uniquely named staging folder is left as debris. Nothing is at `--out`, and no later build is blocked | staging only | — |\\n   215\\t| Crash after the rename, before the report | the package is final and checked; `check` rewrites the report | package | — |\\n   216\\t| The report write fails after publication | exit 2: the package is final and checked; `check` regenerates the report | package | — |\\n   217\\t| Two builds aimed at one `--out` | each stages privately; the first `publish` wins; the second's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`, and its `finally` removes only its own staging | the winner's package | — |\\n   218\\t| Package `as_of` later than the store's last completed day (`check`) | refused by `resolve_bound` | nothing | package `as_of` |\\n   219\\t| A legacy ledger with no completed days, explicit day | the build and `check` both accept any valid date (one rule) | package | requested day |\\n   220\\t| A package file is a symbolic link, or a JSON member name repeats | `check_package` refuses | nothing | — |\\n   221\\t| The package's `class` disagrees with the store's (a Yes/No answer replaced by the marker) | `check_origins` refuses: class is derived from the store | nothing final | bound |\\n   222\\t| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\\n   223\\t| Legacy ledger: no `view_keys` table, `是`/`否` labels | no key, so no event; the labels canonicalise to Yes/No | — | — |\\n   224\\t\\n   225\\t## 3. Value × reader\\n   226\\t\\n   227\\tReaders of the package:\\n   228\\t- `check_package` and `check_origins`;\\n   229\\t- the release page (slice 2);\\n   230\\t- the tests.\\n   231\\t\\n   232\\tThe report's reader is the person building. No POC code imports `release`.\\n   233\\t\\n   234\\t| Value | Permitted source at the bound | Checked by |\\n   235\\t|---|---|---|\\n   236\\t| `id`, `question` | `views.view_id`, `views.question` | `check_origins` |\\n   237\\t| `open` | the latest visible `view_switches.open` | `check_origins` |\\n   238\\t| `class` | `view_keys.measure`, `rungs.label` | `check_origins` derives it from the store; tests and mutants check the identity rule |\\n   239\\t| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label` by position; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | `check_origins` |\\n   240\\t| `forecast` | the constant marker | `check_export` |\\n   241\\t| evidence fields | the `evidence` row; visible `evidence_links` minus visible replacements | `check_origins` |\\n   242\\t| source fields | every visible `evidence_sources` row (`publication_day` as `day`); its `items` row's `title`, `publisher`, `source_uri`, required | `check_origins` (left join; a missing item refuses) |\\n   243\\t| manifest | the data's `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`; the data sha256 | `check_package` |\\n   244\\t| report (outside the package) | `ladder_bands` per number question; counts | read by the builder's user |\\n   245\\t\\n   246\\t**Never read by `release_export`:**\\n   247\\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\\n   248\\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `implied_outcome`, `reference`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\\n   249\\t- `view_switches.reason`;\\n   250\\t- `clean_ladders`;\\n   251\\t- `thesis_groups`;\\n   252\\t- `dependencies`, `successions`.\\n   253\\t\\n   254\\t## 4. New path × old checks\\n   255\\t\\n   256\\t| Check on the old path (`bundle.library`, `view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\\n   257\\t|---|---|\\n   258\\t| `resolve_bound`: unfinished first day, future bound | same call |\\n   259\\t| `bundle.library`: no default day refused; `date.fromisoformat` | same two checks |\\n   260\\t| A view not visible at the bound is not served | same `view_exists` |\\n   261\\t| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence`, verified independently by `check_origins` |\\n   262\\t| Pinned read transaction | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\\n   263\\t| `item_lookup` falls back to the id for a missing item | refused instead |\\n   264\\t| A malformed `clean_ladders` row is refused | not read |\\n   265\\t| Corrupt judgement JSON is refused | no JSON column read |\\n   266\\t| The UI contract rejects unknown fields | the release's own `check_export`; the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\\n   267\\t\\n   268\\t## 5. Prior decisions\\n   269\\t\\n   270\\t- D726: number questions show sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with band, forecast text and history withheld together.\\n   271\\t- D756: Alex's choice.\\n   272\\t- D757: the design, revision 4.\\n   273\\t- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\\n   274\\t- D12/D13: no clock.\\n   275\\t- D163: English product text.\\n   276\\t- D690: poc-v118 stays the product.\\n   277\\t- D261: the ruler is untouched.\\n   278\\t- D274: the extraction prompt is frozen.\\n   279\\t\\n   280\\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\\n   281\\t\\n   282\\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path (`store.create_view`, `store.insert`), with a real items database. Each test names\\n   283\\tits row above:\\n   284\\t1. **Closed set (§1).**\\n   285\\t   - Every dict in a fixture export has exactly its type's keys.\\n   286\\t   - Positive control: an export with one added key fails `check_export`.\\n   287\\t2. **Number with `lo`/`hi`.** The record carries the marker. No rung label, condition, `reasons`, `why_changed` or `implied_outcome` of\\n   288\\t   that view appears in any decoded package field.\\n   289\\t3. **Branch fixtures for identity and the report:**\\n   290\\t   - a condition-only number that resolves: `number`, and absent from `withheld_unresolved`;\\n   291\\t   - an unresolved number with a key: `number`, and present;\\n   292\\t   - an unresolved number without a key: `number`, and present.\\n   293\\t4. **Yes/No with numeric bounds** (`growth_rate` key, labels Yes/No): `yes_no`, with its answer label. A `why_changed` quoting\\n   294\\t   \\\"$1 trillion\\\" is absent.\\n   295\\t5. **Event with the served ledger's `v49` labels,** \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\": `event`, with its label kept. A\\n   296\\t   `why_changed` quoting another question's band is absent.\\n   297\\t6. **Legacy store** with no `view_keys` table and `是`/`否` labels: `yes_no`.\\n   298\\t7. **Closing switch** whose reason names the band label: `open: false`, and the reason is absent.\\n   299\\t8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds. A visible source with a missing item is refused.\\n   300\\t9. **Package:**\\n   301\\t   - staged, then checked, passes;\\n   302\\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\\n   303\\t   - a changed data byte fails;\\n   304\\t   - an extra manifest key with an unchanged data hash fails;\\n   305\\t   - a manifest `as_of` differing from the data's fails;\\n   306\\t   - an existing `--out`, empty or not, is refused, and a leftover staging folder from another build does not block a build.\\n   307\\t10. **Origin check, each from the store:**\\n   308\\t    - in a staged copy, the system's forecast text placed in an evidence `one_line` fails, naming the field;\\n   309\\t    - a Yes/No record turned into a number record, keeping the closed set, fails;\\n   310\\t    - a duplicated question, and a duplicated evidence record, each fails;\\n   311\\t    - a package whose `as_of` is a day later than the store's last completed day fails `check`;\\n   312\\t    - a legacy fixture with no completed days, built at an explicit day later than its last judgement, passes a later `check`.\\n   313\\t11. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted). The package is final and passes `check`.\\n   314\\t12. **Builder refusal, through the real command, on a scratch copy** (the AGENTS §4 mutation procedure; no fake in the suite):\\n   315\\t    - the unchanged command succeeds on the fixture store (test 11);\\n   316\\t    - on a scratch copy, the writer fault \\\"one evidence `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`\\\" is introduced.\\n   317\\t      The same command exits 1 with the origin-mismatch reason, no `--out` and no staging folder left;\\n   318\\t    - on a second scratch copy, the same writer fault plus the builder's staged check removed: the bad package reaches `--out`. That\\n   319\\t      shows the staged check is what prevents publication.\\n   320\\t13. **`check` with a missing item.** A finished package. Then a copy of the items database with one referenced item deleted, and a\\n   321\\t    copy of the package with that same source removed and its manifest hash refreshed. `check` refuses, naming the missing item. (An\\n   322\\t    inner-join mutant accepts this pair, so this case catches it.)\\n   323\\t14. **The publication rule.**\\n   324\\t    - Module steps: builds A and B both stage, then A publishes. B's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`. A's package passes `check`, and\\n   325\\t      B's staging is still there for its owner to remove.\\n   326\\t    - Module steps: after staging, a foreign *empty* folder is put at `--out`. `publish` refuses, and the foreign folder still exists\\n   327\\t      afterwards, empty.\\n   328\\t    - The command: an existing empty `--out` gives exit 1, and the folder survives.\\n   329\\t17. **A database error through the command.** A valid ledger with an items database that has no `items` table: exit 1, the database\\n   330\\t    error printed, nothing at `--out`, no staging folder left. A retry at the same `--out` with the correct items database succeeds.\\n   331\\t15. **Files:**\\n   332\\t    - a symbolic link in place of `release-data.json` fails;\\n   333\\t    - a data file whose repeated `one_line` member has the genuine value last, with the manifest hash refreshed so every other\\n   334\\t      check passes, fails on the repeated name.\\n   335\\t16. **Bound validation:** `2026-08-99` refused; a valid day before the first question gives an empty package.\\n   336\\t\\n   337\\t**Mutants,** on a scratch copy with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; each must fail a test:\\n   338\\t- `condition` emitted on number records;\\n   339\\t- `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`;\\n   340\\t- the event test removed;\\n   341\\t- the Yes/No test removed;\\n   342\\t- `check_package` without the file-set check;\\n   343\\t- manifest keys unchecked;\\n   344\\t- `check_export` without the closed-key check;\\n   345\\t- `check_origins` skipping evidence fields;\\n   346\\t- `check_origins` taking the class from the package;\\n   347\\t- `check_origins` comparing sets instead of ordered lists;\\n   348\\t- `check_origins` with an inner join to `items`;\\n   349\\t- `check` without validating the package's `as_of` against the store;\\n   350\\t- the builder skipping the staged `check_package` (the scratch-copy pair in test 12);\\n   351\\t- `publish` replaced by `os.rename` (test 14's foreign empty folder is then replaced);\\n   352\\t- the `finally` removed (test 17 then leaves staging);\\n   353\\t- the symbolic-link check removed;\\n   354\\t- the duplicate-key check removed;\\n   355\\t- the switch reason emitted;\\n   356\\t- the missing-item refusal replaced by the id fallback.\\n   357\\t\\n   358\\t## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\\n   359\\t\\n   360\\tStores: `old-1`, `old-2`, `old-3` (`comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-N/prod/views.sqlite`, items `items-comparison.sqlite`) and the\\n   361\\tserved ledger with its items database.\\n   362\\t\\n   363\\t**Budgets,** set before the first control (AGENTS §2):\\n   364\\t- the package's data bytes at most `bundle.library`'s JSON bytes on the same store and bound;\\n   365\\t- export plus all checks at most three times `bundle.library`'s seconds on the same store, and at most 120 s per store.\\n   366\\t\\n   367\\tThe steps:\\n   368\\t1. **Build each store's package at its default bound.** The build passes `check_package` with `check_origins`. Report the fields\\n   369\\t   compared, the counts per class and the unresolved list.\\n   370\\t2. **The decisive acceptance case** (council 74), on the `old-1` package:\\n   371\\t   - Morningstar's `$361 billion` estimate (`e2295`) is kept, its summary and quote equal to the stored ones;\\n   372\\t   - the genuine \\\"Bullish confirmation\\\" quote (`e1865`) is kept;\\n   373\\t   - the genuine analyst \\\"$390 billion\\\" quote (`e3597`) is kept, as the control;\\n   374\\t   - in a copy of the staged package, the system's `old-1` j1580 `implied_outcome` (\\\"About $390 billion…\\\") substituted into\\n   375\\t     `e2295`'s summary fails `check_origins`;\\n   376\\t   - the same text added to the manifest fails `check_package`.\\n   377\\t3. **`old-1/v8`:** `class` is `number`, with the marker and the same evidence ids as `service.evidence` at the bound.\\n   378\\t4. **The known event leaks at their own dates.** Export `old-3` at 2026-08-25 (`v36` j799 is the latest judgement) and `old-1` at\\n   379\\t   2026-08-28 (`v10` j865). Each keeps its original answer label, and j799's \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" text and j865's band text are absent.\\n   380\\t5. **Control:** one unchanged event question keeps its label and evidence.\\n   381\\t6. **Closing.** On a temporary copy of `old-1`, add a closing switch for `v8` in the store's own format (\\\"due …, frozen on … at\\n   382\\t   rung N <label>\\\"). First confirm that `bundle.view_bundle` exposes the reason with the band label. Then confirm the package shows\\n   383\\t   `open: false` and not the reason.\\n   384\\t7. **Diagnostics** (not the gate). For every question, take each string the package must not hold:\\n   385\\t   - rung labels and conditions;\\n   386\\t   - judgement `reasons` and `why_changed`, and `implied_outcome` and `reference` where the store has those columns (the served\\n   387\\t     ledger has neither; the report says so);\\n   388\\t   - switch reasons.\\n   389\\t\\n   390\\t   Search every decoded string field of the package for each, with no floor. List every hit with its question, field, evidence id\\n   391\\t   and the stored string it matched, and read each by hand. A genuine source quote, such as `e1865`'s \\\"Bullish\\\", is recorded as such.\\n   392\\t8. **Budgets:** bytes and seconds against the budgets above.\\n   393\\t\\n   394\\t## 8. A disclosed property, not built: evidence summaries keep extraction's wording\\n   395\\t\\n   396\\tThe release shows each evidence summary as extraction stored it; the release computes or converts nothing. A summary can make\\n   397\\tcontext explicit or restate a source figure by arithmetic, attributed to its source: `old-1/e3238` gives \\\"more than $40 billion in\\n   398\\tFY2028\\\" for a quote's \\\"more than double that next year\\\".\\n   399\\t- **Measured:** 25.6%, 25.2% and 25.4% of evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and 35.0% in the served ledger, carry a\\n   400\\t  number not in their quote. In a sample of 24, 23 are context: a year, a date, a quarter, a product name, an amount from the previous\\n   401\\t  sentence. One restates \\\"close to doubling\\\" as \\\"nearly 100%\\\".\\n   402\\t- **Why this is not the forecast D726 withholds.** Extraction never sees the system's forecast. Its request lists each open question\\n   403\\t  only as id, object, due day, question and a \\\"takes\\\" line (`placement.py:19-61`, `extraction.py:398-400`); no rung, label or\\n   404\\t  judged position.\\n   405\\t- **Council 74b** (`codex-r74b.md` §2) verified that extraction sends no rung, label or judged position, and that the census\\n   406\\t  reproduces.\\n   407\\t- **The disagreement that remains is narrow.**\\n   408\\t  - Codex reads revision 4's \\\"amounts as quoted\\\" as requiring source wording for a calculated amount attributed to a source, such\\n   409\\t    as `e3238`'s \\\"more than $40 billion\\\".\\n   410\\t  - Claude reads it as \\\"the release computes or converts nothing\\\".\\n   411\\t  - Both agree: no digit filter, no change to extraction.\\n   412\\t- **The course taken.** By AGENTS' rule for an unsettled disagreement, the cheaper, reversible course is to keep the stored summary.\\n   413\\t  The quote is shown beside it, so the source wording is on the reader's screen. A later version can drop the field from the\\n   414\\t  allow-list or change it.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74e.stream:21:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '245,282p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   245\\t\\n   246\\t**Never read by `release_export`:**\\n   247\\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\\n   248\\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `implied_outcome`, `reference`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\\n   249\\t- `view_switches.reason`;\\n   250\\t- `clean_ladders`;\\n   251\\t- `thesis_groups`;\\n   252\\t- `dependencies`, `successions`.\\n   253\\t\\n   254\\t## 4. New path × old checks\\n   255\\t\\n   256\\t| Check on the old path (`bundle.library`, `view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\\n   257\\t|---|---|\\n   258\\t| `resolve_bound`: unfinished first day, future bound | same call |\\n   259\\t| `bundle.library`: no default day refused; `date.fromisoformat` | same two checks |\\n   260\\t| A view not visible at the bound is not served | same `view_exists` |\\n   261\\t| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence`, verified independently by `check_origins` |\\n   262\\t| Pinned read transaction | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\\n   263\\t| `item_lookup` falls back to the id for a missing item | refused instead |\\n   264\\t| A malformed `clean_ladders` row is refused | not read |\\n   265\\t| Corrupt judgement JSON is refused | no JSON column read |\\n   266\\t| The UI contract rejects unknown fields | the release's own `check_export`; the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\\n   267\\t\\n   268\\t## 5. Prior decisions\\n   269\\t\\n   270\\t- D726: number questions show sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with band, forecast text and history withheld together.\\n   271\\t- D756: Alex's choice.\\n   272\\t- D757: the design, revision 4.\\n   273\\t- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\\n   274\\t- D12/D13: no clock.\\n   275\\t- D163: English product text.\\n   276\\t- D690: poc-v118 stays the product.\\n   277\\t- D261: the ruler is untouched.\\n   278\\t- D274: the extraction prompt is frozen.\\n   279\\t\\n   280\\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\\n   281\\t\\n   282\\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path (`store.create_view`, `store.insert`), with a real items database. Each test names\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.stream:8:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_4\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round74-brief.md docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74h.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# Council round 74: review the slice-1 build design before any code (read-only)\\n\\nYou are an independent reviewer. Do not edit any file. The repository is /Users/lchingen/hivemind. Cite file:line.\\n\\n## What to review\\n\\n`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md`, the build design for the first slice of the \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"\\nrelease. The governing documents:\\n- `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4, ready per `codex-r72d.md`);\\n- D726, D756, D757 and D758 at the end of `docs/DECISIONS-log.md`;\\n- AGENTS.md §2 (design tables before code), §3 (one owner; the writer refuses), §4 (tests) and §5.\\n\\nCode that the design reuses:\\n- `src/hivemind/service.py`: `resolve_bound`, `view_exists`, `is_open_as_of`, `state_as_of`, `evidence`, `evidence_record`,\\n  `ladder_bands`;\\n- `src/hivemind/bundle.py`: `read_snapshot`, `item_lookup`, `view_bundle`;\\n- `src/hivemind/views/store.py`: `view_key`, `rungs_of`;\\n- `src/hivemind/views/identity.py:10`;\\n- `src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24`;\\n- `src/hivemind/idea.py`, for the idea question.\\n\\n## Questions\\n\\n1. **Leaks.** Does the allow-list in §1 let any number forecast reach the package? Check:\\n   - each allowed field's real content in stored stores, read-only (for example `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`):\\n     `question`, evidence `one_line` and `quote`, source titles;\\n   - whether evidence linked to a number question can itself be a system-written forecast rather than a source statement.\\n\\n   Name any path with a stored example.\\n2. **Tables.** Are the state × event, value × reader and new path × old checks tables complete? Name any blank or wrong cell, for\\n   example an event the export can meet that is not listed.\\n3. **Tests and mutants.** Does each named test fail without the code it tests? Is a decisive case missing?\\n4. **The $0 release check (§7).** Is the leak sweep sound? Consider the 12-character floor and the string classes. Would it miss a\\n   forecast restated in different words?\\n5. **The four open points in §8:**\\n   - no idea submission in the release, with the idea acceptance moved to a later slice;\\n   - `object` and `kind` on every record;\\n   - groups left out;\\n   - the sweep floor.\\n\\n   Decide each.\\n6. **Ready to build?** Give a verdict: ready, or not ready with each serious finding.\\n\\n**Out of scope:** the judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen); the closed v13s line; the POC's own behaviour; any other open\\ndefect; wording. Report only findings that change what is built or whether it is safe.\\n**Not ready to build.** Both 74g overwrite findings are closed. Two issues remain in how the command reports success and how the tests verify it.\\n\\n1. **Both overwrite cases are closed.** `check` now creates the report with `os.link`. If a case-variant name already identifies the items database, the link fails and the database survives. `build` uses the same operation, so a file created at the report name while the build runs also survives. Tests 18 and 19 cover the database hash and the late-arriving marker respectively. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:56](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:56) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:363](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:363)\\n\\n2. **The builder can tell the operator a report is missing after it has published it.** Step 8 creates the public link, then removes the temporary name. If that removal fails, the complete report already exists, but the specified error says “report not written” and directs the operator to retry. A retry encounters the existing report and exits 2 again. Treat a successful link as the point when the report is published. A later cleanup error should identify the leftover temporary file. The decisive test forces only that removal to fail and verifies that the command correctly identifies the published report. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:192](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:192) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:200](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:200)\\n\\n3. **The end-to-end tests need an explicit expected exit status.** Test 11 says a successful build then “passes `check`,” but the build has already created the report, so the specified `check` command exits 2. Test 19 has the same issue while its marker occupies the report name. With the occupant in place, assert that `check` prints the successful package result, exits 2, and preserves the occupant. For the exit-0 case, remove the test-owned report first and verify that `check` creates a fresh one. This lets an engineer distinguish a valid package from a failed package check. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:204](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:204) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:342](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:342) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:366](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:366)\\n\\nI found no other serious blocker in slice 1.\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.stream:14:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '1,164p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\t**Status: revision 9, for council round 74i. No code yet.** Release work was opened by the council under D439 (D758). The behaviour is\\n     4\\tfixed by D726, D756 and `FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4). This page holds the AGENTS §2 tables for the first slice.\\n     5\\t\\n     6\\t**Revision 2 answers `codex-r74.md`** (see `claude-r74.md`):\\n     7\\t- the pass condition is an origin check of every field against its stored source, not a string sweep;\\n     8\\t- a missing source item is refused;\\n     9\\t- the package is checked before it is moved into place;\\n    10\\t- the manifest is a closed set;\\n    11\\t- the bound is validated as a date;\\n    12\\t- narrow reads;\\n    13\\t- size and speed budgets;\\n    14\\t- tests that separate every branch;\\n    15\\t- `object`, `kind` and groups dropped;\\n    16\\t- no idea submission.\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\tThe evidence summary stays as extraction stored it (§8, disputed in `claude-r74.md`).\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\t**Revision 3 answers `codex-r74b.md`.**\\n    21\\t- The checker derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package: the date, each question's class, the records and their counts.\\n    22\\t- A missing source item refuses `check` too.\\n    23\\t- The files must be two regular, non-symlink files, with no duplicate JSON member names.\\n    24\\t- The staging folder has one owner.\\n    25\\t- The builder's refusal is tested through the builder.\\n    26\\t- The diagnostics read only the columns a store has.\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\t**Revision 4 answers `codex-r74c.md`.**\\n    29\\t- One date rule for build and `check`.\\n    30\\t- Questions are ordered by `created_seq, rowid`.\\n    31\\t- (Superseded in revision 5.) The build claimed its output folder before staging.\\n    32\\t- Cleanup sits where the staging path is known.\\n    33\\t- A report failure after publication has its own outcome.\\n    34\\t- The builder's refusal is proved through the real command on a scratch copy.\\n    35\\t- Tests 9, 13, 14 and 15 are sharpened.\\n    36\\t\\n    37\\t**Revision 5 answers `codex-r74d.md` with one structural rule** (AGENTS §1: the publication mechanism drew findings in 74b, 74c and\\n    38\\t74d). Staging is private, and the only public step is one atomic move that refuses any existing destination. There is no public\\n    39\\tclaim, so nothing public is created early or cleaned up. Staging is removed in a `finally` covering its whole life, so any error,\\n    40\\tdatabase errors included, leaves nothing at `--out`.\\n    41\\t\\n    42\\t**Revision 6 answers `codex-r74e.md`.**\\n    43\\t- The build's cleanup responsibility ends the moment `publish` succeeds: the staging path is cleared and the `finally` removes nothing\\n    44\\t  after that, so a folder later created at the freed staging name is never touched.\\n    45\\t- The late refusal at `publish`, and the end of cleanup after it, are proved through the real command on scratch copies with a\\n    46\\t  pause.\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t**Revision 7 answers `codex-r74f.md`.**\\n    49\\t- An explicit day is parsed first and used everywhere in its canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` form. Python reads `20260825` as the same day,\\n    50\\t  but the stores compare days as text.\\n    51\\t- Neither command writes a report over an input database.\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\t**Revision 8 answers `codex-r74g.md` with one rule for every public write** (report writing drew findings in 74f and 74g). Nothing the\\n    54\\tbuild or `check` writes ever replaces an existing path:\\n    55\\t- the package is published by `publish` (`RENAME_EXCL`);\\n    56\\t- the report is published by writing a private temporary file, then `os.link` to the report name, which fails with `EEXIST` when\\n    57\\t  anything exists there.\\n    58\\t\\n    59\\tVerified on this Mac: `os.link` refuses an existing file, a case-variant name of it (`ITEMS.SQLITE` for `items.sqlite`), and a\\n    60\\tsymbolic link, leaving each untouched. An input database always exists, so no report can replace one. The path comparison of\\n    61\\trevision 7 is subsumed and dropped.\\n    62\\t\\n    63\\t**Revision 9 answers `codex-r74h.md`.**\\n    64\\t- A report is published the moment its link succeeds. A later failure to remove the temporary file is reported as published, naming\\n    65\\t  the leftover file.\\n    66\\t- `check`'s exit statuses are explicit, and the end-to-end tests assert them.\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\t## 0. Scope\\n    69\\t\\n    70\\t- **Slice 1 (this page), $0:**\\n    71\\t  - the exporter `release_export` and its self-check;\\n    72\\t  - the package writer, the package check and the origin check;\\n    73\\t  - the release builder, which calls the exporter directly;\\n    74\\t  - tests and mutants;\\n    75\\t  - the $0 release check on stored stores.\\n    76\\t- **Slice 2, next.** The release page reads only the package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite\\n    77\\t  trials, no idea submission control or route. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen, which completes D756's screen check.\\n    78\\t- **No idea submission in the release** (council 74). The idea path (`idea.py`) reads the ledger at every step and calls a paid model\\n    79\\t  per idea. The design's §5 idea acceptance (an idea card backed only by `v8`, and its composed request) is carried forward as pending\\n    80\\t  for the first idea-enabled slice.\\n    81\\t- **Not in scope:**\\n    82\\t  - the POC, its API, MCP and page (unchanged);\\n    83\\t  - colleagues' page;\\n    84\\t  - frozen pieces, extraction included;\\n    85\\t  - any model call;\\n    86\\t  - commit, publish, deploy.\\n    87\\t\\n    88\\t## 1. What is built\\n    89\\t\\n    90\\t`src/hivemind/release.py` is the one owner, beside `service.py`.\\n    91\\t\\n    92\\t- **Constants:**\\n    93\\t  - `FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'`;\\n    94\\t  - `ALLOW_LIST = 'release-allow-list/1'`;\\n    95\\t  - `FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE = 'Forecast unavailable'`;\\n    96\\t  - `PACKAGE_FILES = {'manifest.json', 'release-data.json'}`.\\n    97\\t- **`ALLOWED`:** the closed key set per record type.\\n    98\\t\\n    99\\t  | Record | Keys |\\n   100\\t  |---|---|\\n   101\\t  | envelope | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `questions` |\\n   102\\t  | number question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (= `number`), `forecast` (= the marker), `evidence` |\\n   103\\t  | event or Yes/No question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (`event` or `yes_no`), `answers` (the two stored rung labels, in position order), `answer` (the stored label of the latest judgement's rung on or before the bound, or null), `evidence` |\\n   104\\t  | evidence in force at the bound | `id`, `one_line`, `quote`, `tier`, `speaker`, `original_who`, `original_day`, `sources` |\\n   105\\t  | source recorded on or before the bound | `title`, `publisher`, `day`, `uri` |\\n   106\\t  | manifest | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `data_sha256` |\\n   107\\t\\n   108\\t- **`question_class(views_db, view_id, labels)`** (design §3):\\n   109\\t  - `event` when the view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES`. The key is read as `select measure from view_keys`, and\\n   110\\t    only when the table exists;\\n   111\\t  - `yes_no` when there are exactly two labels which, through `vocabulary.canonical('label', …)`, are `Yes` and `No` in either order;\\n   112\\t  - `number` otherwise: a view with no key, or one whose bands cannot be resolved.\\n   113\\t- **`release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None)`:**\\n   114\\t  - pins both connections (`bundle.read_snapshot`);\\n   115\\t  - takes an explicit day only in canonical form: `date.fromisoformat(day).isoformat()` must equal the text given, otherwise\\n   116\\t    `ReleaseRefused` (so `20260825` is refused, not read as `2026-08-25`). It then resolves the bound with `service.resolve_bound`,\\n   117\\t    refuses a store with no default day, and uses that canonical text in every query;\\n   118\\t  - exports every view that exists at the bound (`service.view_exists`), closed ones included, in `created_seq, rowid` order;\\n   119\\t  - builds each record field by field from the table above, with column-limited SQL:\\n   120\\t    - `select view_id, question, created_seq from views order by created_seq, rowid`;\\n   121\\t    - `select position, label from rungs`;\\n   122\\t    - `select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1`;\\n   123\\t    - `service.is_open_as_of`, which reads only `open` and `after_seq`;\\n   124\\t  - takes evidence in force from `service.evidence` and its fields from that record;\\n   125\\t  - looks up each source's `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri` in the items database by `input_id`. A visible source whose item is\\n   126\\t    missing raises `ReleaseRefused` (there is no fallback to the id);\\n   127\\t  - calls `check_export` on its own result before returning (AGENTS §3: the writer refuses).\\n   128\\t- **`check_export(data)`:** the closed-set check.\\n   129\\t  - Every dict at every level has exactly its record type's keys.\\n   130\\t  - Value checks:\\n   131\\t    - `format` and `allow_list` equal the constants, and `as_of` is a canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` day (`date.fromisoformat(as_of).isoformat() == as_of`);\\n   132\\t    - `class` is in its set;\\n   133\\t    - a number record's `forecast` is the marker;\\n   134\\t    - `answers` is two strings, and `answer` is one of them or null;\\n   135\\t    - `open` is a bool and every text field is a string.\\n   136\\t  - It returns the counts it judged: questions per class, evidence, sources.\\n   137\\t- **`check_origins(views_db, items_db, data, expected_as_of)`:** the pass condition. It is independent of the exporter's code path.\\n   138\\t  It derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package.\\n   139\\t  - **The bound: one rule for both commands.** `expected_as_of` is given by the caller.\\n   140\\t    - The builder passes the bound it resolved: `service.resolve_bound` on the requested day, or the default when none is given; an\\n   141\\t      omitted day with no default is refused.\\n   142\\t    - `check` passes the package's `as_of` through the same `service.resolve_bound`, which refuses a day after a store's last\\n   143\\t      completed day. A legacy ledger with no completed days accepts any valid date in both commands alike.\\n   144\\t    - The package's `as_of` must equal `expected_as_of`.\\n   145\\t  - **The class** of each question is derived from the stored measure and labels (`question_class`). The permitted keys and values\\n   146\\t    are then chosen from that class, never from the package's `class` field.\\n   147\\t  - **Order and counts.** The questions are compared as an ordered list in `created_seq, rowid` order, as `bundle.library` orders\\n   148\\t    them (`old-2/v2` and `v3` share sequence 8). Each question's evidence is compared in link order (`evidence_links.id`), and its\\n   149\\t    sources in row order (`evidence_sources.id`). A duplicate question, evidence record or source therefore fails.\\n   150\\t\\n   151\\t  It compares every field with its permitted stored source at the bound, by direct SQL:\\n   152\\t  - the question set equals the views visible at the bound, with `question` equal to `views.question`;\\n   153\\t  - `open` equals the latest visible switch's `open`;\\n   154\\t  - for `event` and `yes_no`: `answers` equal the rung labels in position order, and `answer` equals the label of the latest judgement\\n   155\\t    rung on or before the bound, or null;\\n   156\\t  - for `number`: only the marker;\\n   157\\t  - the evidence id set equals the links visible at the bound, minus those whose latest replacement is visible, computed in its own\\n   158\\t    SQL. Each evidence field equals the `evidence` row's column;\\n   159\\t  - each source list starts from every visible `evidence_sources` row, in row order, with `day` taken from\\n   160\\t    `evidence_sources.publication_day`. Each row needs a matching `items` row for `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri`; a row with no\\n   161\\t    item raises `ReleaseRefused` (a left join, so a missing item is never silently dropped).\\n   162\\t\\n   163\\t  Any difference raises `ReleaseRefused`, naming the question, the field and the evidence id. It returns the number of fields\\n   164\\t  compared.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.stream:15:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '165,330p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   165\\t- **`stage(out_dir)`:** creates a private staging folder with a name unique to this invocation, `tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=out_dir.parent,\\n   166\\t  prefix='.<name>.staging-')`. Creation is exclusive, so only this invocation owns it. It returns the path.\\n   167\\t- **`write_package(data, staged)`:** writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` into the staging folder. It creates nothing\\n   168\\t  else.\\n   169\\t- **`publish(staged, out_dir)`:** one atomic move that refuses any existing destination, empty or not:\\n   170\\t  - on macOS, `renamex_np(staged, out_dir, RENAME_EXCL)` through `ctypes`. Verified on this Mac: onto a free path it succeeds; onto\\n   171\\t    an existing empty or non-empty folder it fails with `EEXIST`, and both folders stay as they were;\\n   172\\t  - on Linux, `renameat2(AT_FDCWD, staged, AT_FDCWD, out_dir, RENAME_NOREPLACE)`;\\n   173\\t  - where neither call exists, or the filesystem lacks support (`ENOTSUP`, `EINVAL`), it raises `ReleaseRefused`.\\n   174\\t\\n   175\\t  It never replaces, creates or removes anything at `out_dir` except by that one move.\\n   176\\t- **`check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None)`:**\\n   177\\t  - the directory holds exactly `PACKAGE_FILES`, each a regular file and not a symbolic link (`os.lstat`), with no subdirectories;\\n   178\\t  - both files parse as JSON with no duplicate member name at any level (an `object_pairs_hook` that refuses a repeated key);\\n   179\\t  - the manifest has exactly its four keys, and its `format`, `allow_list` and `as_of` equal the data's;\\n   180\\t  - its sha256 equals the data file's;\\n   181\\t  - the data passes `check_export`, and, when the stores are given, `check_origins` with the expected bound;\\n   182\\t  - it returns the counts.\\n   183\\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`** is for the report only. It lists the number questions whose `service.ladder_bands(rungs)`\\n   184\\t  returns `(None, reason)`, with the reason and whether the view has a key. Its output never enters the package.\\n   185\\t\\n   186\\t`scripts/release_build.py`:\\n   187\\t- **`build --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:**\\n   188\\t  1. refuse an existing `--out` or `<out>.report.json` early, as a convenience. The no-replace publication of each holds the\\n   189\\t     guarantee;\\n   190\\t  2. resolve the bound once: a given `--as-of` must be canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` (as above), then `service.resolve_bound`;\\n   191\\t  3. `stage(--out)`. From here a `finally` removes this staging folder while the build still owns it;\\n   192\\t  4. `release_export` at that bound;\\n   193\\t  5. `write_package` into the staging folder;\\n   194\\t  6. `check_package` on the staged folder, with the stores and the resolved bound;\\n   195\\t  7. `publish` to `--out`. The moment it succeeds, the build drops its staging path (`staged = None`); the `finally` then removes\\n   196\\t     nothing;\\n   197\\t  8. `publish_report`: write the report to a private temporary file in the same folder (`tempfile.mkstemp`), then `os.link` it to\\n   198\\t     `<out>.report.json`. The link fails with `EEXIST` if anything exists at that name. **A successful link is the moment the report\\n   199\\t     is published.** The temporary file is then removed. If that removal fails, the command still reports the report as published,\\n   200\\t     names the leftover temporary file, and exits 0.\\n   201\\t\\n   202\\t  The failure outcomes:\\n   203\\t  - **Before publication** (steps 2–7): any exception, whether `ReleaseRefused`, `OSError`, `sqlite3.Error` or another, prints the\\n   204\\t    reason and exits 1. The `finally` removes this build's staging folder; nothing exists at `--out` from this build. A corrected\\n   205\\t    retry at the same `--out` succeeds.\\n   206\\t  - **After publication, before the link** (step 8 fails before the link succeeds, including `EEXIST`): the package is final and\\n   207\\t    checked, and whatever is at the report name is untouched. Exit 2 with \\\"package published and checked; report not written; run\\n   208\\t    `check` to write it\\\".\\n   209\\t\\n   210\\t  It has no input path for prepared or translated JSON, and it takes no clock reading; the folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\\n   211\\t- **`check <out> --ledger --items`:** re-runs `check_package` on an existing package, with the stores, the package's canonical\\n   212\\t  `as_of` validated against the store (above), and the regular-file and duplicate-key checks. It leaves the package in place, prints\\n   213\\t  the report, and writes `<out>.report.json` only through `publish_report`, so it never replaces anything. Its exit statuses:\\n   214\\t  - 0: the package passes, and the report was published;\\n   215\\t  - 2: the package passes, and the report name is occupied (an earlier report, or anything else), which stays untouched;\\n   216\\t  - 1: the package is refused, with the reason. This is also the retry after a report write failed. Its report gives `check_seconds` and marks\\n   217\\t  `export_seconds` as not measured.\\n   218\\t- **The report:**\\n   219\\t  - the store path and the bound;\\n   220\\t  - counts per class;\\n   221\\t  - the unresolved list;\\n   222\\t  - the fields compared;\\n   223\\t  - bytes;\\n   224\\t  - `export_seconds` (build only) and `check_seconds`.\\n   225\\t\\n   226\\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\\n   227\\t\\n   228\\t| State / event | What happens | What is written | Day used |\\n   229\\t|---|---|---|---|\\n   230\\t| Store's first day still in progress | `FirstDayNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | none |\\n   231\\t| Store with no completed day and no judgement, `--as-of` omitted | refused: \\\"no default day; supply --as-of\\\" | nothing | none |\\n   232\\t| `--as-of` not a valid date (`2026-08-99`) | refused by `date.fromisoformat` | nothing | none |\\n   233\\t| `--as-of` valid but not canonical (`20260825`) | refused: the stores compare days as text, so a non-canonical day would read rows from later days | nothing | none |\\n   234\\t| The report name is occupied, by a file, a case-variant name of an input, or a symbolic link (build or `check`) | the build refuses at the start; a name occupied later makes `publish_report` fail with `EEXIST` and exit 2; `check` exits 2 after printing; whatever is there is untouched | the package only (build) | — |\\n   235\\t| `--as-of` after the last completed day | `BoundNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | requested day |\\n   236\\t| `--as-of` valid, before the first visible question | empty `questions`; the report says 0 | package | bound |\\n   237\\t| `--as-of` omitted | last completed day (a legacy ledger: its last judgement day) | package | resolved bound |\\n   238\\t| View created after the bound | not exported | — | bound |\\n   239\\t| View closed on or before the bound | `open: false`, with no reason and no day | — | bound |\\n   240\\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\\n   241\\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\\n   242\\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\\n   243\\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\\n   244\\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded | — | bound |\\n   245\\t| Visible source with no row in the items database | `ReleaseRefused`, naming the evidence and input id | nothing final | bound |\\n   246\\t| Store written by a live run | not supported. The builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9), and both connections are pinned | — | — |\\n   247\\t| `--out` exists, empty or not, at the start | refused early; `publish` would also refuse | nothing | — |\\n   248\\t| `check_export`, `check_package` or `check_origins` refuses | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\\n   249\\t| A write, check or move fails, or a database error (`sqlite3.Error`, such as an items database with no `items` table) | exit 1; the `finally` removes this build's staging; a corrected retry at the same `--out` succeeds | nothing | — |\\n   250\\t| A folder, empty or not, appears at `--out` after staging | `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`; that folder is untouched; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing of this build | — |\\n   251\\t| The filesystem has no atomic no-replace move | `publish` refuses; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing | — |\\n   252\\t| Crash while staging | a uniquely named staging folder is left as debris. Nothing is at `--out`, and no later build is blocked | staging only | — |\\n   253\\t| Crash after the rename, before the report | the package is final and checked; `check` rewrites the report | package | — |\\n   254\\t| The report write fails after publication | exit 2: the package is final and checked; `check` regenerates the report | package | — |\\n   255\\t| Two builds aimed at one `--out` | each stages privately; the first `publish` wins; the second's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`, and its `finally` removes only its own staging | the winner's package | — |\\n   256\\t| Package `as_of` later than the store's last completed day (`check`) | refused by `resolve_bound` | nothing | package `as_of` |\\n   257\\t| A legacy ledger with no completed days, explicit day | the build and `check` both accept any valid date (one rule) | package | requested day |\\n   258\\t| A package file is a symbolic link, or a JSON member name repeats | `check_package` refuses | nothing | — |\\n   259\\t| The package's `class` disagrees with the store's (a Yes/No answer replaced by the marker) | `check_origins` refuses: class is derived from the store | nothing final | bound |\\n   260\\t| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\\n   261\\t| Legacy ledger: no `view_keys` table, `是`/`否` labels | no key, so no event; the labels canonicalise to Yes/No | — | — |\\n   262\\t\\n   263\\t## 3. Value × reader\\n   264\\t\\n   265\\tReaders of the package:\\n   266\\t- `check_package` and `check_origins`;\\n   267\\t- the release page (slice 2);\\n   268\\t- the tests.\\n   269\\t\\n   270\\tThe report's reader is the person building. No POC code imports `release`.\\n   271\\t\\n   272\\t| Value | Permitted source at the bound | Checked by |\\n   273\\t|---|---|---|\\n   274\\t| `id`, `question` | `views.view_id`, `views.question` | `check_origins` |\\n   275\\t| `open` | the latest visible `view_switches.open` | `check_origins` |\\n   276\\t| `class` | `view_keys.measure`, `rungs.label` | `check_origins` derives it from the store; tests and mutants check the identity rule |\\n   277\\t| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label` by position; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | `check_origins` |\\n   278\\t| `forecast` | the constant marker | `check_export` |\\n   279\\t| evidence fields | the `evidence` row; visible `evidence_links` minus visible replacements | `check_origins` |\\n   280\\t| source fields | every visible `evidence_sources` row (`publication_day` as `day`); its `items` row's `title`, `publisher`, `source_uri`, required | `check_origins` (left join; a missing item refuses) |\\n   281\\t| manifest | the data's `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`; the data sha256 | `check_package` |\\n   282\\t| report (outside the package) | `ladder_bands` per number question; counts | read by the builder's user |\\n   283\\t\\n   284\\t**Never read by `release_export`:**\\n   285\\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\\n   286\\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `implied_outcome`, `reference`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\\n   287\\t- `view_switches.reason`;\\n   288\\t- `clean_ladders`;\\n   289\\t- `thesis_groups`;\\n   290\\t- `dependencies`, `successions`.\\n   291\\t\\n   292\\t## 4. New path × old checks\\n   293\\t\\n   294\\t| Check on the old path (`bundle.library`, `view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\\n   295\\t|---|---|\\n   296\\t| `resolve_bound`: unfinished first day, future bound | same call |\\n   297\\t| `bundle.library`: no default day refused; `date.fromisoformat` | same two checks |\\n   298\\t| A view not visible at the bound is not served | same `view_exists` |\\n   299\\t| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence`, verified independently by `check_origins` |\\n   300\\t| Pinned read transaction | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\\n   301\\t| `item_lookup` falls back to the id for a missing item | refused instead |\\n   302\\t| A malformed `clean_ladders` row is refused | not read |\\n   303\\t| Corrupt judgement JSON is refused | no JSON column read |\\n   304\\t| The UI contract rejects unknown fields | the release's own `check_export`; the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\\n   305\\t\\n   306\\t## 5. Prior decisions\\n   307\\t\\n   308\\t- D726: number questions show sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with band, forecast text and history withheld together.\\n   309\\t- D756: Alex's choice.\\n   310\\t- D757: the design, revision 4.\\n   311\\t- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\\n   312\\t- D12/D13: no clock.\\n   313\\t- D163: English product text.\\n   314\\t- D690: poc-v118 stays the product.\\n   315\\t- D261: the ruler is untouched.\\n   316\\t- D274: the extraction prompt is frozen.\\n   317\\t\\n   318\\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\\n   319\\t\\n   320\\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path (`store.create_view`, `store.insert`), with a real items database. Each test names\\n   321\\tits row above:\\n   322\\t1. **Closed set (§1).**\\n   323\\t   - Every dict in a fixture export has exactly its type's keys.\\n   324\\t   - Positive control: an export with one added key fails `check_export`.\\n   325\\t2. **Number with `lo`/`hi`.** The record carries the marker. No rung label, condition, `reasons`, `why_changed` or `implied_outcome` of\\n   326\\t   that view appears in any decoded package field.\\n   327\\t3. **Branch fixtures for identity and the report:**\\n   328\\t   - a condition-only number that resolves: `number`, and absent from `withheld_unresolved`;\\n   329\\t   - an unresolved number with a key: `number`, and present;\\n   330\\t   - an unresolved number without a key: `number`, and present.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.stream:16:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '331,500p'; cat docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   331\\t4. **Yes/No with numeric bounds** (`growth_rate` key, labels Yes/No): `yes_no`, with its answer label. A `why_changed` quoting\\n   332\\t   \\\"$1 trillion\\\" is absent.\\n   333\\t5. **Event with the served ledger's `v49` labels,** \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\": `event`, with its label kept. A\\n   334\\t   `why_changed` quoting another question's band is absent.\\n   335\\t6. **Legacy store** with no `view_keys` table and `是`/`否` labels: `yes_no`.\\n   336\\t7. **Closing switch** whose reason names the band label: `open: false`, and the reason is absent.\\n   337\\t8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds. A visible source with a missing item is refused.\\n   338\\t9. **Package:**\\n   339\\t   - staged, then checked, passes;\\n   340\\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\\n   341\\t   - a changed data byte fails;\\n   342\\t   - an extra manifest key with an unchanged data hash fails;\\n   343\\t   - a manifest `as_of` differing from the data's fails;\\n   344\\t   - an existing `--out`, empty or not, is refused, and a leftover staging folder from another build does not block a build.\\n   345\\t10. **Origin check, each from the store:**\\n   346\\t    - in a staged copy, the system's forecast text placed in an evidence `one_line` fails, naming the field;\\n   347\\t    - a Yes/No record turned into a number record, keeping the closed set, fails;\\n   348\\t    - a duplicated question, and a duplicated evidence record, each fails;\\n   349\\t    - a package whose `as_of` is a day later than the store's last completed day fails `check`;\\n   350\\t    - a legacy fixture with no completed days, built at an explicit day later than its last judgement, passes a later `check`.\\n   351\\t11. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted):\\n   352\\t    - the build exits 0, and the package and its report exist;\\n   353\\t    - `check` with the build's report still in place prints a passing result and exits 2;\\n   354\\t    - after the test removes that report, `check` exits 0 and publishes a fresh one.\\n   355\\t12. **Builder refusal, through the real command, on a scratch copy** (the AGENTS §4 mutation procedure; no fake in the suite):\\n   356\\t    - the unchanged command succeeds on the fixture store (test 11);\\n   357\\t    - on a scratch copy, the writer fault \\\"one evidence `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`\\\" is introduced.\\n   358\\t      The same command exits 1 with the origin-mismatch reason, no `--out` and no staging folder left;\\n   359\\t    - on a second scratch copy, the same writer fault plus the builder's staged check removed: the bad package reaches `--out`. That\\n   360\\t      shows the staged check is what prevents publication.\\n   361\\t13. **`check` with a missing item.** A finished package. Then a copy of the items database with one referenced item deleted, and a\\n   362\\t    copy of the package with that same source removed and its manifest hash refreshed. `check` refuses, naming the missing item. (An\\n   363\\t    inner-join mutant accepts this pair, so this case catches it.)\\n   364\\t14. **The publication rule.**\\n   365\\t    - Module steps: builds A and B both stage, then A publishes. B's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`. A's package passes `check`, and\\n   366\\t      B's staging is still there for its owner to remove.\\n   367\\t    - Module steps: after staging, a foreign *empty* folder is put at `--out`. `publish` refuses, and the foreign folder still exists\\n   368\\t      afterwards, empty.\\n   369\\t    - The command, early: an existing empty `--out` gives exit 1, and the folder survives.\\n   370\\t    - The command, late (a scratch copy with a pause before `publish`, released by the test): the test creates an empty folder at\\n   371\\t      `--out` during the pause. The command exits 1, its staging folder is removed, and the same empty folder survives (same device\\n   372\\t      and inode).\\n   373\\t    - The command, after the move (a scratch copy with a pause just after `publish`): the test recreates the freed staging name as a\\n   374\\t      folder holding a marker file. After the command exits 0, the marker is still there.\\n   375\\t18. **Report over an input.** `--out` is chosen so that `<out>.report.json` is the items database, three ways: the same path, a\\n   376\\t    case-variant name on this case-insensitive volume, and a symbolic link to it. `build` refuses, and `check` on an existing package\\n   377\\t    exits 2. The items file's sha256 is unchanged.\\n   378\\t19. **Report name taken during the build** (a scratch copy with a pause just before `publish_report`): the test writes a marker file\\n   379\\t    at the report name. The command exits 2 and the marker is unchanged. `check` then prints a passing result, exits 2, and leaves the\\n   380\\t    marker unchanged.\\n   381\\t20. **Temporary file left after the link** (a scratch copy in which removing the report's temporary file raises): the build exits 0\\n   382\\t    and says the report is published, naming the leftover temporary file. The report exists and equals the build's report.\\n   383\\t17. **A database error through the command.** A valid ledger with an items database that has no `items` table: exit 1, the database\\n   384\\t    error printed, nothing at `--out`, no staging folder left. A retry at the same `--out` with the correct items database succeeds.\\n   385\\t15. **Files:**\\n   386\\t    - a symbolic link in place of `release-data.json` fails;\\n   387\\t    - a data file whose repeated `one_line` member has the genuine value last, with the manifest hash refreshed so every other\\n   388\\t      check passes, fails on the repeated name.\\n   389\\t16. **Bound validation:**\\n   390\\t    - `2026-08-99` is refused;\\n   391\\t    - `20260825` is refused, while `2026-08-25` builds. On a fixture with evidence on both sides of that day, the package holds only\\n   392\\t      the earlier evidence;\\n   393\\t    - a valid day before the first question gives an empty package.\\n   394\\t\\n   395\\t**Mutants,** on a scratch copy with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; each must fail a test:\\n   396\\t- `condition` emitted on number records;\\n   397\\t- `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`;\\n   398\\t- the event test removed;\\n   399\\t- the Yes/No test removed;\\n   400\\t- `check_package` without the file-set check;\\n   401\\t- manifest keys unchecked;\\n   402\\t- `check_export` without the closed-key check;\\n   403\\t- `check_origins` skipping evidence fields;\\n   404\\t- `check_origins` taking the class from the package;\\n   405\\t- `check_origins` comparing sets instead of ordered lists;\\n   406\\t- `check_origins` with an inner join to `items`;\\n   407\\t- `check` without validating the package's `as_of` against the store;\\n   408\\t- the builder skipping the staged `check_package` (the scratch-copy pair in test 12);\\n   409\\t- `publish` replaced by `os.rename` (test 14's foreign empty folder is then replaced);\\n   410\\t- the `finally` removed (test 17 then leaves staging);\\n   411\\t- the staging path not dropped after `publish` (test 14's marker is then removed);\\n   412\\t- the canonical-day check removed (test 16's `20260825` then builds with later evidence);\\n   413\\t- `publish_report` replaced by `os.replace` (tests 18 and 19 then overwrite the items file and the marker);\\n   414\\t- the symbolic-link check removed;\\n   415\\t- the duplicate-key check removed;\\n   416\\t- the switch reason emitted;\\n   417\\t- the missing-item refusal replaced by the id fallback.\\n   418\\t\\n   419\\t## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\\n   420\\t\\n   421\\tStores: `old-1`, `old-2`, `old-3` (`comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-N/prod/views.sqlite`, items `items-comparison.sqlite`) and the\\n   422\\tserved ledger with its items database.\\n   423\\t\\n   424\\t**Budgets,** set before the first control (AGENTS §2):\\n   425\\t- the package's data bytes at most `bundle.library`'s JSON bytes on the same store and bound;\\n   426\\t- export plus all checks at most three times `bundle.library`'s seconds on the same store, and at most 120 s per store.\\n   427\\t\\n   428\\tThe steps:\\n   429\\t1. **Build each store's package at its default bound.** The build passes `check_package` with `check_origins`. Report the fields\\n   430\\t   compared, the counts per class and the unresolved list.\\n   431\\t2. **The decisive acceptance case** (council 74), on the `old-1` package:\\n   432\\t   - Morningstar's `$361 billion` estimate (`e2295`) is kept, its summary and quote equal to the stored ones;\\n   433\\t   - the genuine \\\"Bullish confirmation\\\" quote (`e1865`) is kept;\\n   434\\t   - the genuine analyst \\\"$390 billion\\\" quote (`e3597`) is kept, as the control;\\n   435\\t   - in a copy of the staged package, the system's `old-1` j1580 `implied_outcome` (\\\"About $390 billion…\\\") substituted into\\n   436\\t     `e2295`'s summary fails `check_origins`;\\n   437\\t   - the same text added to the manifest fails `check_package`.\\n   438\\t3. **`old-1/v8`:** `class` is `number`, with the marker and the same evidence ids as `service.evidence` at the bound.\\n   439\\t4. **The known event leaks at their own dates.** Export `old-3` at 2026-08-25 (`v36` j799 is the latest judgement) and `old-1` at\\n   440\\t   2026-08-28 (`v10` j865). Each keeps its original answer label, and j799's \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" text and j865's band text are absent.\\n   441\\t5. **Control:** one unchanged event question keeps its label and evidence.\\n   442\\t6. **Closing.** On a temporary copy of `old-1`, add a closing switch for `v8` in the store's own format (\\\"due …, frozen on … at\\n   443\\t   rung N <label>\\\"). First confirm that `bundle.view_bundle` exposes the reason with the band label. Then confirm the package shows\\n   444\\t   `open: false` and not the reason.\\n   445\\t7. **Diagnostics** (not the gate). For every question, take each string the package must not hold:\\n   446\\t   - rung labels and conditions;\\n   447\\t   - judgement `reasons` and `why_changed`, and `implied_outcome` and `reference` where the store has those columns (the served\\n   448\\t     ledger has neither; the report says so);\\n   449\\t   - switch reasons.\\n   450\\t\\n   451\\t   Search every decoded string field of the package for each, with no floor. List every hit with its question, field, evidence id\\n   452\\t   and the stored string it matched, and read each by hand. A genuine source quote, such as `e1865`'s \\\"Bullish\\\", is recorded as such.\\n   453\\t8. **Budgets:** bytes and seconds against the budgets above.\\n   454\\t\\n   455\\t## 8. A disclosed property, not built: evidence summaries keep extraction's wording\\n   456\\t\\n   457\\tThe release shows each evidence summary as extraction stored it; the release computes or converts nothing. A summary can make\\n   458\\tcontext explicit or restate a source figure by arithmetic, attributed to its source: `old-1/e3238` gives \\\"more than $40 billion in\\n   459\\tFY2028\\\" for a quote's \\\"more than double that next year\\\".\\n   460\\t- **Measured:** 25.6%, 25.2% and 25.4% of evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and 35.0% in the served ledger, carry a\\n   461\\t  number not in their quote. In a sample of 24, 23 are context: a year, a date, a quarter, a product name, an amount from the previous\\n   462\\t  sentence. One restates \\\"close to doubling\\\" as \\\"nearly 100%\\\".\\n   463\\t- **Why this is not the forecast D726 withholds.** Extraction never sees the system's forecast. Its request lists each open question\\n   464\\t  only as id, object, due day, question and a \\\"takes\\\" line (`placement.py:19-61`, `extraction.py:398-400`); no rung, label or\\n   465\\t  judged position.\\n   466\\t- **Council 74b** (`codex-r74b.md` §2) verified that extraction sends no rung, label or judged position, and that the census\\n   467\\t  reproduces.\\n   468\\t- **The disagreement that remains is narrow.**\\n   469\\t  - Codex reads revision 4's \\\"amounts as quoted\\\" as requiring source wording for a calculated amount attributed to a source, such\\n   470\\t    as `e3238`'s \\\"more than $40 billion\\\".\\n   471\\t  - Claude reads it as \\\"the release computes or converts nothing\\\".\\n   472\\t  - Both agree: no digit filter, no change to extraction.\\n   473\\t- **The course taken.** By AGENTS' rule for an unsettled disagreement, the cheaper, reversible course is to keep the stored summary.\\n   474\\t  The quote is shown beside it, so the source wording is on the reader's screen. A later version can drop the field from the\\n   475\\t  allow-list or change it.\\n# \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\\n\\n**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\\n- D726, \\\"同意\\\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\",\\n  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \\\"it is built with the release work, which is not started\\\";\\n- D756, \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\\\".\\n\\nOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\\n\\n**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\\ncould reach a reader:\\n- the idea card;\\n- the closing text;\\n- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\\n- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\\n- a translated export;\\n- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\\n\\nA rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \\\"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\\nstop answering findings: propose one structural rule\\\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\\n\\n## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\\n\\nThe stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\\n- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\\n- **Its idea input** reads \\\"Bullish … $350 billion to under $400 billion\\\".\\n- **Yes/No explanations quote number forecasts:**\\n  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \\\"around $1 trillion\\\" for 2027 spending;\\n  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\\n\\n  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\\n\\n## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\\n\\n- **One exporter writes the release data:** `release_export`, a single function beside `service.py`. It emits only the fields on an\\n  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\\n- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\\n  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\\n  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\\n- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\\n  - no live POC service;\\n  - no `/library` reload (`poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js` must not fetch in a release build);\\n  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\\n  - no `--composite-trials` input.\\n\\n  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\\n- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\\n  - the question and its id;\\n  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\\n  - the marker \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\".\\n\\n  Nothing else is listed:\\n  - no ladder;\\n  - no band, label or condition;\\n  - no reasons or why_changed;\\n  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\\n  - no closing band (\\\"closed\\\" only);\\n  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\\n- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\\n  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\\n  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\\n  delivered card.\\n- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\\n  later choice for Alex.\\n\\n## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\\n\\nA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\\n1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\\n   questions in the three comparison stores.\\n2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\\n   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\\n   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\\n\\nEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\\n(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\\n(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\\n\\nCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\\n- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\\n- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\\n\\nNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\\n\\n**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\\nbinary event such as \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\\nevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\\n\\n## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\\n\\nD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\\nallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\\n- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\\n  readers would see.\\n- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\\n  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\\n- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\\n  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\\n  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\\n  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\\n- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\\n  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\\n  `why_changed`.\\n- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\\n  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\\n\\n## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\\n\\n- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\\n  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\\n  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\\n  - an unresolved one with a key;\\n  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\\n  - an event question;\\n  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\\n  - a real closing switch;\\n  - an idea.\\n- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\\n  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\\n  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\\n- **Mutants:**\\n  - an extra field;\\n  - a fetch left on;\\n  - a ladder read in idea composition;\\n  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\\n\\n  Each must fail.\\n- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\\n  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with no scored driver and no\\n    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\\n  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\\n    prose rule.\\n- **The $0 release check.**\\n  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\\n  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\\n    final band there.\\n  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\\n  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\\n  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\\n\\n## 6. Not in scope\\n\\n- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\\n- The closed v13s line.\\n- Other open defects.\\n- No prompt or pipeline change.\\n- The POC's own behaviour.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.stream:18:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"wc -l docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md docs/CURRENT_STATE.md docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{RELEASE-BUILD,FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN}.md; head -65 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; rg -n '\\\"'^#{1,3} .*D(726|756|757|758)'\\\"\\\\\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     201 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\\n    1232 docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\\n     475 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md\\n     147 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md\\n    2055 total\\n# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\\n\\n> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \\\"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\\\".\\n> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\\n> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\\n> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\\n> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \\\"go\\\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \\\"also file under the other party's question\\\" and puts two\\n> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\\n> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\\n> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\\\"不，用英文吧\\\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\\\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\\\").\\n\\n## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \\\"每次开始前都需要revisit\\\")\\n\\nBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\\n\\n1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\\n2. Check against §3, \\\"not in scope\\\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\\n3. Check against §4, \\\"constraints\\\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\\n   word for it is already given.\\n4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\\n   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\\n5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\\n   AGENTS, \\\"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\\\").\\n\\n## 1. Goal (end to end)\\n\\nEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\\nnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\\nany one step's own score.\\n\\n## 2. The core blocker (proven)\\n\\n**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \\\"states exactly this question's own figure\\\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\\n\\nThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \\\"two problems\\\"):\\n\\n- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\\n  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\\n  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\\n  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\\n  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\\n- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\\n  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \\\"below $40 billion\\\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\\n  nothing at all and were never judged.\\n\\n**Evidence:**\\n\\n| Evidence | Content | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Filing recognises only \\\"its own figure\\\" | The model says \\\"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\\\" and \\\"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\\\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\\n| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \\\"below $40 billion\\\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\\\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\\\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\\n| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \\\"What it does not measure\\\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\\n| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\\n\\nAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\\n\\n## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\\n\\n| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \\\"好，删掉卡片代码\\\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\\n| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \\\"supports\\\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \\\"whose conclusion to read\\\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \\\"total revenue × 92%\\\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \\\"supports\\\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\\n| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\\\"keep only the narrowest question\\\" takes a seed arrow for \\\"a narrower sub-question\\\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\\n| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\\n| One general sentence, \\\"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\\\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\\n10991:## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" as the first-release interim\\n11799:## D755 · 2026-11-23 · The paid re-send STOPs (complete); council 71: close v13s at STOP and carry D726's \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" into the first release\\n11823:## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"\\n11842:## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\\n11867:## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.stream:20:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '151,351p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"   151\\t  It compares every field with its permitted stored source at the bound, by direct SQL:\\n   152\\t  - the question set equals the views visible at the bound, with `question` equal to `views.question`;\\n   153\\t  - `open` equals the latest visible switch's `open`;\\n   154\\t  - for `event` and `yes_no`: `answers` equal the rung labels in position order, and `answer` equals the label of the latest judgement\\n   155\\t    rung on or before the bound, or null;\\n   156\\t  - for `number`: only the marker;\\n   157\\t  - the evidence id set equals the links visible at the bound, minus those whose latest replacement is visible, computed in its own\\n   158\\t    SQL. Each evidence field equals the `evidence` row's column;\\n   159\\t  - each source list starts from every visible `evidence_sources` row, in row order, with `day` taken from\\n   160\\t    `evidence_sources.publication_day`. Each row needs a matching `items` row for `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri`; a row with no\\n   161\\t    item raises `ReleaseRefused` (a left join, so a missing item is never silently dropped).\\n   162\\t\\n   163\\t  Any difference raises `ReleaseRefused`, naming the question, the field and the evidence id. It returns the number of fields\\n   164\\t  compared.\\n   165\\t- **`stage(out_dir)`:** creates a private staging folder with a name unique to this invocation, `tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=out_dir.parent,\\n   166\\t  prefix='.<name>.staging-')`. Creation is exclusive, so only this invocation owns it. It returns the path.\\n   167\\t- **`write_package(data, staged)`:** writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` into the staging folder. It creates nothing\\n   168\\t  else.\\n   169\\t- **`publish(staged, out_dir)`:** one atomic move that refuses any existing destination, empty or not:\\n   170\\t  - on macOS, `renamex_np(staged, out_dir, RENAME_EXCL)` through `ctypes`. Verified on this Mac: onto a free path it succeeds; onto\\n   171\\t    an existing empty or non-empty folder it fails with `EEXIST`, and both folders stay as they were;\\n   172\\t  - on Linux, `renameat2(AT_FDCWD, staged, AT_FDCWD, out_dir, RENAME_NOREPLACE)`;\\n   173\\t  - where neither call exists, or the filesystem lacks support (`ENOTSUP`, `EINVAL`), it raises `ReleaseRefused`.\\n   174\\t\\n   175\\t  It never replaces, creates or removes anything at `out_dir` except by that one move.\\n   176\\t- **`check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None)`:**\\n   177\\t  - the directory holds exactly `PACKAGE_FILES`, each a regular file and not a symbolic link (`os.lstat`), with no subdirectories;\\n   178\\t  - both files parse as JSON with no duplicate member name at any level (an `object_pairs_hook` that refuses a repeated key);\\n   179\\t  - the manifest has exactly its four keys, and its `format`, `allow_list` and `as_of` equal the data's;\\n   180\\t  - its sha256 equals the data file's;\\n   181\\t  - the data passes `check_export`, and, when the stores are given, `check_origins` with the expected bound;\\n   182\\t  - it returns the counts.\\n   183\\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`** is for the report only. It lists the number questions whose `service.ladder_bands(rungs)`\\n   184\\t  returns `(None, reason)`, with the reason and whether the view has a key. Its output never enters the package.\\n   185\\t\\n   186\\t`scripts/release_build.py`:\\n   187\\t- **`build --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:**\\n   188\\t  1. refuse an existing `--out` or `<out>.report.json` early, as a convenience. The no-replace publication of each holds the\\n   189\\t     guarantee;\\n   190\\t  2. resolve the bound once: a given `--as-of` must be canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` (as above), then `service.resolve_bound`;\\n   191\\t  3. `stage(--out)`. From here a `finally` removes this staging folder while the build still owns it;\\n   192\\t  4. `release_export` at that bound;\\n   193\\t  5. `write_package` into the staging folder;\\n   194\\t  6. `check_package` on the staged folder, with the stores and the resolved bound;\\n   195\\t  7. `publish` to `--out`. The moment it succeeds, the build drops its staging path (`staged = None`); the `finally` then removes\\n   196\\t     nothing;\\n   197\\t  8. `publish_report`: write the report to a private temporary file in the same folder (`tempfile.mkstemp`), then `os.link` it to\\n   198\\t     `<out>.report.json`. The link fails with `EEXIST` if anything exists at that name. **A successful link is the moment the report\\n   199\\t     is published.** The temporary file is then removed. If that removal fails, the command still reports the report as published,\\n   200\\t     names the leftover temporary file, and exits 0.\\n   201\\t\\n   202\\t  The failure outcomes:\\n   203\\t  - **Before publication** (steps 2–7): any exception, whether `ReleaseRefused`, `OSError`, `sqlite3.Error` or another, prints the\\n   204\\t    reason and exits 1. The `finally` removes this build's staging folder; nothing exists at `--out` from this build. A corrected\\n   205\\t    retry at the same `--out` succeeds.\\n   206\\t  - **After publication, before the link** (step 8 fails before the link succeeds, including `EEXIST`): the package is final and\\n   207\\t    checked, and whatever is at the report name is untouched. Exit 2 with \\\"package published and checked; report not written; run\\n   208\\t    `check` to write it\\\".\\n   209\\t\\n   210\\t  It has no input path for prepared or translated JSON, and it takes no clock reading; the folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\\n   211\\t- **`check <out> --ledger --items`:** re-runs `check_package` on an existing package, with the stores, the package's canonical\\n   212\\t  `as_of` validated against the store (above), and the regular-file and duplicate-key checks. It leaves the package in place, prints\\n   213\\t  the report, and writes `<out>.report.json` only through `publish_report`, so it never replaces anything. Its exit statuses:\\n   214\\t  - 0: the package passes, and the report was published;\\n   215\\t  - 2: the package passes, and the report name is occupied (an earlier report, or anything else), which stays untouched;\\n   216\\t  - 1: the package is refused, with the reason. This is also the retry after a report write failed. Its report gives `check_seconds` and marks\\n   217\\t  `export_seconds` as not measured.\\n   218\\t- **The report:**\\n   219\\t  - the store path and the bound;\\n   220\\t  - counts per class;\\n   221\\t  - the unresolved list;\\n   222\\t  - the fields compared;\\n   223\\t  - bytes;\\n   224\\t  - `export_seconds` (build only) and `check_seconds`.\\n   225\\t\\n   226\\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\\n   227\\t\\n   228\\t| State / event | What happens | What is written | Day used |\\n   229\\t|---|---|---|---|\\n   230\\t| Store's first day still in progress | `FirstDayNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | none |\\n   231\\t| Store with no completed day and no judgement, `--as-of` omitted | refused: \\\"no default day; supply --as-of\\\" | nothing | none |\\n   232\\t| `--as-of` not a valid date (`2026-08-99`) | refused by `date.fromisoformat` | nothing | none |\\n   233\\t| `--as-of` valid but not canonical (`20260825`) | refused: the stores compare days as text, so a non-canonical day would read rows from later days | nothing | none |\\n   234\\t| The report name is occupied, by a file, a case-variant name of an input, or a symbolic link (build or `check`) | the build refuses at the start; a name occupied later makes `publish_report` fail with `EEXIST` and exit 2; `check` exits 2 after printing; whatever is there is untouched | the package only (build) | — |\\n   235\\t| `--as-of` after the last completed day | `BoundNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | requested day |\\n   236\\t| `--as-of` valid, before the first visible question | empty `questions`; the report says 0 | package | bound |\\n   237\\t| `--as-of` omitted | last completed day (a legacy ledger: its last judgement day) | package | resolved bound |\\n   238\\t| View created after the bound | not exported | — | bound |\\n   239\\t| View closed on or before the bound | `open: false`, with no reason and no day | — | bound |\\n   240\\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\\n   241\\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\\n   242\\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\\n   243\\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\\n   244\\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded | — | bound |\\n   245\\t| Visible source with no row in the items database | `ReleaseRefused`, naming the evidence and input id | nothing final | bound |\\n   246\\t| Store written by a live run | not supported. The builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9), and both connections are pinned | — | — |\\n   247\\t| `--out` exists, empty or not, at the start | refused early; `publish` would also refuse | nothing | — |\\n   248\\t| `check_export`, `check_package` or `check_origins` refuses | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\\n   249\\t| A write, check or move fails, or a database error (`sqlite3.Error`, such as an items database with no `items` table) | exit 1; the `finally` removes this build's staging; a corrected retry at the same `--out` succeeds | nothing | — |\\n   250\\t| A folder, empty or not, appears at `--out` after staging | `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`; that folder is untouched; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing of this build | — |\\n   251\\t| The filesystem has no atomic no-replace move | `publish` refuses; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing | — |\\n   252\\t| Crash while staging | a uniquely named staging folder is left as debris. Nothing is at `--out`, and no later build is blocked | staging only | — |\\n   253\\t| Crash after the rename, before the report | the package is final and checked; `check` rewrites the report | package | — |\\n   254\\t| The report write fails after publication | exit 2: the package is final and checked; `check` regenerates the report | package | — |\\n   255\\t| Two builds aimed at one `--out` | each stages privately; the first `publish` wins; the second's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`, and its `finally` removes only its own staging | the winner's package | — |\\n   256\\t| Package `as_of` later than the store's last completed day (`check`) | refused by `resolve_bound` | nothing | package `as_of` |\\n   257\\t| A legacy ledger with no completed days, explicit day | the build and `check` both accept any valid date (one rule) | package | requested day |\\n   258\\t| A package file is a symbolic link, or a JSON member name repeats | `check_package` refuses | nothing | — |\\n   259\\t| The package's `class` disagrees with the store's (a Yes/No answer replaced by the marker) | `check_origins` refuses: class is derived from the store | nothing final | bound |\\n   260\\t| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\\n   261\\t| Legacy ledger: no `view_keys` table, `是`/`否` labels | no key, so no event; the labels canonicalise to Yes/No | — | — |\\n   262\\t\\n   263\\t## 3. Value × reader\\n   264\\t\\n   265\\tReaders of the package:\\n   266\\t- `check_package` and `check_origins`;\\n   267\\t- the release page (slice 2);\\n   268\\t- the tests.\\n   269\\t\\n   270\\tThe report's reader is the person building. No POC code imports `release`.\\n   271\\t\\n   272\\t| Value | Permitted source at the bound | Checked by |\\n   273\\t|---|---|---|\\n   274\\t| `id`, `question` | `views.view_id`, `views.question` | `check_origins` |\\n   275\\t| `open` | the latest visible `view_switches.open` | `check_origins` |\\n   276\\t| `class` | `view_keys.measure`, `rungs.label` | `check_origins` derives it from the store; tests and mutants check the identity rule |\\n   277\\t| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label` by position; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | `check_origins` |\\n   278\\t| `forecast` | the constant marker | `check_export` |\\n   279\\t| evidence fields | the `evidence` row; visible `evidence_links` minus visible replacements | `check_origins` |\\n   280\\t| source fields | every visible `evidence_sources` row (`publication_day` as `day`); its `items` row's `title`, `publisher`, `source_uri`, required | `check_origins` (left join; a missing item refuses) |\\n   281\\t| manifest | the data's `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`; the data sha256 | `check_package` |\\n   282\\t| report (outside the package) | `ladder_bands` per number question; counts | read by the builder's user |\\n   283\\t\\n   284\\t**Never read by `release_export`:**\\n   285\\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\\n   286\\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `implied_outcome`, `reference`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\\n   287\\t- `view_switches.reason`;\\n   288\\t- `clean_ladders`;\\n   289\\t- `thesis_groups`;\\n   290\\t- `dependencies`, `successions`.\\n   291\\t\\n   292\\t## 4. New path × old checks\\n   293\\t\\n   294\\t| Check on the old path (`bundle.library`, `view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\\n   295\\t|---|---|\\n   296\\t| `resolve_bound`: unfinished first day, future bound | same call |\\n   297\\t| `bundle.library`: no default day refused; `date.fromisoformat` | same two checks |\\n   298\\t| A view not visible at the bound is not served | same `view_exists` |\\n   299\\t| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence`, verified independently by `check_origins` |\\n   300\\t| Pinned read transaction | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\\n   301\\t| `item_lookup` falls back to the id for a missing item | refused instead |\\n   302\\t| A malformed `clean_ladders` row is refused | not read |\\n   303\\t| Corrupt judgement JSON is refused | no JSON column read |\\n   304\\t| The UI contract rejects unknown fields | the release's own `check_export`; the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\\n   305\\t\\n   306\\t## 5. Prior decisions\\n   307\\t\\n   308\\t- D726: number questions show sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", with band, forecast text and history withheld together.\\n   309\\t- D756: Alex's choice.\\n   310\\t- D757: the design, revision 4.\\n   311\\t- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\\n   312\\t- D12/D13: no clock.\\n   313\\t- D163: English product text.\\n   314\\t- D690: poc-v118 stays the product.\\n   315\\t- D261: the ruler is untouched.\\n   316\\t- D274: the extraction prompt is frozen.\\n   317\\t\\n   318\\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\\n   319\\t\\n   320\\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path (`store.create_view`, `store.insert`), with a real items database. Each test names\\n   321\\tits row above:\\n   322\\t1. **Closed set (§1).**\\n   323\\t   - Every dict in a fixture export has exactly its type's keys.\\n   324\\t   - Positive control: an export with one added key fails `check_export`.\\n   325\\t2. **Number with `lo`/`hi`.** The record carries the marker. No rung label, condition, `reasons`, `why_changed` or `implied_outcome` of\\n   326\\t   that view appears in any decoded package field.\\n   327\\t3. **Branch fixtures for identity and the report:**\\n   328\\t   - a condition-only number that resolves: `number`, and absent from `withheld_unresolved`;\\n   329\\t   - an unresolved number with a key: `number`, and present;\\n   330\\t   - an unresolved number without a key: `number`, and present.\\n   331\\t4. **Yes/No with numeric bounds** (`growth_rate` key, labels Yes/No): `yes_no`, with its answer label. A `why_changed` quoting\\n   332\\t   \\\"$1 trillion\\\" is absent.\\n   333\\t5. **Event with the served ledger's `v49` labels,** \\\"Restriction adopted\\\" / \\\"No restriction adopted\\\": `event`, with its label kept. A\\n   334\\t   `why_changed` quoting another question's band is absent.\\n   335\\t6. **Legacy store** with no `view_keys` table and `是`/`否` labels: `yes_no`.\\n   336\\t7. **Closing switch** whose reason names the band label: `open: false`, and the reason is absent.\\n   337\\t8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds. A visible source with a missing item is refused.\\n   338\\t9. **Package:**\\n   339\\t   - staged, then checked, passes;\\n   340\\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\\n   341\\t   - a changed data byte fails;\\n   342\\t   - an extra manifest key with an unchanged data hash fails;\\n   343\\t   - a manifest `as_of` differing from the data's fails;\\n   344\\t   - an existing `--out`, empty or not, is refused, and a leftover staging folder from another build does not block a build.\\n   345\\t10. **Origin check, each from the store:**\\n   346\\t    - in a staged copy, the system's forecast text placed in an evidence `one_line` fails, naming the field;\\n   347\\t    - a Yes/No record turned into a number record, keeping the closed set, fails;\\n   348\\t    - a duplicated question, and a duplicated evidence record, each fails;\\n   349\\t    - a package whose `as_of` is a day later than the store's last completed day fails `check`;\\n   350\\t    - a legacy fixture with no completed days, built at an explicit day later than its last judgement, passes a later `check`.\\n   351\\t11. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted):\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.stream:22:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '10991,11009p;11823,11905p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; tail -4 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md; tail -n +66 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" as the first-release interim\\n\\n- **The questions** (after D725):\\n  - \\\"要不要开一个新的判官版本来试修法（相关的题合在一次里算，每个数字标明出处，程序检查算术和出处）？\\\" Options: 开，先做 0 元那一关\\n    (recommended: the format and checks designed and through the council, then the $0 gate on five stored cases, four gold controls and\\n    three planted errors; the paid gate asks Alex for its ceiling); 先不开.\\n  - \\\"第一版上线前的过渡：数字题只显示问题和来源，档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'，等通过检查再放出来。你同意这个做法吗？\\\" Options: 同意\\n    (recommended); 暂不定.\\n- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \\\"开，先做 0 元那一关 (推荐)\\\"; \\\"同意 (推荐)\\\".\\n- **Decided (Alex):**\\n  - A new judge version is opened for the bounded test of D725: related number questions judged together, with labelled figures and\\n    code checks of identity and arithmetic. It is designed and reviewed at $0, then the $0 gate runs. The paid gate needs Alex's\\n    ceiling.\\n  - Until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\": the band, the\\n    forecast text and its history withheld together. It is built with the release work, which is not started.\\n- poc-v118 stays the product.\\n\\n## D727 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's $0 gate: the design passed council (round 46e); gate runs 1–6 and council rounds 46f–46j; the gate is not yet passed; one choice goes to Alex\\n\\n## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"\\n\\n- **The question** (after D755): \\\"付费重发的结论是“停”：luna 在新格式下格式错误多（36 个首发里 22 个被拒），在说不清的题上还会硬给数；不过“两题合在一起算”确实避免了自相矛盾。数字题这条线下一步怎么走？\\\"\\n  - Options:\\n    - \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\\\": the council's consensus;\\n    - \\\"换更强的模型再小测一次\\\": a stronger model or higher effort, with a small paid probe and a cap Alex names;\\n    - \\\"先停，我想谈谈\\\".\\n- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\\\".\\n- **Decided (Alex):**\\n  - The v13s judge line ends at its STOP. Nothing from it enters the product, and poc-v118 stays the product (D690).\\n  - The first release carries D726: number questions show the question and its sources with \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\", the band, the\\n    forecast text and the history withheld together.\\n  - The one next step, when release work opens, is a $0 check of the reader's screen on a stored number question that has a\\n    forecast and history: only the question, its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" appear.\\n- **Kept for the record, not built:**\\n  - the D725 consistency finding (separate answers contradicted each other in 8 of 9 pairs, joint answers in none);\\n  - the open checker defects in `PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5;\\n  - the v13s request and harness in `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/`.\\n\\n## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\\n\\n- **Why.** Alex's direction tonight was to converge and head toward production (D750), and he chose to release with \\\"Forecast\\n  unavailable\\\" (D756). D726 says it \\\"is built with the release work, which is not started\\\". Council 72 agreed that opening release\\n  work is Alex's call, so tonight's step is the design, not the build.\\n- **The gap, measured at $0** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` §1):\\n  - today every reader of a number question can see its forecast: the service, the idea input, the closing text;\\n  - Yes/No and event explanations can quote number forecasts (`old-3/v36` judgement 799, `old-1/v10` judgement 865).\\n- **The design, after four review rounds** (`codex-r72.md` … `codex-r72d.md`):\\n  - one release exporter with an explicit allow-list, called directly by the release builder; the finished package is checked;\\n  - for a number question, the allow-list holds only the question, its sources and \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\";\\n  - the release reads nothing else: no live POC service, no translated or prepared JSON, no composite trials;\\n  - identity is structural: a question is a number question unless it is an event measure or a canonical Yes/No pair, and unresolved\\n    records are withheld and listed. Verified on four stores with no wrong result;\\n  - tests, mutants and an end-to-end acceptance on `old-1/v8` and the two known event leaks.\\n  - **Why an allow-list.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new leak paths in a reader-by-reader design, so revision 3 replaced that\\n    approach with one structural rule.\\n- **Open for Alex:**\\n  1. whether to open release work now (then: build to this design, then the $0 release check);\\n  2. what questions that are not number questions show in the release:\\n     - (a) answer and label without explanation text, recommended by the council and Claude;\\n     - (b) explanations only where the judge was shown no number question's state: 21 of 85 questions at the latest answer, and it\\n       cannot guarantee that no number forecast is quoted.\\n- **Not done.** Nothing is built and nothing is committed. The POC is unchanged.\\n\\n## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\\n\\n- **Why the council decides.** Alex is asleep and delegated tonight's decisions (D750: \\\"这边的决策交给你，还有 Council … 准备要往\\n  Production 方向去走了\\\"). He had already chosen the behaviour (D726 \\\"同意\\\"; D756 \\\"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\\\"). D757 left two\\n  choices for him; under D439 a choice that would go to Alex goes to the council when it is reversible and within the limits.\\n- **Council round 73** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round73-brief.md`, `codex-r73.md`, `claude-r73.md`), consensus:\\n  1. **Release work opens tonight, local and at $0:** the exporter, the release builder, the package check, tests and mutants, the $0\\n     release check. Nothing committed, pushed, published or deployed; the POC and colleagues' page unchanged. Reversible: the package\\n     can be deleted without touching what the POC serves. D726's \\\"not started\\\" described the state on 2026-11-22 and set no gate.\\n  2. **§4 (a):** an event or Yes/No question shows its question, evidence and answer with its original label, and no generated\\n     explanation. It alone guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose (option (b) cannot: a request carries the\\n     question's earlier reasoning, `views/judging.py:211`). The cost is real: readers lose the written rationale for those answers.\\n  3. **The v13s checker defects** (`PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5) are closed as won't-fix: `calc_small.py` has callers only in research\\n     code, the line is closed (D756), and the STOP bars tuning on the 36 answers. The findings stay on record.\\n  4. **Order:** the exporter and the checked package first; the reader's screen second (it completes D756's screen check). How the\\n     idea path enters the release is settled in the build design's review (round 74).\\n- **Still Alex's:** commit, push, publish, deploy, colleagues' POC page, any paid send or judge work.\\n| 38 | 11-05 | Alex：\\\"好，按这三步做，你不要再搬石头砸自己脚了，你要收敛上生产\\\"。第 1 步：引用检查搬进正式代码 `src/hivemind/baseline.py`，加\\\"行名是报告的、数在同一行就存原文那一整行\\\"的修复（漏脚注记号、跳格）；对照 36 例全对，三个弄坏的版本各抓出 1 个错；重放全部存下的读法，改变的正好是那 6 个被拒的对数。第 2 步：第三版加修好的检查读 8 月留出财报 132 次（0.096 美元），两人分类 | 第 1 步：只改了那 6 条。第 2 步过：44 个数 0 个错（3 条\\\"剩余资本开支承诺 70 亿\\\"两人不一致，对着原文定为\\\"自己的量，别的期间\\\"）；v10 3/3、v12 2/3 | 读法定为第三版加修好的检查，不再改；第 3 步写正式代码 |\\n| 39 | 11-05 | 第 3 步：做进正式系统（设计四张表，Codex 审 3 轮：第 1 轮 4 条严重、第 2 轮 2 条严重，都改；第 3 轮无严重问题） | 建成 `baseline.run` + poc-v116 + baseline-v3 提示词文件；$0 核对：44 份请求和验证时逐字节相同，3 次存下的回答走正式代码写出的记录完全一样，第一天判断正好判这些题，网页从开始跟踪那天可见；新测试 12 条、6 个弄坏版本都抓出、全套 272 条通过；设计页和 PRD 00/03/04/05/06 更新，`docs/check.py` 通过 | 交 Alex：要不要跑 14 天三遍完整验收（约 5 美元） |\\n| 40 | 11-05 | Alex：\\\"跑验收\\\"。14 天三遍完整验收：poc-v116（开始跟踪时读财报）三遍、当天重跑 poc-v108 三遍作对照，冻结尺子打分（事先锁定 `acceptance-design.md`）；电脑中途在电池上睡了约 5 小时，6 遍被暂停，插电后自己接着跑完 | **全过**：v10、v12 各 3/3（对照从没判过）；合计 53 对 45（满分 57，+8）；唯一少两次的 v17（0/3 对 2/3）两人都认定不是起点数：同一份抽取请求，新配置两遍碰巧留下\\\"中国份额归零\\\"那句，对照没留；约 4.79 美元 | 交 Alex：poc-v116 是否成为默认 |\\n| 41 | 11-05 | Alex：\\\"都做\\\"（poc-v116 设成默认；提交代码、开 PR）。默认配置改成 poc-v116，默认的条目数据库换成带财报网页原文的那一份（旧的没有原文，新默认会在它上面拒跑）；测试按用户的用法补上：不给种子题就拒绝，给了就先读财报再跑第一天 | 测试全过，5 个弄坏的版本都抓出；配置的设置和验收三遍记下的校验码一致（只改了配置里的注释）；花钱前的检查脚本在新配置的运行数据上照常跑完，但不复查读财报那一步的引用检查（记为未补的缺口）；D366 | 提交、开 PR；下一类问题等 Alex |\\n| Tightening D259's \\\"leeway\\\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\\n| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\\n| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\\n\\n## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\\n\\n- **The frozen ruler** (AGENTS §7.1, D261, D262): the extraction standard, version 5 (the signed version 3 with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four\\n  evidence boundaries and counting unit), golden-v5, the seed questions and the judgement gold; not a word changes; a disagreement is a gap in the\\n  system (D263).\\n- **The frozen extraction prompt** (D274): v74i (`poc-v108`) does not change by a word; what this phase changes is the one place that holds the filing\\n  rule (the description of the `links` field), made into a new version with a new configuration and compared with v74i. Alex has given his word for this\\n  work (2026-11-04: \\\"好你去解决问题\\\", \\\"开始做\\\"); making it the default needs his word again.\\n- **Frozen opening and judging** (D354): this phase does not touch them.\\n- **The standard's text** (in translation): §6, \\\"file under the narrowest open question; when no question takes it, record no home and drop it, and read\\n  each one at evaluation\\\"; §5.1, \\\"makes the answer to some question more or less likely\\\", with four paths, \\\"demand, supply, competition, pricing\\\"; §5.3,\\n  \\\"another company's matter is not kept when one cannot say which question about the covered company it moves through a path such as demand, supply,\\n  competition or pricing\\\".\\n- **Decisions**: D207 (one home per fact, the narrowest question), D209 (no home means dropped, each one read), D259 (leeway: a figure question takes\\n  \\\"the demand, supply, competition and pricing that make it more or less likely\\\"; the total-revenue question taking more is an accepted cost, \\\"bounded by\\n  the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions\\\"), D265 (code keeps only the narrowest), D273 (the fallback sentence), D355 (the two failed tests\\n  of the previous filing topic).\\n- **Prompt principles** (AGENTS §6): carry only the standard and add no new rule; a general hedge-fund analyst: every rule and example reads the same\\n  for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip company, names neither NVIDIA nor its products or figures, and is not taken from a test article; a\\n  classification is written as a closed set with two or three examples per class, replacing the abstract wording; quality is not fixed by lengthening\\n  the prompt: remove as much as is added, or write down the reason.\\n- **Code decides only \\\"is it the same thing\\\", never \\\"does it matter\\\"** (AGENTS §2).\\n\\n## 5. What to do\\n\\nStatus: the links-rule version that carried items 1–3 (v74l) failed its one test (§8 step 5); D361 keeps the fallback sentence, so item 3 is not carried out. The plan below is kept as written.\\n\\n1. **Replace the abstract sentence \\\"makes the answer more or less likely through demand, supply, competition or pricing\\\" with the few classes in which an analyst recognises an indirect relation, written as a closed set, each class with two or three examples from other industries** (AGENTS §6: one\\n   abstract sentence is a coin flip on every send; examples replace it). A first draft of the classes (checked against the standard line by line at\\n   design time; it holds only meanings the standard already has):\\n   - The question's own figure: this question's figures, guidance, estimates and revisions (estimates for another period or another population follow\\n     the existing rule).\\n   - The other side of the same money: a seller's revenue from the buyers the question counts; those buyers' orders and backlog with these sellers.\\n   - Price and volume: a product's price or shipments, for the question on that product's revenue.\\n   - Variants and parts: a product's variants, alternatives, key parts and schedule changes, for the question on that product's launch.\\n   - Demand, supply and competition moves with a number: customers' orders and capital-spending plans, suppliers' capacity and prices, competitors'\\n     sales and share, for the question they affect.\\n2. **State how to file a fact when two specific questions both bear on it** (the problem the `definition_no_fallback` arm exposed: Morgan Stanley's rack\\n   price was filed under the buyers' capital-spending question, and the seller's Rubin revenue question lost it). One home per fact (D207): file it under\\n   the question its figure measures most directly (for example, a hotel's room rate goes under its room-revenue question, not under the\\n   travellers'-spending question; a parts maker's revenue from carmakers goes under the carmakers' parts-spending question, not under a rival parts\\n   maker's share question); when one sentence gives a separate figure for each of two questions, write two items, each filed under its own question\\n   (code stores two items that quote the same sentence as one record linked to both questions); never also file it under a broader question about the\\n   same company (the failure of D355's test 2: the model filed it under an NVIDIA revenue question as well). The original draft's \\\"when the other\\n   party's question is open … file it there as well\\\" conflicted with D207 and was deleted on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement (D360).\\n3. **Delete the fallback sentence** and return to the standard's §6: when no question takes a fact, it is not filed; code drops it as \\\"no home\\\" and\\n   records it (D209), and evaluation reads each one.\\n4. Change only the one place that holds the filing rule; report its length in characters before and after, and write down the reason for any growth\\n   (this time's reason: examples replace one abstract sentence).\\n\\n## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\\n\\n- **Requests**: rebuild each stored request byte for byte with the production code, changing only the one place that holds the filing rule; the\\n  rebuilt request's archive id must equal the original's, or it is not sent (`resend_filing.py`, AGENTS §5). Never re-send the archive's copy whose\\n  keys were sorted alphabetically.\\n- **Articles**: development set = the 54 articles of `selection.json` (already read many times); held-out set = articles the extraction gold read and\\n  the judgement gold uses that are not among those 54, drawn once before the test, with the list frozen and never changed afterwards. Both sets are\\n  measured and reported apart.\\n- **Control**: the unchanged requests re-sent 3 times the same day. No comparison with the archive (model drift).\\n- **Each answer**: goes through the production code checks and filing first (including \\\"keep only the narrowest\\\" and \\\"no home means dropped\\\"), and is\\n  counted after.\\n- **What is counted** (`measure_filing.py`, with its matching rule fixed: items are matched on the distinct numbers and the proper nouns other than\\n  NVIDIA in the source text; a source passage the system quotes that overlaps the gold's passage also counts as the same matter; \\\"optional\\\" counts as\\n  optional; the citations in the body of the gold's answers are read):\\n  - whether each fact that matters (one the gold uses to judge any question) reached the question that uses it, counted per fact, not per \\\"fact ×\\n    question\\\";\\n  - per question: the facts that matter that reached it and the new noise that appeared, counted by the decision rule below;\\n  - the parking lot: how many facts the total-revenue question (v1, together with v22) takes in, and what they are;\\n  - noise: how many of the sentences the standard does not keep are kept; per question, how noise is filed (links on facts the standard does not keep\\n    or no question uses);\\n  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\\n  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\\n    ones that matter one by one.\\n- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \\\"every draw above the highest of the control's\\n  three\\\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\\n  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\\n  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\\n    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\\n    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\\n      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\\n    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\\n      facts must not fall.\\n  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\\n    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \\\"one fewer\\\" for that\\n      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \\\"lost outright\\\". A move to another question\\n      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\\n      question counts. \\\"One more\\\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\\n    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\\n      control never does counts as \\\"new noise\\\"; filed all three times, it counts as \\\"outright new noise\\\". The opposite direction offsets it.\\n    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\\n      smallest values that keep \\\"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\\\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\\n      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\\n      what was measured.\\n  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\\n    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\\n  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\\n  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\\n\\n## 7. Process (no drift)\\n\\n- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \\\"就测试一种，一次\\\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\\n  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\\n  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \\\"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\\\").\\n- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\\n- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\\n  sentence, in both directions.\\n- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\\n- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\\n\\n## 8. Steps and where we are\\n\\n| # | Step | Output | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\\n| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\\n| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \\\"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\\\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \\\"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\\\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \\\"a restatement of known facts\\\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \\\"乙\\\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \\\"你充分验证\\\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \\\"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\\\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \\\"改\\\"; only this sentence was changed (\\\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\\\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \\\"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\\\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \\\"跑验收\\\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \\\"都做\\\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\\n\\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\\n\\n- \\\"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\\\" (2026-11-03)\\n- \\\"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\\\" (2026-11-04)\\n- \\\"go\\\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74i.stream:40:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_20\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '15,47p' scripts/mock_build.py; sed -n '250,269p' scripts/hivemind_api.py; rg -n 'release|74h' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | tail -12\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"from hivemind.views import store  # noqa: E402\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\\n    parser.add_argument('--data', type=Path, help='explicit legacy JSON export; otherwise read the current ledger')\\n    parser.add_argument('--ledger', type=Path, default=ROOT / 'poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite')\\n    parser.add_argument('--items', type=Path, default=ROOT / 'poc/data/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite')\\n    parser.add_argument('--out', type=Path, default=ROOT / 'poc/mock/index.html')\\n    parser.add_argument('--composite-trials', type=Path, help='explicit JSON trial baskets for the Idea score preview')\\n    parser.add_argument('--market-data', type=Path, default=ROOT / 'poc/ui/data/nvda-2026-10-27.json', help='dated real stock-price snapshot for the Action preview')\\n    args = parser.parse_args()\\n    if args.data:\\n        data = json.loads(args.data.read_text())\\n    else:\\n        conn, items = service.open_ledger(str(args.ledger)), store.open_read_only(str(args.items))\\n        try:\\n            data = bundle.library(conn, items)\\n        finally:\\n            conn.close()\\n            items.close()\\n    if args.data and not data.get('schema_version') and args.ledger.exists():\\n        conn = service.open_ledger(str(args.ledger))\\n        try:\\n            data['sequence_days'] = service.seq_day_map(conn)\\n        finally:\\n            conn.close()\\n    ui = ROOT / 'poc/ui'\\n    bundled = subprocess.run(['node', str(ui / 'build.mjs'), '--json'], capture_output=True, text=True)\\n    if bundled.returncode:\\n        print('UI build failed. Install its pinned dependencies with: npm ci --prefix poc/ui', file=sys.stderr)\\n        print(bundled.stderr, file=sys.stderr)\\n        bundled.check_returncode()\\n            embedded, unchanged, tokens, error = search.ensure_index(db.ledger, db.index, **({'embed': embed} if embed else {}))\\n        except service.FirstDayNotCompleted:\\n            return \\\"index: not built, the store's first day has not completed; search is lexical until a restart after it completes\\\"\\n    return f'index: {embedded} views embedded, {unchanged} unchanged, {tokens} tokens' + (f'; embedding stopped ({error}): search runs lexical until the rest is built' if error else '')\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    global ALIASES, CFG, SEMANTIC\\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\\n    parser.add_argument('--views', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828', 'views.sqlite'))\\n    parser.add_argument('--items', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite'), help='the items database, for source titles in the idea card')\\n    parser.add_argument('--index', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'service-english', 'search-index.sqlite'))\\n    parser.add_argument('--archive', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'service-english', 'idea-archive.sqlite'), help='where idea model calls are archived for replay')\\n    parser.add_argument('--config', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'config', 'poc-v118-idea.json'), help='the config whose idea settings name the mapping and final assessment models and prompts')\\n    parser.add_argument('--universe', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'universe.json'))\\n    parser.add_argument('--host', default='127.0.0.1')\\n    parser.add_argument('--port', type=int, default=8788)\\n    parser.add_argument('--lexical', action='store_true', help='no embedding at all (no network): search ranks by the trigram index and says mode lexical')\\n    args = parser.parse_args()\\n    PATHS.update(views=args.views, items=args.items, index=args.index, archive=args.archive)\\n463:- **No idea submission in the release** (council 74). The idea path reads the ledger at every step and calls a paid model; its\\n470:**Earlier next task (done, D758): Alex chooses whether to open release work, and what non-number questions show (D757).** Decided by\\n475:**Earlier next task (done, D757): when release work opens, a $0 check of the reader's screen for number questions (D756).** On a\\n479:- **Alex closed the v13s judge line at its STOP** (D756: end the line, release with \\\"Forecast unavailable\\\"). Nothing from it enters the\\n481:- **No release work is open yet.** No other task is queued on the number-answer line.\\n486:recommendation: close the v13s judge line, and carry D726 into the first release, so number questions show sources and \\\"Forecast\\n487:unavailable\\\". When release work opens, the first step is a $0 check of the reader's screen.\\n866:- **D688's recommendation, answered by D689:** keep poc-v118 as production and pause the hybrid's release line. Questions on other\\n870:**Earlier next task, closed by D676 and D677 (D665–D675): read the release comparison's six draws when they finish, with the council-reviewed tools**\\n878:- **Result, 2026-11-19 (diagnostic, 5 draws; Alex stopped new-1).** The new system loses on the release comparison.\\n901:  5. `d400_code_check.py` and `step2_lines.py`: the hard checks and the release status.\\n904:- **If a draw stops:** no release verdict; a diagnostic export (plan §1.4 item 10).\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
