{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^##.*D7(26|56|57|58|59)|''^###.*D7(26|56|57|58|59)'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; tail -n 49 docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^##.*D7(26|56|57|58|59)|''^###.*D7(26|56|57|58|59)'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; tail -n 49 docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"10991:## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n11799:## D755 · 2026-11-23 · The paid re-send STOPs (complete); council 71: close v13s at STOP and carry D726's \"Forecast unavailable\" into the first release\n11823:## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \"Forecast unavailable\"\n11842:## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \"Forecast unavailable\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\n11867:## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \"Forecast unavailable\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\n11885:## D759 · 2026-11-23 · Slice 1 of the \"Forecast unavailable\" release is built and accepted at $0 (councils 74–74j design, 75–75g build); nothing committed or published\n     code, the line is closed (D756), and the STOP bars tuning on the 36 answers. The findings stay on record.\n  4. **Order:** the exporter and the checked package first; the reader's screen second (it completes D756's screen check). How the\n     idea path enters the release is settled in the build design's review (round 74).\n- **Still Alex's:** commit, push, publish, deploy, colleagues' POC page, any paid send or judge work.\n\n## D759 · 2026-11-23 · Slice 1 of the \"Forecast unavailable\" release is built and accepted at $0 (councils 74–74j design, 75–75g build); nothing committed or published\n\n- **Under D439 and D758.** Release work was opened by council 73 (D758). This slice carries it out locally at $0. Nothing is\n  committed, pushed, published or deployed. The POC is unchanged: no POC code imports the release module.\n- **The design** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md`):\n  - revision 10 was ready per council 74j, after ten rounds (74 to 74j);\n  - revision 11 records the build changes required by councils 75 to 75f.\n\n  It holds:\n  - one allow-listed exporter: a number question carries its question, its evidence in force and \"Forecast unavailable\"; an event or\n    Yes/No question carries its question, evidence and answer labels (D758 §4 a);\n  - the writer refuses an off-list field;\n  - the pass condition: every package field compared with its stored source at the bound, derived from the store;\n  - a staged check before one atomic no-replace publication (`renamex_np` with `RENAME_EXCL`);\n  - reports published by a no-replace link;\n  - canonical days; keys counted only once visible at the bound; store paths free of URI syntax; package files read once.\n- **Built:** `src/hivemind/release.py`, `scripts/release_build.py`, `tests/test_release.py`.\n- **Proof** (`RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md`):\n  - 36 release tests;\n  - full suite 425 passed;\n  - 31 of 32 mutants caught by failing tests. The 32nd, the canonical-day check, is equivalent on Python 3.10; under 3.13 it is shown\n    to stop a package dated 2026-08-25 from carrying evidence through 2026-09-20;\n  - the $0 release check on `old-1`, `old-2`, `old-3` and the served ledger (`poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/`), passing every\n    item it names:\n    - every field matches its store (69,636 to 91,055 fields per store);\n    - Morningstar's $361 billion, the \"Bullish confirmation\" quote and the analysts' $390 billion are kept;\n    - the system's own \"About $390 billion\" forecast, substituted into a summary or added to the manifest, is refused with its exact\n      reason;\n    - the two known Yes/No leaks keep \"Yes\", without their explanations, at their own days;\n    - a closing reason naming the band is absent;\n    - packages are 0.37–0.40 of the existing library's size, at 1.25–1.28 times its time.\n  - The diagnostic search found no condition, reason, explanation, implied outcome, reference or closing reason anywhere. Its 32\n    distinct label texts are all source wording, read by hand.\n- **What the councils taught** (each in `codex-r74*.md`, `codex-r75*.md`):\n  - a check that searches strings misses a forecast restated in other words; compare each field with its origin;\n  - a checker must derive the date, the class and the record list from the store, never from the package;\n  - one structural rule for every public write: nothing replaces an existing path;\n  - one for verification: compare against fixed values written before the run, and match each refusal's exact reason.\n- **Recorded disagreement** (`RELEASE-BUILD.md` §8): evidence summaries are kept as extraction stored them, beside their quotes.\n  Codex would use source wording for an attributed calculated amount. The cheaper, reversible course was taken.\n- **Not done, and next:**\n  - slice 2, the release page that reads only the package, with a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen (D756's screen check);\n  - the idea path in the release, deferred by council 74;\n  - commit, publish and deploy, which remain Alex's.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md; rg -n 'v8|e2295|j1580|literal|screen|reader|uint|sha256|format' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# \"Forecast unavailable\" release, slice 1: built and checked at $0 (2026-11-23)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Result: accepted by council 75g** (`codex-r75g.md`), after rounds 75 to 75f. Slice 1 is built to `RELEASE-BUILD.md`:\n     4\t- revision 10 was ready per council 74j, after ten review rounds;\n     5\t- revision 11 records what councils 75 to 75f required of the build.\n     6\t\n     7\tIt passes its tests, its mutants and the $0 release check on four stored stores. Nothing is committed, published or deployed. The POC\n     8\tis unchanged; no POC code imports the release module.\n     9\t\n    10\t- Code: `src/hivemind/release.py`, `scripts/release_build.py`, `tests/test_release.py`.\n    11\t- Check: `release_check.py`; mutants: `release_mutants.py` (both in this folder).\n    12\t- Output: `poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/`. The runs `release-check-2026-11-23/` to `-23f/` predate later fixes and are kept for\n    13\t  the record. Their counts and bytes are the same; their seconds differ by run.\n    14\t- The mutant counts below come from separate runs of `release_mutants.py`, not from `results.json`.\n    15\t\n    16\t## 1. Council 75's findings, and what changed\n    17\t\n    18\tCouncil 75 (`codex-r75.md`) reproduced the four packages' counts and both refusals of the substituted forecast. It did not accept the\n    19\tslice. Its findings and the fixes:\n    20\t\n    21\t| Finding | Fix | Proof |\n    22\t|---|---|---|\n    23\t| A key written after the bound could reclassify an earlier package (the key lookup ignored its `seq`) | the key counts only when visible at the bound | test 22; mutant \"key read without its day\" |\n    24\t| Ten text fields accepted null, which revision 10 forbids | strings only | test 23; mutant \"null accepted as text\" |\n    25\t| `check` read the data file three times: it could hash one version and certify another | one read through one folder handle; hash and parse the same bytes; the command reports that data | structural (`check_package`) |\n    26\t| A path holding `%` could make SQLite open a different file from the one named | `release.store_path` refuses `%`, `?`, `#` | test 24; mutant \"store-path refusal removed\" |\n    27\t| Test 14's marker case supplied the very line its mutant removes | the instrumentation no longer touches the line that drops the staging path | test 14; mutant caught |\n    28\t| Test 13 damaged two things | the package copy keeps `e2` with no source, which is what a checker that drops missing items expects | test 13; mutant \"inner join\" caught |\n    29\t| Tests 1, 2 and 9 lacked decisive assertions | test 25 proves the writer's own refusal; test 2 checks all five labels in `v1`'s own fields; test 9 names each refusal's reason | mutants caught |\n    30\t| The mutant runner counted any non-zero exit | it stops on a failing control, and counts a catch only with a failing test and no setup or collection error | run below |\n    31\t| My first result overstated the closing check, the diagnostic search and the dated check, and the script never failed | corrected below; the script now fails on any missed acceptance item or budget | this run |\n    32\t\n    33\t**Council 75b** (`codex-r75b.md`) confirmed the fixes above and found four more gaps, now fixed:\n    34\t\n    35\t| Finding | Fix | Proof |\n    36\t|---|---|---|\n    37\t| The store-path check returned the original path, which the opener resolved again | `store_path` returns the resolved path, and the opener is given that | test 24 (a symbolic link); mutant \"store path returned unresolved\" |\n    38\t| A named pipe in a package would make `check` hang instead of refusing | files are opened without waiting (`O_NONBLOCK`), then refused by type | test 15, through the command with a 30 s bound; mutant \"pipe opened blocking\" |\n    39\t| The check script could pass with a required example missing | the three examples are a fixed list; a missing one fails the script | this run |\n    40\t| No test reordered records, and the runner credited a failure of a test's own scratch edit | test 10 reorders questions and evidence; scratch edits fail with \"scratch anchor\", which the runner does not count | mutant \"check_origins accepting another order\" |\n    41\t\n    42\tIt also asked that test 23 cover all ten text fields (now one case per field) and that test 2 check every question's own fields for\n    43\tthe labels (done).\n    44\t\n    45\t**Council 75c** (`codex-r75c.md`) found no off-list field or mismatched value, and judged every code finding of 75 and 75b closed. It\n    46\tfound three verification gaps, now fixed:\n    47\t\n    48\t| Finding | Fix | Proof |\n    49\t|---|---|---|\n    50\t| The runner read only pytest's short line, which can omit the \"scratch anchor\" message | each failure's full message is read from pytest's XML report | this run |\n    51\t| Test 2 skipped evidence fields; test 21 did not check that the whole report is printed | test 2 allows a `v1` label only in the fixture's known genuine source text; test 21 parses the printed report | mutants \"a number label written into another question's evidence\", \"report not printed\" |\n    52\t| The check script accepted an example id whose text had changed | superseded by council 75d's rule below | this run |\n    53\t\n    54\t**Council 75d** (`codex-r75d.md`) again found no off-list field or mismatched value. Its three findings had one mechanism:\n    55\t- test 2 took its \"genuine\" text from the export under test;\n    56\t- test 21 accepted a partial report;\n    57\t- the acceptance script's \"$390 billion\" also matches the system's own forecast, and a stale-hash refusal satisfied a check meant\n    58\t  for another reason.\n    59\t\n    60\t**One structural rule now holds** (AGENTS §1): every acceptance assertion compares against fixed expected values written down before\n    61\tthe run, never values taken from the output under test, and every refusal check matches its exact reason:\n    62\t- test 2 allows a label only in the fixture's own two constant texts;\n    63\t- tests 11 and 21 require the report's exact key set and fixed values;\n    64\t- the script compares each example's full summary and quote with the stored text written into it (old-1, 2026-11-23), and each\n    65\t  refusal with its exact message;\n    66\t- mutant \"report missing a field\" proves the key-set check.\n    67\t\n    68\t**Council 75e** (`codex-r75e.md`) found no path for a forbidden or mismatched value. It showed the rule was applied only partly, and it\n    69\tis now applied to the release tests' value and refusal assertions and to every check in the script:\n    70\t- the tests compare with literal key sets and the literal marker text, never the module's own constants;\n    71\t- test 2 checks each label occurrence by its location (question, evidence, field);\n    72\t- tests 11 and 21 check the report's full contents: counts `{number 5, event 1, Yes/No 1}`, 5 evidence, 6 sources, 101 fields\n    73\t  compared, 3,313 bytes, and the two unresolved questions with their reason;\n    74\t- every refusal of a value in the tests is matched by its exact message (some occupied-path tests check only the error type or exit\n    75\t  status; see the optional items below);\n    76\t- the script pins each store's day, classes and evidence count, the marker text, `v8`'s 1,284 pieces of evidence, the identity of the\n    77\t  forged value (the system's `j1580` forecast), both leak answers (\"Yes\"), the control (`v3`, \"Yes\") and the closing reason.\n    78\t\n    79\t**Council 75f** (`codex-r75f.md`) found two certification gaps and judged everything else optional under AGENTS §5. Both are fixed:\n    80\t- **Each dated package's own day is checked.** Before, a September package passed as the August one because both answers were \"Yes\".\n    81\t  Now the package and its manifest must carry the requested day, with the evidence count of that day: 2026-08-25, 3,239 pieces; \n    82\t  2026-08-28, 5,673 pieces.\n    83\t- **The delivered format and allow-list identifiers** (`hivemind-release/1`, `release-allow-list/1`) are compared with literal strings\n    84\t  in the script, for the data and manifest of every store, and in test 1. Before, they were compared only with the module's own\n    85\t  constants.\n    86\t\n    87\t**Left as optional (council 75f, AGENTS §5),** none of which lets a wrong package through:\n    88\t- a test helper takes its expected day from the export;\n    89\t- some occupied-path tests check only the error type or the exit status;\n    90\t- test 2's scan of other questions' evidence covers summaries and quotes; the origin check compares every field.\n    91\t\n    92\t**No regression.**\n    93\t- The release tests: 36 pass. The full suite passes: 425 tests, the frozen-ruler guards included.\n    94\t- Mutants: 31 of 32 are caught by failing tests, each judged from its full failure message (a failure of the test's own scratch edit\n    95\t  does not count), with no setup errors.\n    96\t- **The 32nd, the canonical-day check removed, is equivalent on this repository's Python 3.10.10,** whose `date.fromisoformat` already\n    97\t  refuses `20260825`. Under Python 3.13, on a temporary copy of `old-1` with one later completed day:\n    98\t  - the real code refuses `20260825`;\n    99\t  - the mutant exports `v8` with 1,284 pieces of evidence through 2026-09-20 into a package dated 2026-08-25, where the right package\n   100\t    holds 621.\n   101\t\n   102\t## 2. The $0 release check (design §7)\n   103\t\n   104\t| Store | Bound | Number / event / Yes-No | Evidence | Fields compared | Data bytes (library) | Seconds (library) |\n   105\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n   106\t| old-1 | 2026-09-20 | 19 / 28 / 0 | 8,251 | 91,055 | 5,788,634 (14,478,536) | 8.05 (6.36) |\n   107\t| old-2 | 2026-09-20 | 17 / 26 / 0 | 6,306 | 69,636 | 4,427,609 (11,893,701) | 6.19 (4.91) |\n   108\t| old-3 | 2026-09-20 | 18 / 31 / 0 | 6,659 | 73,559 | 4,685,247 (12,375,915) | 6.54 (5.25) |\n   109\t| served | 2026-08-28 | 13 / 55 / 0 | 6,461 | 71,524 | 4,612,321 (12,145,774) | 4.29 (3.36) |\n   110\t\n   111\t- **Every package passed its origin check:** every field compared with its stored source at the bound.\n   112\t- **No number question is unresolved** in these stores.\n   113\t- **Budgets met:**\n   114\t  - the bytes are 0.37–0.40 of the existing library's;\n   115\t  - the seconds are 1.25–1.28 times the library's, against a budget of 3 times and 120 s.\n   116\t- **How the evidence is counted.** The count includes each piece once per question that holds it. Every piece has exactly one source\n   117\t  row (`old-1`: 5,390 rows for 5,390 pieces).\n   118\t- **The script exits non-zero when any check it names fails:** each store's day, classes and evidence; the budgets; each example; each\n   119\t  exact refusal; the forged value's identity; `v8`; each leak; the control; the closing. This run ended \"every acceptance item and\n   120\t  budget met\".\n   121\t\n   122\t**The decisive acceptance case** (council 74, `old-1`):\n   123\t- **Kept, each equal to the store and to its full text written into the script before the run:**\n   124\t  - Morningstar's $361 billion (`e2295`, under `v8`);\n   125\t  - the genuine \"Bullish confirmation\" quote (`e1865`, under `v4`, `v5`, `v8`);\n   126\t  - the analysts' \"$390 billion\" (`e3597`, under `v4`, `v5`).\n   127\t- **The system's own forecast** (`j1580` implied outcome, \"About $390 billion: …\"):\n   128\t  - substituted into `e2295`'s summary, it is refused with exactly \"question v8.evidence e2295.one_line: differs from the store\";\n   129\t  - added to the manifest, it is refused with exactly \"the manifest: keys off the allow-list ['note'], missing []\".\n   130\t\n   131\t**The other checks:**\n   132\t- **`old-1/v8`:** class `number`, marked \"Forecast unavailable\". Its 1,284 pieces of evidence are the same ids as `service.evidence` at\n   133\t  the bound.\n   134\t- **The known Yes/No leaks at their own days.**\n   135\t  - `old-3/v36` at 2026-08-25 (judgement 799) and `old-1/v10` at 2026-08-28 (judgement 865) are the latest judgements there, and\n   136\t    each package carries its own day (3,239 and 5,673 pieces of evidence).\n   137\t  - Both keep \"Yes\".\n   138\t  - The full explanation and reason texts are absent.\n   139\t  - So are the judgements' own phrases: \"around $1 trillion\", \"rung 4\", \"at rung\" and \"capex at rung\" occur in no field.\n   140\t- **Control:** event `old-1/v3` keeps \"Yes\" and its evidence, equal to the store.\n   141\t- **Closing,** on a copy of `old-1` with a closing switch for `v8`, \"due 2026-09-20, frozen on 2026-09-20 at rung 2 Bullish\":\n   142\t  - `bundle.view_bundle` exposes it;\n   143\t  - the package shows `open: false`;\n   144\t  - the reason appears nowhere.\n   145\t  - The word \"Bullish\" does occur inside six `v8` fields: five source titles and the genuine `e1865` quote. That is source wording,\n   146\t    which the design keeps.\n   147\t\n   148\t## 3. The diagnostic search, every hit read\n   149\t\n   150\tThe search covered every decoded string of each package, ids, classes, the marker and the manifest included. For each question it\n   151\ttook every stored string the package must not hold:\n   152\t- rung labels of number questions;\n   153\t- the rung conditions of every question;\n   154\t- judgement reasons, explanations, implied outcomes and references, where the store has those columns (the served ledger lacks the\n   155\t  last two);\n   156\t- every switch reason, \"created\" included.\n   157\t\n   158\t| Store | Stored strings judged | Package strings | Hits |\n   159\t|---|---|---|---|\n   160\t| old-1 | 6,670 | 91,012 | 1,378: \"created\" 987, \"Bullish\" 391 |\n   161\t| old-2 | 6,677 | 69,597 | 771: \"created\" 516, \"Bullish\" 255 |\n   162\t| old-3 | 7,045 | 73,514 | 1,613: \"created\" 1,176, labels 437 (\"Bullish\", \"High\", \"Low\", \"Bearish\", \"Middle\") |\n   163\t| served | 2,149 | 71,460 | 1,794: \"created\" 1,632, \"Bullish\" 162 |\n   164\t\n   165\t- **No condition, reason, explanation, implied outcome, reference or closing reason is found anywhere.**\n   166\t- **The label hits are 257 package fields holding 32 distinct texts, all read.** Every one is source wording:\n   167\t  - headlines: \"Jensen Huang's Bullish Call …\", \"Stock Traded Lower\", \"Earnings Call Highlights\", \"Lows Not Seen Since 2019\",\n   168\t    \"Sky-High P/E\", \"That Bearish Bet\";\n   169\t  - the memory term \"High Bandwidth Memory\";\n   170\t  - the analyst quote \"Bullish confirmation would require …\".\n   171\t- **The \"created\" hits fall in 33 distinct texts, all containing the ordinary word.** It is every question's creation reason and\n   172\t  carries no forecast.\n   173\t\n   174\t## 4. Not shown, and still open\n   175\t\n   176\t- **The reader's screen** (slice 2, D756's screen check) is not built. The release page must read only this package, with no live\n   177\t  fetch and no idea submission, and needs a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen.\n   178\t- **The idea path in the release:** deferred (council 74); its acceptance is pending.\n   179\t- **The recorded disagreement on evidence summaries** (`RELEASE-BUILD.md` §8) stands.\n   180\t- **`store.open_read_only` puts a path into a SQLite URI unescaped.** That is shared POC code; the release refuses such paths\n   181\t  rather than changing it.\n100:  trials, no idea submission control or route. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen, which completes D756's screen check.\n102:  per idea. The design's §5 idea acceptance (an idea card backed only by `v8`, and its composed request) is carried forward as pending\n124:  | envelope | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `questions` |\n129:  | manifest | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `data_sha256` |\n138:  - takes an explicit day only in canonical form: `date.fromisoformat(day).isoformat()` must equal the text given, otherwise\n154:    - `format` and `allow_list` equal the constants, and `as_of` is a canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` day (`date.fromisoformat(as_of).isoformat() == as_of`);\n202:  - the manifest has exactly its four keys, and its `format`, `allow_list` and `as_of` equal the data's;\n203:  - its sha256 equals the data file's;\n256:| `--as-of` not a valid date (`2026-08-99`) | refused by `date.fromisoformat` | nothing | none |\n284:| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\n287:## 3. Value × reader\n294:The report's reader is the person building. No POC code imports `release`.\n305:| manifest | the data's `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`; the data sha256 | `check_package` |\n321:| `bundle.library`: no default day refused; `date.fromisoformat` | same two checks |\n401:    exits 2. The items file's sha256 is unchanged.\n458:   - Morningstar's `$361 billion` estimate (`e2295`) is kept, its summary and quote equal to the stored ones;\n461:   - in a copy of the staged package, the system's `old-1` j1580 `implied_outcome` (\"About $390 billion…\") substituted into\n462:     `e2295`'s summary fails `check_origins`;\n464:3. **`old-1/v8`:** `class` is `number`, with the marker and the same evidence ids as `service.evidence` at the bound.\n468:6. **Closing.** On a temporary copy of `old-1`, add a closing switch for `v8` in the store's own format (\"due …, frozen on … at\n500:  The quote is shown beside it, so the source wording is on the reader's screen. A later version can drop the field from the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'read_package|read_once|data_bytes|FORMAT|check_package|canonical|as_of|sources|question_class' src/hivemind/release.py; rg -n 'v8|j1580|e2295|literal|hash|format|package' tests/test_release.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'read_package|read_once|data_bytes|FORMAT|check_package|canonical|as_of|sources|question_class' src/hivemind/release.py; rg -n 'v8|j1580|e2295|literal|hash|format|package' tests/test_release.py\"","aggregated_output":"24:FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'\n32:    'envelope': frozenset({'format', 'allow_list', 'as_of', 'questions'}),\n35:    'evidence': frozenset({'id', 'one_line', 'quote', 'tier', 'speaker', 'original_who', 'original_day', 'sources'}),\n37:    'manifest': frozenset({'format', 'allow_list', 'as_of', 'data_sha256'}),\n52:def canonical_day(text):\n64:def resolve(views_db, as_of=None):\n65:    \"\"\"The bound of a build or a check, one rule for both: a given day must be canonical; `service.resolve_bound` then refuses an\n67:    if as_of is not None:\n68:        canonical_day(as_of)\n69:    bound = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of)\n72:    return canonical_day(bound)\n81:def key_measure(conn, view_id, as_of):\n87:    return row['measure'] if row is not None and service.visible(conn, row['seq'], as_of) else None\n95:def question_class(conn, view_id, labels, as_of):\n99:    if key_measure(conn, view_id, as_of) in identity.EVENT_MEASURES:\n101:    if len(labels) == 2 and {vocabulary.canonical('label', label) for label in labels} == {'Yes', 'No'}:\n106:def _answer(conn, view_id, as_of, positions):\n108:    row = conn.execute('select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1', (view_id, as_of)).fetchone()\n127:def _visible_views(conn, as_of):\n128:    return [row for row in conn.execute('select view_id, question, created_seq from views order by created_seq, rowid') if service.visible(conn, row['created_seq'], as_of)]\n131:def release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None):\n135:        bound = resolve(views_db, as_of)\n141:            kind = question_class(views_db, view_id, labels, bound)\n142:            record = {'id': view_id, 'question': view['question'], 'open': service.is_open_as_of(views_db, view_id, bound), 'class': kind}\n150:                sources = []\n151:                for source in piece['sources']:\n153:                    sources.append({'title': item['title'], 'publisher': item['publisher'], 'day': source['publication_day'], 'uri': item['source_uri']})\n154:                evidence.append({'id': piece['evidence_id'], **{name: piece[name] for name in EVIDENCE_TEXT}, 'sources': sources})\n157:        data = {'format': FORMAT, 'allow_list': ALLOW_LIST, 'as_of': bound, 'questions': questions}\n182:    if data['format'] != FORMAT or data['allow_list'] != ALLOW_LIST:\n184:    canonical_day(data['as_of'])\n187:    counts = {'questions': {kind: 0 for kind in CLASSES}, 'evidence': 0, 'sources': 0}\n213:            if not isinstance(piece['sources'], list):\n214:                raise ReleaseRefused(f'{where} evidence {piece[\"id\"]}: sources is not a list')\n215:            for source in piece['sources']:\n218:            counts['sources'] += len(piece['sources'])\n226:def _open_at(conn, view_id, as_of):\n228:        if service.visible(conn, row['after_seq'], as_of):\n233:def _expected_evidence(views_db, items_db, view_id, as_of):\n238:        if not service.visible(views_db, link['seq'], as_of):\n241:        if latest is not None and service.visible(views_db, latest['seq'], as_of):\n246:        sources = []\n247:        for source in views_db.execute('select input_id, publication_day, seq from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (link['evidence_id'],)).fetchall():\n248:            if not service.visible(views_db, source['seq'], as_of):\n253:            sources.append({'title': item['title'], 'publisher': item['publisher'], 'day': source['publication_day'], 'uri': item['source_uri']})\n254:        out.append({'id': row['evidence_id'], **{name: row[name] for name in EVIDENCE_TEXT}, 'sources': sources})\n281:def check_origins(views_db, items_db, data, expected_as_of):\n282:    \"\"\"Every package field against its permitted stored source at `expected_as_of`, derived from the store and never from the\n283:    package: the day, each question's class, the questions, evidence and sources in order with their counts. Its reads are its own\n284:    SQL, apart from the identity rule (`question_class`) and the day of a sequence number (`service.visible`). Returns the number of\n287:        as_of = canonical_day(expected_as_of)\n288:        if data['as_of'] != as_of:\n289:            raise ReleaseRefused(f'the package is dated {data[\"as_of\"]}, the store bound is {as_of}')\n291:                 if service.visible(views_db, row['created_seq'], as_of)]\n296:        compared = _compare(FORMAT, data['format'], 'package.format') + _compare(ALLOW_LIST, data['allow_list'], 'package.allow_list') + 1\n301:            kind = question_class(views_db, view_id, labels, as_of)\n302:            record = {'id': view_id, 'question': view['question'], 'open': _open_at(views_db, view_id, as_of), 'class': kind}\n306:                latest = views_db.execute('select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1', (view_id, as_of)).fetchone()\n311:            expected_evidence = _expected_evidence(views_db, items_db, view_id, as_of)\n338:    manifest = {'format': data['format'], 'allow_list': data['allow_list'], 'as_of': data['as_of'], 'data_sha256': hashlib.sha256(payload).hexdigest()}\n394:    \"\"\"The package's data, read with the repeated-member check. `check_package` returns the data it checked, which is the copy to\n442:def check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None):\n445:    parsed; data that passes `check_export` and, with the stores, `check_origins` at `expected_as_of` (or at the package's own day\n466:    for name in ('format', 'allow_list', 'as_of'):\n470:        bound = expected_as_of if expected_as_of is not None else resolve(views_db, data['as_of'])\n486:            out.append({'id': question['id'], 'reason': reason, 'has_key': key_measure(views_db, question['id'], data['as_of']) is not None})\n1:\"\"\"The \"Forecast unavailable\" release package (docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md, revision 10; D726, D758).\n6:import hashlib\n149:    \"\"\"Every decoded string in the package (keys excluded).\"\"\"\n166:def build_package(stores, out, as_of=None):\n171:        release.write_package(data, staged)\n172:        release.check_package(staged, views_db, items_db, expected_as_of=data['as_of'])\n180:def rewrite_data(package, data):\n181:    \"\"\"A copy of the package's data with its manifest hash refreshed, so every other check still passes.\"\"\"\n183:    (package / release.DATA_FILE).write_bytes(payload)\n184:    manifest = json.loads((package / release.MANIFEST_FILE).read_text())\n185:    manifest.update(as_of=data['as_of'], data_sha256=hashlib.sha256(payload).hexdigest())\n186:    (package / release.MANIFEST_FILE).write_text(json.dumps(manifest))\n189:def check(stores, package):\n190:    \"\"\"The counts of `check_package` with the stores.\"\"\"\n193:        return release.check_package(package, views_db, items_db)[0]\n208:    assert (data['format'], data['allow_list']) == ('hivemind-release/1', 'release-allow-list/1')     # revision 11's identifiers, literal\n298:# ---------- §6 tests 9, 10, 13, 15, 16: the package and the origin check\n301:def test_9_package_files_hash_and_manifest(stores, tmp_path):\n302:    \"\"\"§1 check_package, §6 test 9.\"\"\"\n304:    data = build_package(stores, out)\n324:        release.write_package(data, staged)\n327:    assert build_package(stores, tmp_path / 'other')\n334:    data = build_package(stores, out)\n380:    build_package(pair, tmp_path / 'release', '2026-09-30')\n384:def test_13_check_refuses_a_missing_item_even_when_the_package_omits_its_source(stores, tmp_path):\n385:    \"\"\"§6 test 13: the items copy lacks item-3; the package copy drops every item-3 source, keeping e2 with none, its hash refreshed.\n388:    data = build_package(stores, out)\n401:    build_package(stores, out)\n416:    manifest['data_sha256'] = hashlib.sha256(payload).hexdigest()\n442:def test_16_a_day_before_the_first_question_gives_an_empty_package(stores):\n483:    items_hash = hashlib.sha256(stores[1].read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n487:    assert refused.returncode == 1 and hashlib.sha256(same.read_bytes()).hexdigest() == items_hash\n494:    assert linked.returncode == 2 and hashlib.sha256(stores[1].read_bytes()).hexdigest() == items_hash\n500:        assert checked.returncode == 2 and hashlib.sha256(variant.read_bytes()).hexdigest() == items_hash\n507:    \"\"\"A copy of the package and the command with text edits applied; each edit must match once.\"\"\"\n542:STAGED_CHECK = (\"counts, data, size = release.check_package(staged, views_db, items_db, expected_as_of=bound)\", \"counts, size = release.check_export(data), 0\")\n546:    \"\"\"§6 test 12: with a writer fault the command refuses and leaves nothing; with the fault and no staged check the bad package is\n565:    release.write_package(data, first)\n566:    release.write_package(data, second)\n573:    release.write_package(data, staged)\n636:    build_package(stores, out)\n653:    the 08-24 package.\"\"\"\n655:    store.create_view(conn, view_id='v8', looks_at='NVIDIA buyback', question='How large a buyback will NVIDIA announce by 2027?',\n658:    judge(conn, 'v8', 1, 1, 'The estimate is about $70 billion.')\n659:    store.insert(conn, 'view_keys', view_id='v8', measure='event', scope='NVIDIA', scope_key='nvidia', period_start='2026-02-01', period_end='2027-01-31',\n663:    early, late = by_id(export(stores, DAYS[0]))['v8'], by_id(export(stores, DAYS[1]))['v8']\n667:    build_package(stores, out, DAYS[0])\n668:    assert by_id(release.read_data(out))['v8']['class'] == 'number'\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
