{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'budget|first control' AGENTS.md; rg -n 'reader|release|screen|filter' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | head -35\"","aggregated_output":"120:- A foundation's acceptance carries a size and speed budget from its first control, not only correctness.\n1:# \"Forecast unavailable\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\n3:**Status: revision 11. Built** (`src/hivemind/release.py`, `scripts/release_build.py`, `tests/test_release.py`; result in\n12:- **A store path whose resolved form holds `%`, `?` or `#` is refused** (`release.store_path`), because `store.open_read_only` puts\n23:  `tests/test_release.py` and every check in `release_check.py`. Release work was opened by the council under D439 (D758). The behaviour is\n94:  - the exporter `release_export` and its self-check;\n96:  - the release builder, which calls the exporter directly;\n98:  - the $0 release check on stored stores.\n99:- **Slice 2, next.** The release page reads only the package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite\n100:  trials, no idea submission control or route. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen, which completes D756's screen check.\n101:- **No idea submission in the release** (council 74). The idea path (`idea.py`) reads the ledger at every step and calls a paid model\n113:`src/hivemind/release.py` is the one owner, beside `service.py`.\n116:  - `FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'`;\n117:  - `ALLOW_LIST = 'release-allow-list/1'`;\n119:  - `PACKAGE_FILES = {'manifest.json', 'release-data.json'}`.\n136:- **`release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None)`:**\n190:- **`write_package(data, staged)`:** writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` into the staging folder. It creates nothing\n209:`scripts/release_build.py`:\n215:  4. `release_export` at that bound;\n287:## 3. Value × reader\n291:- the release page (slice 2);\n294:The report's reader is the person building. No POC code imports `release`.\n308:**Never read by `release_export`:**\n328:| The UI contract rejects unknown fields | the release's own `check_export`; the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\n335:- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\n342:## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\n394:    - The command, late (a scratch copy with a pause before `publish`, released by the test): the test creates an empty folder at\n412:    - a symbolic link in place of `release-data.json` fails;\n445:## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\n483:The release shows each evidence summary as extraction stored it; the release computes or converts nothing. A summary can make\n497:  - Claude reads it as \"the release computes or converts nothing\".\n498:  - Both agree: no digit filter, no change to extraction.\n500:  The quote is shown beside it, so the source wording is on the reader's screen. A later version can drop the field from the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba tests/test_release.py | sed -n '290,326p;328,364p;396,444p;622,655p'; rg -n 'release-data|manifest|sha256|write_bytes|rewrite|3313|3_313|hivemind-release/1' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py\"","aggregated_output":"   290\t    assert [e['id'] for e in early['evidence']] == ['e1', 'e3']\n   291\t    assert [e['id'] for e in late['evidence']] == ['e1', 'e2', 'e4']\n   292\t    assert [s['day'] for s in early['evidence'][0]['sources']] == [DAYS[0]]\n   293\t    assert [s['day'] for s in late['evidence'][0]['sources']] == [DAYS[0], DAYS[2]]\n   294\t    short = make_items(tmp_path / 'short.sqlite', ids=('item-1', 'item-2'))\n   295\t    refused_with(lambda: export((stores[0], short)), 'evidence e1: source item item-3 is not in the items database')\n   296\t\n   297\t\n   298\t# ---------- §6 tests 9, 10, 13, 15, 16: the package and the origin check\n   299\t\n   300\t\n   301\tdef test_9_package_files_hash_and_manifest(stores, tmp_path):\n   302\t    \"\"\"§1 check_package, §6 test 9.\"\"\"\n   303\t    out = tmp_path / 'release'\n   304\t    data = build_package(stores, out)\n   305\t    assert check(stores, out)['fields_compared'] > 0\n   306\t    files = \"not exactly ['manifest.json', 'release-data.json']\"\n   307\t    variants = {\n   308\t        'foreign file': (lambda p: (p / 'notes.txt').write_text('x'), lambda p: f\"{p}: holds ['manifest.json', 'notes.txt', 'release-data.json'], {files}\"),\n   309\t        'subdirectory': (lambda p: (p / 'extra').mkdir(), lambda p: f\"{p}: holds ['extra', 'manifest.json', 'release-data.json'], {files}\"),\n   310\t        'changed byte': (lambda p: (p / release.DATA_FILE).write_bytes((p / release.DATA_FILE).read_bytes().replace(b'Morningstar', b'Morningstan')),\n   311\t                         lambda p: 'the manifest sha256 does not match the data file'),\n   312\t        'manifest prose': (lambda p: (p / release.MANIFEST_FILE).write_text(json.dumps({**json.loads((p / release.MANIFEST_FILE).read_text()), 'note': 'About $390 billion'})),\n   313\t                           lambda p: \"the manifest: keys off the allow-list ['note'], missing []\"),\n   314\t        'manifest day': (lambda p: (p / release.MANIFEST_FILE).write_text(json.dumps({**json.loads((p / release.MANIFEST_FILE).read_text()), 'as_of': DAYS[0]})),\n   315\t                         lambda p: f\"the manifest as_of '{DAYS[0]}' differs from the data '{DAYS[2]}'\"),\n   316\t    }\n   317\t    for name, (damage, message) in variants.items():\n   318\t        copy = tmp_path / f'copy-{name.replace(\" \", \"-\")}'\n   319\t        shutil.copytree(out, copy)\n   320\t        damage(copy)\n   321\t        refused_with(lambda: check(stores, copy), message(copy))\n   322\t    with pytest.raises(FileExistsError):\n   323\t        staged = release.stage(out)\n   324\t        release.write_package(data, staged)\n   325\t        release.publish(staged, out)\n   326\t    (tmp_path / '.other.staging-x').mkdir()            # another build's debris blocks nothing\n   328\t\n   329\t\n   330\tdef test_10_origin_check_derives_everything_from_the_store(stores, tmp_path):\n   331\t    \"\"\"§1 check_origins, §6 test 10: a forecast in a summary, a class swap, duplicates, another order and a future day are each\n   332\t    refused.\"\"\"\n   333\t    out = tmp_path / 'release'\n   334\t    data = build_package(stores, out)\n   335\t    cases = {}\n   336\t    forged = json.loads(json.dumps(data))\n   337\t    by_id(forged)['v1']['evidence'][1]['one_line'] = 'About $390 billion'\n   338\t    cases['forecast in a summary'] = (forged, 'question v1.evidence e2.one_line: differs from the store')\n   339\t    swapped = json.loads(json.dumps(data))\n   340\t    v5 = by_id(swapped)['v5']\n   341\t    for name in ('answers', 'answer'):\n   342\t        del v5[name]\n   343\t    v5.update({'class': 'number', 'forecast': MARKER})\n   344\t    cases['class swap'] = (swapped, 'question v5: fields differ from the store')\n   345\t    doubled = json.loads(json.dumps(data))\n   346\t    doubled['questions'].insert(1, doubled['questions'][0])\n   347\t    cases['duplicate question'] = (doubled, 'the questions differ from the store: 8 entries where the store has 7')\n   348\t    repeated = json.loads(json.dumps(data))\n   349\t    by_id(repeated)['v1']['evidence'].append(by_id(repeated)['v1']['evidence'][0])\n   350\t    cases['duplicate evidence'] = (repeated, 'question v1.evidence: 4 entries where the store has 3')\n   351\t    future = json.loads(json.dumps(data))\n   352\t    future['as_of'] = '2026-08-27'\n   353\t    cases['future day'] = (future, 'day not completed: 2026-08-27 is after the last completed day 2026-08-26')\n   354\t    reordered = json.loads(json.dumps(data))\n   355\t    reordered['questions'][0], reordered['questions'][1] = reordered['questions'][1], reordered['questions'][0]\n   356\t    cases['reordered questions'] = (reordered, 'the questions or their order differ from the store')\n   357\t    swapped = json.loads(json.dumps(data))\n   358\t    pieces = by_id(swapped)['v1']['evidence']\n   359\t    pieces[0], pieces[1] = pieces[1], pieces[0]\n   360\t    cases['reordered evidence'] = (swapped, 'question v1.evidence e1.id: differs from the store')\n   361\t    for name, (changed, reason) in cases.items():\n   362\t        copy = tmp_path / f'copy-{name.replace(\" \", \"-\")}'\n   363\t        shutil.copytree(out, copy)\n   364\t        rewrite_data(copy, changed)\n   396\t\n   397\t\n   398\tdef test_15_symbolic_links_and_repeated_member_names_are_refused(stores, tmp_path):\n   399\t    \"\"\"§6 test 15: a symbolic link, a repeated member name and a named pipe are refused (the pipe without waiting).\"\"\"\n   400\t    out = tmp_path / 'release'\n   401\t    build_package(stores, out)\n   402\t    linked = tmp_path / 'linked'\n   403\t    shutil.copytree(out, linked)\n   404\t    (tmp_path / 'outside.json').write_bytes((linked / release.DATA_FILE).read_bytes())\n   405\t    (linked / release.DATA_FILE).unlink()\n   406\t    (linked / release.DATA_FILE).symlink_to(tmp_path / 'outside.json')\n   407\t    refused_with(lambda: check(stores, linked), f'{linked}/release-data.json: not a regular file')\n   408\t    repeated = tmp_path / 'repeated'\n   409\t    shutil.copytree(out, repeated)\n   410\t    raw = (repeated / release.DATA_FILE).read_bytes()\n   411\t    genuine = b'\"one_line\":\"Morningstar estimates $361 billion of revenue for the year.\"'\n   412\t    assert raw.count(genuine) == 1\n   413\t    payload = raw.replace(genuine, b'\"one_line\":\"About $390 billion\",' + genuine)\n   414\t    (repeated / release.DATA_FILE).write_bytes(payload)\n   415\t    manifest = json.loads((repeated / release.MANIFEST_FILE).read_text())\n   416\t    manifest['data_sha256'] = hashlib.sha256(payload).hexdigest()\n   417\t    (repeated / release.MANIFEST_FILE).write_text(json.dumps(manifest))\n   418\t    refused_with(lambda: check(stores, repeated), \"a JSON member name repeats: ['one_line']\")\n   419\t    piped = tmp_path / 'piped'\n   420\t    shutil.copytree(out, piped)\n   421\t    (piped / release.DATA_FILE).unlink()\n   422\t    os.mkfifo(piped / release.DATA_FILE)\n   423\t    result = run('check', piped, '--ledger', stores[0], '--items', stores[1], timeout=30)      # a blocking open would hang here\n   424\t    assert result.returncode == 1\n   425\t    stderr_line(result, f'refused: ReleaseRefused: {piped}/release-data.json: not a regular file')\n   426\t\n   427\t\n   428\tdef test_16_the_day_must_be_valid_and_canonical(stores):\n   429\t    \"\"\"§2 day rows, §6 test 16.\"\"\"\n   430\t    refused_with(lambda: export(stores, '2026-08-99'), \"not a day: '2026-08-99'\")\n   431\t    with pytest.raises(release.ReleaseRefused) as caught:      # Python 3.10 refuses the spelling as a day; 3.11+ reads it, and the canonical rule refuses it\n   432\t        export(stores, '20260825')\n   433\t    assert str(caught.value) in (\"not a day: '20260825'\", \"a day must be written YYYY-MM-DD: '20260825'\")\n   434\t    assert [e['id'] for e in by_id(export(stores, '2026-08-25'))['v1']['evidence']] == ['e1', 'e4']\n   435\t    views_db = service.open_ledger(str(stores[0]))\n   436\t    try:\n   437\t        refused_with(lambda: release.resolve(views_db, '2026-08-27'), 'day not completed: 2026-08-27 is after the last completed day 2026-08-26', service.BoundNotCompleted)\n   438\t    finally:\n   439\t        views_db.close()\n   440\t\n   441\t\n   442\tdef test_16_a_day_before_the_first_question_gives_an_empty_package(stores):\n   443\t    \"\"\"§2 row \"valid day before the first visible question\", §6 test 16: the store's questions open on 08-24.\"\"\"\n   444\t    data = export(stores, '2026-08-23')\n   622\t    command = scratch(tmp_path, [('src/hivemind/release.py', '    try:\\n        os.unlink(temporary)\\n    except OSError:',\n   623\t                                  \"    try:\\n        raise PermissionError('test: cannot remove')\\n    except OSError:\")])\n   624\t    out = tmp_path / 'release'\n   625\t    result = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(command), 'build', '--ledger', stores[0], '--items', stores[1], '--out', out], capture_output=True, text=True)\n   626\t    leftovers = list(tmp_path.glob('.release.report.json.*'))\n   627\t    assert result.returncode == 0 and len(leftovers) == 1\n   628\t    stderr_line(result, f'report published; its temporary file {leftovers[0]} could not be removed')\n   629\t    assert json.loads(out.with_name('release.report.json').read_text())['as_of'] == DAYS[2]\n   630\t    assert list(tmp_path.glob('.release.report.json.*'))\n   631\t\n   632\t\n   633\tdef test_21_check_that_cannot_write_its_report_exits_2(stores, tmp_path):\n   634\t    \"\"\"§1 check's statuses, §6 test 21.\"\"\"\n   635\t    out = tmp_path / 'release'\n   636\t    build_package(stores, out)\n   637\t    command = scratch(tmp_path, [('src/hivemind/release.py', \"    descriptor, temporary = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=path.parent, prefix=f'.{path.name}.')\",\n   638\t                                  \"    raise PermissionError('test: cannot create')\")])\n   639\t    result = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(command), 'check', out, '--ledger', stores[0], '--items', stores[1]], capture_output=True, text=True)\n   640\t    assert result.returncode == 2 and result.stdout.startswith(f'passes {out}: ')\n   641\t    stderr_line(result, 'report not written (test: cannot create); run check to write it')\n   642\t    printed = json.loads(result.stdout[result.stdout.index('\\n{') + 1:])    # the whole report, printed on its own lines, though not written\n   643\t    assert set(printed) == REPORT_KEYS and (printed['ledger'], printed['items'], printed['as_of']) == (str(stores[0]), str(stores[1]), DAYS[2])\n   644\t    assert printed['counts'] == FIXTURE_COUNTS and printed['withheld_unresolved'] == FIXTURE_UNRESOLVED and printed['data_bytes'] == FIXTURE_DATA_BYTES\n   645\t    assert printed['export_seconds'] is None and printed['check_seconds'] >= 0\n   646\t\n   647\t\n   648\t# ---------- council 75: key visibility, text fields, store paths, the writer's own refusal\n   649\t\n   650\t\n   651\tdef test_22_a_key_written_after_the_day_does_not_reclassify_it(stores, tmp_path):\n   652\t    \"\"\"§1 question_class (council 75): a question with no key on 08-24 that gains an event key on 08-25 stays a number question in\n   653\t    the 08-24 package.\"\"\"\n   654\t    conn = store.open_db(str(stores[0]))\n   655\t    store.create_view(conn, view_id='v8', looks_at='NVIDIA buyback', question='How large a buyback will NVIDIA announce by 2027?',\n24:FORMAT, ALLOW_LIST = 'hivemind-release/1', 'release-allow-list/1'   # revision 11's identifiers, written here, not read from the module\n60:def fields(data, manifest=None):\n62:    every level (ids, classes and the marker included) and of the manifest.\"\"\"\n75:    if manifest is not None:\n76:        yield from walk(manifest, 'manifest', None, None)\n128:def refresh(package, data=None, manifest_extra=None):\n131:        (package / release.DATA_FILE).write_bytes(payload)\n132:    manifest = json.loads((package / release.MANIFEST_FILE).read_text())\n133:    manifest['data_sha256'] = hashlib.sha256((package / release.DATA_FILE).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n134:    manifest.update(manifest_extra or {})\n135:    (package / release.MANIFEST_FILE).write_text(json.dumps(manifest))\n195:    prose = out / 'old-1' / 'forged-manifest'\n197:    refresh(prose, manifest_extra={'note': implied})\n201:                           'added_to_manifest_refused': refused(ledger, items, prose),\n216:        dated_manifest = json.loads((out / name / f'package-{day}' / release.MANIFEST_FILE).read_text())\n219:            'package_as_of': dated['as_of'], 'manifest_as_of': dated_manifest['as_of'], 'evidence': report['counts']['evidence'],\n259:    for name in STORES:                                          # the delivered identifiers, data and manifest, against the literal ones\n269:                        'added_to_manifest_refused': \"the manifest: keys off the allow-list ['note'], missing []\"}   # exact, so another refusal (a stale hash) does not count\n276:        failures += [] if (leak['package_as_of'], leak['manifest_as_of'], leak['evidence']) == (DATED[name][0], DATED[name][0], DATED[name][1]) else [f'{name}: package day or evidence']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py | sed -n '1,145p'; ls -la poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/old-1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py | sed -n '1,145p'; ls -la poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/old-1\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"The $0 release check of RELEASE-BUILD.md §7 on four stored stores, read-only (a closing switch is added only to a copy).\n     2\t\n     3\t    python3 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py <new output folder>\n     4\t\n     5\tBuilds each store's package with the real command, then: the decisive acceptance case on old-1; old-1/v8; the two known Yes/No leaks\n     6\tat their own days; an unchanged event control; a closing switch on a copy; the diagnostic search of every forbidden stored string in\n     7\tevery decoded package field; the size and speed budgets against `bundle.library` on the same store. Writes results.json there.\"\"\"\n     8\timport hashlib\n     9\timport json\n    10\timport shutil\n    11\timport sqlite3\n    12\timport subprocess\n    13\timport sys\n    14\timport time\n    15\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    16\t\n    17\tREPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]\n    18\tsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n    19\tfrom hivemind import bundle, release, service  # noqa: E402\n    20\tfrom hivemind.views import store  # noqa: E402\n    21\t\n    22\tCOMMAND = REPO / 'scripts' / 'release_build.py'\n    23\tMARKER = 'Forecast unavailable'                     # D726's words, written here, not read from the module under test\n    24\tFORMAT, ALLOW_LIST = 'hivemind-release/1', 'release-allow-list/1'   # revision 11's identifiers, written here, not read from the module\n    25\tDATED = {'old-3/v36@2026-08-25': ('2026-08-25', 3239), 'old-1/v10@2026-08-28': ('2026-08-28', 5673)}   # each dated package's day and evidence\n    26\tEXPECTED = {   # each store's default day, classes and evidence, fixed before this run from the reviewed first run (councils 75–75e reproduced them)\n    27\t    'old-1': ('2026-09-20', {'number': 19, 'event': 28, 'yes_no': 0}, 8251),\n    28\t    'old-2': ('2026-09-20', {'number': 17, 'event': 26, 'yes_no': 0}, 6306),\n    29\t    'old-3': ('2026-09-20', {'number': 18, 'event': 31, 'yes_no': 0}, 6659),\n    30\t    'served': ('2026-08-28', {'number': 13, 'event': 55, 'yes_no': 0}, 6461),\n    31\t}\n    32\tJ1580_PREFIX = 'About $390 billion: $164 billion reported in the first half'   # the system's own forecast used as the forged value\n    33\tCLOSING_REASON = 'due 2026-09-20, frozen on 2026-09-20 at rung 2 Bullish'\n    34\tCOMPARISON_ITEMS = REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/items-comparison.sqlite'\n    35\tSTORES = {\n    36\t    'old-1': (REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite', COMPARISON_ITEMS),\n    37\t    'old-2': (REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite', COMPARISON_ITEMS),\n    38\t    'old-3': (REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/views.sqlite', COMPARISON_ITEMS),\n    39\t    'served': (REPO / 'poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite', REPO / 'poc/data/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite'),\n    40\t}\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\tdef build(ledger, items, out, as_of=None):\n    44\t    args = [sys.executable, str(COMMAND), 'build', '--ledger', str(ledger), '--items', str(items), '--out', str(out)] + (['--as-of', as_of] if as_of else [])\n    45\t    result = subprocess.run(args, capture_output=True, text=True, env={'PATH': '/usr/bin:/bin', 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE': '1'})\n    46\t    if result.returncode != 0:\n    47\t        raise SystemExit(f'build {out} exited {result.returncode}: {result.stderr}')\n    48\t    return json.loads(out.with_name(out.name + '.report.json').read_text()), release.read_data(out)\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef check(ledger, items, package):\n    52\t    views_db, items_db = service.open_ledger(str(ledger)), store.open_read_only(str(items))\n    53\t    try:\n    54\t        return release.check_package(package, views_db, items_db)[0]\n    55\t    finally:\n    56\t        views_db.close()\n    57\t        items_db.close()\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\tdef fields(data, manifest=None):\n    61\t    \"\"\"(question id, field path, evidence id, text) for every decoded string of the package: every string value of the data at\n    62\t    every level (ids, classes and the marker included) and of the manifest.\"\"\"\n    63\t    def walk(value, path, question_id, evidence_id):\n    64\t        if isinstance(value, dict):\n    65\t            question_id = value['id'] if 'class' in value else question_id\n    66\t            evidence_id = value['id'] if 'one_line' in value else evidence_id\n    67\t            for key, item in value.items():\n    68\t                yield from walk(item, f'{path}.{key}' if path else key, question_id, evidence_id)\n    69\t        elif isinstance(value, list):\n    70\t            for n, item in enumerate(value):\n    71\t                yield from walk(item, f'{path}[{n}]', question_id, evidence_id)\n    72\t        elif isinstance(value, str):\n    73\t            yield question_id, path, evidence_id, value\n    74\t    yield from walk(data, '', None, None)\n    75\t    if manifest is not None:\n    76\t        yield from walk(manifest, 'manifest', None, None)\n    77\t\n    78\t\n    79\tdef forbidden(ledger, data):\n    80\t    \"\"\"Every stored string the package must not hold, by question and kind; judgement columns read only where the store has them.\"\"\"\n    81\t    conn = service.open_ledger(str(ledger))\n    82\t    try:\n    83\t        columns = {row[1] for row in conn.execute('pragma table_info(judgements)')}\n    84\t        texts = [c for c in ('reasons', 'why_changed', 'implied_outcome', 'reference') if c in columns]\n    85\t        out = []\n    86\t        for question in data['questions']:\n    87\t            view_id = question['id']\n    88\t            for row in conn.execute('select label, condition from rungs where view_id=?', (view_id,)):\n    89\t                if question['class'] == 'number':                # an event's or Yes/No question's labels are its shown answers\n    90\t                    out.append((view_id, 'rung label', row['label']))\n    91\t                out.append((view_id, 'rung condition', row['condition']))\n    92\t            for row in conn.execute(f'select {\", \".join(texts)} from judgements where view_id=?', (view_id,)):\n    93\t                out += [(view_id, name, row[name]) for name in texts]\n    94\t            out += [(view_id, 'switch reason', row['reason']) for row in conn.execute('select reason from view_switches where view_id=?', (view_id,))]\n    95\t        return [entry for entry in out if entry[2]], [c for c in ('implied_outcome', 'reference') if c not in columns]\n    96\t    finally:\n    97\t        conn.close()\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\tdef diagnostics(ledger, data, package):\n   101\t    stored, absent = forbidden(ledger, data)\n   102\t    located = list(fields(data, json.loads((package / release.MANIFEST_FILE).read_text())))\n   103\t    joined = '\\x00'.join(text for *_, text in located)\n   104\t    hits = []\n   105\t    for view_id, kind, text in set(stored):\n   106\t        if text in joined:\n   107\t            for question_id, path, evidence_id, field in located:\n   108\t                if text in field:\n   109\t                    hits.append({'stored_in': view_id, 'kind': kind, 'text': text[:200], 'found_in': question_id, 'field': path, 'evidence': evidence_id})\n   110\t    return {'stored_strings_judged': len(set(stored)), 'package_strings': len(located), 'judgement_columns_absent': absent, 'hits': hits}\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\tdef library_baseline(ledger, items):\n   114\t    views_db, items_db = service.open_ledger(str(ledger)), store.open_read_only(str(items))\n   115\t    try:\n   116\t        started = time.monotonic()\n   117\t        payload = bundle.library(views_db, items_db)\n   118\t        return len(json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False).encode()), time.monotonic() - started\n   119\t    finally:\n   120\t        views_db.close()\n   121\t        items_db.close()\n   122\t\n   123\t\n   124\tdef by_id(data):\n   125\t    return {q['id']: q for q in data['questions']}\n   126\t\n   127\t\n   128\tdef refresh(package, data=None, manifest_extra=None):\n   129\t    if data is not None:\n   130\t        payload = json.dumps(data, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(',', ':')).encode()\n   131\t        (package / release.DATA_FILE).write_bytes(payload)\n   132\t    manifest = json.loads((package / release.MANIFEST_FILE).read_text())\n   133\t    manifest['data_sha256'] = hashlib.sha256((package / release.DATA_FILE).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n   134\t    manifest.update(manifest_extra or {})\n   135\t    (package / release.MANIFEST_FILE).write_text(json.dumps(manifest))\n   136\t\n   137\t\n   138\tdef refused(ledger, items, package):\n   139\t    try:\n   140\t        check(ledger, items, package)\n   141\t    except release.ReleaseRefused as error:\n   142\t        return str(error)\n   143\t    return None\n   144\t\n   145\t\ntotal 16\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 9 lchingen  staff  288 Nov 23 11:34 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 7 lchingen  staff  224 Nov 23 11:34 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 5 lchingen  staff  160 Nov 23 11:34 closing\ndrwx------@ 4 lchingen  staff  128 Nov 23 11:32 forged-manifest\ndrwx------@ 4 lchingen  staff  128 Nov 23 11:32 forged-summary\ndrwx------@ 4 lchingen  staff  128 Nov 23 11:32 package\ndrwx------@ 4 lchingen  staff  128 Nov 23 11:33 package-2026-08-28\n-rw-------@ 1 lchingen  staff  471 Nov 23 11:34 package-2026-08-28.report.json\n-rw-------@ 1 lchingen  staff  471 Nov 23 11:32 package.report.json\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '11823,11885p'; ls -1 poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g; rg --files docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers | rg -i 'unavailable|release-design|r75d\\\\.md'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '11823,11885p'; ls -1 poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g; rg --files docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers | rg -i 'unavailable|release-design|r75d\\\\.md'\"","aggregated_output":" 11823\t## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \"Forecast unavailable\"\n 11824\t\n 11825\t- **The question** (after D755): \"付费重发的结论是“停”：luna 在新格式下格式错误多（36 个首发里 22 个被拒），在说不清的题上还会硬给数；不过“两题合在一起算”确实避免了自相矛盾。数字题这条线下一步怎么走？\"\n 11826\t  - Options:\n 11827\t    - \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\": the council's consensus;\n 11828\t    - \"换更强的模型再小测一次\": a stronger model or higher effort, with a small paid probe and a cap Alex names;\n 11829\t    - \"先停，我想谈谈\".\n 11830\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\".\n 11831\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11832\t  - The v13s judge line ends at its STOP. Nothing from it enters the product, and poc-v118 stays the product (D690).\n 11833\t  - The first release carries D726: number questions show the question and its sources with \"Forecast unavailable\", the band, the\n 11834\t    forecast text and the history withheld together.\n 11835\t  - The one next step, when release work opens, is a $0 check of the reader's screen on a stored number question that has a\n 11836\t    forecast and history: only the question, its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\" appear.\n 11837\t- **Kept for the record, not built:**\n 11838\t  - the D725 consistency finding (separate answers contradicted each other in 8 of 9 pairs, joint answers in none);\n 11839\t  - the open checker defects in `PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5;\n 11840\t  - the v13s request and harness in `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/`.\n 11841\t\n 11842\t## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \"Forecast unavailable\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\n 11843\t\n 11844\t- **Why.** Alex's direction tonight was to converge and head toward production (D750), and he chose to release with \"Forecast\n 11845\t  unavailable\" (D756). D726 says it \"is built with the release work, which is not started\". Council 72 agreed that opening release\n 11846\t  work is Alex's call, so tonight's step is the design, not the build.\n 11847\t- **The gap, measured at $0** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` §1):\n 11848\t  - today every reader of a number question can see its forecast: the service, the idea input, the closing text;\n 11849\t  - Yes/No and event explanations can quote number forecasts (`old-3/v36` judgement 799, `old-1/v10` judgement 865).\n 11850\t- **The design, after four review rounds** (`codex-r72.md` … `codex-r72d.md`):\n 11851\t  - one release exporter with an explicit allow-list, called directly by the release builder; the finished package is checked;\n 11852\t  - for a number question, the allow-list holds only the question, its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\";\n 11853\t  - the release reads nothing else: no live POC service, no translated or prepared JSON, no composite trials;\n 11854\t  - identity is structural: a question is a number question unless it is an event measure or a canonical Yes/No pair, and unresolved\n 11855\t    records are withheld and listed. Verified on four stores with no wrong result;\n 11856\t  - tests, mutants and an end-to-end acceptance on `old-1/v8` and the two known event leaks.\n 11857\t  - **Why an allow-list.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new leak paths in a reader-by-reader design, so revision 3 replaced that\n 11858\t    approach with one structural rule.\n 11859\t- **Open for Alex:**\n 11860\t  1. whether to open release work now (then: build to this design, then the $0 release check);\n 11861\t  2. what questions that are not number questions show in the release:\n 11862\t     - (a) answer and label without explanation text, recommended by the council and Claude;\n 11863\t     - (b) explanations only where the judge was shown no number question's state: 21 of 85 questions at the latest answer, and it\n 11864\t       cannot guarantee that no number forecast is quoted.\n 11865\t- **Not done.** Nothing is built and nothing is committed. The POC is unchanged.\n 11866\t\n 11867\t## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \"Forecast unavailable\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\n 11868\t\n 11869\t- **Why the council decides.** Alex is asleep and delegated tonight's decisions (D750: \"这边的决策交给你，还有 Council … 准备要往\n 11870\t  Production 方向去走了\"). He had already chosen the behaviour (D726 \"同意\"; D756 \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\"). D757 left two\n 11871\t  choices for him; under D439 a choice that would go to Alex goes to the council when it is reversible and within the limits.\n 11872\t- **Council round 73** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round73-brief.md`, `codex-r73.md`, `claude-r73.md`), consensus:\n 11873\t  1. **Release work opens tonight, local and at $0:** the exporter, the release builder, the package check, tests and mutants, the $0\n 11874\t     release check. Nothing committed, pushed, published or deployed; the POC and colleagues' page unchanged. Reversible: the package\n 11875\t     can be deleted without touching what the POC serves. D726's \"not started\" described the state on 2026-11-22 and set no gate.\n 11876\t  2. **§4 (a):** an event or Yes/No question shows its question, evidence and answer with its original label, and no generated\n 11877\t     explanation. It alone guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose (option (b) cannot: a request carries the\n 11878\t     question's earlier reasoning, `views/judging.py:211`). The cost is real: readers lose the written rationale for those answers.\n 11879\t  3. **The v13s checker defects** (`PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5) are closed as won't-fix: `calc_small.py` has callers only in research\n 11880\t     code, the line is closed (D756), and the STOP bars tuning on the 36 answers. The findings stay on record.\n 11881\t  4. **Order:** the exporter and the checked package first; the reader's screen second (it completes D756's screen check). How the\n 11882\t     idea path enters the release is settled in the build design's review (round 74).\n 11883\t- **Still Alex's:** commit, push, publish, deploy, colleagues' POC page, any paid send or judge work.\n 11884\t\n 11885\t## D759 · 2026-11-23 · Slice 1 of the \"Forecast unavailable\" release is built and accepted at $0 (councils 74–74j design, 75–75g build); nothing committed or published\nold-1\nold-2\nold-3\nresults.json\nserved\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r75d.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
