{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"web_search","id":"exec-8e8b2f90-849b-492f-ba08-242714f1388f","query":"site:chromium.googlesource.com inspector-protocol network blocked by CSP fetch Network.loadingFailed blockedReason csp requestWillBeSent inspector test Content Security Policy fetch ...","action":{"type":"search","queries":["site:chromium.googlesource.com inspector-protocol network blocked by CSP fetch Network.loadingFailed blockedReason csp requestWillBeSent inspector test Content Security Policy fetch","site:w3.org CSP3 meta policy navigate links navigation hash base64 style script securitypolicyviolation resource hints DNS prefetch","site:html.spec.whatwg.org script data restrictions escaping script noscript scripting enabled details toggle coalesced charset UTF-8 first 1024"]},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.w3.org","ref_id":"turn0search0","snippet":"A server MAY declare a policy for a particular resource representation via an HTTP response header field whose value is a serialized CSP. ... When","title":"Content Security Policy Level 3","url":"https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-CSP3-20261027/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.w3.org","ref_id":"turn0search1","snippet":"This document is an iteration on Content Security Policy Level 2, with the goal of more clearly explaining the interactions between CSP, HTML, and Fetch","title":"Content Security Policy Level 3","url":"https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"chromium.googlesource.com","ref_id":"turn0search2","snippet":"| inspectorBackend.registerEnum(\"Network.BlockedReason\", {Other: \"other\", Csp: \"csp\", MixedContent: \"mixed-content\", Origin: \"origin\", Inspector: \"inspector\", Integrity: \"integrity\", SubresourceFilter","title":"front_end/generated/InspectorBackendCommands.js - devtools/devtools-frontend - Git at Google","url":"https://chromium.googlesource.com/devtools/devtools-frontend/%2B/b6c7456a9a228c45bcdd7cf5f35eb278b2698f0d/front_end/generated/InspectorBackendCommands.js"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.w3.org","ref_id":"turn0search3","snippet":"This document defines directives which govern resource fetching (in § 6.1 Fetch Directives), directives which govern the state of a document (in § 6.3 Document","title":"Content Security Policy Level 3","url":"https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-CSP3-20260306/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"chromium.googlesource.com","ref_id":"turn0search4","snippet":"diff --git a/third_party/blink/web_tests/http/tests/inspector-protocol/fetch/blocked-by-client-expected.txt b/third_party/blink/web_tests/http/tests/inspector-protocol/fetch/blocked-by-client-expected","title":"Diff - 2962966045e7e741d2ed3d598f067864086b4275^! - chromium/src - Git at Google","url":"https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/%2B/2962966045e7e741d2ed3d598f067864086b4275%5E%21/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.w3.org","ref_id":"turn0search5","snippet":"#### 2.3.1. ... hash-source = \"'\" hash-algorithm \"-\" base64-value \"'\" ... algorithm attempts to mitigate this specific attack by walking through `script` or `style` element","title":"Content Security Policy Level 3","url":"https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"chromium.googlesource.com","ref_id":"turn0search6","snippet":"| # The reason why request was blocked. ... | csp | mixed-content ... | inspector ... | # Resource mimeType as determined by the","title":"third_party/WebKit/Source/core/inspector/browser_protocol.pdl - chromium/src - Git at Google","url":"https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/%2B/66.0.3359.158/third_party/WebKit/Source/core/inspector/browser_protocol.pdl"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"chromium.googlesource.com","ref_id":"turn0search7","snippet":"| { \"name\": \"requestId\", \"$ref\": \"Network.RequestId\", \"description\": \"Identifier of the network request to get content for.\" ... | \"dependencies\": [\"Runtime\", \"Security\"], ... | \"enum\": [\"Failed\",","title":"third_party/WebKit/Source/core/inspector/browser_protocol.json - chromium/src - Git at Google","url":"https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/%2B/16c95656c2e3d266d10fd2af768b87c9b6574ce2/third_party/WebKit/Source/core/inspector/browser_protocol.json"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"chromium.googlesource.com","ref_id":"turn0search8","snippet":"diff --git a/third_party/blink/web_tests/http/tests/inspector-protocol/network/load-network-resource-csp-expected.txt b/third_party/blink/web_tests/http/tests/inspector-protocol/network/load-network-r","title":"Diff - 65c2187d64cb6fadc17087fa9cff4e2e945835c8^! - chromium/src - Git at Google","url":"https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/%2B/65c2187d64cb6fadc17087fa9cff4e2e945835c8%5E%21/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"chromium.googlesource.com","ref_id":"turn0search9","snippet":"| # Whether the request complied with Certificate Transparency policy ... | # The reason why request was blocked. ... | csp | mixed-content ...","title":"third_party/blink/public/devtools_protocol/domains/Network.pdl - devtools/devtools-frontend - Git at Google","url":"https://chromium.googlesource.com/devtools/devtools-frontend/%2B/main/third_party/blink/public/devtools_protocol/domains/Network.pdl"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"html.spec.whatwg.org","ref_id":"turn0search10","snippet":"For example, scripts with their `type` attribute set to \"`text/javascript; charset=utf-8`\" will not be evaluated, even though that is a valid JavaScript MIME type when","title":"HTML Standard","url":"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.w3.org","ref_id":"turn0search11","snippet":"For example, observing the content of prefetched or prerendered resources, or observing the DNS, IP, and hostname information exposed during connection establishment, both for secure","title":"Resource Hints","url":"https://www.w3.org/TR/2020/WD-resource-hints-20201005/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"html.spec.whatwg.org","ref_id":"turn0search12","snippet":"A page might choose to mitigate the risk of cross-site scripting attacks by preventing the execution of inline JavaScript, as well as blocking all plugin","title":"HTML Standard","url":"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/print.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"lists.w3.org","ref_id":"turn0search13","snippet":"script-src ... Content Security Policy (CSP) is a W3C standard de-","title":"CCSP: Controlled Relaxation of Content Security Policies","url":"https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-webappsec/2017Jun/att-0012/main.pdf"}]}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py | sed -n '145,228p;249,292p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py | sed -n '145,228p;249,292p'\"","aggregated_output":"   145\t\n   146\tdef main(out):\n   147\t    out = Path(out).absolute()\n   148\t    out.mkdir()                                            # a new folder; refuses an existing one\n   149\t    results = {'stores': {}}\n   150\t    packages = {}\n   151\t    for name, (ledger, items) in STORES.items():\n   152\t        (out / name).mkdir()\n   153\t        report, data = build(ledger, items, out / name / 'package')\n   154\t        packages[name] = data\n   155\t        library_bytes, library_seconds = library_baseline(ledger, items)\n   156\t        seconds = report['export_seconds'] + report['check_seconds']\n   157\t        results['stores'][name] = {\n   158\t            'as_of': report['as_of'], 'counts': report['counts'], 'withheld_unresolved': len(report['withheld_unresolved']),\n   159\t            'unresolved': report['withheld_unresolved'], 'data_bytes': report['data_bytes'], 'library_bytes': library_bytes,\n   160\t            'seconds': round(seconds, 2), 'library_seconds': round(library_seconds, 2),\n   161\t            'bytes_within_budget': report['data_bytes'] <= library_bytes,\n   162\t            'seconds_within_budget': seconds <= 3 * library_seconds and seconds <= 120,\n   163\t            'diagnostics': diagnostics(ledger, data, out / name / 'package')}\n   164\t        print(name, json.dumps({k: v for k, v in results['stores'][name].items() if k not in ('unresolved', 'diagnostics')}), 'hits', len(results['stores'][name]['diagnostics']['hits']))\n   165\t\n   166\t    ledger, items = STORES['old-1']\n   167\t    data, package = packages['old-1'], out / 'old-1' / 'package'\n   168\t    conn = service.open_ledger(str(ledger))\n   169\t    stored = {row['evidence_id']: row for row in conn.execute(\"select * from evidence where evidence_id in ('e2295','e1865','e3597')\")}\n   170\t    implied = conn.execute('select implied_outcome from judgements where judgement_id=1580').fetchone()[0]\n   171\t    in_force_v8 = [e['evidence_id'] for e in service.evidence(conn, 'v8', data['as_of'])]\n   172\t    conn.close()\n   173\t    required_text = {   # each example's full stored text, written down before the run (old-1, 2026-11-23); compared exactly\n   174\t        'e2295': ('Morningstar cites NVIDIA Data Center revenue of $3 billion in FY2020 and $194 billion in FY2026, and estimates $361 billion in FY2027, up 86% year over year.',\n   175\t                  'Nvidia’s DC business has achieved exponential growth already, rising from $3 billion in fiscal 2020 to $194 billion in fiscal 2026, and we estimate it will be $361 billion in fiscal 2027, representing 86% annual growth.'),\n   176\t        'e1865': ('The author identifies firm SpaceX procurement commitments and NVIDIA Data Center growth above 60% into FY2028 as bullish confirmation conditions.',\n   177\t                  'Bullish confirmation would require firm procurement commitments for the SpaceX buildout and continued NVIDIA Data Center growth above 60% into fiscal 2028.'),\n   178\t        'e3597': ('The author says analysts estimate NVIDIA revenue of about $390 billion in calendar 2027 and over $550 billion in calendar 2028, with annual sales growth of roughly 24% to 25%.',\n   179\t                  'Analysts see revenue reaching about $390 billion in 2027 and more than $550 billion in 2028, with annual sales growth of roughly 24% to 25%.')}\n   180\t    kept = {}\n   181\t    for evidence_id in ('e2295', 'e1865', 'e3597'):              # the fixed examples: a missing one is a failure, not a smaller list\n   182\t        if evidence_id not in stored:\n   183\t            kept[evidence_id] = {'questions': [], 'equal_to_store': False, 'present': False}\n   184\t            continue\n   185\t        holders = [(q['id'], e) for q in data['questions'] for e in q['evidence'] if e['id'] == evidence_id]\n   186\t        kept[evidence_id] = {'questions': [h[0] for h in holders],\n   187\t                             'equal_to_store': all(e['one_line'] == stored[evidence_id]['one_line'] and e['quote'] == stored[evidence_id]['quote'] for _, e in holders) and bool(holders),\n   188\t                             'present': bool(holders),\n   189\t                             'holds_its_wording': bool(holders) and all((e['one_line'], e['quote']) == required_text[evidence_id] for _, e in holders)}\n   190\t    forged = out / 'old-1' / 'forged-summary'\n   191\t    shutil.copytree(package, forged)\n   192\t    changed = json.loads(json.dumps(data))\n   193\t    next(e for e in by_id(changed)['v8']['evidence'] if e['id'] == 'e2295')['one_line'] = implied\n   194\t    refresh(forged, changed)\n   195\t    prose = out / 'old-1' / 'forged-manifest'\n   196\t    shutil.copytree(package, prose)\n   197\t    refresh(prose, manifest_extra={'note': implied})\n   198\t    v8 = by_id(data)['v8']\n   199\t    results['decisive'] = {'kept': kept, 'implied_outcome_j1580': implied[:120],\n   200\t                           'substituted_into_e2295_refused': refused(ledger, items, forged),\n   201\t                           'added_to_manifest_refused': refused(ledger, items, prose),\n   202\t                           'unchanged_package_passes': check(ledger, items, package)['fields_compared']}\n   203\t    results['decisive']['forged_value_is_j1580'] = implied.startswith(J1580_PREFIX)\n   204\t    results['old-1/v8'] = {'class': v8['class'], 'forecast': v8['forecast'], 'evidence': len(v8['evidence']),\n   205\t                           'same_ids_as_service_evidence': [e['id'] for e in v8['evidence']] == in_force_v8}\n   206\t\n   207\t    leaks = {}\n   208\t    for name, view_id, day, judgement_id in (('old-3', 'v36', '2026-08-25', 799), ('old-1', 'v10', '2026-08-28', 865)):\n   209\t        ledger, items = STORES[name]\n   210\t        report, dated = build(ledger, items, out / name / f'package-{day}', day)\n   211\t        conn = service.open_ledger(str(ledger))\n   212\t        row = conn.execute('select judgement_id, rung, why_changed, reasons from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1', (view_id, day)).fetchone()\n   213\t        label = conn.execute('select label from rungs where view_id=? and position=?', (view_id, row['rung'])).fetchone()[0]\n   214\t        conn.close()\n   215\t        record = by_id(dated)[view_id]\n   216\t        dated_manifest = json.loads((out / name / f'package-{day}' / release.MANIFEST_FILE).read_text())\n   217\t        texts = [text for *_, text in fields(dated)]\n   218\t        leaks[f'{name}/{view_id}@{day}'] = {\n   219\t            'package_as_of': dated['as_of'], 'manifest_as_of': dated_manifest['as_of'], 'evidence': report['counts']['evidence'],\n   220\t            'latest_judgement': row['judgement_id'], 'expected_judgement': judgement_id, 'label_kept': record['answer'] == label, 'answer': record['answer'],\n   221\t            'why_changed_absent': not any(row['why_changed'] in t for t in texts), 'reasons_absent': not any((row['reasons'] or '\\x01') in t for t in texts),\n   222\t            'phrase_fields': {phrase: [(q, p, e, t[:160]) for q, p, e, t in fields(dated) if phrase in t]\n   223\t                              for phrase in ('around $1 trillion', 'rung 4', 'at rung', 'capex at rung')}}\n   224\t    results['leaks'] = leaks\n   225\t\n   226\t    ledger, items = STORES['old-1']\n   227\t    conn = service.open_ledger(str(ledger))\n   228\t    control = next(q for q in data['questions'] if q['class'] == 'event' and q['id'] not in ('v10',) and q['answer'] is not None)\n   249\t    views_db.close()\n   250\t    items_db.close()\n   251\t    report, closed = build(copy, items, closing / 'package')\n   252\t    texts = [text for *_, text in fields(closed)]\n   253\t    results['closing'] = {'reason': reason, 'bundle_exposes_reason': any(s.get('reason') == reason for s in exposed['switches']),\n   254\t                          'package_open': by_id(closed)['v8']['open'], 'reason_absent': not any(reason in t for t in texts),\n   255\t                          'rung_label_inside_v8_fields': [(p, e, t[:120]) for q, p, e, t in fields(closed) if q == 'v8' and rung_label in t]}\n   256\t    (out / 'results.json').write_text(json.dumps(results, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))\n   257\t    print(json.dumps({k: v for k, v in results.items() if k != 'stores'}, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))\n   258\t    failures = [f'{name}: {key}' for name, s in results['stores'].items() for key in ('bytes_within_budget', 'seconds_within_budget') if not s[key]]\n   259\t    for name in STORES:                                          # the delivered identifiers, data and manifest, against the literal ones\n   260\t        delivered = json.loads((out / name / 'package' / release.MANIFEST_FILE).read_text())\n   261\t        failures += [] if (packages[name]['format'], packages[name]['allow_list'], delivered['format'], delivered['allow_list']) == (FORMAT, ALLOW_LIST, FORMAT, ALLOW_LIST) else [f'{name}: format or allow-list']\n   262\t    failures += [f'{name}: day, classes or evidence' for name, (day, classes, evidence) in EXPECTED.items()\n   263\t                 if (results['stores'][name]['as_of'], results['stores'][name]['counts']['questions'], results['stores'][name]['counts']['evidence']) != (day, classes, evidence)]\n   264\t    failures += [] if results['decisive']['forged_value_is_j1580'] else ['the forged value is not the system forecast j1580']\n   265\t    decisive = results['decisive']\n   266\t    failures += [f'kept {e}' for e in ('e2295', 'e1865', 'e3597')\n   267\t                 if not (decisive['kept'].get(e, {}).get('present') and decisive['kept'][e]['equal_to_store'] and decisive['kept'][e]['holds_its_wording'])]\n   268\t    expected_reasons = {'substituted_into_e2295_refused': 'question v8.evidence e2295.one_line: differs from the store',\n   269\t                        'added_to_manifest_refused': \"the manifest: keys off the allow-list ['note'], missing []\"}   # exact, so another refusal (a stale hash) does not count\n   270\t    failures += [k for k, reason in expected_reasons.items() if decisive[k] != reason]\n   271\t    failures += [] if (results['old-1/v8']['same_ids_as_service_evidence'] and results['old-1/v8']['forecast'] == MARKER\n   272\t                       and results['old-1/v8']['class'] == 'number' and results['old-1/v8']['evidence'] == 1284) else ['old-1/v8']\n   273\t    for name, leak in results['leaks'].items():\n   274\t        failures += [f'{name}: {k}' for k in ('label_kept', 'why_changed_absent', 'reasons_absent') if not leak[k]]\n   275\t        failures += [] if leak['answer'] == 'Yes' else [f'{name}: answer']\n   276\t        failures += [] if (leak['package_as_of'], leak['manifest_as_of'], leak['evidence']) == (DATED[name][0], DATED[name][0], DATED[name][1]) else [f'{name}: package day or evidence']\n   277\t        failures += [] if leak['latest_judgement'] == leak['expected_judgement'] else [f'{name}: judgement']\n   278\t        failures += [f'{name}: {phrase} found' for phrase, hits in leak['phrase_fields'].items() if hits]\n   279\t    failures += [] if (results['control']['id'], results['control']['answer']) == ('v3', 'Yes') and results['control']['label_equals_store'] and results['control']['evidence_equals_store'] else ['control']\n   280\t    closing = results['closing']\n   281\t    failures += [] if closing['reason'] == CLOSING_REASON and closing['bundle_exposes_reason'] and closing['package_open'] is False and closing['reason_absent'] else ['closing']\n   282\t    if failures:\n   283\t        raise SystemExit(f'release check FAILED: {failures}')\n   284\t    print('release check: every acceptance item and budget met; diagnostic hits to read by hand:',\n   285\t          {name: len(s['diagnostics']['hits']) for name, s in results['stores'].items()})\n   286\t\n   287\t\n   288\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   289\t    main(sys.argv[1])\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md | rg -n 'screen|question|sources|history|website' | tail -45\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md | rg -n 'screen|question|sources|history|website' | tail -45\"","aggregated_output":"1:     1\t# \"Forecast unavailable\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\n4:     4\t- D726, \"同意\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\",\n5:     5\t  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \"it is built with the release work, which is not started\";\n17:    17\t- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\n25:    25\t- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\n29:    29\t  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\n31:    31\t  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\n47:    47\t- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\n48:    48\t  - the question and its id;\n49:    49\t  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\n56:    56\t  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\n59:    59\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\n60:    60\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\n66:    66\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\n68:    68\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\n70:    70\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\n71:    71\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\n72:    72\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\n75:    75\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\n85:    85\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\n87:    87\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\n89:    89\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\n91:    91\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\n93:    93\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\n95:    95\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\n96:    96\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\n99:    99\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\n101:   101\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\n102:   102\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\n110:   110\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\n113:   113\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\n114:   114\t  - an event question;\n119:   119\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\n129:   129\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", with no scored driver and no\n134:   134\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\n139:   139\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
