{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md | sed -n '43,62p;116,148p'\"","aggregated_output":"    43\t  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\n    44\t  - no `--composite-trials` input.\n    45\t\n    46\t  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\n    47\t- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\n    48\t  - the question and its id;\n    49\t  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\n    50\t  - the marker \"Forecast unavailable\".\n    51\t\n    52\t  Nothing else is listed:\n    53\t  - no ladder;\n    54\t  - no band, label or condition;\n    55\t  - no reasons or why_changed;\n    56\t  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\n    57\t  - no closing band (\"closed\" only);\n    58\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\n    59\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\n    60\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\n    61\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\n    62\t  delivered card.\n   116\t  - a real closing switch;\n   117\t  - an idea.\n   118\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\n   119\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\n   120\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\n   121\t- **Mutants:**\n   122\t  - an extra field;\n   123\t  - a fetch left on;\n   124\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\n   125\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\n   126\t\n   127\t  Each must fail.\n   128\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\n   129\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", with no scored driver and no\n   130\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\n   131\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\n   132\t    prose rule.\n   133\t- **The $0 release check.**\n   134\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\n   135\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\n   136\t    final band there.\n   137\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\n   138\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\n   139\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\n   140\t\n   141\t## 6. Not in scope\n   142\t\n   143\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\n   144\t- The closed v13s line.\n   145\t- Other open defects.\n   146\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\n   147\t- The POC's own behaviour.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
