{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'filter|dark|phone|mobile|class count|opening|source link|page|screen' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md,RELEASE-BUILD.md,codex-r74.md} | head -70; nl -ba web/design-system/tokens.css | head -22; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md | tail -32; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r75d.md | head -45\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'filter|dark|phone|mobile|class count|opening|source link|page|screen' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md,RELEASE-BUILD.md,codex-r74.md} | head -70; nl -ba web/design-system/tokens.css | head -22; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md | tail -32; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r75d.md | head -45\"","aggregated_output":"docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:48:| Research groups | **Leave them out.** They add generated names, scopes and aliases, and the agreed release screen needs none of them. [Group reader:213](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/bundle.py:213) · [D756 screen requirement:11833](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11833) |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:8:Opening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:15:- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:38:  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:40:- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:63:- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:120:  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:134:  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:143:- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:24:fixed by D726, D756 and `FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4). This page holds the AGENTS §2 tables for the first slice.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:93:- **Slice 1 (this page), $0:**\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:99:- **Slice 2, next.** The release page reads only the package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:100:  trials, no idea submission control or route. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen, which completes D756's screen check.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:105:  - the POC, its API, MCP and page (unchanged);\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:106:  - colleagues' page;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:291:- the release page (slice 2);\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:328:| The UI contract rejects unknown fields | the release's own `check_export`; the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:498:  - Both agree: no digit filter, no change to extraction.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:500:  The quote is shown beside it, so the source wording is on the reader's screen. A later version can drop the field from the\n     1\t/* Shared Hivemind theme tokens. */\n     2\t:root {\n     3\t  --paper: #f5f2eb;\n     4\t  --wash: #ebe9e2;\n     5\t  --wash-strong: #e3e0d9;\n     6\t  --rule: #dfddd6;\n     7\t  --rule-strong: #c9c7c0;\n     8\t  --ink: #0f140d;\n     9\t  --ink-2: #393d36;\n    10\t  --ink-3: #6a6c65;\n    11\t  --ink-4: #9f9f98;\n    12\t  --scrim: rgba(245, 242, 235, 0.72);\n    13\t  --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(15, 20, 13, 0.04), 0 12px 32px rgba(15, 20, 13, 0.10);\n    14\t\n    15\t  --sans: \"Geist\", \"Helvetica Neue\", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\n    16\t  --mono: \"Geist Mono\", \"SF Mono\", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;\n    17\t\n    18\t  --gutter: 40px;\n    19\t  --control-height: 30px;\n    20\t  --ease: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1);\n    21\t  color-scheme: light;\n    22\t}\n   130\t**Recorded for each page:**\n   131\t- the page's own network requests (`Network.requestWillBeSent` for the page target). Only the document itself may appear;\n   132\t- console errors, exceptions and CSP violations (`Runtime.exceptionThrown`, `Log.entryAdded`). Zero are allowed.\n   133\t\n   134\t**The screen of `old-1/v8`:**\n   135\t- its article shows exactly the stored question, \"Open\", \"Forecast unavailable\" and \"1284 pieces of evidence\";\n   136\t- opening its details shows `e2295`'s stored summary;\n   137\t- the article's text holds none of `v8`'s five labels, five conditions, or the system's \"About $390 billion\" (`j1580`) outside the\n   138\t  quoted evidence;\n   139\t- a screenshot of the card is saved with the result.\n   140\t\n   141\t**The leak screens:** `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` show \"Answer: Yes\" at their own days, and their explanations appear nowhere in the\n   142\tpage text.\n   143\t\n   144\t**The fetch mutant.** The same check on a copy of the `old-1` page with a fetch inserted must fail. That proves the check sees a\n   145\trestored live fetch.\n   146\t- **Measured on this Mac (Chrome 158, headless, scratchpad probe):** a fetch blocked by the CSP produces **no**\n   147\t  `Network.requestWillBeSent`. It produces two `Log.entryAdded` errors:\n   148\t  - source `security`: \"Connecting to '…' violates the following Content Security Policy directive …\";\n   149\t  - source `javascript`: \"Fetch API cannot load …\".\n   150\t- **So the check fails a page on either signal:** any request other than the document, or any `Log.entryAdded` error.\n   151\t- **The mutant fetch targets `http://127.0.0.1:9/library`,** a port nothing listens on, never Alex's service on 8788.\n   152\t  The scratchpad probe page itself named port 8788. Chrome refused it under the CSP before connecting (\"Refused to connect\"), so no\n   153\t  request reached that service.\n   154\t\n   155\t**Budget,** set before the first control: the `old-1` page renders its question list within 3 s of load in headless Chrome, and its\n   156\tsize is at most the data's bytes plus 64 KB.\n   157\t\n   158\t## 7. Prior decisions\n   159\t\n   160\tD726, D756, D757, D758, D759; council 74 (no idea input); council 75d (literal expected values); D690 (poc-v118 stays the product);\n   161\tD163 (English product text).\n     1\t**Verdict — slice 1 is not accepted.** I rechecked all four saved packages against their stores and found no off-list field or mismatched value. The production checker also refused both copies containing the substituted `$390 billion` forecast for the expected reasons. Three verification gaps remain. [results.json:44597](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23d/results.json:44597)\n     2\t\n     3\t1. **Test 2 still accepts a forecast label in an evidence summary.** I replaced `e6`’s summary with the single word `Bullish` in memory. Test 2 passed. It takes the text it considers genuine from `e6` in the export under test, so changing the summary also changes the expected answer. The production checker correctly refused `question v5.evidence e6.one_line`. The test needs to compare each permitted occurrence with the fixture’s original text at that location. [Fixture, test_release.py:107](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:107) · [Assertion, test_release.py:203](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:203)\n     4\t\n     5\t2. **Test 21 still accepts an incomplete printed report.** I replayed its assertions with a report containing only the date, one comparison count and `export_seconds`. It passed with both store paths, the unresolved list, byte size and check time missing. The command currently prints the full report, and the new mutant proves that removing *all* report output is caught. The test needs to check the complete set of required fields. [Test, test_release.py:610](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:610) · [Report contents, RELEASE-BUILD.md:238](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:238) · [Command, release_build.py:100](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/release_build.py:100)\n     6\t\n     7\t3. **The decisive acceptance check can pass after the genuine analyst quote is gone.** In memory, I replaced `e3597`’s quote in both the stored record and its package copies with the system’s own `j1580` forecast. The script marked the quote present, equal to the store and holding its own wording. It returned zero failures because both texts contain `$390 billion`. The refusal checks have a related gap. A stale-hash refusal also satisfied the check that specifically requires the substituted summary to fail comparison with its store. The acceptance case needs wording that distinguishes the analyst quote and the specific reason for each refusal. [Required case, RELEASE-BUILD.md:453](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:453) · [Wording check, release_check.py:162](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:162) · [Pass decision, release_check.py:240](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:240)\n     8\t\n     9\tThe other findings from rounds 75, 75b and 75c are closed for the reviewed snapshots. Those fixes cover historical classification, all ten required text fields, resolved store paths, nonblocking pipe refusal, hashing and parsing the same bytes, ordered records, and the staging, missing-item and writer self-check tests. The mutant runner now checks the full XML failure text for a failed scratch edit. [release.py:87](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:87) · [release.py:458](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:458) · [test_release.py:329](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:329) · [test_release.py:642](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:642) · [release_mutants.py:86](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_mutants.py:86)\n    10\t\n    11\t**The rewritten report’s measurements hold.** I reproduced all four comparison counts and byte sizes, both forecast refusals, and the 257 label-matching fields containing 32 distinct texts. The saved timings support the reported 1.24–1.26× range. The recorded runs show 36 release tests passed, 30 of 31 mutants caught and 425 full-suite tests passed. The overstatements are that the two test gaps are closed and that every missed acceptance item makes the script fail. [Report claims, RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:49](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:49) · [Acceptance claim, RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:79](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:79) · [Full-suite output:2](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/tasks/bwx9cysnh.output:2)","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
